TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Meaningful Citations
DESCRIPTION:Discover strategies for integrating sources into your writing so that your own ideas respond to those of other scholars. Learn when, how, and why crediting your sources is so important in university writing.\nThe Write Now! series consists of four workshops, each of which focuses on one aspect of the writing process:\nWorkshop 1: Analyze Your Assignment\nWorkshop 2: Construct an Argument\nWorkshop 3: Meaningful Citations\nWorkshop 4: Effective Editing\nAt the end of each workshop, you’ll receive access to a quiz, which you will need to complete within 72 hours of the workshop date. If you pass the quiz, you will receive a badge, which will be recorded on the Write Now! eClass site.\nIf you attend all four workshops and pass each workshop’s quiz within one academic calendar year, you’ll attain a Certificate of Completion that can be added to your resume and professional networking sites, such as LinkedIn. Students must join workshop in the first 15 minutes and attend at least 60 minutes of it to take the test.\nClick to authenticate and join!\nClick Here\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/meaningful-citations-6/
ORGANIZER;CN=James Robertson:MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Community Hub,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Student Success,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp;PS Students-International,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,LA&amp;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
LOCATION:Online Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/laptop-students-sources_James-Robertson-6-1.jpg
