TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:From Vision to Action: Mobilizing Unions, Workers and Students For a Radically-Just Transition
DESCRIPTION:With: Garance Malivel, Education Sector Coordinator at Workers for Climate Justice / Travailleuses et travailleurs pour la justice climatique (TJC)  \nDrawing on the work of Montreal-based TJC, this workshop will explore how popular education, participatory research, and collective organizing can strengthen democratic power in the workplace. It will highlight Transformations en cours, a pilot campaign led with teachers’ unions and student associations to develop a shared vision and strategy for transforming Quebec’s higher education system.   \n[RSVP here] \nThis event is part of the 2026-2027 series Up in Flames: Anticolonial Impulses for a Radically-Just Transition, a collaboration between the Global Labour Research Centre (GLRC) ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/glrc/ ), Infrastructure Beyond Extractivism (IBE) and Trade Unions and Labour Environmentalism Network (TULE).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/from-vision-to-action-mobilizing-unions-workers-and-students-for-a-radically-just-transition/
ORGANIZER;CN=Global Labour Research Centre:MAILTO:glrc@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Research &amp; Innovation,YFile newsletter
LOCATION:140 HNES Building
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Garance-Malivel_YFile-Banner.png
END:VEVENT
