TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Book Launch: “Austerity & Resistance: The Ontario Days of Action, 1995-1998”
DESCRIPTION:[HYBRID EVENT – Author in attendance (in-person)!]\nJoin us online and in-person for the launch of Paul Kellogg’s new book Austerity and Resistance: The Ontario Days of Action, 1995–1998. Published 30 years after the Toronto general strike of October 1996, Austerity and Resistance aims to tell its story of the social movement and lessons that we can carry forward today.\nThe launch event will feature a moderated panel discussion and author remarks. Light refreshments will be served.\n[Register for the event here ( https://forms.gle/M1KvGbqyDoHtTnDV8 )]\n—-\nPanelists: \n\nJudy Rebick, author of Heroes in My Head (House of Anansi Press, 2018)\nEsther Reiter, author of A Future Without Hate or Need (Between the Lines, 2016)\nHerman Rosenfeld, retired national staff, Canadian Auto Workers (Unifor)\n\nPanel Moderator: Phil Henderson, Banting Postdoctoral Fellow at the GLRC\nFor questions, email glrc@yorku.ca.\nEvent coordinated by the Global Labour Research Centre (GLRC) at York University, and co-sponsored by Society for Socialist Studies and the Department of Politics, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies at York University.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-austerity-resistance-the-ontario-days-of-action-1995-1998/
ORGANIZER;CN=Global Labour Research Centre:MAILTO:glrc@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Open to the Public,Research &amp; Innovation,YFile newsletter
LOCATION:4700 Keele St, Ian MacDonald Blvd, North York, ON M3J 1P3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/YFile_Banner-scaled.jpg
