TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:EUC Co-op Information Session
DESCRIPTION:\nCo-op is available for students in Environmental Arts & Justice, Sustainable Environmental Management, Cities, Regions & Planning, and Global Geography.\nThe York University Co-op Program provides students with an opportunity for paid, hands-on learning and industry experience.\nCo-op Information Session for Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) students\nDate: October 28, 2026\nTime: 1:30 pm-2:30 pm\nJoin us to learn about:\n\nCo-op and Internship Advantage\nEligibility Requirements\nFees\nRegistration Process\nGeneral Q & A\n\nWhat’s the difference between attending a live session or webinar and engaging in  the self-paced/asynchronous modules on the Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)? \n\nWe value students’ feedback and based on past feedback, students asked for flexible ways to complete the required sessions. There are benefits to each modality. The benefit of attending the live session is that you will have a Q& A session with a Co-op Coordinator. The benefit of completing the sessions through eClass via learning modules is that you can complete these at a time that is more convenient for you!\n\nIMPORTANT REMINDERS: \n\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete the mandatory sessions again. You do not need to re-apply to the program to state your interest. If you have an eligible work term for Fall 2027, simply log-in to the portal and accept the terms and conditions.\n\nWe are looking forward to your participation!\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\nACCESSIBILITY: Should you require accommodations, please contact us at askcoop@yorku.ca and a member of our team will connect with you regarding your request.\nCODE OF CONDUCT\nPrior to the event, we kindly ask you to review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the York University Office of Student Community Relations, so that we can ensure an enjoyable experience for everyone in our community. Please note, guests who exhibit behaviours that violate this code will be exited from the event by the hosts. If you face behaviours that violate this code, please connect with our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/euc-co-op-information-session/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mandatory Sessions (CCC),Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Information Sessions (CCC)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:York University
CLASS:PUBLIC
UID:MEC-3946286620b2e1ed380a77193fb7add7@events.yorku.ca
DTSTART:20261019T183000Z
DTEND:20261019T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T132500Z
CREATED:20261002
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
SEQUENCE:4
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session: In Person
DESCRIPTION:\nYork University Co-op Information Session \nDate: October 19, 2026\nTime: 2:30pm-4:00pm\nLocation: Victor Phillip Dahdaleh Building, Room 1012\nThe York University Co-op Program provides students with opportunities for paid, hands-on learning and valuable industry experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education website to review program details and confirm that you meet the academic requirements.\nDuring this session, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nEligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\nGeneral Q&A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nWho should attend? These sessions are for York University students intending to begin their first co-op work term in Summer 2027. Before registering, please self-assess your eligibility for the program ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunities/co-op/eligibility/ ).\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased on student feedback, we now offer flexible options to complete the required sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a Co-op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a time that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired sessions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready attended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to attend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete the mandatory sessions or re-apply.\nIf you have an eligible work term for Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and conditions when prompted.\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nHaving trouble logging in? \nPlease make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Single Sign-On), you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials. If you use a different login, you may not be able to access the system.\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\n \nAccessibility\nIf you require accommodations, please contact askcoop@yorku.ca, and a member of our team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore attending, please review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the York University Office of Student Community Relations to help ensure a respectful and positive experience for all participants.\nGuests who exhibit behaviour that violates this code may be removed from the event. If you experience behaviour that does not align with these expectations, please contact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-in-person/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mandatory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
END:VEVENT
