SUMMARY:Flow & Sew
DESCRIPTION:Every cycle comes with a cost. Menstrual products like pads and tampons are a necessity, but with prices climbing, that monthly run to the store adds up fast. Long term, it’s expensive and it’s not sustainable for everyone or the planet.\n\nJoin Help A Girl Out (HAGO) for an informative, hands-on session on reusable menstrual products. The workshop opens with a short education segment on reusable options, followed by a beginner-friendly sewing session where you’ll make your own reusable menstrual pad.\n\nYou will learn how…\n\nReusables save money and cut waste\nTo advance menstrual equity\nTo sew your own reusable pad\n\nNo prior sewing experience needed. All materials and tools are provided and you’ll leave with a finished pad plus practical care tips.\n\nSpaces are limited – register for Flow & Sew ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=506509 ) to save your spot!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/flow-sew/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being:MAILTO:schw@yorku.ca
