SUMMARY:Rent Ready: Rights and Responsibilities for Tenants in Ontario
DESCRIPTION:Leaky taps, pests or issues with your tenancy? Get informed before small problems escalate.\nJoin CLASP ( https://www.yorku.ca/osgoode/clasp/ ), York’s on-campus legal clinic, for a practical, student-focused legal information session that breaks down rights and responsibilities as a tenant. Learn about maintenance issues, notices and what to expect during a Landlord and Tenant Board (LTB) hearing. Led by supervising lawyer Anum Malik and CLASP law students.\nDate: Friday, October 9\nTime: 1:30 to 3PM\nLocation: First Student Centre, Room 307\nYou’re welcome to drop in, but if you think you’ll be coming, please register. Registration helps us plan for enough food, without so much that it goes to waste. It also lets us account for allergies and dietary preferences, so everyone can enjoy the snacks safely.\nRegister for Rent Ready! ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=506383 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/rent-ready-rights-and-responsibilities-for-tenants-in-ontario/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being:MAILTO:schw@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,BE-YU,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp; Culture,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Health Education &amp; Promotion,Indigenous,LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,Libraries,Osgoode Hall Law School,School of Continuing Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Schulich School of Business,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre,Well-being,Well-being Week
LOCATION:FSC (First Student Centre) Room 307
