SUMMARY:Graduate Admissions – Community Drop In Hour (Newmarket)
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a Graduate Admissions 1:1 Drop In Session, in person, in your community!\nJoin us on the following dates: to ask any questions that you might have about York University and our graduate admissions process.\nWednesday October 28, 10:00 a.m. – 1:00 p.m. (Scarborough Civic Centre Library)\nTuesday November 3rd, 4:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m. (Mississauga – Hazel McCallion Library)\nTuesday November 10th, 4:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m. (Toronto Reference Library)\nThursday November 19th, 5:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m. (Newmarket Public Library)\nRegistration is required for specific event location info (room number).\nWhile you are welcome to drop in at any point during the session, attendees will be seen on a first-come-first-serve basis. When you arrive, please add your name to the sign in sheet, and we will see participants one-by-one, for a maximum of ten minutes each. We cannot guarantee a specific meeting time. If you are interested in a (timed) 1:1 online appointment, we offer those as well.\nPLEASE NOTE: During these sessions we will not be able to answer any questions about Schulich School of Business programs, or Osgoode Law School Professional LLM programs (either Part Time, or Full Time), or PAcc (Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting).\nFor all other questions about graduate diplomas, master’s programs, and doctoral degrees, we look forward to having you attend.\nIf you have any accessibility requirements for this event, please let us know at ewatson@yorku.ca ( mailto:ewatson@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/graduate-admissions-community-drop-in-hour-newmarket/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Glendon Masters in Public &amp; International Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Socia