SUMMARY:EmpowerAbility’s Experience Matching Program – Information Session
DESCRIPTION:\nEmpowerAbility\n\n\n\n\nEmpowerAbility is a career transition program dedicated to helping students with disabilities build the skills, knowledge and confidence needed to successfully enter the workforce.\nLooking for an opportunity to gain experience and build your résumé? Join us to learn about EmpowerAbility’s Experience Matching program, designed for first- and second-year students with little to no prior experience.\nDiscover how the program can help you connect with volunteer and experiential learning opportunities. The session will cover:\n\nEligibility requirements\nThe application and selection process\nProgram expectations\nHow to prepare for a successful experience\n\nCome learn how Experience Matching can help you gain valuable experience, develop your skills, and strengthen your résumé.\nNote: Students requiring accommodations to participate in the event should email their requests to empowerability@yorku.ca (Please do not disclose diagnosis in your email).\nDetails:\nEvent Date: Thursday Oct 8, 2026\nEvent Time: 2:30-3:30PM\nEvent Location: VDB 1014\n \n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/empowerabilitys-experience-matching-program-information-session/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,EmpowerAbility (CCC),Workshops &amp; Webinars (CCC)
LOCATION:1014 Victor Philip Dahdaleh Building
