SUMMARY:Sustainable Energy Systems (MEng)
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Sustainable Energy Systems ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/Hd7g515vT2iwkKMHAv1XIQ )? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/Hd7g515vT2iwkKMHAv1XIQ )!\nThe Master of Engineering (MEng) in Sustainable Energy Systems is a course-based graduate degree offered through the Department of Mechanical Engineering at York University’s Lassonde School of Engineering. It’s designed for people who want to enter or advance within the sustainable energy sector, with a strong focus on career outcomes, applied learning, and professional growth. Rather than a research thesis, this program emphasizes advanced coursework, real-world applications, and leadership development—so you graduate ready to contribute at a higher level. Please note: this session will cover all programs available in the Lassonde School of Engineering.\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs  ( http://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sustainable-energy-systems-meng/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
