SUMMARY:Financial Accountability (MFAc)
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Financial Accountability ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/6wmCtT2aR5KnUrJwtr7kVQ )? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/6wmCtT2aR5KnUrJwtr7kVQ ).\nYork’s Master of Financial Accountability (MFAc) is the only program of its kind in the world. The MFAc is a way to accelerate your entry into senior management, assurance, and oversight functions. Students are equipped with the appropriate tools and knowledge required to deal innovatively with complex organizational, ethical, legislative, and financial realities faced by organizations. You will acquire strong critical knowledge and practical skills from across a broad range of areas, from information technology to climate change. As a graduate of the program, you will be in a position to assess and strengthen accountability and governance relationships in any public, private, or not-for-profit organization.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy.  ( http://Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy. )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\nRegistration Required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/6wmCtT2aR5KnUrJwtr7kVQ ).\n
