SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub | Beyond Tokenism: Building meaningful inclusion for women, girls, and gender-diverse youth in sports
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Lyndsay Hayhurst, Research Chair and Associate Professor, School of Kinesiology and Health Science, Faculty of Health\nIn this session, we’ll explore the idea that sport is a human right and why inclusion is essential to making that right a reality. Community-based sport-for-development programs can create more welcoming, supportive, and meaningful opportunities for gender-diverse youth to participate in sport. Attendees will gain a practical framework for thinking about inclusion, not as an add-on to sport, but as essential to its purpose. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-beyond-tokenism-building-meaningful-inclusion-for-women-girls-and-gender-diverse-youth-in-sports/
