SUMMARY:Graduate School: The Hidden Curriculum
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled Graduate School: The Hidden Curriculum. Join us!\nGraduate school involves more than coursework, research, and degree milestones. Beyond the formal requirements exists a “hidden curriculum”—the unwritten expectations, academic norms, professional practices, and ways of navigating scholarly communities that shape the graduate experience. This session explores these often-unspoken aspects of academic life and provides practical strategies for building confidence, accessing resources, developing networks, and successfully navigating graduate school. Whether you are new to graduate studies or looking to better understand the culture of academia, this workshop will help make the invisible more visible.\nDate: Wednesday, March 24, 2027\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_DYWb1fJYR-66X1xY_DL1lQ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-the-hidden-curriculum-march-24/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
