SUMMARY:From CV to Resume: Preparing for Careers Beyond Academia
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled From CV to Resume: Preparing for Careers Beyond Academia. Join us!\nTransitioning from academia to other professional pathways often requires rethinking how you communicate your experience, expertise, and accomplishments. While a CV highlights your academic journey, a resume focuses on the skills, impact, and contributions that matter across a range of career contexts. This session explores how to translate graduate training, research experience, teaching, project management, and scholarly achievements into a resume that resonates with employers beyond the university. Participants will gain practical strategies for identifying transferable skills, tailoring application materials, and confidently presenting their experiences for diverse career opportunities.\nDate: Wednesday, February 24, 2027\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN__U8L_p3xQuOdAlE-htRu5Q )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-careers-beyond-academia-february-24/
