SUMMARY:Digital Research Tools for Doctoral Success
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled Digital Research Tools for Doctoral Success. Join us!\nDoctoral research involves managing complex projects, vast amounts of information, and evolving workflows. The right digital tools can help researchers work more efficiently, stay organized, and make the research process more manageable. This session explores practical tools and strategies for citation management, note-taking, collaboration, writing, project planning, and organizing your research workflow. Participants will learn how digital approaches can support effective research practices and help develop sustainable systems for navigating the demands of advanced scholarship.\nDate: Wednesday January 20, 2027\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_YqxllMC-SZuq55Q6grgDag )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-digital-research-tools-january-20/
