SUMMARY:From Research to Real-World Impact: An Introduction to Knowledge Mobilization for Graduate Student Scholars
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled From Research to Real-World Impact: An Introduction to Knowledge Mobilization for Graduate Student Scholars. Join us!\nResearch creates knowledge, but impact happens when knowledge is shared, understood, and used. This interactive session introduces graduate students to the fundamentals of Knowledge Mobilization (KMb) and explores how to move research beyond traditional academic audiences. Topics will include how to identify key audiences, develop effective knowledge-sharing strategies, build meaningful partnerships, and communicate research in ways that support social, community, policy, and professional impact. Whether you are just beginning your research journey or preparing for future careers inside or outside academia, this session will provide practical tools to help amplify the reach and relevance of your work.\nDate: Tuesday December 1, 2026\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_QjJF7v5jQFiV-H6m70-kwg )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-research-to-impact-december-1/
