SUMMARY:Getting Unstuck: Tips for Moving Forward with Your Research
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled Getting Unstuck: Tips for Moving Forward with Your Research. Join us!\nResearch rarely progresses in a straight line. Graduate students often encounter moments of uncertainty, competing priorities, stalled projects, or challenges maintaining momentum over the course of their degree. This session explores practical approaches for planning, prioritizing, and moving research forward when challenges arise. Participants will learn strategies for breaking complex projects into manageable steps, developing sustainable research habits, and maintaining progress throughout the graduate journey.\nDate: Wednesday November 25, 2026\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7IhjteccQV6GUwruclx5cQ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-moving-forward-with-your-research-november-25/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
