SUMMARY:Dissertation Proposal Essentials
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled Dissertation Proposal Essentials. Join us!\nA strong dissertation proposal provides the foundation for a successful research project. A crucial academic milestone, the proposal is also an opportunity to refine your research questions, establish the significance of your work, and develop a clear plan for moving your research forward. This session explores the key elements of an effective dissertation proposal, including developing a research rationale, articulating your methodology, organizing your ideas, and aligning your goals with disciplinary expectations. Participants will gain practical strategies for preparing a proposal that communicates the value and direction of their research with clarity and confidence.\nDate: Wednesday October 21, 2026\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_-9MpLwhdSn-5qhP94aJRrg )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-dissertation-proposal-essentials-october-21/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
