SUMMARY:Theatre at York presents Casimir and Caroline
DESCRIPTION:Casimir and Caroline by Ödon von Horváth ( https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96d%C3%B6n_von_Horv%C3%A1th ) – Adapted by Paolo Santalucia, Holgar Syme with The Howland Co. From an original translation by Holgar Syme\nCasimir and Caroline is a play about love in the cold atmosphere of modern capitalism. We follow these ultra star-crossed lovers, as they navigate clingy co-workers, sketchy best friends, questionable HR representatives, the playboy boss, that powerhouse from the Montreal office and those beautiful few who might actually possess an ounce of wisdom. They all desperately long for something more. None of them can say what that might be. But at least their lives look good on Instagram.\nPerformance Schedule:\nSaturday, November 21 – 7:30pm (Preview)\nSunday, November 22 – 7:30pm (Preview)\nTuesday, November 24 – 7:30pm\nWednesday, November 25 – 7:30pm\nThursday, November 26 – 7:30pm\nFriday, November 27 – 7:30pm\nSaturday, November 28 – 2:00pm | 7:30pm\nLocation: Joseph G. Green Theatre\nTickets ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/index.asp ): \nPreview Tickets (Nov 21 & 22): $ 15.00 | Student: $ 15.00\nAdvanced (until Sunday Nov 22): $ 20.00\nRegular Tickets: $ 25.00\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/theatre-at-york-casimir-and-caroline/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/1.jpg
END:VEVENT
