SUMMARY:Grad program in Environmental Studies (PHD)
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in the PhD in Environmental Studies ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/2dbCbppjQ4Krmcz6TKYOZA )? We invite you to attend our program session!\nCreatively redefine the boundaries of environmental research. Adopting an interdisciplinary lens for your PhD in Environmental Studies, you will create a unique Program Plan, to be guided by your supervisory committee. Using various conceptual approaches to explore environmental issues in their historical and comparative contexts, you will analyze how theoretical and practical matters intersect, and how reflexive, rigorous, critical and creative thinking can inform environmental research, practice and policy. Explore conventional disciplines such as social sciences, humanities, arts and natural sciences in ways that encourage viewing issues through a broader, more contextual perspective, with an emphasis on social justice.\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs  ( http://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\nRegistration Required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/2dbCbppjQ4Krmcz6TKYOZA ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grad-program-in-environmental-studies-phd/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Program in Environmental Studies
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
