SUMMARY:From Wildfire Challenges to ClimateTech Opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Climate AI Innovation Hub: Scaling Climate Solutions with AI\nClimate challenges have accelerated the need for innovative solutions that drive sustainability, resilience, circular economies, and low-carbon transitions. Entrepreneurs play a key role in developing technologies and business models that address environmental issues at scale.\nThis speaker series aims to highlight those innovators, increase awareness of climate entrepreneurship pathways, expose barriers and opportunities in the sector, and empower youth, students, founders, and professionals to engage in meaningful climate innovation.\nSpeaker: Dr. Shahab Bahrami, CBTO, SenseNet Inc.\nMore Information ( https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/climate-ai-innovation/ )\nRegistration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_68b7VXNUS1SN3sc96siaIQ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/from-wildfire-challenges-to-climatetech-opportunities/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Artificial Intelligence,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Faculties,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Future Students,Glendon,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,Lassonde School of Engineering,ORUs,Regional Alumni Events,Research &amp; Innovation,School of Continuing Studies,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,Y-EMERGE,YFile newsletter
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
