SUMMARY:Durham University (England): Graduate Studies Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in graduate studies in England?\nDurham University ( https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/ ) was founded in 1832 as the third-oldest university in England and is a Russell Group research-intensive University. The university currently has over 22,000 students, with 150 bachelor’s and 130 postgraduate programs. Durham University has four faculties: the Business School, Arts and Humanities, Science, and Social Sciences. It is ranked a top 5 university in the UK, a top 100 university in the world, is a collegiate university, and is top 5 in the UK for team sport.\nLearn how you can continue your studies abroad! \nConnect with the recruitment team at this information session, offered at Keele Campus, to learn how you can receive a master’s degree or PhD at Durham. During the presentation, you will learn about postgraduate programs, scholarship opportunities, the application process, life in Durham, England and more.\n\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″] ( https://yorku-csm.symplicity.com/students/?s=event&ss=ws&mode=form&id=7cc9d46d61ec0e8c1d478d46e89fd12a )\n \nTo register, you must log in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/ ) with your Passport York credentials.\n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/durham-university-england-graduate-studies-information-session/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
END:VEVENT
