SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 3 | Making meaningful connections: Staying present in conversations
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\nBuilding connections can sometimes feel exciting, awkward or even a little intimidating.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance, we will focus on helping students feel more comfortable meeting new people, strengthening the relationships they already have and recognizing what makes a connection healthy and supportive.\nStudents will explore ways to:\n\nManage social anxiety\nBuild confidence in social settings\nThink intentionally about who they can turn to for support.\n\nThis session is part of a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended, participants will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card, you must attend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately, we’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards will be emailed after the session to the same email address used to register and join the session.\nSpace is limited, and registration is offered on a first-come, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like to be added to the waitlist, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re registered but can no longer attend, please let us know as soon as you can so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Making meaningful connections: Staying present in conversations ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=499412 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-3-making-meaningful-connections-staying-present-in-conversations/
