SUMMARY:Key Ingredients for Child and Family Well-Being
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nFamily life can be rewarding – but it can also be challenging, particularly when work, school, and other demands compete for our time and attention. Join Dr. Heather Prime, a child psychologist, and Gillian Shoychet, a clinical-developmental doctoral student, from the York University Psychology Clinic for an engaging, research-informed session exploring the key ingredients for fostering family and child well-being. We will discuss how family stress can affect relationships and what helps parents work effectively as a team. We will also explore skills for supporting children’s emotional and behavioural well-being, including emotion coaching and other evidence-informed parenting strategies. The session will conclude by highlighting some of the family-focused supports available through the York University Psychology Clinic.\n\n\n\n\n\nOrganized by Department of Psychology\nFormat: Virtual\nAudience: York Community\nZoom Link\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/key-ingredients-for-child-and-family-well-being/
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
END:VEVENT
