SUMMARY:CineSiege 2026
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nIn its 24th year, CineSiege is an annual showcase screening of outstanding productions created in the previous year by undergraduate students in the Department of Film and Media Arts at York University ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/department-of-film-and-media-arts/ ). CineSiege features a juried selection of short films, chosen by industry leaders in Canadian film and media.\nWe hope you can join us to celebrate the next generation of filmmakers! All nominated films in 3rd and 4th year are also eligible for craft awards i.e. Best Cinematography, Best Sound Design, etc.\nCineSiege 2026\nThursday, November 5, 2026\n7:00 PM – 10:30 PM\n(Please arrive at 6:30 PM, as the show will start promptly at 7:00 PM)\nHot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema: 506 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1Y3\nFREE Admission \nTICKETS \nThis event is made possible with the continued support of our founding sponsor, Cinespace Studios ( https://cinespace.com/cinespace-toronto/ ).\n\n \n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/cinesiege-2026/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema @ 506 Bloor St. West, Toronto
