TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:BIPOC Artist HUB Sign-Up & Welcome Meeting – Vanier College Productions
DESCRIPTION:Vanier College Productions (VCP) is excited to continue with the first-ever BIPOC Artist Hub at York University, open to all BIPOC artists (performance, craft, music, film, visual art, digital, design, literary, etc.) Join us for group discussions, games, guest lecturers and our end of the season showcase where artists curate their own, theme-based, exhibit or performance.\nPrevious showcase themes have been Lost/Found, Fantasy & The World of BIPOACH, World Building & Alternate Worlds along with the Inaugural Showcase that focused on the theme of intersectionality.\nWELCOME MEETING:\nTUE. SEP. 22 4:30-6:00pm in Vanier College, Rm 256 (Conference Room).\nSign up NOW to confirm your attendance!\nWEEKLY MEETINGS:\nTUE 4:30-6:30pm\nTECH/SHOWCASE:\nJan. 27 – Jan. 30, 2027\nTo learn more about the BIPOC Artist HUB, please visit tinyurl.com/vcp-hub\n***IF ALL SLOTS ARE FULL, PLEASE EMAIL VCP@YORKU.CA AND WE’LL HELP YOU GET SIGNED UP***\nSign Up Here\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/bipoc-artist-hub-sign-up-welcome-meeting-vanier-college-productions/
ORGANIZER;CN=Vanier College Productions:MAILTO:smendes@yorku.ca, vcp@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Student Success,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Vanier College Productions
END:VEVENT
