SUMMARY:Screening of The Knowing by Tanya Talaga
DESCRIPTION:From September 21 to 24, community members are invited to attend screenings of The Knowing by award-winning investigative journalist Tanya Talaga. In this powerful documentary series, Talaga pieces together a family mystery that spans more than 150 years, tracing the stories of the maternal matriarchs in her family and travelling to the James Bay coast in search of answers.\nA different episode will be screened each day, with each episode running approximately 45 minutes. Screenings will take place from 2:30 to 3:30 p.m. in 301A York Lanes ( https://map.concept3d.com/?id=1200#!m/354811?share ). Registration is required. Please register online at https://yorku.ca/go/T&RFilmScreening2026 ( https://yorku.ca/go/T&RFilmScreening2026 ). Please note that this series includes stories that may be triggering for survivors of Indian Residential Schools and their families.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/screening-of-the-knowing-by-tanya-talaga/
