SUMMARY:What is Graduate School, and How Do I Pick a Program?
DESCRIPTION:Join us ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_E0Gh0eeESgKjcqvALif5qw ) to learn more about what graduate school actually is!\nDuring this session we’ll go over the details of each graduate credential offered at York: master’s degrees, PhD/doctoral degrees, and graduate diplomas. We’ll discuss admission requirements, program/degree requirements, and what to expect as a graduate student.\nLastly, we’ll discuss how to go about choosing a graduate pathway to pursue.\nIf you have any accessibility requirements for this event, please let us know at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\nRegistration is required. ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_E0Gh0eeESgKjcqvALif5qw )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/what-is-graduate-school-and-how-do-i-pick-a-program/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Conference Interpreting,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Po