SUMMARY:Dean’s Session: How to Write a Statement of Interest
DESCRIPTION:In this session, Vice-Provost and Dean Alice MacLachan will walk you through some essential steps for your graduate studies applications.\nJoin us ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7WJysQSXR_iZaThdK_aJDw ) to learn more about: – how to write a statement of interest – choosing a graduate program – finding and approaching potential research supervisors – other tips and tricks for putting your best foot forward in your graduate studies application.\nThis session ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7WJysQSXR_iZaThdK_aJDw ) is happening as part of Experience Grad York. To find other sessions covering graduate admissions at York, please visit https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nIf you have any accessibility requirements for this event, please let us know at fgsapply@yorku.ca.\nRegistration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7WJysQSXR_iZaThdK_aJDw ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/deans-session-how-to-write-a-statement-of-interest-3/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
