SUMMARY:Heart Garden Campaign
DESCRIPTION:On Sept. 28, community members can visit Heart Garden reflection tables from noon to 3 p.m. at Vari Hall (Keele Campus), the Welcome Desk (Glendon Campus) and the West Atrium (Markham Campus). Participants will be invited to respond to the reflection question and add their thoughts to the Heart Garden. Reflections will be incorporated into the Sept. 30 installation at Skennen’kó:wa Gamig\nA digital reflection ( https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/5evJuqRW00 ) option is also available, and all reflections will be collected and digitized to support a permanent, online Heart Garden for future learning and reflection.\nYU community members are invited to reflect on the question: How does reconciliation manifest in your learning, teaching, research, professional practice, daily work or personal life?\n
