TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Film Screening and Panel Discussion: To Stay, to Leave, to Intervene: Art and Migration through La Última Cachada
DESCRIPTION:In conjunction with the RUTAS festival ( https://www.alunatheatre.ca/festival/rutas-2026/ ) on Monday, September 28, Sensorium, Centre for Research on Latin America and the Caribbean (CERLAC), and the Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance, and Performance Studies will co-host a screening and discussion with artists-activists-scholars from the Hemispheric Encounters Network (HEN), including documentary filmmaker Andrea Rodríguez Marín (Mexico), Magdalena Henríquez (Salvadoran actress and co-founder of La Cachada Teatro), Alina Peña (researcher-professor, ITESO, Universidad Jesuita de Guadalajara), and Amparo Marroquín Parducci (researcher-professor, José Simeón Cañas Central American University).\nJoin us for a screening of La Última Cachada, a powerful documentary about the work of La Cachada Teatro, a Salvadoran feminist theatre collective whose members draw on their own lived experiences to create socially engaged performance about migration amid the shifting political and social realities of El Salvador.\nDate: Monday, September 28\nTime: 2:30 – 4:00 p.m.\nLocation: Sensorium Flex Space – Room 326, Centre for Fine Arts, York University\nRSVP HERE ( https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScM3zYpNQKQ_srMF-KA8IfAmiHYMHO1F5J_q1_Kl62sXo3ZGw/viewform )\nDrawing on the short documentary, the conversation that follows asks the question, “What does a country lose when its people leave?” This discussion brings together theatrical experience, audiovisual creation, and research to approach migration as displacement, desire, loss, and possibility. Through the voices and bodies of La Cachada Teatro, we will explore how art intervenes in reality, transforms lived experience, and opens collective spaces for resistance, memory, and hope.\nFollowing the screening of La Última Cachada and subsequent discussion, Sensorium is inviting all attendees, as well as Sensorium members and prospective members, to join us for a  Fall Meet & Greet in the Sensorium Loft Space to mark the beginning of the semester. This event will be a fantastic opportunity to meet each other informally, learn more about the Sensorium and CERLAC communities, their upcoming events, and ways to get involved. Light refreshments will be served.\nPlease RSVP for both the Film Screening and Meet & Greet, to help us with snacks ordering (drop-ins also welcome).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/film-screening-and-panel-discussion-to-stay-to-leave-to-intervene-art-and-migration-through-la-ultima-cachada/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sensorium Flex Space, 326 Joan and Martin Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts (CFA)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/doc.jpg
END:VEVENT
