SUMMARY:Globally Networked Learning (GNL) Info Session for York Faculty
DESCRIPTION:The Globally Networked Learning (GNL) team is excited to invite you to join the upcoming GNL Information Session on Monday, Sep. 28 (10am-11am ET). The online session is open to all York faculty members and staff who are interested in innovative pedagogies that combine internationalization, experiential education, and co-teaching a course with an international partner.\nAn Overview of the GNL Info Session:\n\n\nWhat and why York GNL\n\n\nGNL examples by York course leaders: Prof. Dominique Scheffel-Dunand (LA&PS) and a guest speaker from faculty of Health \n\n\nPedagogy of GNL (or in other contexts it might be referred to as Collaborative Online International Learning (COIL)),\n\n\n$1000 Award to support piloting your GNL initiatives and other supports and Expression of Interesthttp://Registration link: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/7RIB6kYZQXygqs_KOj2Y9w ( http://Registration link: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/7RIB6kYZQXygqs_KOj2Y9w )\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/globally-networked-learning-gnl-info-session-for-york-faculty/
