SUMMARY:Sparkshop: Guiding Graduate Student Writing
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this Sparkshop with Marlene Bernholtz, Associate Professor in the Writing Department. This session will highlight how reciprocal, considerate writing processes, and clear supervisory communication, help graduate students meet academic and developmental goals.\n\nreflect on the challenges graduate students face when navigating the writing process\nreview and receive a copy of the Writing Centre Guide for Graduate Student Support \nconsider challenges in the writing process that impact the supervisory relationship\nidentify roles and key strategies graduate students can use to support their writing\n\nDate: Tuesday, October 13, 2026\nTime: 11:00AM to 11:30AM ET\nLocation: Online via Zoom\nRegistration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/B1yKNj68RFO_vqrjgsmJiQ ) (click link)\n \nFor more information, contact Tracy Bhoola, Manager, Graduate Supervision Support Hub tbhoola@yorku.ca\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sparkshop-guiding-graduate-student-writing/
