TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Graduate Student Wellness Support Group (for Grad Students)
DESCRIPTION:In this group, you’ll have the opportunity to connect with fellow graduate students, talk openly about the challenges and wins of academic life, and build practical tools for managing stress, strengthening resilience, and caring for your mental well-being. Whether you’re navigating deadlines, self-doubt, isolation, or simply looking for a place to feel grounded, you are welcome here.\nAbove all, this is a confidential and supportive environment designed to help you feel heard, understood, and less alone as you move through your graduate journey. This will be a closed virtual group, and there will be 5 sessions in total.\nThe Dates are as follows: Sept. 17, Oct. 1, 15, 29, and Nov. 12\nWith the following times of each session: 2:30 pm -4:00 pm\nIf you are interested, please register below:\nGraduate Student Wellness Support Group – Fall 2026 (Closed Group) – Fill out form ( https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/Y95T48iq4H )\nThe Zoom link will be sent to you after you register above. If you have any questions, please email gradwell@yorku.ca ( mailto:gradwell@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/graduate-student-wellness-support-group-for-graduate-students/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
