TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:York University Terry Fox Run
DESCRIPTION:Join the York University community for the annual Terry Fox Run, a non-competitive event that brings together students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community members to celebrate Terry Fox’s legacy of courage, determination, and hope. Participants of all ages and fitness levels are welcome to walk, run, or roll while raising awareness and supporting cancer research.\nThis year marks York University’s 30th Terry Fox Run, a significant milestone celebrating three decades of community participation, fundraising, and commitment to Terry’s dream of a world without cancer.\nThe event will begin at the Tait McKenzie Centre, with participants traveling throughout York University’s Keele Campus on a scenic route that showcases the campus while honoring Terry’s inspiring journey. This community event promotes health, wellness, and school spirit while supporting the ongoing fight against cancer.\nRegister individually or as part of a team, invite friends and family, and be part of one of Canada’s most meaningful fundraising traditions.\nTogether, let’s celebrate 30 years of the Terry Fox Run at York University, keep Terry’s dream alive, and make every step count.\nFor more information, visit our run website: https://run.terryfox.ca/129725 ( https://run.terryfox.ca/129725 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-university-terry-fox-run/
ORGANIZER;CN=Athletics &amp; Recreation:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Athletics &amp; Recreation
LOCATION:Tait McKenzie @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Untitled-design-9-1.png
END:VEVENT
