SUMMARY:Multispectral Mapping with Drone
DESCRIPTION:This course aims to give participants a thorough understanding of multispectral mapping and its drone applications. Combining classroom instruction, hands-on drone flying, and practical image analysis, it prepares learners to plan and execute multispectral surveys, gather quality data, and analyze multispectral images for real-world uses. By course end, participants will acquire both theoretical knowledge and practical skills applicable to sectors like agriculture, environmental monitoring, forestry, water resource management, and disaster risk reduction.\nA microcredit certificate will be issued to all participants from CIFAL York upon completion of the course.\nMore Information ( https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/multispectral/ )\nRegistration ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/multispectral-mapping-with-drone-september-19-tickets-1982809980026?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/multispectral-mapping-with-drone-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
