TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session (Online)
DESCRIPTION:\nYork U Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLocation: Online\nDate: October 7, 2026\nTime: 2:00pm-3:30pm\nThe York University Co-op Program provides students with opportunities for paid, hands-on learning and valuable industry experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education website to review program details and confirm that you meet the academic requirements.\nDuring this session, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nEligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\nGeneral Q&A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nThese sessions are available in three formats to support your schedule and learning preferences:\n\nIn-person\nLive webinar (Zoom)\nSelf-paced online modules through the Lassonde Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)\n\nTarget Audience:\nYork U students intending to begin their first co-op work term in Summer 2027. Before registering, please self-assess your eligibility for the program\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased on student feedback, we now offer flexible options to complete the required sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a Co-op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a time that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired sessions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready attended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to attend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete the mandatory sessions or re-apply.\n\nIf you have an eligible work term for Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and conditions when prompted.\n\n\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\nAccessibility\nIf you require accommodations, please contact askcoop@yorku.ca, and a member of our team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore attending, please review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the York University Office of Student Community Relations to help ensure a respectful and positive experience for all participants.\nGuests who exhibit behaviour that violates this code may be removed from the event. If you experience behaviour that does not align with these expectations, please contact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\nHaving trouble logging in? \nPlease make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Single Sign-On), you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials. If you use a different login, you may not be able to access the system.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Co-op Mandatory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
END:VEVENT
