SUMMARY:Sociology Annual Lecture – Pre-Determined Purchasing Power: Governing Algorithmic Price and Wage Discrimination
DESCRIPTION:The annual lecture is a key event for the Department of Sociology. This yearly address offers faculty, staff and students a unique opportunity to meet prominent leaders in the field.\nDistinguished Lecturer: Professor Veena Dubal\nHow do algorithms quietly determine your wages and the prices you pay? Guest speaker professor Veena Dubal reveals how data-driven systems are reshaping economic life—and entrenching inequality—before transactions even begin.\nRegister Here\nLearn More\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sociology-annual-lecture-2026/
