SUMMARY:2026 Vico Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Immigration posed a difficult question for interwar Canadian socialists. One the one hand, they promoted a universalist vision of a Cooperative Commonwealth; on the other, they wished to protect Canadian workers from foreign competition. This lecture explores how social democrats like J.S. Woodsworth, Agnes Macphail and A.A. Heaps navigated these turbulent waters.\nSpeaker: Edward Dunsworth\nRegister (In-Person)\nRegister (Online)\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2026-vico-lecture/
ORGANIZER;CN=Abril Liberatori:MAILTO:lapscoms@yorku.ca
