SUMMARY:A Panel on Digital Health: How Technology Is Transforming Health Care
DESCRIPTION:Discover how technology is transforming the way we access, experience and manage health care at a free community lecture hosted by York University, in collaboration with the City of Vaughan and Mackenzie Health.\nThe event features speakers and experts from York University, City of Vaughan, Southlake Health, Mackenzie Health, and Oak Valley Health.\nAsk questions of the experts. Learn about emerging digital health innovations that are shaping the future of patient care while connecting with partners offering health resources and hands-on activities.\nAs York University works toward the launch of its new School of Medicine (pending accreditation), discussions like these highlight our commitment to modern, technology-enabled community health care.\nLight refreshments provided. Registration is preferred but not required. All are welcome.\n\nThursday, Sept. 24 | 6:30 to 9 p.m.\nVaughan City Hall, 2141 Major Mackenzie Drive\nVaughan Room, first floor\n\n\nPanelists:\n\nDr. Aviv Gladman, Chief Medical Information Officer, Mackenzie Health\nDr. Nour Khatib, Emergency Department Physician and Chief Medical Information Officer, Oak Valley Health\nSam Fielding, Chief Information Officer, Southlake Health\nDr. Vijay Mago, Associate Professor, School of Health Policy and Management, York University\nPanel Moderator: Mira Backo-Shannon, Vice Dean, Integrated Community-Based Learning Network and Health Systems, York University School of Medicine\n\n\n\nRegister here: yorku.ca/go/2026VaughanCommunityHealthLecture ( https://yorku.ca/go/2026VaughanCommunityHealthLecture )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/digital-health-a-panel-on-exploring-the-future-of-health-care/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculties,Faculty of Health,Well-being
LOCATION:2141 Major MacKenzie Dr W, Vaughan
