SUMMARY:Writing into Summer: Building a Productive Writing Practice
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are developing a dissertation proposal, drafting a thesis chapter, or preparing a journal article, this workshop will help you make meaningful progress on your academic writing. Participants will explore practical strategies for planning and managing large writing projects, maintaining motivation, and developing sustainable writing routines. With an emphasis on overcoming common writing challenges and creating achievable goals, it may be of particular interest to graduate students planning for a summer term of focused writing.\nThe workshop is open to graduate students at all stages of their programs and across disciplines. Participants are encouraged to bring a current writing project or idea and be prepared to engage in hands-on exercises and collaborative activities designed to support the development of a successful writing practice.\nEvent Details:\nDATE: Thursday, April 1, 2027\nTIME: 1:00-2:30 p.m.\nLOCATION: online (Zoom)\nPartner: Writing Centre\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/writing-into-summer/
