SUMMARY:Applied Qualitative Research: A Practical Guide for Graduate Student Researchers
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in gaining an understanding of how to design, conduct, and present applied qualitative research? If so, these online workshops are for you! While this series is particularly intended for graduate students, FGS additionally invites and warmly welcomes graduate faculty including supervisors and committee members, as well as research staff, and postdocs. Feel free to come to one, two or all of them! Workshops will be delivered virtually and will be recorded. Registration is required.\nFacilitated by Dr. Karen Campbell, RN, PhD ( https://www.linkedin.com/in/kcamp232/?originalSubdomain=ca ), Assistant Professor, School of Nursing, York University. Dr. Campbell’s program of research focuses on the intersections of women’s health with physical and social geography. She has taught graduate-level courses in qualitative research and designed and conducted multiple applied qualitative research projects using a broad range of study designs and approaches to analysis.\nHosted by Associate Dean, Academic, Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith, RN, PhD\nWebinar One: A Guide to Applied Qualitative Research\nThis webinar provides graduate students, supervisors, and researchers with a practical foundation in applied qualitative research. Participants will explore key qualitative methodologies, research design considerations, data collection strategies, and approaches to generating rigorous and meaningful findings.\nWhen: Tuesday, January 12, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\nWebinar Two: Coding Qualitative Data\nThis webinar introduces the principles and practices of qualitative data coding, from developing initial codes to identifying patterns and themes. Through practical examples, participants will learn strategies for organizing, analyzing, and interpreting qualitative data in a systematic and transparent manner.\nWhen: Tuesday, February 9, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\nWebinar Three: Generative AI in Qualitative Data Analysis \nThis webinar examines the emerging role of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) in qualitative research and data analysis. Participants will explore opportunities, limitations, ethical considerations, and practical applications of GenAI tools to support coding, theme development, data synthesis, and research productivity while maintaining methodological rigor.\nWhen: Tuesday, March 9, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/applied-qualitative-research/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/pexels-cottonbro-studio-9400300-2-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
