SUMMARY:AI at York: From Awareness to Action
DESCRIPTION:Artificial Intelligence is rapidly transforming higher education, changing how we teach, learn, conduct research, and support university operations. This session will provide an overview of York University’s AI journey, explore what generative AI is and why it matters, and examine the opportunities and challenges AI presents for the higher education sector, including environmental considerations and responsible use.\nParticipants will learn how to effectively work with AI by combining artificial intelligence with their own expertise, discover the AI tools available and approved at York, including Microsoft Copilot and GitHub Copilot, explore resources available to graduate students and postdoctoral researchers, and gain insight into York-developed innovations such as YU AURA and the Modular Authentication & RBAC System (MARS). The session is designed to help researchers move beyond AI awareness toward practical, productive, and responsible AI adoption.\nEvent Details\nDATE: Wednesday, November 11, 2026\nTIME: 1:00-2:00 p.m.\nLOCATION: Online (Zoom)\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ai-at-york-from-awareness-to-action/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
