SUMMARY:FGS Tri-Council and OGS Application Workshop – Master’s Students
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is offering a virtual workshop to support Master’s students preparing applications for the upcoming Tri-Council and Ontario Graduate Scholarship (OGS) competitions. This workshop provides an overview of the application process and practical guidance on preparing a strong research proposal for the Canada Graduate Research Scholarships (CGRS) competitions (Master’s; SSHRC, NSERC, and CIHR), as well as the Ontario Graduate Scholarship (OGS) competition at the master’s level. The session will conclude with a live Q&A, giving participants the opportunity to ask questions about the application process and proposal development.\nDate: Tuesday, October 20, 2026\nTime: 9:30-11:30 a.m.\nLocation: Online Zoom\nRegistration is required. ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/BbNltNFbTyKFVyywvaL0cw )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tri-council-ogs-scholarship-workshop-masters-2/
