SUMMARY:Fostering Black Scholar Scholarship Success Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is pleased to host the fourth annual Fostering Black Scholars Scholarship Success Workshop. This workshop is designed to highlight funding opportunities available to Black graduate students and provide practical strategies for navigating the scholarship application process. Participants will hear from accomplished Black faculty members and graduate scholars who have received prestigious awards as they share their experiences, insights, and advice on pursuing funding and building a successful academic career. Zoom details will be shared with participants upon registration.\nDigital Badge Opportunity\nAttend and participate in this workshop to be eligible for a digital badge recognizing your professional development and engagement.\nDate: Wednesday, August 26, 2026\nTime: 10:00 a.m.-12:00 p.m.\nLocation: Online Zoom\nRegistration is required. ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/XKKbW6KDQs2X0iDVlKqihQ#/registration )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-shcolar-scholarship-workshop/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
