TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:YU Speak: Where Ideas Take Shape
DESCRIPTION:Nervous about presentations or public speaking?\nYU Speak is a supportive, hands-on workshop series designed to help you build confidence, strengthen your communication skills, and become a more effective presenter. Through interactive activities, peer feedback, and guided practice, you’ll learn how to:\n\nUnderstand your audience and craft clear, engaging messages\nStructure presentations and tell compelling stories\nDesign effective slides and visual aids\nImprove delivery, body language, and presentation presence\nNavigate group and online presentations with confidence\n\nWhether you’re preparing for class presentations, competitions, interviews, or future career opportunities, YU Speak provides a low-stakes environment to practice and grow. Students can also earn certificates and participation badges by completing workshop milestones. \n\nLocation: Markham Campus, Room 2050\nFormat: 6-week series (5 workshops + 1 culminating presentation event)\nDuration: Every Thursdays from 10:00am – 11:30am\nDates:\n\nSeptember 24th\nOctober 1st\nOctober 8th, no session during Reading Week\nOctober 22nd\nOctober 29th\nNovember 5th\n\nRegistration Link: YU Speak: Where Ideas Take Shape (Fall 2026) – Fill out form ( https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/KUSWKDCbtg )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/yu-speak-where-ideas-take-shape/
ORGANIZER;CN=Learning Skills &amp; Academic Success:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp; Student Success,Markham Campus
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Events-Calendar-Image-3.png
END:VEVENT
