SUMMARY:GradForward Online Series (for Master’s & Doctoral Students)
DESCRIPTION:Kickstart Fall 2026 with Confidence!\nOur GradForward series at York University offers a comprehensive lineup of 30-minute virtual sessions designed to support both incoming and continuing graduate students. Scheduled from September 9 to September 11, 2026, these sessions cover essential topics such as scholarships and awards, graduate funding, academic integrity, professional skills development, student affairs, and effective use of graduate portals.\nLed by experienced faculty and staff, the series aims to equip students with the knowledge and resources needed to navigate their graduate studies successfully. All sessions are free and accessible via Zoom, providing an excellent opportunity for students to engage with the University’s support services and build a strong foundation for their academic journey.\nEvent Details:\nDATE: September 9 to September 11, 2026\nTIME: various time throughout the day\nLOCATION: via Online Webinar\nVIEW FULL SCHEDULE ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/grad-forward-series/ )\n*Registration is required | yorku.ca/gradstudies/grad-forward-series ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/grad-forward-series/ )\n
URL:https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/grad-forward-series/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
