SUMMARY:Creative Course Content: Instructional Strategies for Learning (Online – 1 Feb.-5 Mar., 2027)
DESCRIPTION:This course can count toward the Certificates in University Teaching: https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/certificates/\nCommunicating course content to students is one of the biggest challenges instructors face in any classroom. While the lecture is a mainstay of the traditional classroom, there are several challenges to this approach, ranging from the technical to the cognitive. In this fully online course, participants will learn by doing through ongoing participation in weekly learning activities. Together we will model alternatives to the “standard” lecture, practice creative and efficient ways to convey content to students, apply best practices for designing instruction of all types, and troubleshoot common challenges.\nVisit our registration page to learn more and to sign up: https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2125 ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2125 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/creative-course-content-instructional-strategies-for-learning-online-1-feb-5-mar-2027/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Online via eClass and Zoom
