SUMMARY:The Ecological Value of Ontario’s Greenbelt
DESCRIPTION:This webinar marks the launch of new biocapacity data for Ontario’s Greenbelt. Developed through a collaboration between York University’s Ecological Footprint Initiative and the Greenbelt Foundation, this research highlights the Greenbelt’s ecological value and demonstrates the important benefits it provides to all Ontarians, in terms of both regenerating the natural resources we consume and absorbing the waste we produce.\nJoin us to explore findings from the report, The Ecological Value of Ontario’s Greenbelt ( https://greenbelt.ca/research-report/the-ecological-value-of-ontarios-greenbelt/ ), and see the new digital data dashboard ( https://footprintpartnership.net/greenbelt/ ) in action.\nRegister for the virtual event at this link ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_0NrJXlknRKmFXDjyvtSm0g#/registration ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-ecological-value-of-ontarios-greenbelt/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Sustainability
LOCATION:Online @ zoom link to be provided
END:VEVENT
