SUMMARY:AI and Education (Online – 21 Sept.-23 Oct., 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Looking to get some hands-on time as you respond to LLMs and other AI technologies in your teaching? Join us for a fully online course in the practical pedagogy of technology-enhanced teaching in the age of artificial intelligence. We will explore a range of topics and resources to determine what this technology might mean for your course policies, your assessments, and your teaching strategies. Participants will learn by doing as they apply course learning to make changes to their own course(s) – whether you are new to generative AI, already using it in your classroom, or skeptical about its role in education, this course will support you in developing a robust and pedagogically informed approach to its many facets and implications.\nVisit our registration page to learn more and register: https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2123 ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2123 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ai-and-education-online-21-sept-23-oct-2026/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence,Teaching &amp; Learning
