SUMMARY:Centre for Feminist Research Graduate Student Conference: “Assemblia”
DESCRIPTION:Date: October 22, 2026\nTime: 10:00 AM–4:00 PM\nLocation: York University, Keele Campus\nThe Centre for Feminist Research is pleased to announce that we are accepting submissions for our upcoming conference, ASSEMBLIA, taking place on October 22, 2026.\nThis is the inaugural conference in what we hope will become an annual event organized by graduate students and members of the CFR. It provides an interdisciplinary forum for emerging and independent artists and scholars by bringing together studio practice, criticism and theory, gender studies, and art history.\nWe welcome academic articles, poetry, short fiction, artworks, and essays. Any questions can be directed towards the Assemblia Graduate Student Leadership Team (Julia and Ame) at CFRfeministfestival@gmail.com\nThe conference is free and open to graduate students, independent scholars, artists, and interdisciplinary practitioners. Any questions can be directed towards the Assemblia Graduate Student Leadership Team (Julia and Ame) at CFRfeministfestival@gmail.com\nOur Objective\nAssemblia is organized through a collaborative, non-hierarchical structure grounded in accessibility, shared decision-making, and collective accountability.\nAssemblia approaches feminism as a lived practice—often present even when it is not named. Across cultures and histories, feminist resistance has been misrecognized as hysteria, sanctity, deviance, or danger. Assemblia brings together people interested in attending to the language of feminism as acts of care, survival, and uprising.\n \nClick HERE  ( https://www.yorku.ca/cfr/cfr-feminist-festival-call-for-volunteers/ )to apply to be a volunteer.\nClick HERE  ( https://www.yorku.ca/cfr/assemblia2026-information-submission-guidelines/ )to access the Call for Papers\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/centre-for-feminist-research-graduate-student-conference-assemblia-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Feminist Research:MAILTO:cfr-coor@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies
LOCATION:519 Kaneff Tower
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Assemblia.png
END:VEVENT
