SUMMARY:Human Teaching in an Age of AI (Online – 7 July, 2026, 11:00-12:30)
DESCRIPTION:This workshop can count towards the Teaching Commons’ Certificates in AI Pedagogies. Learn more at our website: https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/certificates/#AIPedagogies\nIn this workshop we will critically reflect on how AI changes our roles as educators—from feedback to content delivery—and how disciplinary norms shape these shifts. Participants will discuss how institutional and student expectations are evolving and explore strategies for maintaining pedagogical integrity amidst change.\nRegister in YULearn: https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2090 ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=2090 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/human-teaching-in-an-age-of-ai-online-7-july-2026-1100-1230/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence,Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
