SUMMARY:Stratford Festival: A Midsummer Night’s Dream and alumni reception
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Stratford Festival for a matinee performance of A Midsummer Night’s Dream, followed by an exclusive reception and behind-the-scenes conversation with two York alumni cast members: Davinder Malhi (BFA ’20), featured in the role of Peaseblossom and Richard Lee (BFA ’00), featured in the role of Philostrate’s Associate/Burdock.\nStratford Festival: A Midsummer Night’s Dream and alumni reception\nDate: Sunday, Sept. 20\nTime: 2 p.m. (performance followed by alumni reception featuring a Q&A with cast members)\nLocation: Tom Patterson Theatre, 111 Lakeside Dr, Stratford, ON N5A 3B9 \n\nYour ticket includes both the performance and the post-show reception.\n\n\nTwo ticket tiers are available based on seat location:\n\n\n\nB Zone seats: $111.32 CAD (tax included)\nBravo Zone seats: $44.85 CAD (tax included)\n\n\n\nAvailability is limited.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/stratford-festival-a-midsummer-nights-dream-and-alumni-reception/
