SUMMARY:Point of View Talk with Ecologist Dawn Bazely and Screening of Brakfesten / La Grande Bouffe
DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to invite you to a special screening and talk next Tuesday, June 2, 6-7:30PM at The Goldfarb Gallery featuring York Biology Professor Dawn Bazely.\nResponding to Anne Duk Hee Jordan: Worlds Away, Professor Bazely will offer insights through the lens of ecology, with a focus on plant–animal relationships and interdependence within natural systems.\nThe program includes a screening of Brakfesten / La Grande Bouffe (2022–23), a film by Anne Duk Hee Jordan and Pauline Doutreluingne. Set in a Swedish forest threatened by Elm disease, the film reveals a fragile ecosystem and highlights the complex relationships among the species that inhabit it.\nThe event will also be part of Toronto Climate Week.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/point-of-view-talk-with-ecologist-dawn-bazely-and-screening-of-brakfesten-la-grande-bouffe/
CATEGORIES:Goldfarb Gallery,Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery
LOCATION:Keele Campus, York University 4700 Keele Street Toronto Ontario M3J 1P3 Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Brakfesten-invigning_-63-3-2.jpg
