SUMMARY:The Archive of Missing Things
DESCRIPTION:Created by Zuppa with Kate Cayley, A Zuppa Production ( https://zuppa.works/about-us/ ),\nCo-produced and Presented by Theatre Direct ( https://theatredirect.dreamhosters.com/the-archive-of-missing-things/ ) and\nYork University – School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/ )\nand York University Libraries ( https://www.library.yorku.ca/web/ )\nDate: May 20 – 23, 2026\nTime: May 20, 21 & 22  (1:00 – 2:30 p.m.) | May 23 (1:00 – 2:30 p.m. & 4:00 – 5:30 p.m.)\nLocation: Scott Library (115 Campus Walk) ( https://www.library.yorku.ca/web/scott/ )\nTickets: General Admission: $15 | Student $10 ( https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/the-archive-of-missing-things )\n“The Archive of Missing Things was founded in order to collect, catalogue and store all missing objects that are in the world. The Archive was built around a secret.”\nThe Archive of Missing Things is a live/digital show for libraries, as well as an online game available at home. You have 90 minutes to explore a maze-like archive in search of the secret at its centre. Toggling between different views can reveal clues: if you look and listen closely enough, you may just notice them.\nA meditative quest for the age of rising sea levels.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-archive-of-missing-things/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/mar.jpg
