SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Sinful, Sultry and Salacious: A Recent History of Toronto’s Identity Crisis
DESCRIPTION:Sex workers have always been part of the city’s history, but they often felt like outsiders in their own home. This session explores how sex work shaped Toronto’s identity between 1970 and 2014 and how this semi-hidden history of the sinful, sultry, and salacious created an identity crisis that continues to shape its citizens today.\n
