SUMMARY:A Soirée for Curious Minds: Stories and the Science of How We Remember
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to A Soirée for Curious Minds, an intimate series presented in partnership with the Rosedale United Church. Each event features a Glendon professor sharing their expertise on engaging and timely topics.\nUp Next:\n\nMay 5: Stories and the Science of How We Remember – Prof. Buddhika Bellana\n\nRegister here! ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/memory-stories-and-the-science-of-how-we-remember-tickets-1983674192910?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n\n\n\nEach evening begins with live piano music to welcome you, followed by a thought-provoking talk and engaging discussions on literature, culture, psychology, or politics.\nNo pretension, just inspiring ideas, lively conversation and plenty to think about.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/a-soiree-for-curious-minds-stories-and-the-science-of-how-we-remember/
ORGANIZER;CN=Julie Marguet:MAILTO:jmarguet@glendon.yorku.ca
