SUMMARY:Building and Sustaining Research Relationships with School Boards
DESCRIPTION:Interested in conducting research with schools/boards but unsure where to start or what they might expect of you? Your search is over! Come meet our expert researchers representing four Ontario school boards. They will discuss important aspects of building university/public education research relationships and strategies on how to sustain them. Lots of time for discussion so please bring your questions!\nSession will be facilitated by professors James and Gillian Parekh.\nPanelists:\nChris Conley is the manager of research and strategic analytics with the Durham District School Board and has a focus on making research meaningful, enlightening, and timely.\nDavid Lane is the executive manager of research and organizational transformation at the Waterloo Region District School Board where his primary responsibilities include board improvement and equity planning and research-informed decision-making.\nAmie Presley is a senior researcher and co-chair of the external research review committee at the Toronto District School Board.\nMarcelle McShine-Quao is the research manager at the York Catholic District School Board, with over 30 years of experience leading equity-focused research and data-driven system improvements.\nREGISTER HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/p4z5YhfkQu2YWYdc9ou0fA#/registration )\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the meeting.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/building-and-sustaining-research-relationships-with-school-boards/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of the Associate Dean Research, Faculty of Education:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Education
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
END:VEVENT
