SUMMARY:Visual Art & Art History Showcase 2026 – Where to Next?
DESCRIPTION:\n\n \nThis exhibition celebrates the culmination of years of work for the Visual Art & Art History’s class of 2026. Showcasing media from sculpture, painting, drawing, photography and print; we embrace the end of a chapter and stumble our way onto the next.\nWe now come together one last time as a collective. Through our vast and diverse collection of works, this gallery serves as a pinnacle of the efforts and creative talent of the exhibiting artists as we stand at the edge and ask – where to next?\n\n\n \nWhere: Gallery 1313\nWhen: April 1-12th with an opening reception on April 2nd, 6:30pm – 9:30pm\n\n\n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/where-to-next/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Gallery 1313 @ 1313 Queen Street West, Toronto
