SUMMARY:Earth Day Tree Planting
DESCRIPTION:Join the York University community for a fun, hands‑on tree planting event at the Keele Campus! In collaboration with Regenesis@York, the Office of Sustainability and Facilities Services, this event is a great opportunity to get outside, connect with others and help make our campus greener and more climate‑resilient.\n\nCome out, dig in, and help us grow a healthier York!\n🌳 Tree Planting at the Keele Campus\n📅 Date: Wednesday, April 22\n🕛 Time: Noon to 2 p.m.\n📍 Meeting Location: York Blvd & James Gillies Street\n(East side of the Rob & Cheryl McEwan Building)\nThis is your chance to spend time outdoors, meet fellow community members, and contribute to a more sustainable campus—no experience required!\n🌱 Spots are limited, so be sure to register early: https://events.yorku.ca/events/earth-day-tree-planting/?occurrence=2026-04-22 ( https://events.yorku.ca/events/earth-day-tree-planting/?occurrence=2026-04-22 )\nhttps://sustainability.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=58203 ( https://sustainability.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=58203 )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/earth-day-tree-planting/
