SUMMARY:Connecting with Canada’s Federal Public Service: Learn, Ask, Network Panel
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with federal public service leaders who will share insights on how Canada’s public institutions are evolving – and what this means for the next generation of talent. A moderated panel discussion will be followed by an informal networking session.\nPanelists will explore themes such as:\n\nWhat the federal public service does and how it serves Canadians\nHow modernization and digital transformation can reshape federal work\nThe competencies and mindsets the public service is seeking in future candidates\nHow students can build readiness early through skill development, academic pathways, experiential learning, and staying informed\nWhere to look for opportunities – from student programs to talent inventories and public service-wide initiatives\nThe value of networks, mentorship and community involvement\n\nAfter the panel, students will have an opportunity to ask questions and engage directly with federal officials to gain personal perspectives on working in government.\nWhether you are curious about how government functions, passionate about the public service, or exploring where your skills might fit, this event will help you build clarity, confidence and direction!\nRegistration is required via Experience York (Career Centre > Employer Events)\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/connecting-with-canadas-federal-public-service-learn-ask-network-panel/
