SUMMARY:York-France Engagement Event
DESCRIPTION:York University’s York–France Engagement Event on Friday, March 20 at Glendon Campus will bring together York faculty, researchers, students and external partners for a morning focused on research collaboration with France.\n\nThe program includes welcome remarks from York leadership, greetings from Bertrand Pous, Consul General of France in Toronto, an online presentation from CNRS Ottawa, a York faculty spotlight on a CNRS collaboration, and two sessions on research opportunities in France, including funding, support structures and mobility pathways.\nThe morning will also feature an online presentation on the Ontario/Rhône-Alpes Program, followed by a plenary panel, Making France–Canada Research Work, with York researchers sharing practical insights on building partnerships, creating student research opportunities, overcoming barriers and growing collaborations into larger initiatives. The event will conclude with closing remarks and a networking brunch, giving participants the chance to continue the conversation and connect with colleagues and partners.\nProgram at a glance9:00 to 9:20 a.m. Welcome remarks and opening greetings9:20 to 10:20 a.m. Presentations on York–France research collaborations and opportunities in France, including CNRS and the Ontario/Rhône-Alpes Program10:20 to 10:40 a.m. Break10:40 to 11:30 a.m. Research opportunities in France and plenary panel discussion: Making France–Canada Research Work11:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. Closing remarks and networking brunch\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-france-engagement-event/
ORGANIZER;CN=York International:MAILTO:goglobal@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculties,Glendon,International,ORUs,Research &amp; Innovation,YFile newsletter
LOCATION:A301 York Hall @ Glendon Campus, 2275 Bayview Avenue @ Lawrence E
END:VEVENT
