SUMMARY:Supervision Sparkshop: Guiding Graduate Writing
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this Sparkshop with Marlene Bernholtz, associate professor in the Writing Department. This session will highlight how reciprocal, considerate writing processes and clear supervisory communication, help students and supervisors meet academic and developmental goals.\nDuring this 30-minute session, we will:\n\nreflect on the often-hidden aspects of graduate writing\nreview and receive a copy of the Writing Centre Guide for Graduate Student Support\nidentify key moments where supervision practices shape writing progress\ndiscuss strategies for establishing reciprocal writing processes, including shared expectations, timelines, and feedback\nshare practical tips supervisors can use for themselves and with students to support drafting, revision and momentum\n\nDate: Tuesday, May 5\nTime: 11:00 to 11:30 a.m.\nLocation: Online (via Zoom) Registration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/NvLcVOrOS5erIBNKlPWoug ) (click link)\n \nFor more information, contact Tracy Bhoola, Manager, Graduate Supervision Support Hub tbhoola@yorku.ca\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/supervision-sparkshop-guiding-graduate-writing/
