SUMMARY:YU Pickleball For The Future
DESCRIPTION:\nYork alumni are invited to the annual Pickleball for the Future event presented by York University Women’s Volleyball Alumni Network. Funding directly supports the future of women’s volleyball student athletes, benefitting the Mosher-Silver Women’s Volleyball Legacy Award.\n\n\n\nThis year, we have two sections for our event: a pickleball clinic and a pickleball tournament.\nDate: April 12\nLocation: Tait McKenzie Centre, Main Gymnasium (1 Thompson Rd., North York, ON)\nClinic Time: 9:30-11:30 a.m.\nTournament Time: 12:15 a.m. – 3:15 p.m.\nWho: Pickleball levels beginner to advanced (2.5-4.0 level)\nRegistration:\nClinic ONLY: $40\nTournament ONLY: $50\nBoth Clinic & Tournament $80\nREGISTER TODAY to win prizes, learn the game, connect with friends new and old and most importantly make an impact on the future of Lions women’s volleyball athletes!\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/yu-pickleball-for-the-future/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
LOCATION:Tait McKenzie Center @ 1 Thompson Rd, North York
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/aleksander-saks-WLufWd6CXLA-unsplash-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
