SUMMARY:Institute for Technoscience & Society Virtual Seminar Series with Suze Berkout
DESCRIPTION:Register here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_Lor96MN6QbOWgVXJR8VZbw#/registration ) to join us for an ITS virtual talk “Mediation, Curation, Materialization: Art-Science Collaborations, Feminist STS, and the Invisible, Contested, and Ephemeral in Biomedicine” with Dr. Suze Berkhout (University of Toronto) on March 12, 2026 from 12:00 pm till 1:30 pm\nThis talk considers a series of art-science collaborations at the intersections of feminist STS and crip technoscience, looking to the role of mediation, curation, and materialization as processes that endanger new forms of knowing in biomedicine that are at once experimental, emergent and ephemeral, offering transformative ways of collectively reimagining the outputs of science and medicine.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/institute-for-technoscience-society-virtual-seminar-series-with-suze-berkout/
