SUMMARY:Indigenous Student Life Skills Workshop: Study Strategies by Science
DESCRIPTION:What if you could get better grades and spend less time studying? Join the Center for Indigenous Student Services (CISS) for a short, interactive, science-backed session on the study methods that actually work – so you can study smarter, stress less, and feel more in control of your academic career. Expect practical takeaways you can start using today, with a friendly, casual vibe.\nCatered, fresh lunch is provided, so registration is required to reserve your spot, and feel free to show up with any and all questions that you have on any topic.\nThis event is designed for Indigenous students at York University.\nWhen: Tuesday March 10, from 1 to 2 p.m.\nWhere: CIKL Boardroom, York Lanes 353B (YL).\nFor more events like this one, be sure to follow us on Instagram! @yorkuindigenous\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-student-life-skills-workshop-study-strategies-by-science/
