SUMMARY:Atelier sur le langage inclusif: workshop on inclusive language when writing/speaking in French
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will explore the concept of binary thinking, both in terms of identity and how it is integrated into the systems and structures that surround us, particularly language – with an emphasis on French.\nWe will also look at tools that can help us make our communication more inclusive, both spoken and written. Together, we will reflect on ways to create spaces that are welcoming to all people, going beyond traditional binary frameworks.\nThis virtual workshop will be hosted by Miriam Greenblatt and will take place on the Zoom platform and will be offered in French with simultaneous interpretation in English.\nZoom information ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/94315308207 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/atelier-sur-le-langage-inclusif-workshop-on-inclusive-language-when-writing-speaking-in-french/
ORGANIZER;CN=Salon francophone:MAILTO:uviswanathan@glendon.york.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Glendon,Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Virtually via Zoom
