SUMMARY:African Dance Workshop (with Lua Shayenne)
DESCRIPTION:Led by, Lua Shayenne who is passionate about studying traditional Mandé dances and rhythms, her workshops with percussion are suitable for all levels. Through African dance movements, Lua Shayenne invites you to celebrate your body as a temple of the spirit connected to Mother Earth. We explore breathing, the ground, inner rhythm, and flow.\nThis bilingual (French/English) workshop will be held in the Group Exercice Room, seocnd floor at the Glendon Athletic Centre (on the Glendon Campus of York University – 2275 Bayview Ave.)\nAll levels of dance and interest welcome.\nMonday March 23 from 1 to 2:25 p.m.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/african-dance-workshop-with-lua-shayenne/
ORGANIZER;CN=Salon francophone:MAILTO:uviswanathan@glendon.york.ca
