TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:The Goldfarb Gallery Opening Reception
DESCRIPTION:\nPlease join The Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery for the opening of our exhibitions and the start of our winter/spring program. On Thursday, March 5, from 6 to 9 p.m., we will host a reception in celebration of the solo exhibitions Anne Duk Hee Jordan: Worlds Away and D’Andrea Bowie: Winter Wheat.\n\n\nWorlds Away is the first solo exhibition in Canada by Berlin-based artist Anne Duk Hee Jordan. Shifting the focus away from humans, Jordan brings to light unseen connections between different species and the forces of the world that usually remain imperceptible. The installation unfolds as a multisensory environment centred on ocean organisms such as phytoplankton and other deep-sea life. Visitors will encounter an immersive sound composition that moves through states of descent, breath and vibration. This exhibit runs until July 25.\nThere will be an artist talk ( https://events.yorku.ca/events/artist-talk-with-anne-duk-hee-jordan-at-the-goldfarb-gallery/?occurrence=2026-03-07 ) on March 7.\n\n\nGTA artist and York University alumni D’Andrea Bowie’s exhibition, Winter Wheat, consists primarily of ceramics and glasswork and is a deep investigation of her immediate surroundings, using materials sourced primarily on-site. Touchpoints for her are critical place-based thinking, a phenomenological approach to considerations of place and locale as being primary above and beyond human intervention. This exhibition is the first in a series of alumni exhibitions. This exhibit will be on display until July 25.\nFor more information and to RSVP, visit our website!\nTheGoldfarbGallery.ca ( https://thegoldfarbgallery.ca/project/rsvp/ )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-goldfarb-gallery-opening-reception/
CATEGORIES:Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery
LOCATION:Keele Campus, York University 4700 Keele Street Toronto Ontario M3J 1P3 Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Poster-Opening-Reception-SpringSummer-26-1-scaled-e1772555312791.jpg
END:VEVENT
