SUMMARY:Inclusion Week: Restoring Our Fractured Communities: An Indigenous Restorative Session with Knowledge Keeper Greg Loft
DESCRIPTION:As part of Inclusion Week and Well-Being Week, join us for an in‑person Indigenous restorative session rooted in care, and community connection. This gathering invites participants to slow down, reflect, and engage in collective healing as we navigate the fractures of the world we live in today.\nThrough story, dialogue, and gentle restorative practice, we will explore what it means to mend relationships—with ourselves, with one another, and with the lands that sustain us.\nOpen to all, however priority will be given to Indigenous community members. Participation is capped at 30 to ensure a grounded and meaningful circle experience.\nLunch will be served.\nRegister here ( https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0Nk_k7whMglPk0Tlp6gLHU5UN1E5NjA0UFNNVTM1QjROWjI2T1NJTTVGNC4u )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/inclusion-week-restoring-our-fractured-communities-an-indigenous-restorative-session-with-knowledge-keeper-greg-loft/
ORGANIZER;CN=CHREI:MAILTO:chrwkshp@yorku.ca
