SUMMARY:Indigenous Environmental Justice Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Participants of ENVS 4311, Indigenous Environmental Justice class, present art, film and community teachings that show how Indigenous values transform environmental justice practice. Engaging these teachings expands the scope and ethical grounding of environmental action for Indigenous and non-Indigenous communities alike. Join our arts-based workshop. Bring your skill and passion, meet community need and clarify your responsibility to act.\nFacilitator: Paulette Moore\nTime: 2:30 to 5:30 p.m.\nLocation: ACW 302\nHosted in: Paulette Moore’s Indigenous Environmental Justice (ENVS 4311)\n \n
