SUMMARY:Writing Our Heritage (Part One)
DESCRIPTION:This workshop guides participants in exploring and sharing our cultural backgrounds as we collectively define the meaning and power of heritage. This first day asks participants to reflect on their personal cultural stories and create a heritage map, highlighting key traditions, places and objects. Participants will learn storytelling techniques and research methods that preserve our cultural narratives for future generations.\nFacilitator: Zainab Gaafar\nTime: 10:00 to 11:30 a.m.\nLocation: Black Community Space (HNES 248)\n
