SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop: Field Notes in Blue
DESCRIPTION:We will create camera-less blue images using plant materials. During this process, participants will examine cyanotype’s origins and reflect on its role in colonial botany, map-making, and industrial “blueprints”. Come experience taking artful field notes with respect and care for humans, plants, and other beings around us.\nFacilitator: Farida Rady\nTime: 2:30 to 4:10 p.m.\nLocation: EUC Lounge(HNES 136)\nHosted in: Ahmed A.R. Abushaban’s Climate Justice (ENVS 4350/ENVS 5055)\n
