SUMMARY:Wampums Woven through Anishinaabe History
DESCRIPTION:This presentation delves into wampum and the talk that they carry. Knowledge holder, Brian Charles will present his wampum collection and offer the shared histories between settler and Indigenous nations in treaty making and Land stewardship within Indigenous worldviews and legal orders.\nFacilitator: Brian Charles\nTime: 2:30 to 5:30 p.m.\nLocation: ACW 206\nHosted in: Lisa Myers’ The Land We’re On (ENVS 1100)\n \n
