SUMMARY:Why DIY When You Can DO It Together
DESCRIPTION:Join the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change for a reflective sharing the importance of collaboration and working together in creative practices. The facilitators are part of various art collectives focused on community engagement and also work on Collective Collective: a project uniting eight BIPOC-majority collectives to challenge systemic racism and exploitation in the arts.\nFacilitator: Collective Collective\nTime: 8:30 to 11:30 a.m.\nLocation: Online ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/why-diy-when-you-can-do-it-together-tickets-1983837699964 ) \nHosted in: Muna-Udbi Ali’s Race/Racism and Environmental Justice (ENVS 3160)\nReserve a seat through Eventbrite ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/why-diy-when-you-can-do-it-together-tickets-1983837699964 ). Participants will receive a Zoom link the day before the event.\n \n \n
