SUMMARY:Sports Betting: Separating Skill from Illusion of Control
DESCRIPTION:Have you noticed betting everywhere? No seriously—sports betting ads bombard games, online apps tempt 24/7 and youth and young adults face 5X higher problem gambling rates compared to any other age group.​\nJoin YGAP’s (Youth Gambling Awareness Program ( https://www.ymcagta.org/youth-programs/youth-gambling-awareness-program )) “Separating Skill from Illusion of Control” workshop to unpack the illusion, online dangers, ads and safety strategies.​\nThis workshop is being delivered as part of an Impact Research study by York University and Toronto Metropolitan University, and includes a brief pre- and post-survey. As a thank-you for participating and completing both surveys, you’ll receive a $10 Amazon gift card. If you choose to complete the optional 6-week follow-up survey, you’ll receive an additional $20 Amazon gift card.\n2 sessions available—spots are limited!\nSession 1 | 1:30PM – 3PM\nSession 2 | 3PM – 4:30PM\nLocation: York Psychology Clinic, Behaviour Science Building (BSB) 102A\n\n Register for Sports Betting: Separating Skill from Illusion of Control ( https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScuRAaxaBlsU5EdstMqTjG4NEZUlkLaSdzrFUVl3ZhgINfhDw/viewform )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sports-betting-separating-skill-from-illusion-of-control/
