SUMMARY:Tea Time Talks: Mental Health & Student Well-being
DESCRIPTION:Tea Time Talks is a student-led initiative that creates welcoming and inclusive spaces for students to connect, reflect and learn from one another’s lived experiences. Each session centers conversation, shared reflection and community-building in an informal and supportive environment.\nThis March session invites students to engage in open and thoughtful conversation about mental health and well-being, with a focus on the everyday challenges students navigate throughout the academic year. Together with Student Counselling, Health & Well-being (SCHW), we will explore how students can better understand their well-being, recognize when support may be helpful and learn about the resources available to them within the York community.\nThis session is not lecture-based or clinical in nature. Instead, it emphasizes dialogue, practical reflection and accessible conversations around well-being, creating space for students to listen, share and ask questions in a respectful and supportive setting.\nWhether you are looking to learn, reflect, or simply be present in a supportive environment, all York students are welcome to join us. Light refreshments will be provided.\n\nDate: Wednesday, March 11, 2026\nTime: noon – 2:00 PM\nLocation: Founders College 305\n\n\n\nThe Tea Time Talks is coordinated by the LA&PS Colleges, and rooted in DEDI values: Decolonization, Equity, Diversity and Inclusion.\n\n\n\nRegister for Tea Time Talks: Mental Health & Student Well-being ( https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0Cjqa8T1uJ5NpTdXAR_SdkJUN0NUMk0xR1pKNE9CVzZaOUcySEw2RlRFSC4u&route=shorturl )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tea-time-talks-mental-health-student-well-being/
