SUMMARY:Free Cooking Class – Korean Kimbap with Teaching Kitchen
DESCRIPTION:Ready to roll? Join us on campus for a hands-on Korean Kimbap workshop as part of York’s Well-Being Week with Student Counselling, Health & Well-being!\nOur executive chef and dietitian Dahlia will guide you step-by-step through crafting the perfect, delicious, and nutritious Korean Kimbap. Learn about the ingredients, explore how food nourishes our bodies, and enjoy tasting your handmade creation.\nCome for the cooking, stay for the conversation, and leave with a warm heart and belly Whether you’re new to the kitchen or a seasoned pro, this event is for everyone!\nThursday, March 5,\n2 to 3 p.m.\nRoss Building, South 166\nSpots are limited—mark your calendars and register now ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/teaching-kitchen-korean-kimbap-tickets-1982706935818?aff=oddtdtcreator ). We can’t wait to see you there!\n
