TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Inclusion Week: Care, Conflict, and (in)Civility in Academic Life
DESCRIPTION:Faculty Affairs is delighted to welcome a special guest, Professor Alice MacLachlan, Vice-Provost & Dean, Graduate Studies to an online conversation series on (re)building academic spaces of care and inclusion.\nIn an era marked by political polarization, social fragmentation, and moral disagreements, how can individuals, communities, institutions including universities rebuild trust and move forward together? Professor MacLachlan’s scholarship offers valuable insights towards this urgent question.\nDrawing on political philosophy and feminist ethics, Professor MacLachlan’s writings engage with the nature and limits of forgiveness, the power and complexity of public apologies, and the role that emotions such as resentment and indignation play in reconciliation and repair. Her work offers ideas for thinking through what practices and responsibilities are involved in restoring relationships in the aftermath of wrongdoing, injustice, and democratic strain.\nProfessor MacLachlan’s publications include “Apologizing for Evil” “Trust Me, I’m Sorry: The Paradox of Public Apology,” “Closet Doors and Stage Lights: On the Goods of Out,” and “Unreasonable Resentments.” She is also the co-editor of Justice, Responsibility, and Reconciliation in the Wake of Conflict. Her current research investigates the ethics and politics of (in)civility in contexts of disagreement—an especially timely and resonant topic for our academic communities today.\nOur conversation with Professor MacLachlan aligns beautifully with the theme of CHREI’s Inclusion Week (March 2–6): Building Inclusive Spaces Through Community Support and Restoration.\nWe look forward to a rich conversation with Faculty and graduate students on how practices of apology, repair, and relational ethics can help cultivate more compassionate and inclusive academic spaces.\nClick here to learn more and register.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/inclusion-week-care-conflict-and-incivility-in-academic-life/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty Affairs, EPC:MAILTO:FacAffairs@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp; Culture,Faculties,Faculty Affairs,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Conference Interpreting,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate