SUMMARY:World Music Festival 2026
DESCRIPTION:York University’s World Music Festival is a cross-cultural celebration spotlighting musical traditions around the world.\nProduced by Professor Sherry Johnson ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/people/sherry-johnson/ ), this global sonic journey showcases a vibrant sampling of music featured in York’s World Music program.\nMaps and Directions ( http://maps.info.yorku.ca/keele-campus/ )\nTHURSDAY, MARCH 12, 2026\n10:45 a.m. – Toronto Chinese Orchestra (Patty Chan, Director)\n11:15 a.m. – Toronto Chinese Orchestra with Celtic Ensemble\n11:30 a.m. – Celtic Ensemble (Sherry Johnson, Director)\n12:15 p.m. – Steelpan Ensemble (Gareth Burgess, Director)\n1:45 p.m. – West African Ensemble (Larry Graves, Director)\n2:30 p.m. – Afro-Cuban Ensemble (Rick Lazar, Director)\n7:00 p.m. – Balkan Ensemble (Irene Markoff, Director)\nLOCATION: Tribute Communities Recital Hall  ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ )\nFREE ADMISSION\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/world-music-festival-2026/
