SUMMARY:Level Up | How to File your Taxes
DESCRIPTION:Thinking about filing your taxes, but not sure where to start? Join our upcoming webinar designed to help you confidently navigate the Canadian tax system and file your own tax return with ease.\nHow to File your Taxes\nDate: Wednesday, March 11\nTime: 12 p.m. ET\nFormat: Zoom webinar\nThis session will dive into:\n\nAn overview of the Canadian tax system\nCommon types of income and how they impact your tax return\nKey tax slips for new graduates\nImportant deadlines and filing options\nCredits and deductions that can reduce your taxes\n\nFeaturing guest speaker, Gurjot Mann, (BCom ‘20), Senior Accountant – Assurance, Bateman MacKay LLP\n\nGurjot Mann, CPA is a dedicated assurance professional currently serving as a Senior Associate in Assurance at Bateman MacKay LLP, a midsized Canadian public accounting firm. In this role, Gurjot focuses on financial reporting, audit and review engagements for a diverse portfolio of clients. His work encompasses preparing and reviewing detailed working papers, conducting substantive testing and analytical procedures, and assisting in the preparation of financial statements with accuracy and integrity. Gurjot collaborates closely with clients and engagement teams to deliver high-quality assurance results that support sound financial decision-making.\nBefore joining Bateman MacKay, Gurjot developed broad experience in corporate, trust, and personal tax compliance, as well as compilation engagements and complex account reconciliations. He has also supported clients through Canada Revenue Agency compliance reviews and audits, gaining practical exposure to regulatory and reporting requirements.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/level-up-how-to-file-your-taxes/
