SUMMARY:Equitable Green Homes? Housing, Health, and Energy in a Changing Climate
DESCRIPTION:As the impacts of climate change exacerbate all over the world, issues around housing, energy poverty and gentrification become more complex to deal with in equitable ways.\nThe Dahdaleh Institute for Global Health Research invites you to be part of a conversation with three interdisciplinary panellists who’s work intersects at the core of the question “How can we keep everyone healthy and well as we work towards mitigating and adapting to climate change?”\nJoin us as we find unexpected connections and points of intervention.\nPlease register for the event ( https://www.yorku.ca/dighr/events/equitable-green-homes/ ).\n
