SUMMARY:Information Session for Graduate Psychology Programs at York University
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Psychology at York University is hosting an information session for prospective students interested in its non clinical graduate programs, including the MA and PhD.\nAttendees will learn about the application process and funding opportunities, and connect directly with faculty members and current graduate students to learn more about research opportunities and student life. This session covers all graduate psychology programs at York except clinical psychology.\nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday, March 26, 2026\nTime: 4:00 – 6:00 PM\nFormat: Hybrid, in person and via Zoom\nLocation: Vari Hall room A, York University\nRegistration required: RSVP HERE ( https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0C70JRGEG-NFo_xioJ4HV4lURjVCNVlIMDZJRTJPSExNUEFYNTJDRFhVRS4u ). A Zoom link will be sent to registered participants prior to the session.\nIf you have questions about the event or about psychology at YorkU, we welcome inquiries at gradpsyc@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/info-session-grad-psychology/
