SUMMARY:Paws & Pause: Puppy Therapy for Mature Students and Student Parents
DESCRIPTION:Take a well deserved break and join us on March 4th for a relaxing and uplifting Puppy Therapy session designed specifically for mature students and mature student parents. This welcoming event offers a chance to unwind, connect with others, and enjoy the comfort of spending time with friendly, playful pups.\nAnimal assisted activities have been shown to reduce anxiety, ease feelings of loneliness, boost motivation, and provide emotional comfort. Whether you’re balancing academics, parenting, or both, this is a wonderful opportunity to de stress in a supportive environment.\nChildren are welcome to attend with their student parent. Come meet some adorable four legged friends and give yourself a moment of calm—you deserve it.\nOrganized by Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-Time Students (ACMAPS).\nFormat: In-Person\nLocation: Alumni & Career Lounge (York Lanes)\nAudience: Students\nRegister Online\n \n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/paws-pause-puppy-therapy-for-mature-students-and-student-parents/
CATEGORIES:the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,Well-being,Well-being Week
END:VEVENT
