SUMMARY:The Mine Action Innovation Hub: challenges and enablers of the mine action innovation system
DESCRIPTION:Mine Action: Innovation, Sustainability and Global Partnerships Speaker Series\nLandmines and explosive remnants of war (ERW) continue to pose a critical humanitarian and developmental challenge worldwide. These hazards hinder infrastructure development, agricultural productivity and socio-economic recovery, directly impacting the achievement of multiple UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\nEmerging technologies such as AI, unmanned systems, robotics and digital twins offer transformative opportunities to accelerate clearance operations, improve safety,and enhance cost efficiency. Simultaneously, climate change impacts exacerbate contamination dynamics, demanding integrated approaches that link technology, sustainability and policy.\nThe Subsphere Co. in partnership with York University, Kyiv National Aviation University, Kyiv Polytechnic Institute and Ukrainian deminers and technology developers proposes a global speaker series that unites deminers, applied research centers, academia, policymakers, industry and humanitarian actors to shape the future of mine action through innovation and sustainability.\nSpeakers:\nPedro Basto – program manager, Research & Innovation, Geneva International Centre for Humanitarian Demining (GICHD)\nMiodrag Milenković – senior advisor for training organization and mine action coordination, Mine Action Centre of the Republic of Serbia\nModerators:\nShahab Moenini – director and strategy lead, SubSphere Co.\nMishal Arif – research and development coordinator, SubSphere Co.\nMore info ( https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/mine-action/ )\nRegistration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_QosLMH1RQOuzcYUXC2lnRA )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-mine-action-innovation-hub-challenges-and-enablers-of-the-mine-action-innovation-system/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Colleges,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Science,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,International,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp;PS Students-International,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,Research &amp; Innovation,Y-EMERGE,YFile newsletter
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
