SUMMARY:1UP Conference 2026: Blueprint to Bloom
DESCRIPTION:\n\nTrying to shape tomorrow’s cities? Start here!\n\n\n\n\nThe 1UP Conference is where young people from across Ontario come together to imagine, design, and build the future of our communities. Over two energizing days, join 200-plus youth for hands-on workshops, inspiring speakers, design challenges and real conversations about city-building, creativity, climate and community.\nThis is your platform.\nYou bring the passion – we bring the space, the tools and the people who want to hear your ideas.\nSecure your spot at the 1UP Conference and help shape the cities of tomorrow!\n\n\n\n\nLocation:\nVari Hall, York University, 198 York Blvd, North York, ON M3J 1P3\nDates:\nSaturday, March 28 | 9:30 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nSunday, March 29 | 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. (Note the earlier start!)\n\nRegistration: 1UP Conference 2026 – Blueprint to Bloom Tickets, Sat, Mar 28, 2026 at 9:30 AM | Eventbrite ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1up-conference-2026-blueprint-to-bloom-tickets-1977384690840?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/1up-conference-2026-blueprint-to-bloom/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:Vari Hall Rotunda @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
