SUMMARY:Samuel J. Zacks Gallery – Well-Being Week x Inclusion Week Art Show – Sponsored by the William & Nona Heaslip Foundation
DESCRIPTION:The Well-being & Restoration exhibition centers on the idea that many of the world’s greatest changes have emerged through conflict. Through the lens of the six dimensions of Wellness, artists are invited to reflect on the conflicts they have witnessed, personal, social, or global, and to explore the Well-being & Restoration exhibition, which centers on the idea that many of the world’s greatest changes have emerged through conflict. Through the lens of the six dimensions of Wellness, artists are invited to reflect on conflicts they have witnessed, personal, social, or global, and to explore their perspectives on restoration and rebuilding trust. Join us for the night to celebrate the prize winners and experience the art and messages that our community is creating!\nFormat: In-Person\nLocation: Stong College Room 109 (Samuel J. Zacks Gallery)\nThis exhibition will run from February 23rd to March 7th.\nZacks Gallery Opening Hours:\n\nMonday- 9:00am- 4:00pm\nTuesday- 9:00am- 1pm\nWednesday- 9:00am-10:30am and 11am-2:30pm\nThursday- 9:00am- 4:30pm\nFriday- 9:00am- 11:30am and 12:30pm-4:30pm\n\nAudience: All York Community\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/samuel-j-zacks-gallery-well-being-week-x-inclusion-week-art-show-sponsored-by-the-william-nona-heaslip-foundation/
CATEGORIES:Calumet College,Inclusion Week,Stong College,Well-being,Well-being Week
END:VEVENT
