TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Happy Year of the Horse – Display at Ross S580
DESCRIPTION:Early happy Chinese New Year — welcome the Year of the Horse!\nThe Chinese program warmly invites the entire York University community to visit our Chinese New Year display celebrating the Year of the Horse, presented as part of the Department of Languages, Literatures, and Linguistics’ World Cultures Celebrations Initiative. This initiative highlights and honours the rich cultural traditions represented within our global community.\n📅 Chinese New Year: Feb. 17\n📍 Location: Ross Building, Room S580\n🗓 Display period: Feb. 10 to 20\nIn Chinese culture, the horse symbolizes energy, speed, productivity and success. May the Year of the Horse bring vitality, achievement and good fortune to all members of the York community.\nPlease stop by the display, take photos and check in to celebrate the New Year with us. Bring your friends and classmates – everyone is welcome.\nThis display was organized by Professor Gang Pan and collaboratively created by students from CH1000A, CH1000B and CH2000. Special thanks to our students for their creativity and wonderful work.\nWith best wishes for a joyful and prosperous Year of the Horse.\nThe Chinese Program\nDepartment of Languages, Literatures, and Linguistics\nFaculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies (LAPS), York University\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/happy-year-of-the-horse-display-at-ross-s580/
ORGANIZER;CN=Chinese Studies:MAILTO:gangpan@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of Languages, Literatures &amp; Linguistics
LOCATION:Keele Campus, York University
END:VEVENT
