SUMMARY:Managing Small Scale Projects with Microsoft Planner
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Planner is a user friendly application which enables teams to effectively and visually organize small projects, assign tasks, and monitor progress. This course demonstrates how you can use Planner for small scale planning whether with a team or for individual projects.\nKey Learning Outcomes:\nReview the Planner interface and notification settings;\nLearn how to create and manage a Plan;\nCreate, assign, organize and monitor tasks;\nUnderstand how Planner integrates with Microsoft 365 apps.\nThis is an optional course within the Digital Workplace Series: Leveling Up.\nOrganized by Organizational Learning and Leadership, HR\nFormat: Virtual\nAudience: York Staff\nRegister Online\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/managing-small-scale-projects-with-microsoft-planner/
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
