SUMMARY:Management Activities at York (for people managers)
DESCRIPTION:Management activities guide people leaders as they seek to create order and stability in the successful operation of their teams at work. Typically, these activities include building relationships, developing people, leading change, inspiring others, thinking critically, communicating clearly, and creating accountability. At York, management work features working with and managing employees across a range of employee affiliations. This course supports managers in developing their skills to do this work effectively.\nKey Learning Outcomes:\nLearn and understand how to apply core management activities in day to day work;\nAppreciate the importance of adopting and leveraging key management behaviours;\nIdentify the key features of working with and managing diverse employee groups.\nOrganized by Organizational Learning and Leadership, HR\nFormat: Virtual\nAudience: York People Managers\nRegister Online\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/management-activities-at-york-for-people-managers/
