SUMMARY:Beyond the Tri-Council: Alternative Grants for Researchers
DESCRIPTION:\nThis session offers a practical look at what it means to pursue research funding beyond the federal Tri-Council agencies. Through a panel conversation with researchers experienced in securing alternative grants, we’ll explore how they identify opportunities, why they pursue them, what the application process can look like and how this type of funding has supported or expanded their work.\nYou’ll also hear about the support available through York International and SIRI that can help you navigate these pathways.\n\n\nRegister here \nPanelists:\n\n\n\nUzo Anucha, associate vice-president, Faculty Affairs, Full Professor, School of Social Work; York Research Chair in Youth and Contexts of Inequity\n\n\nManar Jamal, associate professor, School of Information Technology\n\n\nKohitij Kar, assistant Professor, department of Biology Canada Research Chair in Visual Neuroscience\n\n\nSkandha Sunderasen, associate director, Global Engagement & Strategic Initiatives, York International\n\n\nDiana Frasca, specialist, Strategic and Institutional Research Initiatives, Office of Research Services (SIRI)\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/beyond-the-tri-council-alternative-grants-for-researchers/
ORGANIZER;CN=Research Commons:MAILTO:rescom@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
