SUMMARY:Book Discussion: Skills to Build the Nation: Immigrant Labour Market and Canadian Nationalism
DESCRIPTION:In this talk Soma Chatterjee will discuss her book, Skills to Build the Nation: Immigrant Labour Market and Canadian Nationalism which originated as her doctoral thesis at OISE. She challenges the prevalent understanding of skilled immigrants’ labour market integration in Canada as a public policy problem awaiting training remedial solutions.\nThe session will be chaired by Dr. Kiran Mirchandani, Professor, Department of Leadership, Higher and Adult Education at the Ontario Institute for Studies in Education.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-skills-to-build-the-nation-by-soma-chatterjee-643-292/
