SUMMARY:Narratives of Movement: Centering Migrant Women’s Voices in Research and Resistance
DESCRIPTION:Soma Chatterjee, professor at the School of Social Work, will be presenting a special hands-on workshop entitled, From Thesis to Book: A Practical Guide for Emerging Scholars, drawing from her forthcoming book Skills to Build the Nation: Immigrant Labour Market and Canadian Nationalism. This workshop offers an accessible, demystifying look at how graduate students and earlycareer researchers can transform a thesis into a publishable monograph.\nLearn More\n
