SUMMARY:Theatre @ York presents The Children’s Hour by Lillian Hellman
DESCRIPTION:The Children’s Hour by Lillian Hellman is a powerful drama about a false accusation that devastates the lives of two women who run a girls’ boarding school. When a student’s malicious lie sparks scandal and suspicion, the play exposes the destructive force of rumor, fear, and societal prejudice.\nLocation:\nSandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/sandra-faire-and-ivan-fecan-theatre/ )\nDates and Times:\nSaturday, March 21 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview)\nSunday, March 22 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview)\nTuesday, March 24 – 7:30 p.m. (Opening)\nWednesday, March 25 – 1:00 p.m. | 7:30 p.m.\nThursday, March 26 – 7:30 p.m. (Relaxed)\nFriday, March 27 – 1:00 p.m. | 7:30 p.m.\nSaturday, March 28 – 2:00 p.m. (Closing)\nBox Office Information:\nPreview Tickets (March 21 & 22): $15.00\nStudent: $ 15.00\nAdvanced: (until Sunday, March 22nd): $ 20.00\nRegular Tickets: $ 25.00\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/theatre-york-presents-the-childrens-hour-by-lillian-hellman/
