SUMMARY:Critical Approaches to DEDI in NSERC Research
DESCRIPTION:This workshop explores how decolonization, equity, diversity, and inclusion (DEDI) can be meaningfully integrated into research applications. Through a guided discussion with York researchers and research officers, you will hear practical insights, common pitfalls, and strategies for using DEDI to strengthen both proposals and research practices. While we will focus on NSERC research, the workshop is also applicable and relevant to SSHRC and CIHR researchers.\n\nRegister here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/ShXY3QKxTKWB2ixD8gdsYA )\nSpeakers:\n\n\n\n\nChris Caputo, Associate Professor, Department of Chemistry, Faculty of Science\n\n\nDenise Henriques, Professor, School of Kinesiology & Health Science, Faculty of Science\n\n\nMaleknaz Nayebi, Associate Professor, Department of Electrical Engineering & Computer Science, Lassonde School of Engineering\n\n\nSoma Tripathi, Grant Development Specialist, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies\n\n\nStuart MacGregor, Research Officer, Faculty of Science\n\n\nYasmine Abou Taha, Research Officer, Faculty of Health\n\n\n\n\n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/critical-approaches-to-dedi-in-nserc-research/
