SUMMARY:Instructional Skills Workshop (ISW) (IN-PERSON) – July 13, 15 and 17
DESCRIPTION:This 3-day intensive workshop encourages examination of one’s teaching practices with feedback focused on the learning process rather than on the specific lesson content. The ISW engenders participatory learning and community building that can transfer back into the classroom. Participants work collaboratively in a small group setting of 4-5 participants to further develop their teaching effectiveness as they design and lead three 10-minute lessons. Following each, participants receive reflective verbal, written, and video feedback from the other participants who have been learners.\nThis is a three-day workshop series scheduled for July 13, 15 and 17. Each day will run from 9 am to 4:30 pm in DB 1014.\nRegister using the registration form ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1149411 )\nPlease note due to the small group nature of this workshop, there are limited spaces (10), so please email teaching@yorku.ca ( mailto:teaching@yorku.ca ) if you are unable to register and we’ll add you to a waiting list.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/instructional-skills-workshop-isw-in-person-july-13-15-and-17/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:DB 1014 Victor Philip Dahdaleh Bldg.
END:VEVENT
