SUMMARY:Geography Alumni Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Thursday, Feb. 26, for this year’s Geography Alumni Lecture. Presented by the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change and the York University Geography Alumni Network (YUGAN), we are thrilled to invite Grace Adeniyi-Ogunyankin, Canada Research Chair in Youth and African Urban Futures and Associate Professor of Gender Studies at Queen’s University.\n\n \nGrace Adeniyi-Ogunyankin is the Canada Research Chair in Youth and African Urban Futures and an associate professor in the Department of Gender Studies at Queen’s University. Her research examines how contemporary urban transformations shape youth identity, labour practices, psychosocial well-being, and futurity in Lagos and Ibadan, Nigeria. She also explores questions of subjectivity and belonging, as well as the use of Afrofuturism in projects that address the politics of difference in popular culture.\nGeography Alumni Lecture\nDate: Thursday, February 26\nTime: 3-5 p.m.\nLocation: Health, Nursing and Environmental Studies Building, Room 140, Keele Campus.\nNote: Reception to follow\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/geography-alumni-lecture/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Graduate Program in Geography
LOCATION:Health Nursing &amp; Environmental Studies (HNES) Room 140 @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/YUGAN.jpg
END:VEVENT
