SUMMARY:Growing Black Food Sovereignty in Toronto
DESCRIPTION:Join the Faculty of Enviornmental & Urban Change for a panel discussion called “Growing Black Food Sovereignty in Toronto” on Monday, Feb. 23 at 1 p.m. in HNES 140.\nThe event will feature the panelists: Nicole Jacobs (MES Student, Farmers Market Manager at the Dufferin Grove Farmers Market), Aaron Joseph (MES Student),  and Charlyn Ellis (MES Student, Director of Ecological Stewardship at the Let’s Bee Connected Foundation, Garden Coordinator at Emmet Communal Garden). Panel will be moderated by Professor Martha Stiegman.\n
