SUMMARY:IP Innovation Clinic x Sensorium: Intellectual Property in Digital Arts Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Sensorium welcomes back the IP Innovation ( https://www.yorku.ca/osgoode/ip-innovation-clinic/about-us/ ) to present a digital art and technology focused workshop where participants can learn about the intellectual property (IP) issues surrounding collaborative creative practice in digital art and technology. Topics covered will include the fundamentals of copyright and trademark law, how IP affects artists, in particular artists working in digital arts in interdisciplinary and collaborative contexts, and best practices.\nCoffee, tea and snacks will be provided.\nTo suggest a topic of interest to be discussed in this workshop, please submit your RSVP by February 4, 2025.\nDate: Wednesday, February 11, 2026\nTime: 1:30 – 3:00 PM\nLocation: Sensorium Loft, Fourth Floor CFA\nFree Admission\nRSVP HERE ( https://ampd.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=230051 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ip-innovation-clinic-x-sensorium-intellectual-property-in-digital-arts-workshop/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sensorium Loft, 4th Floor CFA @ 86 Fine Arts Road
