SUMMARY:Free cooking class: Teaching Kitchen x BE YU, celebrate Black History Month and make Saladu Nebbe
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin our Executive Chef and Dietitian Dahlia on campus to learn how to make Senegalese Black Eyed-Pea Salad (Saladu Nebbe) in celebration of Black History Month, in collaboration with Black Excellence at York University (BE YU).\nEnjoy a live cooking demo, learn the cultural history of the dish, and take part in meaningful conversations about Black History Month, BE YU, and upcoming workshops. Come for the cooking, stay for the conversation, and leave well fed.\nThis in-person event is open to all York University students. No cooking experience required. Please bring a takeout container for leftovers and your EpiPen if prescribed.\nDate: Wednesday, Feb. 4, 2026Time: 2:00–3:00 PMLocation: Ross Building, South 166\nRegister now. ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/teaching-kitchen-saladu-nebbe-x-black-excellence-at-york-u-be-yu-tickets-1981800312082?aff=oddtdtcreator ) We look forward to seeing you there.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/free-cooking-class-teaching-kitchen-x-be-yu-celebrate-black-history-month-and-make-saladu-nebbe/
ORGANIZER;CN=YUeats:MAILTO:food@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning,Well-being
LOCATION:Keele Campus
