SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Owning Your Voice: Self‑advocacy, impostor syndrome, and the growth mindset advantage
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Scholars’ Hub @ Home on Feb. 4 with Minerva Cernea, Director, Centre for Career Design, Schulich School of Business.\nThis session explores how to build confidence, advocate for themselves, and overcome the hidden barriers of impostor syndrome. Through real examples and strategies, you will learn how to recognize self‑doubt, reframe limiting beliefs, and cultivate a growth mindset that supports personal and career success. Participants will walk away with actionable techniques to communicate their needs, seek opportunities, and strengthen their sense of belonging.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-owning-your-voice-self%e2%80%91advocacy-impostor-syndrome-and-the-growth-mindset-advantage/
