SUMMARY:Book Launch – The Story of a Generation: Life Course Pathways of the Class of ‘73
DESCRIPTION:About the Book\nBased on nearly 50 years of research, this landmark book offers rare insight into how social change, work, family, and identity have shaped the lives of one Canadian generation over time. It’s a reflection on how societies transform and how people adapt along the way. For anyone interested in sociology, history, or the human experience, this book provides a rare, intimate look at the passage of time – and the stories we leave behind.\nPraise for The Story of a Generation “A remarkable, insightful and highly engaging account…It sets the standard for life course research.” – Johanna Wyn, University of Melbourne\nJoin the authors – Paul Anisef, Paul Axelrod, Carl E. James, Wolfgang Lehmann, Karen Robson, Erika McDonald, and Erica Fae Thomson; the publisher – University of Toronto Press; and the York University community for an afternoon of conversation and celebration. Light refreshments will be served.\nRSVP HERE ( https://educationforms.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=320038 )\nBook available for purchase at UTPpublishing.com. Regular price, $39.95.\n20% OFF UNTIL MARCH 20, 2026. Apply the code Anisef20 at checkout.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-the-story-of-a-generation-life-course-pathways-of-the-class-of-73/
ORGANIZER;CN=Dean's Office, Faculty of Education:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Education
LOCATION:Schulich Executive Dining Room, Schulich School of Business (York University, Keele Campus)
END:VEVENT
