SUMMARY:The Biyuti Project: The Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:The Biyuti Project: Queer and Trans Filipinx Youth in Catholic Education is an arts-based research project which explores the experiences of queer and trans Filipinx youth as former Ontario Catholic school students through art production and storytelling. The exhibition includes mixed media installations and textile works created from deconstructed Catholic school uniforms, Filipino materiality, and fabrics from the TMC’s Reuse Program. Learn about their experiences of faith, identity, and resistance through creative expression and storytelling.\nThe Biyuti Project: The Exhibition – Opening Reception\nDate: January 18, 2026\nTime: 1:00 – 4:00 pm\nLocation: Textile Museum of Canada (55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON)\nRSVP here ( https://textilemuseum.ca/event/the-biyuti-project-the-exhibition-opening-reception/ )\nThe Biyuti Project: Guided Tour & Roundtable Discussion\nDate: January 28, 2026\nTime: 5:30 – 7:30 pm\nLocation: Textile Museum of Canada (55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON)\nRSVP here ( https://textilemuseum.ca/event/roundtable-discussion-with-dr-marissa-largo-and-guided-tour-of-the-biyuti-project/ )\nPamaypay Extravaganza: Queer and Trans Filipinx FANtastica\nDate: January 31, 2026\nTime: 2:00 – 4:00 pm\nLocation: Textile Museum of Canada (55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON)\nRSVP here ( https://textilemuseum.ca/event/pamapay-hand-fan-pamaypay-extravaganza-beginner/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-biyuti-project-the-exhibition/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:55 Centre Ave, Toronto, ON
