SUMMARY:Kickstart your research: Topics, searching, and academic success
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Think, Research, Create: Intro to Library Research Series (2 out of 4). Sign in with Passport York (PPY). Please arrive on-time and stay. Presenters will allow you in for the first 15 mins.\nThis interactive workshop will break down typical research steps in undergraduate research and make it manageable. You’ll learn what academic research really means and how it’s different from everyday Googling. We’ll help you turn your interests into clear, focused research questions that guide your work. You’ll also learn smart search strategies to help you find reliable, relevant sources without wasting time. Whether you’re researching your first paper or just want to feel more confident using the library, this session will give you the tools to get started. Come with your questions and leave ready to tackle your next assignment.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/kickstart-your-research-topics-searching-and-academic-success-13/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
