SUMMARY:[Scholarly Skills Webinar] Developing a Growth Mindset in Graduate Studies: Strategies to Thrive as a Grad Student
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a series entitled Scholarly Skills. Join us for our next workshop!\nAre you ready to unlock your full potential as a graduate student? York University graduate students are invited to an empowering workshop with Dr. Minerva Cernea (from Schulich School of Business) and FGS’ Associate Dean, Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith, dedicated to cultivating a growth mindset that can transform your academic journey.\nThis caring session will explore practical strategies to tackle common graduate school challenges—perfectionism, imposter syndrome, and navigating feedback—with confidence and resilience. You’ll discover the difference between a fixed and growth mindset, learn the transformational power of “yet,” and leave with actionable tools to thrive in your studies and beyond.\nJoin us to reframe challenges as opportunities, embrace continuous growth, and connect with fellow students on the path to success. Your next breakthrough starts here!\nDate: March 3, 2026\nTime: 12:00pm (1-hour workshop)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_mLekexTZSle-DwRjGU3fPA#/registration )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholarly-skills-workshop-march/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
