SUMMARY:Where Music Leads 2026 – Annual Virtual Conference
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an online webinar series that will highlight a wide range of career options in the ever-changing music landscape. Our all-star lineup of panelists have represented a diverese cross section of industry leaders, including ensemble founders, artistic directors, freelance performers, small businesss owners, recording artists, music therapists, arts administrators, sound engineers, community music facilitators, instrument repair technicians and more.\nWhether you’re a prospective music student, currently enrolled in a post-secondary program or a recent grad, this event is for you!\nIn partnership with the National Youth Orchestra of Canada (NYO Canada), come explore the practical skills and knowledge you need to succeed in today’s music industry. This year’s edition comprises four roundtable discussions, a pedagogy workshop and an interactive career fair. Each event features panelists with a range of fulfilling careers, sharing their insights about cultivating a sustainable career in music, as well as discuss the value of a musical education both within and outside the music industry.\n\nThe conference runs January 24 – 25th from 10:00 a.m. – 3:45 p.m. EST via ZOOM.\n\nRegister for FREE here ( https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_msUhnJyhRXqguPdV7ZN1dA#/registration ). Complete details and full schedule available at wheremusicleads.com\n.\n\n\nQuestions? Contact Dr. Hillis at ahillis@yorku.ca ( mailto:ahillis@yorku.ca ).\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/where-music-leads-2026/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Online event via Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/wheremusicleads-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
