SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Genomics, Artificial Intelligence and Personalized Healthcare: The Canadian story
DESCRIPTION:Canada’s healthcare system is stretched to its limits. As demand on the system continues to grow, so does the hope that new technologies like artificial intelligence, genomic medicine, 3D bioprinting and neurotechnology, will come online and help us bring health care back from the brink. Join us on Jan. 21 at 12 p.m. as Ian Stedman, Associate Professor, School of Public Policy and Administration, Faculty of Liberal Arts and Professional Studies explores some of the major Canadian initiatives that are already underway to help lead us to the promised land of having more efficient, cost-effective and personalized health care.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/genomics-artificial-intelligence-and-personalized-healthcare-the-canadian-story/
