SUMMARY:Dialogues: AI in the Classroom (In-Person – Jan. 20, 2026, 11:00-1:00 ET)
DESCRIPTION:This event brings York faculty and students together in informal collegial dialogue to discuss how AI is being incorporated into post-secondary education. Conversation will address student and faculty experiences of AI in teaching and learning at York. We will begin with time for the two groups to discuss key issues separately, followed by facilitated time for sharing of insights, experiences, and priorities between faculty and students.\nThis event is co-hosted by York’s Teaching Commons ( https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/ )/Office of the VP Teaching and Learning and Connected Minds ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/connected-minds/ ).\nFaculty members can learn more and register here. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1147036 )\nStudents can learn more and register here.  ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1147988 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/dialogues-ai-in-the-classroom-in-person-jan-20-2026-1100-100-et/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Location TBC @ 4700 Keele St
END:VEVENT
