SUMMARY:Not Just a Tool: AI, Access, and the Ownership of Student Work (Online – March 11, 2026, 3:00-4:30 ET)
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop we will investigate how AI tools mediate access and equity for students—especially in writing-rich contexts—while also raising new ethical concerns about digital divides, data ownership, student consent, and commodification. How can we meet student access needs and preserve IP and data ownership in the AI-saturated environment?\nLearn more and register with our registration form. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1145537 )\n
