SUMMARY:Dean’s Session: AMA (AGA) – Ask Me Anything (About Graduate Admissions)
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an hour-long drop in session where you can ask Vice-Provost and Dean of the Faculty of Graduate Studies, Alice MacLachlan anything about the Graduate Admissions process!\nTake advantage of this opportunity to ask an expert any burning questions you have about the admissions process. How to pick a graduate program? How much do grades really matter? What’s it like to be on the receiving end of requests for a supervisor? What is grad school really like? How do I become a professor, or even Dean?\nRegistration is required. To RSVP or learn more, visit yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_n1NmJonMRUmlbd0xm38BbQ ).\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs ( https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nFor any questions, please email us at FGSAPPLY@YORKU.CA ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
