SUMMARY:1:1 Drop-In Sessions for Graduate Admissions (In-Person)
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a Graduate Admissions 1:1 Drop In Session, in person!\nJoin us to ask any questions that you might have about York University and our graduate admissions process.\nRegistration is required ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/graduate-admissions-11-drop-in-session-in-person-tickets-1967745236974?aff=oddtdtcreator ).\nWhile you are welcome to drop in at any point during the session, attendees will be seen on a first-come-first-serve basis. When you arrive, please add your name to the sign in sheet, and we will see participants one-by-one. We cannot guarantee a specific meeting time. If you are interested in a (timed) 1:1 online appointment ( https://outlook.office.com/book/ONLINEProspectiveGraduateStudentMeeting@yuoffice.yorku.ca/?ismsaljsauthenabled ) (linked) , we offer those as well.\nPLEASE NOTE: During these sessions we will not be able to answer any questions about Schulich School of Business programs, or Osgoode Law School Professional LLM programs (either Part Time, or Full Time).\nFor all other questions about graduate diplomas, master’s programs, and doctoral degrees, we look forward to having you attend.\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs ( http://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nFor any questions, please email us at FGSAPPLY@YORKU.CA ( mailto:FGSAPPLY@YORKU.CA ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/11-drop-in-sessions-for-graduate-admissions-in-person/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Glendon Maîtrise en affaires publiques et internationales (MAPI),Glendon Masters in Public &amp; International Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Conference Interpreting,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Theatre,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp; Performance Studies,Graduate Program in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art
