TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Question Everything: Evaluating in an era of bias, spin and social polarization
DESCRIPTION:Part of the Think, Research, Create: Intro to Library Research Series (3 out of 4). Sign in with Passport York (PPY). Please arrive on-time and stay. Presenters will allow you in for the first 15 mins.\nNot all information is created equally—and not all search tools work the same way. This interactive workshop will help you compare popular tools for information discovery from AI to academic search platforms. You’ll learn the differences between misinformation, disinformation, malinformation, AI hallucinations and deepfakes. We’ll show you practical fact-checking tools and strategies to help you figure out what’s real and what’s not. You’ll also practice evaluating sources, including academic ones, so you can choose the most reliable information for your assignments. By the end, you’ll feel more confident navigating the information jungle!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/question-everything-evaluating-in-an-era-of-bias-spin-and-social-polarization-14/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:York University
