SUMMARY:From PhD to Postdoc: Crafting Competitive Applications for External Fellowships
DESCRIPTION:Are you considering a postdoctoral position after graduate school but unsure where to start? This workshop is designed to help graduate students navigate the competitive landscape of postdoc funding. Topics include writing compelling application materials, including the research proposal and CV, securing effective letters of support, and aligning your application with the funding opportunity. You’ll also gain insights into funding sources, timelines, and strategies for reaching out to potential mentors. Whether you’re just beginning to explore postdoc options or getting ready to apply, this session will equip you with the tools and confidence to take the next step in your research career.\nEvent Details:\nDATE: Thursday, March 12, 2026\nTIME: Noon to 1:30 p.m.\nLOCATION: online (Zoom)\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/from-phd-to-postdoc-crafting-competitive-applications-for-external-fellowships/
