SUMMARY:Assessing Learning: Grading, Evaluation, and Feedback (Online: 2 Feb.-6 Mar., 2026)
DESCRIPTION:This course can count toward the Certificates in University Teaching. ( https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/certificates/ )\nResearch suggests that frequent feedback on learning progress is key to student success in postsecondary learning. However, assessing student learning can also be challenging, whether you are looking to give weekly graded feedback or are grappling with how best to ensure academic integrity for a final exam. In this fully online course, participants will learn by doing through ongoing participation in weekly learning activities. Together we will test out strategies for maximizing feedback to students while keeping the workload manageable, explore principles and tools to streamline grading, apply best practices for designing assessments, and troubleshoot common challenges.\nLearn more and register with our registration form. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1143646 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/assessing-learning-grading-evaluation-and-feedback-online-2-feb-6-mar-2026/
