SUMMARY:VCP presents BIPOC ARTIST HUB – ART INSTALLATION
DESCRIPTION:Since September, students from VCP’s BIPOC Artist HUB at York University have been working towards bringing this art installation to life, this year focusing on the theme of LOST/FOUND.\nNew this year, patrons and audiences can get an exclusive look at the featured art exhibits throughout the month of January. Stop by Vanier College, Room 001 between 9am-4pm, Monday-Friday, to catch all the amazing artwork on display.\nWant to see more from the HUB? Join us for VCP’s BIPOC Artist HUB Showcase happening at the end of January. For more information on tickets please visit our website. With exhibits that range from visual art, board games, live performances, and more, we hope to transport you to other worlds with our personal stories, reflections and ideations.\nDirected by Alex Jyn-Li Cairns\nAssistant Directed by Danny Sylvan\nStage Managed by Tiara Suluma\nJan. 5-31, 2026\n9-4pm\nVanier Renaissance Room, 001 Vanier College\nTo reach the room, take the stairs or elevator on the east side of Vanier College to the basement.\nFREE ADMISSION\nWebsite: https://www.yorku.ca/laps/vcp/\nEmail: vcp@yorku.ca\nFacebook: @VanierCollegeProductions\nInstagram: @vancproductions\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/vcp-presents-bipoc-artist-hub-art-installation/
