SUMMARY:Industry Connections: Real – Talk Series
DESCRIPTION:Date: Dec. 5\nTime: 12:30 to 1:30 p.m.\nLocation: HNES  Room 102\nDetails: \nJoin us for an honest conversation with industry professionals as they share their real-life journeys to success – including the twists, turns and lessons learned along the way. This is your chance to gain insights into non-linear career paths and ask the questions you’ve always wondered like, “What do you wish someone told you?”\nFeatured Guest: Adhithya Kurup, Corporate Sustainability Specialist at Sobeys\nBio: Adhithya Kurup is a Corporate Sustainability Specialist at Sobeys, where he leads initiatives on circularity, packaging, and waste reduction as part of the company’s national sustainability team. With over three years of experience in the Canadian grocery retail industry, he has managed multiple sustainability projects focused on packaging compliance, innovation, and waste reduction across operations and supply chains. His work bridges strategy, collaboration, and implementation to drive measurable progress toward a more circular and sustainable retail system. Adhithya is passionate about embedding sustainability into business strategy to create lasting, system-wide impact.\nPLEASE REGISTER\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/industry-connections-real-talk-series/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
