SUMMARY:VCP presents BIPOC ARTIST HUB SHOWCASE
DESCRIPTION:Since September, students from VCP’s BIPOC Artist HUB at York University have been working towards bringing this showcase to life, this year focusing on the theme of LOST/FOUND. With exhibits that range from visual art, board games, live performances, and more, we hope to transport you to other worlds with our personal stories, reflections and ideations.\nDirected by Alex Jyn-Li Cairns\nAssistant Directed by Danny Sylvan\nStage Managed by Tiara Suluma\nJan. 30-31, 2026\n7-9pm\nVanier Renaissance Room, 001 Vanier College\nTo reach the room, take the stairs or elevator on the east side of Vanier College to the basement.\nPay-What-You-Can-Afford Tickets\nSuggested Pricing: VCP Supporter $50 | General $25 | VCP Alumni $20 | Students $15 | VCP Current Company $10\nAvailable online or CASH ONLY at door\nWebsite: https://www.yorku.ca/laps/vcp/\nEmail: vcp@yorku.ca\nFacebook: @VanierCollegeProductions\nInstagram: @vancproductions\n
