SUMMARY:Music Mirrors Minds: Neuroaesthetics and Neuro-Music with Gene Coleman
DESCRIPTION:On December 3, composer and director Gene Coleman ( https://www.genecolemancomposer.com/ ) will give a talk on Neuroaesthetics and Neuro-Music, introducing his research-informed compositional methods and exploring how perception, cognition, and creativity intersect in this emerging field. Coleman’s work, which he describes as “Neuro-Music,” is shaped by insights from auditory neuroscience and examines how artistic practice and brain science inform one another.\nMani Mazinani ( https://manimazinani.net/ ), Connected Minds’ current Artist-in-Residence, will join the session as a co-respondent during the Q&A, bringing perspectives from his residency research. This event is part of the Body Electric exhibition and workshop series and is organized by Mark-David Hosale ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/people/mark-david-hosale/ ), AMPD faculty member and Connected Minds researcher.\nDate: Wednesday, December 3\nLocation: Sensorium Loft, Fourth Floor CFA\nTime: 4:30 – 5:30 p.m.\nFREE Admission\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/music-mirrors-minds-neuroaesthetics-and-neuro-music-with-gene-coleman/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sensorium Loft, 4th Floor CFA @ 86 Fine Arts Road
