SUMMARY:Publishing your research data in a data repository
DESCRIPTION:Many scholarly journals are now requiring authors to submit a Data Availability Statement (DAS). Because of this requirement, the importance of publishing research data in a data repository and obtaining a permanent URL, such as a digital object identifier (DOI), is becoming increasingly important. This workshop introduces the guiding principles of data publishing. During this workshop, you will learn:\n\nHow to prepare your data for sharing and long-term access\nHow to select a data repository that meets your needs\nA brief overview of the data deposit process for York’s institutional research data repository, York University’s Dataverse, will also be provided.\nThis workshop will be taught by the Libraries’ Research Data Management team and is part of the Libraries’ programming for International Love Data Week 2026.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/publishing-your-research-data-in-a-data-repository-3/
