SUMMARY:Indigenous Research – tending to a garden of information
DESCRIPTION:Researching Indigenous topics is undeniably complex. Indigenous knowledges are deeply rooted in community but identifying authentic Indigenous voices in academia among numerous colonial narratives can be a daunting task. Processing this material can take an emotional toll. By learning how to navigate these resources thoughtfully, you can respectfully and ethically incorporate Indigenous knowledge into your assignments and research.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-research-tending-to-a-garden-of-information-2/
