SUMMARY:ES PhD Research Day: REFUSAL//REFUGIA
DESCRIPTION:ES PhD Research Day: REFUSAL//REFUGIA\nFriday November 14, 9am to 4pm, HNES 140\nThe PhD Environmental Studies Students Association (PhESSA), with the support of the ES PhD Program and the Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change, invites you join us at ES PhD Research Day 2025. This annual event showcases the rich diversity of work being done by PhD students in Environmental Studies as it addresses the increasingly fraught social, ecological, economic, spiritual, and political conditions of our time.\nThe day’s theme, refusal // refugia, speaks to the need for work that is oppositional and confrontational, and work that nurtures relationships of protection and sanctuary. How can our diverse research refuse and/or become refuge?\nPlease join us for a rich lineup of student presentations. Featured is an exciting keynote talk from ES PhD aluma Laurence Butet-Roch: “Attuning Research: Reflections on Resisting Extractive Practices”\nWe look forward to seeing you there!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/es-phd-research-day/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies
LOCATION:140 HNES Building
