SUMMARY:Book Launch: Indigeneity in the Philippines: Studies on Knowledge, Identity, and Rights
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the launch of this interdisciplinary volume exploring Indigenous peoples in the Philippines. Contributors examine Indigenous rights, knowledge, colonial histories, and identity, with a focus on northern Luzon’s Cordillera region, highlighting how Indigenous communities assert their presence, preserve knowledge, and engage with national and global conversations on Indigeneity.\nSponsored by the Centre for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages (CIKL), the York Centre for Asian Research (YCAR), the Philippines Study Group, and York International. Attendees receive a 30% discount code on the book from UHP.\nPlease register ( https://tinyurl.com/mvrff5tb )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-indigeneity-in-the-philippines-studies-on-knowledge-identity-and-rights/
