SUMMARY:Women in STEM Wikipedia Edit-a-thon
DESCRIPTION:York University Libraries will be hosting our annual Women in STEM Wikipedia Edit-a-thon from 1 to 4 p.m. on Thursday, Nov. 6. This in-person event will be held in Scott Library room 530. \nHonouring the memory of Ada Lovelace, the first computer programmer whose contributions were overlooked for decades, this event is held every year to celebrate, recognize and most of all promote and remember the contributions of women in all the various STEM fields. Women in STEM are underrepresented in Wikipedia and this edit-a-thon is one way to help create a more representative Wikipedia.  \nWe encourage anyone to drop-by and to contribute, no previous Wikipedia editing experience necessary. We will have facilitators and lists of articles to work on to help novices get up and running. This year’s Edit-a-thon will focus on creating and improving both Wikipedia articles and Wikidata items about women in STEM fields.  \nMore information on the event can be found through the York University Libraries research guides website ( https://researchguides.library.yorku.ca/ada ).\nLearn more about Ada Lovelace and women in STEM Wikipedia edit-a-thons ( https://findingada.com/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/women-in-stem-wikipedia-edit-a-thon-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=John Dupuis:MAILTO:jdupuis@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Scott Library, Room 530 (5th floor computer lab) @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
