SUMMARY:Master in Environmental Studies (MES) Virtual Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Master in Environmental Studies (MES) Information Session\n📅 Date: Wednesday, Nov. 26\n🕛 Time: Noon to 1 p.m.\n📍 Location: Online (Zoom)\n🔗Registration: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/X_BKqn6JRC2RzPPDZ4lbTg ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/X_BKqn6JRC2RzPPDZ4lbTg )\nAre you passionate about tackling complex environmental challenges through interdisciplinary approaches? Join us to learn more about the MES degree, a 2-year, self-directed, full-time program designed to empower students to lead change in diverse environmental fields.\n🌱 Program Highlights:\n\nTailor your studies to your interests and career goals\nEngage with cutting-edge research and community-based learning\n\n📚 Explore Areas of Study:\n\nClimate Change and Sustainable Energy Transitions\nEnvironmental, Climate and Indigenous Justice\nUrban and Regional Planning and Infrastructures\nEcological Economics and Sustainability Analytics\nEnvironmental Arts, Culture and Justice\nCritical Theories of International Development and Global Inequities\nEnvironmental Management and Conservation\nSustainable Food Systems\nLaw, Justice and Sustainability (MES/JD)\nBusiness and the Environment\nEnvironmental Education\n\nIf you have questions about applying to the program or the upcoming information session, please contact envsgrad@yorku.ca ( mailto:envsgrad@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/master-in-environmental-studies-mes-virtual-information-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies
LOCATION:Online
END:VEVENT
