SUMMARY:Demystifying Graduate Academic Writing
DESCRIPTION:Writing at the Graduate-Level carries with it a whole array of expectations that are often unclear for graduate writers at the Masters or Doctoral level. This workshop is designed to clarify some of what those expectations entail, and to help you develop strategies to better navigate the demands of graduate writing. Whether in your thesis, course-work, or more public facing work, we can make progress productively and in ways that develop our capacities. Important also is thinking about the support and resources available to put forward work that is meaningful for you and for your audience. No writer is an island, and developing ways to keep connected are vital in meeting your writing goals.\nEvent Details\nDATE: Thursday, October 8, 2026\nTIME: 11:00 a.m.-12:00 p.m.\nLOCATION: Online (Zoom)\nPartner: Writing Centre\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/demystifying-graduate-academic-writing/
