SUMMARY:Geographic Information System (GIS) Day 2025
DESCRIPTION:Attention GIS enthusiasts, curious minds, and secondary school educators (Grades 9 to 12)!\nJoin us in celebrating Geographic Information System (GIS) Day on November 19th and discover how maps reveal more than just directions.\nDid you know that geomatics technology seamlessly integrates into our everyday lives, often without us even realizing it? Explore innovative technology and its practical applications to real-world challenges at GIS Day. Don’t miss out on this opportunity to learn more about GIS while celebrating and networking with peers.\nThis event is hybrid, open to anyone curious about geomatics, with both in-person and online options available. Register today and choose your attendance type. Access to this event is exclusively for registered attendees.\nFor current students: Discover the various career paths available and learn about our Certificate in Geomatics ( https://euc.yorku.ca/continuing-studies/certificate-in-geomatics-geographic-information-systems-gis-and-remote-sensing/ ). Connect with industry leaders, meet geomatics professors and graduate students, and expand your professional network.\nFor educators: We warmly invite you to bring your students along for a day of discovery and inspiration. Students will explore geomatics technologies through demonstrations, career talks, and research presentations.\nCheck out our website below for a detailed agenda and to register.\nMore information: https://euc.yorku.ca/events-euc/2025-gis-day/ ( https://euc.yorku.ca/events-euc/2025-gis-day/ )\nRegister: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/geographic-information-system-gis-day-tickets-1761036500579 ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/geographic-information-system-gis-day-tickets-1761036500579 )\nFor any questions, contact Doris at dorissiu@yorku.ca ( mailto:dorissiu@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/geographic-information-system-gis-day-2025/
