SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | The Quest for a Great Place to Work
DESCRIPTION:Join Anirban Kar, Assistant Professor, School of Administrative Studies, Faculty of Liberal Arts and Professional Studies on Nov. 26. When do employees perceive an organization to be a great place to work? Understanding this is critical given how popular yet largely unresearched the notion of a great place to work is. In this session, Anirban will speak about reconceptualization of a great place to work based on affect and preference and share a model of a great place to work, strongly supported by data gathered in three studies.\n
