SUMMARY:Women in STEM Meet-Up: Teaching, Mentorship and Community
DESCRIPTION:All women faculty in STEM fields are invited to a meet-up on Women in STEM: Teaching, Mentorship and Community, co-hosted by Faculty of Health and Faculty Affairs.  Join us for an interactive afternoon to celebrate and support women faculty in STEM – share stories, explore challenges, and build connections around teaching excellence and peer support.\nCome and connect with other women in STEM over a light lunch and share your experiences and wisdom and build an inclusive community, whether you’re early in your career or a seasoned educator!\nThe meet-up will feature a presentation by Professor Rebecca Pillai Riddell about DIVERT ( https://divertmentalhealth.ca/ ) Mental Health and how this transdisciplinary project funded by CIHR equips new and emerging/trainee health scientists with a broad range of knowledges, skills, and mentoring supports to improve inclusivity and accessibility of the traditional mental health system. Everyone who participates in DIVERT ( https://divertmentalhealth.ca/ ) is a teacher and a learner interested in expanding their understanding of mental health.\nPlease RSVP ( https://forms.office.com/r/Q5Ts6vC7LP ) by Wednesday, October 29\nPlease reach out to FacAffairs@yorku.ca ( mailto:FacAffairs@yorku.ca ) for questions.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/women-in-stem-meet-up-teaching-mentorship-and-community/
