SUMMARY:NSERC Alliance Advantage: A Deep Dive into the Application
DESCRIPTION:Join Research Commons for an in-depth walkthrough of the NSERC Alliance Advantage Grant application process, led by experienced Research Officers from the Lassonde School of Engineering and the Faculty of Science.\nThe NSERC Alliance Advantage Grant offers funding for collaborative research projects between academic researchers and partner organizations, providing an edge in advancing innovations through partnerships. This grant is ideal for researchers looking to work closely with industry, non-profits, or government sectors to apply scientific discoveries and engineering solutions to real-world challenges. \nIn this session, we’ll cover common mistakes that applicants make and showcase examples of strong applications, offering practical insights to help you develop a competitive proposal. Whether you’re new to the process or looking to refine your application strategies, this event is open to researchers across all disciplines and will provide valuable guidance for anyone seeking to secure funding through collaborative research. \nRegister here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/wTeSjgVjSFKAnkmcQE1XfQ )\n \nSpeakers:  \n\nGeorge Bikopolous, Research Officer, Faculty of Science \n\n\nStuart Macgregor, Research Officer, Faculty of Science \n\n\nSoma Tripathi, Grant Development Specialist, Faculty of LA&PS\n \n\nThis workshop will be recorded and saved in our archive. Visit our website for a list of upcoming workshops.  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/nserc-alliance-advantage-a-deep-dive-into-the-application/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
