SUMMARY:Let’s Talk About It: A Conversation with Author Suzette Mayr
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin us for a compelling author talk with Suzette Mayr, part of the Let’s Talk About It series hosted by York University Libraries.\nMayr is an award-winning Canadian novelist and professor of creative writing at the University of Calgary. Her most recent novel, The Sleeping Car Porter, won the 2022 Scotiabank Giller Prize and has been celebrated for its vivid portrayal of a Black, queer train porter navigating race, sexuality, and class in 1920s Canada.\nThrough humour, history, and poetic insight, Mayr’s work explores themes of identity, belonging, and the untold stories of marginalized communities.\nAll students, faculty, staff, and community members are welcome.\n
URL:https://yorku.libcal.com/event/3951452
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Collaboratory, Scott Library (Second Floor) @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 2S5
END:VEVENT
