SUMMARY:Navigating Professional Development at York: A Guide for Graduate Students and Postdocs
DESCRIPTION:York University offers a wide range of professional development resources to support graduate students and postdoctoral researchers in building skills for academic and non-academic careers. With so many options available, however, it can be difficult to identify which opportunities are most relevant to your personal goals and interests. This workshop will introduce participants to programs, services, and opportunities across campus in key areas from career development to teaching and research training. It will also provide details on the new digital badges available to graduate students and postdoctoral researchers for participation in professional development activities.  Whether you’re planning your next steps or looking to enhance your current skill set, this session will help you make the most of your time at York and strategically prepare for your future.\nEvent Details:\nDATE: Thursday, September 24, 2026\nTIME: 11:00 a.m.-12:00 p.m. (ET)\nLOCATION: online (Zoom)\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/TtGVJfyQSQ6izr0kooF9ww )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grad-career-skills-workshop/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
