SUMMARY:Teaching Kitchen x Diabetes Education Month – Burrito Bowls
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a hands-on cooking class celebrating Diabetes Education Month! Learn how to make delicious and nutritious burrito bowls from scratch, guided by Chef Donna and our registered dietitian, Dahlia.\nThis interactive experience will teach you how to prepare budget-friendly and balanced meals that support blood sugar management without sacrificing flavour.\nPublic health nurses will be on-site to share valuable insights into the health benefits of whole foods, portion control, and how lifestyle changes can positively impact diabetes prevention and management. Whether you’re living with diabetes, supporting a loved one, or simply interested in healthier eating, this class is for you!\nEvent Highlights:\n\nStep-by-step burrito bowl preparation using fresh, wholesome ingredients\nNutrition tips from a registered dietitian\nHealth education from public health nurses\nBudgetig tips\nTasty samples and take-home recipes\n\nRegister here! ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/teaching-kitchen-x-diabetes-education-month-burrito-bowls-tickets-1848978457339?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-kitchen-x-diabetes-education-month-burrito-bowls/
ORGANIZER;CN=YUeats:MAILTO:food@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Financial Literacy Month,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning,Well-being
LOCATION:Keele Campus
