SUMMARY:​The Automotive Innovation Challenge (AIC) Hackathon
DESCRIPTION:Apply Now: 2025 Automotive Innovation Challenge\nHosted by YSpace, York University, the Automotive Innovation Challenge (November 8–9) is a two-day hackathon where post-secondary students tackle real-world challenges in the automotive and mobility sectors.\nParticipants will gain hands-on experience through workshops and prototyping, receive mentorship from industry professionals, and pitch innovative solutions to real industry partners.\nOpen to undergraduate and graduate students from all disciplines, with a focus on engineering, computer science, business, and design.\nApplication Deadline: Oct 31\nTop teams will earn exclusive networking opportunities with industry executives along with an opportunity to engage in a career mentorship conversation.\nIn partnership with Vinfast and SmartTO, and sponsored by the Ontario Vehicle Innovation Network (OVIN).\nLearn more and apply ( https://luma.com/8w43ejya )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-automotive-innovation-challenge-aic-hackathon/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:York University Keele Campus
