SUMMARY:Navigating Financial Challenges & Building Resilience
DESCRIPTION:Join Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) for a dynamic and practical workshop designed to help you take charge of your financial future. Navigating Financial Challenges & Building Resilience will explore effective strategies for managing debt, handling unexpected expenses, and making the most of a limited income.\nFacilitated by Tino Mutsvangwa, financial advisor at CIBC Imperial Service, this session will also highlight valuable resources available through campus programs, community services, and financial institutions. Participants will gain insights into building strong financial habits that promote long-term resilience, confidence, and peace of mind.\nWhether you’re navigating current financial hurdles or preparing for the future, this workshop will offer tools and support to help you thrive.\nOpen to all York University students who are interested in maximizing their financial resources, with a special encouragement for those who identify as Black to participate. Register for the event here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/4FruhclUS0af16TFUJ4wvg#/registration ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/navigating-financial-challenges-building-resilience/
ORGANIZER;CN=Black Excellence at York University:MAILTO:beyu@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Financial Literacy Month
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
