SUMMARY:Virtual Drop-In Session: Master of Biotechnology Management (MBM) & Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology (GDB)
DESCRIPTION:The Master of Biotechnology Management ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/biotech-mgmt/ )  is a graduate program for students who hold a bachelor of science degree in biology, biological sciences, biotechnology, life science, or related discipline, and have little/no work experience in biotechnology. It provides practical interdisciplinary training in biotechnology and management to enhance their competitiveness and employability in the biotechnology management related sectors.\nThe Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/biotech-diploma/ ) is a graduate certification for students who hold a bachelor of science degree in biology, biological sciences, biotechnology, life science, or related discipline, and have little/no work experience in biotechnology, to enhance their competitiveness and employability in the biotechnology sector. The graduate diploma in biotechnology is designed to provide professional preparation for our graduates to fill current labor needs in the biotechnology sector and strengthen the Canadian economy.\nDrop by one of our virtual sessions every other Thursday from 11:30 a.m. to noon to meet the graduate program director and graduate program administrator who will be able to answer any of your questions about the programs.\nPlease Join us on Zoom\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biotechnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Zoom
END:VEVENT
