SUMMARY:Victorian Studies Symposium: Expect the Unexpected
DESCRIPTION:For 17 years, the Victorian Studies Network at York has been linking researchers and enhancing connections among graduate students, post-docs, and faculty. Our goal is to facilitate interdepartmental and interdisciplinary work, to enrich our personal and collective experience of research, and to showcase York as a centre for Victorian studies.\nThe cross-disciplinary scope of the program – music, art history, literature, humanities, archaeology, cultural critique – is particularly inviting.\nLunch and refreshments will be served at the symposium.\nRSVP: Prof. Lesley Higgins via email ( mailto:19higgins55@gmail.com ).\n24 October 2025\n10 am to 3:30 pm\nHarry Crowe Room (Atkinson 109)\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/victorian-studies-symposium-expect-the-unexpected/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Research &amp; Innovation,Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:109 Atkinson College, Harry Crowe Room
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/VSNY-2025-poster-scaled.jpg
