SUMMARY:Research Impact Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking to boost your research visibility? Sign-up for York University Libraries’ Research Impact Challenge! The challenge will run from October 20 to October 24, 2025.\nEach day, the Libraries will release a new daily challenge that will help York researchers develop their online scholarly presence and help improve the visibility of their research.\nWho can participate? All York faculty, staff, and students are encouraged to participate. The challenges are particularly helpful to early career faculty, postdoctoral researchers, and graduate students.\nHow to participate? Register for the challenge using our MS Form ( https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0O8idOr1Np9GvufNTQ8ZTlJUNEpPQlBXUFQwWUE1VTZBUDZOTVpEVVhUMC4u&route=shorturl ). This will ensure you receive the daily challenge email.\nWhen? October 20 to October 24, 2025\nTime commitment? Each challenge takes no more than 20 to 30 minutes to complete and can be done fully online.\nThe Research Impact Challenge is part of the Libraries’ Open Access Week events. Read our blog post ( https://www.library.yorku.ca/web/blog/2025/10/07/explore-open-access-this-october/ ) to learn more about the other events happening in October.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/research-impact-challenge/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Virtual Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/YUL-Event-image-768x3001-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
