SUMMARY:The Overdose Crisis: Spotlight on Opioids, Sedatives & Stimulants
DESCRIPTION:The Overdose Crisis: Spotlight on Opioids, Sedatives & Stimulants \nIn collaboration with the YFS Wellness Centre ( https://www.yfswellness.ca/ ) and Student Counselling, Health & Well-being SCHW ( https://students.yorku.ca/counselling ), this workshop explores opioids, sedatives and stimulants; three drug classes at the core of Canada’s overdose crisis, which has taken over 50,000 lives since 2016. Designed for students, educators, caregivers and community members alike, the session offers a neutral, evidence-based look at these substances, covering their history, effects, youth usage trends, risks and harm reduction strategies. Participants will leave with practical tools to foster open conversations and support safer choices. \nThis event is offered in a hybrid format. Come join us in person in Room 109 at the Second Student Centre for some light snacks and beverages, or tune in virtually from wherever you are most comfortable.\nRegister for The Overdose Crisis: Spotlight on Opioids, Sedatives & Stimulants \n \n\n \nAbout Substance \nSubstance (formerly Drug Free Kids Canada ( https://www.drugfreekidscanada.org/ )) is a national non-profit organization that delivers clear, evidence-based information about substance use to support youth and those around them. By fostering open, stigma-free conversations about substances—including alcohol, cannabis, nicotine, opioids, sedatives and stimulants—Substance empowers communities with the knowledge and tools to navigate these topics with confidence, empathy and care. \n \n \n \n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-overdose-crisis-spotlight-on-opioids-sedatives-stimulants/
