SUMMARY:FGF Brands – Information Session (On-Campus)
DESCRIPTION:Calling all York U students and recent grads interested in finance, supply chain, sales and marketing, and more!\nWe are excited to invite you to the FGF Brands On-Campus Information Session: \n\n📅 Wednesday, October 1st\n🕔 11:30 AM – 1:00 PM\n📍 Schulich School of Business, Private Dining Room\n🎯 Open to all York U students and recent graduates\nJoin us for an ON-CAMPUS info session to hear more about FGF Brands and our exciting opportunities!\n\nWe make disruption delicious. We’re not just a bakery — we’re a technology company that bakes We’re redefining what a bakery can be. Our Innovation Campuses in Canada and USA are constantly engineering new sustainable ways to bring the cleanest possible ingredients back to global-scale food — and we won’t stop until the whole world is eating great food. We bring life to North America’s most trusted brands like ACE Bakery and Stonefire. Our products include butter croissants, delicious naan, muffins, sliced cakes, donuts, and artisan breads like baguettes, buns, bagels and more! To become the world’s greatest baker, you need to have the world’s greatest people – our passion is baked in. This work matters. It’s why we attract the best minds out there with rewarding, cutting-edge careers that are making the world a better place to eat.\nNOTE: This event is open to all York University students and recent graduates. York students must use their @yorku.ca email address to register. Schulich students must register via Handshake ( https://yorku.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1780952 ).\nThis event is NOT OPEN to Non-York students. Student identification will be required for entry to this event. As spots are limited we encourage you to register early to secure your place. Don’t miss this chance to engage with one of the world’s top employers and explore exciting career opportunities!\nREGISTER HERE ( https://schulich.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_b3kHqgHQ8YABsTI )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgf-brands-information-session-on-campus/
ORGANIZER;CN=Schulich School of Business:MAILTO:admissions@schulich.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Schulich School of Business
LOCATION:Schulich Private Dining Room, Main Floor, Schulich Executive Learning Centre @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
