SUMMARY:Nature’s Wild with Andil Gosine (RETURNS) PREE-Views: A Special Launch of Writings from the Censored Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:In advance of the forthcoming exhibition Nature’s Wild with Andil Gosine (RETURNS), CERLAC presents “PREE-Views: A Special Launch of Writings from the Censored Exhibition.”\nJamaica-based writer Annie Paul was also the catalog editor for Nature’s Wild before it was abruptly cancelled at the Art Museum of the Americas this past February. Paul is recuperating the unpublished writings about Professor Gosine’s artworks, by such Caribbean luminaries as Shani Mootoo, Marsha Pearce, Rajiv Mohabir and Shivanee Ramlochan, as a special supplement for her PREE journal. This event celebrates the launch of these writings, which make their first appearance at www.preelit.com that day.\nIn conversation with CERLAC Director Professor Tameka Jones-Samuel, Annie will also entertain questions about the running of her literary and arts magazine and working in the Caribbean.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/natures-wild-with-andil-gosine-returns-pree-views-a-special-launch-of-writings-from-the-censored-exhibition/
ORGANIZER;CN=CERLAC:MAILTO:cerlac@yorku.ca
