SUMMARY:Interfaith Panel Discussion
DESCRIPTION:The interfaith panel discussion is an opportunity for community members to come together encouraging safe, curious and collaborative exchanges fostering a space for learning and growing together while respecting each other’s religious practices and understanding. Student Leaders and Faith leaders will provide their perspective and background as it relates to their faith and religious journey; and what they lean upon during times of hardship to support themselves and their faith communities.\nKey objectives of the gathering and discussion would focus on promoting community growth and learning, impacting the student experience, promoting inclusivity and collaboration.\nLocation: 280A York Lanes\nAudience: Open to all York community members; no registration required\nPanel Moderator: Yvette Munro, Vice Provost Students\n
