SUMMARY:Reaching Adolescents with Health Services: Case Studies from Ghana, with Benedict Weobong
DESCRIPTION:Adolescents face unique barriers in accessing health services, particularly in low- and middle-income countries where health systems are often not designed with their needs in mind.\nThis upcoming seminar will draw on case studies from two innovative initiatives in Ghana – YMIND and Y-Check – to explore scalable strategies for improving adolescent health service delivery. YMIND focuses on school-based mental health early intervention for depression among adolescents, while Y-Check implements the integration of routine health and wellbeing screening into adolescent health systems. Together, these case studies highlight the importance of co-designed, youth-centered, and context-responsive approaches.\nLearn more and register to attend here: Reaching Adolescents with Health Services: Case Studies from Ghana, with Benedict Weobong\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/reaching-adolescents-with-health-services-case-studies-from-ghana-with-benedict-weobong/
