SUMMARY:Interfaith Tabling & Community Connection
DESCRIPTION:Religious faith leaders and affiliated religious clubs will be tabling in Central Square from 2-4pm Tuesday October 7 for an afternoon of interfaith dialogue and community connection. Representatives from various religious backgrounds, along with affiliated student clubs, will be present to offer support, share perspectives, and engage in meaningful conversations. Whether you’re seeking guidance, curious to learn more, or simply interested in connecting with others, all are welcome to drop by.\nThis event is open to students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and beliefs. We look forward to fostering a respectful and inclusive space for exploration and understanding.\nLocation: Central Square\nAudience: open to all York community members; no registration required\nFacilitator: Student Community & Leadership Development\n
