SUMMARY:Grant Writing Workshop Series for Postdoctoral Researchers (online)
DESCRIPTION:York University’s postdoctoral researchers are invited to join a two-part funding workshop series designed to empower postdocs to secure research funding, both now and in the future.\nJoin Jane Ramachandran of Resonant Solutions, a seasoned expert with nearly three decades of grant-writing experience, for specialized sessions on finding and applying for grant funding.\nSession One: Grants 101 for Postdoctoral Researchers\nWednesday, October 15, 2025 at 1:00-2:00 PM ET\nLed by Jane Ramachandran, this workshop will introduce the fundamentals of funding. Topics include different types of funding, assessing your grant readiness, techniques for finding the right funding sources, and how to make your research ideas stand out.\nBy the end of the workshop, you will be better equipped to identify the right grants for your needs and position your ideas more competitively.\nRecommended Prerequisite: None\nData and Recording Policy\nAttendees will have the opportunity to complete a very brief survey before and after the workshop to understand its impact and improve future events. All survey data is anonymous, and no identifying information will be collected. The teaching and presentation portions will be recorded for liability and further training purposes. The Q&A segment will not be recorded. No personal data will be shared nor sold.\nAll participants are invited to attend the second interactive workshop on October 29th, “Grant Application Budget Development,” and may also sign up for a 30-minute personalized funding advisory consultation, with opportunities for additional grant application support.\nWhat’s Next?\nAll participants are invited to attend the second interactive workshop on October 29th, “Grant Application Budget Development,” and may also sign up for a 30-minute personalized funding advisory consultation, with opportunities for additional grant application support.\nThe MS Teams link will be provided to registrants before the workshop. Please register by Tuesday, October 14.\nRegistration Link ( https://fgs.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=315025 )\n \n
