SUMMARY:Unlocking NCFDD: Tools and Networks for Graduate Student & Postdoc Success
DESCRIPTION:As part of York’s institutional membership with the National Center for Faculty Development & Diversity (NCFDD), this session is designed to increase awareness and accessibility of resources for graduate students and postdoctoral fellows. Learn about NCFDD’s support, the Community space, and how to activate your membership. The session features 30 minutes of content followed by a 15-minute live Q&A with Frank Sesso, Partnership Success Director at NCFDD. Frank brings over 25 years of higher education experience. A former associate professor with expertise in distance education, interdisciplinary curriculum development, and fostering collaborative learning communities, Frank works to connect faculty, graduate students, and academic leaders across North America with valuable resources and networks to support their success. The Zoom link will be provided after registration. Learn more about NCFDD ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/gpps-opportunity/ncfdd/ ).\nRegistration is Required: RSVP\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ncfdd-tools-and-networks-for-grad-student-postdoc-success/
