SUMMARY:The Faculty Insider’s Guide to Library Research Supports
DESCRIPTION:Research Commons is pleased to invite you to a Libraries overview session titled, The Faculty Insider’s Guide to Library Research Supports.\n\nAll faculty and research staff are welcome.\n\nDiscover how York University Libraries can be your research superpower. Beyond just books, the library offers research tools and services you may not have explored, from funding support to data management and everything in between. Level up your research game with resources designed to help you work smarter, not harder.\n\nRegister here\n\nSpeakers: \n\n\nKris Joseph, Director, Department of Digital Scholarship Infrastructure\n\n\nStephanie Quail, Director of Open Scholarship\n\nJohn Dupuis, Scholarly Publishing Librarian, Open Scholarship Department\n\n\nThis workshop will be recorded and saved in our archive. Visit our website for a list of upcoming workshops.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-faculty-insiders-guide-to-library-research-supports/
