SUMMARY:Strategies for Managing Your Research Data
DESCRIPTION:Research Commons is pleased to invite you to a Libraries session titled, Strategies for Managing Your Research Data.\nAll faculty and research staff are welcome.\n\nManaging research data is becoming increasingly complex for York researchers. Attend this workshop to learn general principles and best practices for data documentation, deposit, and sharing. This workshop will cover the following topics:\n\n\n\nFunder and journal data deposit requirements;\n\n\nEmerging research data management principles;\n\n\nStrategies to implement data management best practices throughout the data lifecycle;\n\n\nand York-specific resources and tools for research data management.\n\n\n\n\nParticipants will walk away from this workshop with awareness of the changing culture of data sharing, practical resources and tips to implement in their research data management workflows, and templates they can use to begin creating a data management plan for their grant applications. This workshop will be taught by the Libraries’ Research Data Management team.\n\nRegister here\n\nSpeakers: \n\n\nStephanie Quail, Director of Open Scholarship\n\n\nMinglu Wang, Associate Librarian, Research and Open Scholarship, Library\n\n\n\nThis workshop will be recorded and saved in our archive. Visit our website for a list of upcoming workshops.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/strategies-for-managing-your-research-data/
ORGANIZER;CN=Research Commons:MAILTO:rescom@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Libraries,Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
