SUMMARY:Orientation to Video and Audio Editing: Demystifying the Editing Process
DESCRIPTION:This orientation is designed to demonstrate the essential tools and techniques of video and audio editing. This session breaks down the often-intimidating editing process into simple, manageable steps, covering everything from basic cuts and transitions to adding effects, sound, and text. Whether you’re editing a vlog, podcast, or presentation, you’ll gain confidence in using editing software to transform raw footage into a polished, professional final product.  Please bring your laptop along so you can download and try the tools we’ll show you!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/orientation-to-video-and-audio-editing-demystifying-the-editing-process-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Scott Library, 4700 Keele Street
