SUMMARY:Across the Screen featuring Beto Skubs
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an exclusive online event featuring Beto Skubs ( https://www.imdb.com/name/nm2899307/ ), writer and producer of “Grey’s Anatomy.”\nModerated by Fabio Montanari, an assistant professor at York University, in the Department of Cinema & Media Arts ( https://cma.ampd.yorku.ca/ ), and a screenwriter with credits on Netflix, HBO and Amazon Prime video.\nOpen to all AMPD students, this event is a unique opportunity to gain insight from a seasoned screenwriter about the art and craft of writing for TV in the current marketplace.\nDATE: Wednesday, September 24, 2025\nTIME: 6:30 p.m.\nLOCATION: Zoom – Link to be provided upon RSVP\nRSVP: Secure your spot by emailing fbm@yorku.ca \nAcross the Screen is a monthly conversation series that brings accomplished screenwriters and producers to share their experiences, insights, and career journeys. Each session highlights professionals who are shaping the industry in different ways, offering students and emerging creators the chance to learn directly from their paths.\nThis term, the focus is on international markets — exploring how writers and producers have expanded their work across borders, navigated cultural differences, and built careers on a global scale. The goal is to provide practical advice, inspiration, and a deeper understanding of the opportunities and challenges of working “across the screen,” beyond one’s local industry.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/across-the-screen-featuring-beto-skubs/
CATEGORIES:Graduate Program in Film,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Online event via Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/beto.jpg
END:VEVENT
