SUMMARY:Take a Paws
DESCRIPTION:Take a Paws is a drop-in wellness initiative where staff and students are invited to spend time with certified therapy dogs on campus. This event offers a calming and joyful space to decompress, reduce stress, and boost overall well-being through gentle interaction with trained canine companions. Research shows that even brief time spent with therapy animals can improve mood, lower anxiety, and create a sense of connection. No registration required, just drop in and enjoy a moment of calm with a furry friend.\nOrganized by Student Accessibility Services.\nLocation: DB1017, Dahdahleh Building, Keele Campus\nFormat: Drop-In In-Person Event\nAudience: York Community\n \n
