SUMMARY:Identifying and Responding to Students in Distress Toolkit Drop-In Sessions
DESCRIPTION:As part of the launch of our new Identifying and Responding to Students in Distress Toolkit, we are offering drop-in sessions to provide additional support. These sessions are designed to create an open and supportive space where staff, faculty, instructors can ask questions, seek clarification, and discuss how to apply the toolkit in their roles.\nWhether you would like guidance on recognizing signs of student distress, strategies for responding effectively, or simply want to learn more about the resources available, these sessions are an opportunity to connect and receive support.\nGuides Available At: https://www.yorku.ca/well-being/finding-help/\nFormat: Virtual\nAudience: Staff and Faculty\nZoom Details: \nLink ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/95737252172?pwd=BRLCiHMcrBwRqAzzXi1b4Q6qf4wveF.1&from=addon )\nMeeting ID: 957 3725 2172\nPasscode: 723140\n\n
