SUMMARY:Data Discovery for your Research: Social Sciences
DESCRIPTION:Do you need to find published data to use in your research projects or assignments, and you don’t know where to start? We can help!\nThis practical workshop will be conducted by members of the York University Libraries’ Data Services Team. It will introduce various sources of data, such as Statistics Canada and international data producers. In addition we will explore strategies to locate and evaluate relevant datasets for research in the social sciences.\n
