TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:The Changing Landscape of Doctoral Education: Implications for Supervision – Online
DESCRIPTION:An online workshop with Dr. Stan Taylor, Honourary PROFESSOR, Durham University UK\nThe Graduate Supervision Support Hub ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/supervisiontoolkit/ ) at York University, in collaboration with the National Community of Practice ( https://cags.ca/national-community-of-practice-on-graduate-supervision/#:~:text=The%20National%20Community%20of%20Practice,supervisor%20wellness%20through%20collaborative%20learning. ) on Graduate Supervision is pleased to welcome international graduate supervision scholar and author Dr. Stan Taylor ( https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/stan-taylor/#publications ) to share insights from his long-standing commitment to support doctoral supervisors to enhance their practice.\nIn this national webinar, Dr. Taylor will:\n\nLook briefly at the traditional model of supervision in the Humboldtian world\nOutline the changing landscape of doctoral education, including massification, diversification, McDonaldisation, regulation, structuration, and capitalisation\nConsider the implications of these shifts on graduate supervision highlighting the additional knowledge and skills which supervisors need to be effective\nFoster discussion regarding how programs and institutions can support supervisors to develop and enhance their supervision.\n\nDate: Wednesday, March 4th, 2026\nTime: 12:00PM-1:15PM (EST)\nLocation: Online via Zoom                                          \nRegistration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_Zbh33C_TSb2kxR4B-eJVuA#/registration )\nFor more information contact Tracy Bhoola, Manager, Graduate Supervision Support Hub tbhoola@yorku.ca ( mailto:tbhoola@yorku.ca ) or Associate Dean, Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith fgsadacd@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsadacd@yorku.ca ).\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-changing-landscape-of-doctoral-education-implications-for-supervision-online/
