SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Mentors, Peers, and the Hidden Networks of Learning
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Scholars’ Hub on Oct. 1, Marie-Hélène Budworth, Associate Professor and Director at the School of Resource Management at the Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies explores why traditional feedback often falls short and how genuine growth happens through relationships at work. Drawing on feedback theory and the concept of high-quality connections, Dr. Budworth highlights how mentors, peers, and everyday colleagues create the networks that truly support learning and development. Alumni will leave with fresh insights into how to build and sustain these connections for long-term career success.\n
