SUMMARY:Theatre @ York presents Much Ado About Nothing
DESCRIPTION:by William Shakespeare\nwith Additional Text by Erin Shields\nShakespeare presents two very different love stories. Hero and Claudio fall in love almost instantly, but their relationship is threatened by the interference of Don John, who seeks to ruin their happiness. In contrast, Beatrice and Benedick are kept apart by their pride and constant bickering—until their friends step in and play matchmaker.\nLOCATION\nJoseph G. Green Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/joseph-g-green-studio-theatre/ )\nThe Joseph G. Green Theatre has very limited seating and performances often sell out in advance. There is no guarantee of ticket availability on the day of show. Online advance ticket purchasing highly recommended.\nPERFORMANCE SCHEDULE\nSaturday, Nov 15 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview 1)\nSunday, Nov 16 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview 2)\nTuesday, Nov 18 – 7:30 p.m.\nWednesday, Nov 19 – 1:00 p.m.\nWednesday, Nov 19 – 7:30 p.m.\nThursday, Nov 20 – 7:30 p.m.\nFriday, Nov 21 – 1:00 p.m. | 7:30 p.m.\nFriday, Nov 21 – 7:30 p.m.\nSaturday, Nov 22 – 2:00 p.m.\nTICKETS\nPreview Tickets (Nov 15 & 16): $15.00\nStudent: $15.00\nAdvanced:(until Sunday Nov 16th): $20.00\nRegular Tickets: $25.00\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/theatre-at-york-presents-much-ado-about-nothing/
