TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Who’s At the Table? Bias, Positionality, and Pedagogical Power (ONLINE- December 2nd, 2025 11-12:30 )
DESCRIPTION:Unpack how AI systems reflect and reproduce existing social biases, and how our positionality as educators shapes the way we introduce or resist AI in the classroom. Participants will work through cases and frameworks to examine the hidden curriculum AI tools may carry into our pedagogy.\nNote that registration for this workshop closes on Dec. 1 at noon.\nPlease register using our Who’s At the Table? registration form. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1132027 )\nNote: this workshop counts toward our Certificates in AI Pedagogies ( https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/certificates/#ai-pedagogies ) and is part of the Critical Lens theme.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/whos-at-the-table-bias-positionality-and-pedagogical-power-online-december-2nd-2025-11-1230/
ORGANIZER;CN=Teaching Commons:MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
