SUMMARY:Black Inclusion: Historic and Current Efforts to Dismantle Anti-Black Racism
DESCRIPTION:This session will follow the birth and development of anti-Black racism both globally and locally, and the historic and on-going efforts to dismantle it. Through case-studies and scenarios, participants will be offered tools and examples of how to respond to anti-Black racism in effective and sustainable ways.\nFurther information and registration can be found through YU Learn ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=1853 ).\n \n
