TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Connected Minds Workshop: How to Build and Maintain International Partnerships Responsibly
DESCRIPTION:\nLooking to expand your research network and make a global impact? This workshop breaks down how to build new research partnerships and collaborations from initial contact, setting project milestones, drafting agreements, how to share findings and maintaining working relationships. Whether you are looking for international industry or community connections, or maybe both, learn how to best prepare to embark on an emerging and a rewarding global research relationship.\n\nAttending this workshop you will learn the following:\n1. How to support global community/partner interest as a researcher\n2. How to begin developing or strengthening, new or existing partnerships and collaborations with global scholars and organizations\n3. Practical advice for bridging community/partner capacity-building and goals, with research goals and feasibility.\n4. Solutions to practical challenges of building International partnerships/collaborations.\n\nSpeakers:\n\nSamuel Dahan, MA, LLM, PhD\nDirector, Conflict Analytics Lab\nFounder, OpenJustice.ai\nAssociate Professor & National Scholar, Queen’s Law\nChair, Deel Lab\n\n\n\nRegistration: https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/BJ2VQ53 ( https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/BJ2VQ53 )\nZoom Information:\nZoom Link: https://yorku.zoom.us/j/97474788183\nMeeting ID: 974 7478 8183\nPasscode: 007845\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/connected-minds-workshop-how-to-build-and-maintain-international-partnerships-responsibly/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
