TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Connected Minds: Better Practices for Building and Maintaining Community Partnerships Responsibly
DESCRIPTION:Better Practices for Building and Maintaining Community Partnerships is a workshop led by Janet Jull focused on using shared decision-making tools and approaches to support person-centered care with a particular focus on health-care systems.\nThe workshop breaks down how to build new research partnerships and collaborations from initial contact, setting project milestones, drafting agreements, how to share findings and how to maintain working relationships. Whether you are looking for industry or community connections, or maybe both, learn how to best prepare to embark on an emerging and rewarding research relationship.\nAttending this workshop you will learn the following:\n\nHow to support community/partner interest as a researcher\nHow to begin developing or strengthening, new or existing partnerships and collaborations\nPractical advice for bridging community/partner capacity-building and goals, with research goals and feasibility.\nSolutions to practical challenges of building partnerships/collaborations.\n\nRegistration: https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/MZKGR5S ( https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/MZKGR5S )\nZoom Information: \nZoom Link: https://yorku.zoom.us/j/98288775924\nMeeting ID: 982 8877 5924\nPasscode: 179839\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/connected-minds-better-practices-for-building-and-maintaining-community-partnerships-responsibly/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
