SUMMARY:Experience Grad York | Social & Political Thought (MA, PhD)
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Social & Political Thought? We invite you to attend our program session!\nFounded in 1973, York’s Graduate Program in Social and Political Thought (SPTH) undertakes to encourage, develop and advance the analysis of social and political ideas with the aim of integrating intellectual interests common to the humanities and social sciences. The curriculum is structured around three areas of study: The History of Social and Political Thought; Black Studies and Theories of Race and Racism; Economy, Consciousness, Aesthetics, and Society. The program is ideal for self-directed students with diverse intellectual interests.\nRegistration is required. To RSVP or learn more, visit yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/no4fth6nTDSU3CH_lPPbkw ).\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs ( https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fa25-egy-spth/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought
END:VEVENT
