SUMMARY:Experience Grad York | Science & Technology Studies (MA, PhD)
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Science & Technology Studies? We invite you to attend our program session!\nWe are Canada’s largest first English STS graduate program in Canada, offering a PhD and a one-year MA program. Students in our program have an opportunity to work with interdisciplinary faculty whose research specialities include adaptive design, feminist technoscience, Indigenous and postcolonial STS, technoscientific capitalism, pandemics and epidemics, new genomics and pharmaceutical innovation, histories of experiments, ethics of artificial intelligence, Big Tech and the power of digital platforms, agnotology, public understanding of science, space exploration, and technological embodiments. We have spent the last three years revisioning and redesigning a new curriculum for the MA and PhD programs that focuses on improving student experience in light of changing student needs. A major new feature of the re-envisioned MA and PhD programs are the dynamic, experimental, and flexible Research Clusters that we have introduced. We have two Clusters running for the next three years: (1) Technoscientific Injustices; and (2) Bodies: Organic, Inorganic, Technological.\nRegistration is required. To RSVP or learn more, visit yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/6ORJ9i1xSTm0_7Rcpm6Kdw ).\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs ( https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fa25-egy-sts/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies
LOCATION:Online Zoom
