SUMMARY:Orientation to video production: From concept to final cut
DESCRIPTION:Have an idea that you want to bring to life but have no idea where to start? We can help you! This orientation guides you through the entire production process, from brainstorming your initial idea to creating a polished final product. In this session, we’ll demonstrate how to plan and organize your project, including writing a script, storyboarding, and understanding the roles involved in a production team. We’ll cover the basics of shooting and capturing sound before diving into the editing process where you’ll see how to cut, arrange, and refine your footage. Whether you’re creating a short film, promotional video, or documentary, this workshop will provide you with the essential skills to bring your creative vision to life.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/orientation-to-video-production-from-concept-to-final-cut-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Scott Library, 4700 Keele Street
END:VEVENT
