SUMMARY:Building AI Literacy: Helping Students Use Tools Thoughtfully and Transparently (ONLINE – September 25, 2025, 2:00-3:30)
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by Teaching Commons, this event will highlight the evolving landscape of AI literacy in higher education—what it is, why it matters, and how it intersects with student agency, academic integrity, and disciplinary expectations.\nRegistration for this workshop closes on Sept. 24 at noon.\nPlease register using the event registration form. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=1131758 )\nNote: this workshop counts toward the Teaching Commons’ Certificates in AI Pedagogy ( https://www.yorku.ca/teachingcommons/artificial-intelligence/#AICertificate ) and is part of the Practical Pedagogy theme.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/building-ai-literacy-helping-students-use-tools-thoughtfully-and-transparently-online-september-25-2025-200-330/
