TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Webinar for Grad Students: Fostering Black Scholar Scholarship Success Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate studies is excited to host the third annual Fostering Black Scholars Scholarship Success Workshop which aims to share new funding opportunities to support Black scholars and provide advice for how to leverage these supports. This workshop will feature speakers including seasoned Black faculty members and graduate scholars that hold prestigious awards, who will speak on their personal experiences and scholarship successes, and provide valuable insights on how to successfully navigate different funding opportunities as a Black scholar.\nDate: Thursday, August 28\nTime: 10:00am–12:00pm\nLocation: Online Zoom\nRegister\nShould you have any questions, please connect with our Research Officer, Nawroos Shibli at nshibli@yorku.ca ( mailto:nshibli@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fa25-fostering-black-scholar-scholarship-success-workshop/
