TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:A World Café: Conversations on Climate Change and Belonging
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever felt like the places that shaped you, whether nearby or far across the world, are changing? \nA World Café: Conversations on Climate Change and Belonging is a space to reflect, share, and connect through guided conversations about how environmental change impacts our sense of identity, memory, and the idea of home.\nTogether, we will explore how climate change affects our emotional lives and sense of belonging, while creating space for connection, community, and hope. Whether you are thinking about places like Sudan, the Philippines, the Caribbean, Bangladesh, Brazil, Syria, or right here in Toronto, your experiences are welcome. \nYou do not need to be an expert to join. This is a space for emotional honesty, shared reflection, and meaningful conversation. The session will be audio recorded to help us better understand how climate change affects people emotionally and culturally. \n \nFind us at Stong College, room 101\nHosted by: The Wellness Impact Lab at York University Open to students, faculty, staff, and community members.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/a-world-cafe-conversations-on-climate-change-and-belonging/
ORGANIZER;CN=Dahdaleh Institute for Global Health Research:MAILTO:dighr@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Calumet College,Faculties,Stong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning,Well-being
LOCATION:101 Stong College (MDR)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/1.png
