SUMMARY:Mature Student Orientation
DESCRIPTION:Resiliency, Resources & Reflection: Navigating University Life as a Mature Student\nJoin us on this transformative journey, where we empower you to thrive as a mature student! This orientation session focuses on learning about ACMAPS supports and services, building resilience and thriving strategies specifically tailored for mature students.\nLearning outcomes\n\nLearn Diana Brecher’s 5-factor model of resilience and how it contributes to flourishing as a mature student.\nDiscover various campus resources that support your well-being and academic success.\nExplore positive reflection techniques to enhance resilience and personal growth. Learn how to seamlessly integrate resilience and resources into your university life.\n\nIn-person session: Wednesday Aug. 20, 6 to 8 p.m.\nLocation: Vari Hall A\nRegistration begins at 5:30 p.m.\nRSVP for the session here: https://machform.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=386326 ( https://machform.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=386326 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mature-student-orientation/
