SUMMARY:How to be a Trans Ally in the Workplace & Classroom
DESCRIPTION:If you think you have never met a transgender person, think again. There are common misconceptions about trans people and how to be a trans ally. As hate rises in North America, transgender people are in more danger and in need of allies. \n \nJoin this workshop to learn how you can be a better trans ally in the workplace and the classroom.\n \nCreated for York U students and community members by Brian Ginther, Communications & Marketing Assistant (work-study Student) in the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/how-to-be-a-trans-ally-in-the-workplace-classroom/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Pride Month
LOCATION:140 HNES Building
