SUMMARY:National AccessAbility Week | Building your path: Post-secondary pathways to rewarding careers for students with disabilities
DESCRIPTION:\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nJoin us at National AccessAbility Week! This empowering week of panel discussions, networking opportunities and VR-powered soft skills workshops will prepare you to enter the working world with confidence. Learn how to advocate for your accessibility and inclusion in the workplace by building practical skills, meeting industry experts and connecting with potential employers.\nThis virtual webinar aims to provide post-secondary students with valuable insights to help you manage the school-to-work transition, plan and develop your careers and navigate the complex topics of workplace accommodations and disclosure. CCRW will also share data and insights highlighting intersectional considerations for post-secondary students with disabilities, emphasizing the need for tailored supports and resources.\nRegister for Building Your Path\n*All virtual National AccessAbility Week sessions will have ASL interpreters and closed captioning.\n \nFind more National AccessAbility Week events ( https://students.yorku.ca/accessibility/national-accessability-week ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/national-accessability-week-empowering-access-career-resource-fair-and-panel-discussion-334-597/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Accessibility Services:MAILTO:sasinfo@yorku.ca
