SUMMARY:Mitacs GRI Info Session: Faculty Call for 2026 (Zoom)
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in hosting a student for research during summer 2026?  York International and Mitacs will be hosting an information session to answer faculty members’ questions about the Mitacs GRI 2026 submission process and support provided for faculty members.\nZoom Registration: HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/dMC9ejdiTn-ZqW17dJRXJw )\nSpeakers:\n\nMs Rachel Sung, Mitacs Specialist, Innovation York, VPRI\nMs Ashley Laracy, Associate Director, Global Learning, York International\n\nAbout Mitacs: Mitacs Globalink Research Internship (GRI) is a competitive initiative for international undergraduates from the following countries and regions: Australia, Brazil, Chile, China, Colombia, France, Germany, Hong Kong, India, Mexico, Pakistan, South Korea, Taiwan, Tunisia, Ukraine, the United Kingdom and the United States. From May to October of each year, top-ranked applicants participate in a 12-week research internship under the supervision of Canadian university faculty members in a variety of academic disciplines, from science, engineering and mathematics to the humanities and social sciences. The GRI call for faculty project submissions for the summer of 2026 is now open. To submit your project, visithttps://www.mitacs.ca/our-programs/globalink-research-internship-professors/ ( https://www.mitacs.ca/our-programs/globalink-research-internship-professors/ ) . The deadline for submissions is June 5, 2025 at 1 p.m. PT.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mitacs-gri-info-session-faculty-call-for-2026-zoom/
CATEGORIES:International
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
