SUMMARY:Black Grad Celebration hosted by York University’s Black Alumni Network
DESCRIPTION:As a York alumni, we invite you and a guest to join us at our upcoming Black Grad Celebration. Celebrate with faculty, staff, graduates and allies, as we honour the Black-identifying graduates of the Class of 2025. Dress to impress and enjoy food, music and heartfelt words from York community members. We hope to see you there!\nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday, June 5\nTime: 6 – 8 p.m.\nLocation: Tribute Communities Recital Hall & CIBC Lobby | York University, 112 Accolade East Building, 83 York Blvd, Toronto, ON M3J 2S5\nAgenda\n5:45 p.m.: Doors open\n6:50 p.m.: Recognition ceremony begins\n7:30 p.m.: Dinner service\nAs the York University Black Alumni Network (YUBAN) celebrates the accomplishments of their grads, the group also acknowledges the work that remains to achieve equity. These events are being held in partnership with the Division of Advancement, Division of Students and Division of Equity, People and Culture.\nThese celebrations are complimentary to attend, but registration is required. For more information, please email Yasmine Mensah at mensahy@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-grad-celebration-hosted-by-york-universitys-black-alumni-network/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp; Culture,Students
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ Accolade East Building 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/blackgrad_event.jpg
END:VEVENT
