SUMMARY:16th Annual Muscle Health Awareness Day
DESCRIPTION:Each year Muscle Health Awareness Day (MHAD), hosted by York University, brings together doctors, scientists and trainees from across Canada and the United States. It aims to help advance understanding of the physiology and adaptation of muscles, vasculature and the heart during exercise and aging.\nSponsored by York’s Muscle Health Research Centre (funded by the Faculty of Health), the Office of the Vice-President, Research & Innovation, this year’s MHAD will once again feature several speakers and trainee presentations.\nView the full MHAD program outline ( https://www.yorku.ca/mhrc/wp-content/uploads/sites/236/2025/04/MHAD16-draft-program_April-21.pdf ) for further information.\nThis is the current list of confirmed distinguished invited speakers for this years’ event:\n\nDr. Susanna Mak, Associate Professor, University of Toronto, Cardiologist & Researcher, Sinai Health, Director, of the Anna Prosserman Heart Function Clinic and of the Harold & Esther Mecklinger and Posluns Family Cardiac Catheterization Research Laboratory at Mt. Sinai Hospital\nDr. Stephanie Tobin, Assistant Professor, Trent University\nDr. Olasunkanmi Adegoke, Associate Professor, MHRC, York University\nDr. Hanns Lochmuller, Clinician- Scientist, University of Ottawa, NMD4C Lead Investigator, Neurologist, Senior Scientist, Children’s Hospital of Eastern Ontario (CHEO) Research Institute, Schools of Neurology and Medicine, University of Ottawa\nDanielle Campo, Paralympian, Award Winning Speaker, Paralympic Gold Medalist, Resiliency Expert, National Hero Honour Recipient\nEmily Sutton, Post Doctoral Fellow, The Ottawa Hospital Research Institute\nDr. Chris McGlory, Assistant Professor, Queen’s University\nDr. Jenna Gillen, Assistant Professor, University of Toronto\n\nRegistration fee paid in advance via Eventbrite registration page ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/16th-annual-muscle-health-awareness-day-mhad16-tickets-1259986436349?aff=oddtdtcreator ): $30 for all attendees.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/16th-annual-muscle-health-awareness-day/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Health,Health Education &amp; Promotion,Research &amp; Innovation,Well-being
LOCATION:Life Sciences Building (LSB) Lobby
END:VEVENT
