SUMMARY:Building Blocks for Family Well-Being: A Multi-Family Parent Skills Group
DESCRIPTION:The York University Psychology Clinic is offering a new parent group!\nThis is a 6-week online program starting on April 29th for caregiving teams where the latest evidence from family science is used to help caregivers build on their ability to:\n\nRecognize family members unique needs and strengths\n\n\nHelp children regulate emotions & behaviours\n\n\nManage challenging sibling dynamics\n\n\nSupport one another and manage disagreements in your caregiving roles\n\n\nPinpoint the tools and practices that work for your family\n\nThis program is designed for families with children 16 years and under. It is suitable for many family circumstances:\n\nConcerns about child behaviour, emotions and/or mental health\nDifficulties managing the daily tensions of family life\nChallenges with family relationships or disagreements\n\nHosted by Dr. Madison Aitkens & Dr. Heather Prime\nThe cost is $250.00 for one person or $400 for caregiving pairs. There are spaces reserved at lower costs for those who would benefit from financial support.\nRegister HERE ( https://www.yorku.ca/health/yupc/wp-content/uploads/sites/441/2025/04/registration-form-Parent-Skills-Group-25.pdf )\nFlyer HERE ( https://www.yorku.ca/health/yupc/wp-content/uploads/sites/441/2025/04/Building-Blocks-for-Family-Well-Being.png )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/building-blocks-for-family-well-being-a-multi-family-parent-skills-group/
CATEGORIES:Faculty Affairs,Well-being
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Building-Blocks-for-Family-Well-Being-Flyer.png
END:VEVENT
