SUMMARY:WVB Pickleball for the Future
DESCRIPTION:\nWe invite you for our annual Pickleball for the Future event presented by York University Women’s Volleyball and our Women’s Volleyball Alumni Network. Funding raised directly supports the future of women’s volleyball student athletes, benefitting the Mosher Silver Women’s Volleyball Legacy Award.\n\n\n\nThis year we have two sections on for our event; a pickleball clinic and a pickleball tournament you can choose to enter one or both!\nDate: April 13\nLocation: Tait McKenzie Centre, Main Gymnasium (1 Thompson Rd., North York, ON)\nClinic Time: 9:30-11:30 a.m.\nTournament Time: 11:30 a.m. – 4:00 p.m.\nWho: Pickleball levels beginner to advanced (2.5-4.0 level)\nRegistration:\nClinic ONLY: $40\nTournament ONLY: $50\nBoth Clinic & Tournament $80\nDeadline to register is APRIL 6th!\n\nClinic: Join us and our Pickleball Pros (Anne Evans, Anette Happel, Marilyn Joostema and Fiona MacGregor) for a 2 hour clinic to improve your game or learn the game, regardless of level, you will advance your play!\nTournament: Our 2nd annual Pickleball for the Future! Join us in this round robin style tournament with raffle prizes, and prizes for our winners whether a single or you have a partner we will match you up and have a great day!\nREGISTER TODAY to win prizes, learn the game, connect with friends new and old and most importantly make an impact on the future of Lions women’s volleyball athletes!\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/wvb-pickleball-for-the-future/
