SUMMARY:YUBAN and BBBST Mentorship Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an inspiring and interactive information session to learn about the power of mentorship and ways to get involved with Big Brothers Big Sisters of Toronto (BBBST), in partnership with the York University Black Alumni Network (YUBAN).\nMake a lasting difference in a young person’s life and become an inspiration to others. BBBST has a particularly strong need for Big Brothers for Black boys in the GTA.\nDid you know that 60% of youth on BBBST’s mentorship waitlist identify as Black or Mixed Race? Hear firsthand from a Big Brother’s mentorship journey and get started on yours!\nDate: Thursday, April 24\nTime: 6-8 p.m.\nLocation: Alumni and Career Lounge in York Lanes on our Keele Campus (across from the bookstore).\nRegistration is required. Light refreshments will be served.\nWe hope to see you there!\nFor more information, contact Yasmine Mensah (BA ’20), Alumni Engagement Officer at mensahy@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/yuban-and-bbbst-mentorship-information-session/
