SUMMARY:Africa Is Not a Country Series(4th Edition)
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change at York University presents the seminar series: “Africa Is Not a Country’’\nThis series aims to address the absent, inadequate, skewed, and inaccurate representation of Africa and African issues in global discourse.\nJoin us for a thought-provoking conversation on how Africa navigates the complex terrain of intellectual property in a globalized world. Our panel will unpack the tensions between Western legal paradigms and African approaches to knowledge and innovation, highlighting strategies that both protect local creators and challenge dominant IP frameworks that often marginalize African contributions.\nFourth Seminar: ‘It Is My Work! Intellectual Property and Glocalization in Africa’\nDate and Time: Friday, April 4, 2025, 12:00 PM – 2:00 PM EDT\nSpeakers\nTeshager Dagne, PhD. – Associate Professor, York University\nFaith Majekolagbe, PhD. – Assistant Professor, University of Alberta\nDesmond O. Oriakhogba, PhD. – Associate Professor, University of the Western Cape\n How to Attend\nOnline: Register here: https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_2375MjpWSbmqNcWkivItmw\n \nFor more information and answers to questions, kindly email dasiedu@yorku.ca\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/africa-is-not-a-country-series4th-edition/
