SUMMARY:Teaching Kitchen – Fuel Your Brain with Food!
DESCRIPTION:Take a Study Break: Fuel Your Brain with Food!\nJoin us for an exciting and interactive Teaching Kitchen at Keele Campus, hosted by Food Services, in collaboration with Innov8 (C4 Capstone Team), and the French Association (AEFFY). This event is a unique opportunity for cultural exchange through food.\nYork U dietitian, Dahlia, will guide you in making delicious no-bake energy bites featuring maple syrup while sharing expert nutrition tips along the way. You’ll gain hands-on experience, enhance your nutrition knowledge, and immerse yourself in vibrant flavors. You’ll also learn about maple syrup and its cultural significance.\nWhether you’re a beginner or an experienced cook, this event is perfect for anyone looking to expand their culinary knowledge. Don’t miss this chance to learn, have fun, and connect with fellow food enthusiasts!\nMake sure to bring your own takeout container to take any leftovers with you!\nThis event is exclusively for York University Students.\nMark your calendars and register now. We can’t wait to see you there!\nDate: Wednesday April 2, 2025\nTime: 2:00PM – 3:00PM\nLocation: Ross South S166\n \nClick here to register now! ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/teaching-kitchen-fuel-your-brain-with-food-at-keele-campus-tickets-1299672408159?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n
