SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Is Race a Social Determinant of Health
DESCRIPTION:Join Sachil Singh, Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology and Health Science, Faculty of Health on April 9 as he discusses the dominant social and scholarly view that race is a social determinant of health. By offering a number of examples pertaining to the treatment of race in healthcare, this talk examines if this is indeed the case.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-is-race-a-social-determinant-of-health/
