SUMMARY:That wasn’t the deal: Immigration Policy Change in Canada and the US
DESCRIPTION:🌍 That Wasn’t the Deal: Immigration Policy Change in Canada and the US🗓️ Date: March 19th🕧 Time: 12:30 PM – 2:00 PM📍 Location: Online – Teams link ( https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_NmU2MDQ1ZGQtM2I2Yi00NmY3LTlmNDUtNmFiZDA3NTA3NzY1%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%2245f26ee5-f134-439e-bc93-e6c7e33d61c2%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%2222b025c6-f702-492e-90b5-e11419aba1ab%22%7d )\nJoin us for an engaging discussion on the evolving landscape of immigration policies in Canada and the US. Our panel of experts will explore how recent changes are reshaping migration patterns, impacting communities, and influencing political and social dynamics. Don’t miss this opportunity to gain valuable insights and engage in meaningful dialogue about the future of immigration.\n🖥️ Hosted by: Glendon School of International and Public Affairs (GSPIA) & Kennesaw State University (KSU)\n👉 Register now and be part of the conversation!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/that-wasnt-the-deal-immigration-policy-change-in-canada-and-the-us/
