SUMMARY:CAN-ACN Satellite Symposium: New Frontiers in Integrative Neuroscience
DESCRIPTION:Satellite theme: Although reductionist approaches have provided many scientific advances, a more wholistic, integrative approach is required to understand how a structure as complex as the brain provides cognition and behaviour. A challenge for researchers is that often such work does not fit neatly within traditional neuroscience disciplines. For this one-day symposium, we encourage abstracts and presentations from trainees whose research cuts across traditional neuroscience systems, levels and approaches, bridging both theoretical and experimental work.\nRegistration is free, limited to 100 attendees.\nCoffee breaks and lunch will be provided for presenters/registrants up to 100 attendees.\nAbstracts will be accepted until the program is full or April 1, whichever comes first.\nFor registration and more information visit: https://www.yorku.ca/research/cian/can-satellite/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/cian/can-satellite/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/can-acn-satellite-symposium-new-frontiers-in-integrative-neuroscience/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Integrative and Applied Neuroscience (CIAN):MAILTO:CIANadm@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Congress,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Science,Lassonde School of Engineering
LOCATION:Convention Centre, Second Student Centre @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/CAN-ACN-Satellite-events-5.png
END:VEVENT
