SUMMARY:Connected-EDI workshop: EDI as a Project Catalyst
DESCRIPTION:All researchers interested in learning more about how to run and engage in co-creation practices in research from the outset are invited to attend the event. While approaches may be different depending on your field, inspiration from best practices can come from anywhere and can be applied to future granting and funding opportunities!  \nLearn from our speakers, Leela Visawanthan, principal and founder of Viswali Consulting, and Vincent DePaul, lead of the EDI Committee at Connected Minds, as they outline the steps for positively engaging with communities to develop research questions. The information shared by both speakers provides tremendous insight into the nuances and benefits co-creation can have on your works’ impact.\nFrom exploring how to make initial connections, expanding recruitment processes and understanding how to support a community through research, this workshop will show you how to build research programs with community and end users from the beginning through relationship building.\nRegister today through SurveyMonkey and we look forward to seeing you on Zoom.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/connected-edi-workshop-edi-as-a-project-catalyst/
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp; Culture,Faculty Affairs,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,LA&amp;PS Addressing Anti-Black Racism,Lassonde School of Engineering,Markham Campus,Osgoode Hall Law School,Research &amp; Innovation,School of Continuing Studies,School of Medicine,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Schulich School of Business,Student Accessibility Services,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning
END:VEVENT
