SUMMARY:Publish and Flourish: Navigating Open Access and YorkSpace
DESCRIPTION:Join Research Commons for an in-depth exploration of open access publishing and how to effectively use YorkSpace, York’s institutional repository. This workshop, led by our library experts and experienced researchers, will clarify the various aspects of open access, author rights, journal publishing policies, and more. You will learn how to navigate these practices to understand their impact on your work’s visibility and accessibility. We’ll also discuss the various uses of YorkSpace to manage how your research is accessed, so you can make informed decisions about sharing your scholarly work. \n\nThursday, March 20, 2025 \n10:30 am – 12:00 pm \nZoom \nRegister here  \n\nSpeakers:  \n\nJohn Dupuis, Scholarly Publishing Librarian, Open Scholarship Department, Libraries  \nJack Leong, Digital Initiatives Librarian, Digital Scholarship Infrastructure Department, Libraries \nEnrico Moretto, Course Director, Department of History, Faculty of LA&PS \nJoshua Thienpont, Assistant Professor; Environmental Science Coordinator, Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change \n\nThis workshop will be recorded and saved in our archive. For a list of upcoming workshops, please find our program here.  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/publish-and-flourish-navigating-open-access-and-yorkspace/
ORGANIZER;CN=Research Commons:MAILTO:rescom@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculties
