SUMMARY:Taking Care of Your Brain: Study Strategies that Work
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Calumet & Stong Colleges\nThis workshop will introduce students to three study techniques that will promote academic and personal well-being.\nStudents will be introduced to the brain’s unconscious assistant (your own personal assistant) to better understand the myths of multitasking, how the Pomodoro technique can help you manage your time, and the importance of sleep. Students will learn how to study smarter, not harder. Throughout this interactive workshop, students will have an opportunity to reflect on their study habits and daily activities and create a schedule that will incorporate the strategies introduced. Light refreshments will be served. Hope to see you there!\nAudience: All York Community\nFormat: In-person\nLocation: In-Person at Stong College Room 101\nRegister Online\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/taking-care-of-your-brain-study-strategies-that-work/
