SUMMARY:York University Game Jam
DESCRIPTION:A game jam is typically a weekend-long event in which participants try to make a game from scratch. The goal of a jam is to come together and make a videogame, or a traditional game like a board game or card game.\nA jam asks participants to create a game from beginning to end in a prescribed time. The brief time span is meant to help encourage creative thinking which results in small but innovative and experimental games.\nThis game jam is part of The Save Play Series a series that celebrates and explores the preservation of video games.\nDates: March 14 – 16, 2025\nLocation: 102 and 103 Accolade West Building\nRegister HERE ( https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeInS9jrEOsDM4YDKUHOPdd9AEXKGmKq-VN8DT6t4JwyrDvOw/viewform )\nMore Information ( https://yorkugamejam.carrd.co/ )\nFULL SCHEDULE \nFRIDAY, MARCH 14\n5:00 – 6:00 p.m. – Check-In • Team Formation\n6:00 p.m. – Game Jam starts • Dinner\n12:00 a.m. – Ends \nSATURDAY, MARCH 15\n8:00 a.m. – Day 2 Begins\n9:00 – 10:00 a.m. – Breakfast\n12:00 a.m. – Ends \nSUNDAY, MARCH 16\n9:00 – 10:00 a.m. – Breakfast\n10:00 a.m. – Day 3 Begins\n5:00 p.m. – Game Jam Ends\n5:00 – 7:30 p.m. – Judging • Closing Ceremonies • Prizes\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-university-game-jam-2/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Transmedia Lab &amp; Art and Technology Learning Lab, 102 Accolade West Building and Transmedia Lab, 102 &amp; 103 Accolade West Building, York University @ 89 York Blvd. Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/gamejam.jpg
END:VEVENT
