SUMMARY:Let’s Talk About It: York University Libraries Authors Series
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Let’s Talk About It: York University Libraries Authors Series! Join us for an evening of insightful discussion and engaging conversation with the talented author, Robin Stevenson. We’ll be discussing the challenges her books have faced, and larger challenges that libraries are facing in today’s environment. Joining Robin will be Michelle Arbuckle, the Executive Director of the Ontario Library Association, and James Turk, the Director of the Centre for Free Expression. Salvy Trojman, Managing Director of Canada Commons & Trojman Corporation, will moderate the discussion.\n \nThis in-person event will take place on Friday, April 4, 2025, at 5:00pm at the Church of the Redeemer in downtown Toronto. Don’t miss this opportunity to connect with fellow book lovers and hear from some of the brightest literary minds. See you there!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/lets-talk-about-it-york-university-libraries-authors-series/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Libraries
