SUMMARY:Well-Being Week at Markham Campus
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Winter Well-Being Week on March 26 at York University Markham Campus! Stop by from 12 PM – 4 PM for interactive well-being activities on the 1st and 2nd floors. Engage in activities across different well-being domains, including Physical, Mental, Social, Spiritual and Cultural, Occupational, and Financial Well-Being.\nParticipate at least once in each well-being domain to collect stamps on your activity card and enter to win a gift basket prize. Pick up your activity card upon arrival and submit it at the designated area for your chance to win. Winners will be announced on our social media channels at a later date.\nWinter Well-Being Week: Embracing All Dimensions of Well-Being\nYork University is hosting Winter Well-Being Week from March 24 to 28! This year’s theme, Embracing All Dimensions of Well-Being, invites community members to participate in free events and activities highlighting York’s six well-being dimensions. Join us in fostering a healthier community as part of York’s commitment to the UN Sustainable Development Goal #3: Good Health & Well-Being.\nLearn more at: https://www.yorku.ca/well-being/well-being-week/winter-well-being-week/\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/well-being-week-at-markham-campus/
CATEGORIES:Markham Campus,Well-being Week
LOCATION:Markham Campus 1st Floor Atrium
END:VEVENT
