SUMMARY:Tubman’s Black History Month 2025: Community Organizing
DESCRIPTION:This event was originally scheduled for Thursday, Feb. 27th @12pm EST. It is now changed to Friday, Feb. 28th at 12pm to allow everyone more time to vote in the Ontario election on the 27th.\nJoin Us for the Final Panel in Tubman’s Black History Month Series!\nOn February 28, we conclude our Labour Movements and Organizing series with a powerful discussion on community advocacy, youth activism, and collective care. Our panelists will share insights on sustaining racial justice work, supporting young movement leaders, and navigating the challenges of organizing within Black communities.\nDate: Thursday, February 28, 2025Time: 12-2 PM ESTLocation: Nat Taylor Cinema (Room 102, Ross North, York University)Register Now:In-person: https://research.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=253495Online: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/gGeUeeNRQsyx4wfZcBnsLA\nPanelists:Xavier McLaughlin – Parents of Black ChildrenMischka Crichton – Toronto Caribbean CarnivalTatiana Ferguson – Black Queer Youth Collective\nModerators:Clifton Grant – Tubman Executive CommitteeSharon Henry – Tubman Executive Committee\nLet’s engage in critical conversations about labour, advocacy, and self-preservation. See you there!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tubmans-black-history-month-2025-community-organizing/
ORGANIZER;CN=The Harriet Tubman Institute:MAILTO:tubman@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Black History Month
LOCATION:(3rd flr York Lanes, Rm 314)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Feb-28-Community-Organizing-poster.png
END:VEVENT
