SUMMARY:INCLUSION WEEK: Fidget and Focus: Exploring Neurodiversity Through DIY Fidget Toys
DESCRIPTION:An interactive event where we discuss the importance of neurodiversity while creating personalized fidget toys. As we explore the different ways people think and process the world, we’ll make sensory tools that can help with focus, calm, and comfort. Join us for a fun and informative session where creativity meets mindfulness in support of neurodivergent individuals. This event will be in person.\nThis event is offered in partnership with The Centre for Sexual Violence Response, Support & Education.\nRegister here ( https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0DpTPsK46VJMnMLbdBlEa89UNEtSMkNQNUtQRk9GWldCQ08xUDJYNVBNVC4u&route=shorturl )\nFor a full list of Inclusion week events, please go to Inclusion Week 2025 – Centre for Human Rights, Equity and Inclusion ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-2025/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/inclusion-week-fidget-and-focus-exploring-neurodiversity-through-diy-fidget-toys/
ORGANIZER;CN=CHREI:MAILTO:chrwkshp@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,SDG Month
LOCATION:305 York Lanes
END:VEVENT
