SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | How to get into Finance and Banking Careers
DESCRIPTION:Join us for in-person and informal mentoring session at the Alumni & Career Lounge, York Lanes (opposite the Bookstore). This session will provide students with valuable insights into networking, building expertise in business and financial markets and key professional certifications to land a job.\nNote: Spaces are limited, RSVP today ( https://forms.office.com/r/X47P94u7da ).\nAlumni Mentors:\n\nMaliha Farhad (BA ’21, MA ‘22), Market Risk Analyst, TD Bank Group. Maliha graduated with a Bachelor of Economics, and followed up with her Masters in Economics from York University. She is a Market Risk Analyst at TD Bank Group. In her role, she’s responsible for monitoring stock market movements and its impact on margin accounts held by TD ultra high net worth clients.\n\nTinotenda Mutsvangwa (BA ’20, MSTM’21), Financial Advisor, CIBC. Tinotenda is a devoted CIBC Imperial Service Financial Advisor, holding both the (CSC) and (CPH) certifications. With a Bachelor’s degree in Political Science and a Master’s in Business Management from Schulich School of Business, Tino combines academic excellence with practical expertise to deliver exceptional financial solutions.\nLight food and refreshments will be provided.\n\nLearn more about the Mentor Circles Program and explore a wide range of sessions on various career fields and industries through engaging discussions with our experienced alumni.\nIf you have any questions about this event or Mentor Circles, please email Issa Abdi Jamaa, Alumni Engagement Officer at issajama@yorku.ca ( mailto:issajama@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-how-to-get-into-finance-and-banking-careers/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,International,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Department of Economics,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,Schulich School of Business
LOCATION:4700 Keele Street, York Lanes, 80 York Lanes Blvd., North York, ON, M3J 1P3
