SUMMARY:AI and the University: A Critical Conversation
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a panel discussion about the challenges associated with the rapid adoption of AI and the university’s role in addressing these challenges. Panelists from across York will discuss the environmental, ethical, and social impact of AI in a facilitated conversation, with time for questions at the end.\nPanelists:\n\nChris Cavanagh, Instructor and PhD candidate, Environmental Studies\nRegina Rini, Canada Research Chair in Social and Moral Cognition, Associate Professor, Philosophy\nsava saheli singh, Assistant Professor, Digital Futures in Education\n\nPlease use this link to register: Registration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/q4VwXzhjTdekSE8P4axypQ )\n
