SUMMARY:Sociology Annual Lecture – Marx’s Late Writings: Theories of Revolutionary Change and of Alternatives to Capitalism 
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Sociology welcomes distinguished guest lecturer and author, Kevin B. Anderson for this year’s annual lecture. \nJoin us on Wednesday, March 12, as Anderson discusses the findings from his new book, The Late Marx’s Revolutionary Roads, which analyzes the late writings of Marx covering topics such as Indigenous communism, gender and anti-colonialism as well as a broader perspective on a global, multilinear theory of modern society and its revolutionary possibilities. \nRegister here ( https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0CRCTrePSHhGuPfm6UO4H5pUQktSVklOU0wyRkxKMjdHOUVKSVhVSUFBTS4u&route=shorturl ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sociology-annual-lecture-marxs-late-writings-theories-of-revolutionary-change-and-of-alternatives-to-capitalism-2/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies
LOCATION:Harry Crowe Room @ 109 Atkinson Building
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
