SUMMARY:The Paradox of Accommodation in a Disabled and Disabling World
DESCRIPTION:Accommodating disability is vital to removing barriers in everyday life for disabled people/ people with disabilities. However, there are many paradoxes within the accommodation process including how disability is conceptualized, how systemic barriers are reinforced or dismantled, and how accommodation can bring about in/exclusion.  In this fireside chat, Enable York will host Marian McGregor and Roberto Lattanzio in conversation to explore the nuances, strengths, and flaws in our legal and policy frameworks that seek to uphold our right to disability accommodation.\nThis session is offered in partnership with Enable York.\nFor further information, visit the the Inclusion Week 2025 micro-site. ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-2025/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-paradox-of-accommodation-in-a-disabled-and-disabling-world/
