TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Devised Theatre Festival 2025
DESCRIPTION:ART NOW. ART THEN. ART FOREVER.\nYork University’s Devised Theatre class of 2025 is excited to present this year’s Devised Theatre Festival. The Festival consists of three different shows by three different companies consisting of students from the class, their crews, and the PM team.\nSHOWTIMES\nThe Forest Ends With You (Big Kids Theatre Company)\nThursday March 6 – 7:00 pm\nFriday, March 7 – 7:00 pm\nSaturday, March 8 – 1:00 pm | 7:30 pm\nSunday, March 9 – 2:00 pm\nLocation: Joseph G. Green Studio Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/joseph-g-green-studio-theatre/ )\n151 CFT (Centre for Film & Theatre)\nShow Description:\nSet in your childhood basement, The Forest Ends With You, is a magical-realist exploration of suburbia and its pressures on the young people who inhabit it. The show follows a group of teenage friends through the night after they find the dead body of their former classmate, Elliott. As pieces of the puzzle of his death come out of the woodwork, their favourite video game begins to come alive in a grotesque way. Implicating its audience in its mystical world of Markham, Ontario, The Forest Ends With You is a Y2K multimedia explosion of what it means to grow up in an environment that presses for conformity.\nContent Warnings:\nOur show, The Forest Ends With You, Contains mentions of death, animal death, violence, and mature subject matter. If anything bothers you at any point feel free to step out, there will be ushers there to support and assist you!\nTICKETS ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/devised-theatre-festival-2025-tickets-1244866933509?aff=oddtdtcreator ) ($5, $10 and $15) \n_________________________\nCandy Eyes (Sugar Rush Collective)\nTuesday, March 11 – 7:00 pm\nWednesday, March 12 – 7:00 pm\nThursday, March 13 – 7:00 pm\nFriday, March 14 – 7:30 pm\nSaturday, March 15 – 1:00 pm | 7:30 pm\nSunday, March 16 – 1:00 pm\nLocation: 207 Accolade East Building (ACE) ( https://maps.info.yorku.ca/2010/06/accolade-east/ )\n83 York Blvd\nShow Description:\nWhat does a star hide when she has nothing to lose?\nImmerse yourself into the story of Candy Eyes, the world-famous Hollywood starlet. By travelling to different rooms, representing different time periods and memories, you will piece together who this woman truly was in life. Was she a woman driven by passion for the arts? Did she abandon her family for stardom? What has she destroyed to keep her fame? The possibilities are open to you, but one thing is for certain: you will never see Candy Eyes the same way again.\nContent Warnings:\nOur show, Candy Eyes, contains depictions of period-typical misogyny and sexism, domestic abuse, homophobia, and death of family members. If you do not wish to participate or witness certain scenes, please feel free to step out and take care of yourself. If you need any help, please let one of our assistant stage managers know.\nTICKETS ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/devised-theatre-festival-2025-tickets-1244866933509?aff=oddtdtcreator ) ($5, $10 and $15) \n_________________________\nTake Me Out To The Ball Game (Rick Roy Productions)\nTuesday, March 11 – 8:20 pm\nWednesday, March 12 – 8:20 pm\nThursday, March 13 – 8:20 pm\nFriday, March 14 – 8:50 pm\nSaturday, March 15 – 8:50 pm\nLocation: 207 Accolade East Building (ACE) ( https://maps.info.yorku.ca/2010/06/accolade-east/ )\n83 York Blvd\nShow Description:\nAh, a good old-fashioned ball game on a beautiful mild August evening. Make sure you’re paying attention to what’s happening on the field though, this is one game you want to stay focused during. Don’t get too distracted by the hot dog vendors in the bleachers, one of them in particular has a way with words. He really needs someone to listen.\nContent Warnings:\nMentions of death and suicide, mentions and depictions of alcoholism and addiction, the use of profanity and loud noises in the space.\nTICKETS ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/devised-theatre-festival-2025-tickets-1244866933509?aff=oddtdtcreator ) ($5, $10 and $15) \n_________________________\nLOCATIONS \nJoseph G. Green Studio Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/joseph-g-green-studio-theatre/ )\n151 CFT (Centre for Film & Theatre)\nThis location features Big Kids Company presenting – The forest ends with you & Rick Roys Production presenting – Take me out to the ballgame\n207 Accolade East Building (ACE) ( https://maps.info.yorku.ca/2010/06/accolade-east/ )\n83 York Blvd\nThis location features Sugar Rush Collective presenting – Candy Eyes\nMORE INFORMATION\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/devised-theatre-festival-2025/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Accolade East Building (2nd Floor) @ 83 York Blvd
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/devised2025.jpg
END:VEVENT
