SUMMARY:From Distanced to Connected: COVID-19 Five-Years On
DESCRIPTION:March 11, 2025 marks the fifth anniversary of the World Health Organization‘s declaration of the COVID-19 pandemic. Join us on this day between 9am-6pm for a gallery that reflects on where we were, and where we have come since the start of the COVID-19 pandemic. Share your pictures for our Reflective Gallery of COVID-19 Lived Experiences, which will be on display all day on March 11, 2025 at York University, in the VPD ADERSIM lab. The gallery is open to the public and is a drop-in event with no registration required!\nFollowing the gallery, join us for a workshop from 6pm-9pm to reflect on the negative impacts of stigma during COVID-19, and to learn how to become a more informed, conscious and empathetic collective moving forward. We will hear first-hand experiences of the adverse impacts of stigma at the community level, and also get a glimpse into the lived reality of emergency management leaders within the Greater Toronto Area as they managed all aspects of the pandemic, from policy decisions regarding mask-wearing and social distancing, to testing and vaccine rollout.\nWorkshop Registration ( https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/covid19-stigma/#:~:text=Resilient%20Risk%20Consultant-,Workshop%20Registration,-From%20Distanced%20to )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/from-distanced-to-connected-covid-19-five-years-on/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Room N004 Schulich School of Business Building (Basement Floor)
