SUMMARY:Book Launch - Maraña: War and Disease in the Jungles of Colombia
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Tuesday, March 4 from 10 – 11:30 a.m. for the launch of LA&PS post-doctoral fellow, Lina Pinto-García’s new book, Maraña: War and Disease in the Jungles of Colombia, published by the University of Chicago Press. \nLina Pinto-García earned her MA (2014) and PhD (2020) from York’s science, technology & society (STS) program. Maraña is the final output of her PhD dissertation, offering a compelling exploration of the entangled relationship between war and disease in Colombia. This special event will be chaired by Denielle Elliott, with insightful commentary from Aryn Martin, Drew Belsky and Luis Van Isschot. \nIf you would like to get your copy of the book you can take advantage of a 30% pre-order discount at the University of Chicago Press website using Code UCPNEW. \nRegister here ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/launch-of-the-book-marana-war-and-disease-in-the-jungles-of-colombia-tickets-1224004613749?aff=oddtdtcreator ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-marana-war-and-disease-in-the-jungles-of-colombia/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies
LOCATION:(3rd flr York Lanes, Rm 314)
END:VEVENT
