SUMMARY:Grainger Canada – Information Session (On-Campus)
DESCRIPTION:Open to: \n-Schulich students- BBA year 2-4, MBA, Masters\n-York students- Undergrads year 2-4\nJoin Grainger Canada for an Exclusive Information Session on Internship Opportunities\nAre you looking for a rewarding internship where you can gain real-world experience, develop professional skills, and work with a company that values innovation, collaboration, and career growth? Join Grainger Canada’s Information Session to explore Summer 2025 internship opportunities in marketing, finance, supply chain, operations, and more!\nGrainger Canada is a leading business-to-business distributor of maintenance, repair, and operating supplies, helping businesses keep their operations running and their people safe. With a strong workplace culture recognized as Great Place to Work-Certified™, we are committed to fostering an inclusive, engaging, and supportive environment where team members feel valued and empowered.\n \n📅 Date: Feb 26th 2025\n🕦 Time: 11:30 AM – 1:00 PM\n📍 Location: X211, Seymour Schulich Building\n🥪 Lunch Provided\n⏳ Agenda:\n11:30 AM – 11:50 AM | Company Overview & Internship Opportunities\n11:50 AM – 1:00 PM | Open Networking with Grainger Team\n \nInternship Opportunities (May–August 2025 | Full-Time | Hybrid)\no    Marketing Analyst Intern – Assist in tradeshow planning, sales collateral management, and marketing initiatives to support brand visibility.\no    Finance Analyst Intern – Work with financial reporting, budgeting, sales performance analysis, and forecasting to drive business success.\no    Supplier Performance Analyst Intern – Ensure supplier compliance, manage purchase orders, and enhance supply chain efficiency.\no    Inventory Analyst Intern – Play a key role in inventory planning, process flow analysis, and continuous improvement projects to optimize product availability.\no    Operations Engineering Analyst Intern – Improve storage capacities, enhance warehouse efficiency, and implement automation solutions.\no    Field Operations Analyst Intern – Work with data analytics, reporting tools, and staffing models to improve operational performance.\no    Merchandising & Supplier Management Analyst Intern – Analyze product imports, supplier engagement, and assortment gaps for process improvements.\n \nThis is a great opportunity to network with Grainger professionals, ask questions, and learn how you can build your career with a company that has been a leader in its industry for over 100 years!\n \nINFO SESSION PREP RESOURCES:\n\nMeet with a CCD Advisor\nWatch the “Navigating the Networking Scene & Making a Great First Impression” video\n\nYORK STUDENTS REGISTER HERE: https://schulich.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_3qrntdnR0998G8K  ( https://schulich.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_3qrntdnR0998G8K )\nSCHULICH STUDENTS REGISTER ON HANDSHAKE: https://yorku.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1687408 ( https://yorku.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1687408 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grainger-canada-information-session-on-campus/
ORGANIZER;CN=Schulich School of Business:MAILTO:admissions@schulich.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Schulich School of Business
LOCATION:Executive Dining Room, ELC | Seymour Schulich Building, Keele Campus
END:VEVENT
