SUMMARY:Collaborative Research and Funding: All About Mitacs
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in collaborative research projects with industry and community partners? Join us to learn all about Mitacs grant opportunities ( https://www.mitacs.ca/ ), which fund projects across all disciplines and connect researchers with businesses, non-for-profits, municipalities, and hospitals. York’s Mitacs expert will provide an overview of the program, discuss recent changes that have been made, and review examples of successful applications. You will also have a chance to hear from fellow researchers who have benefitted from Mitacs funding.\nSpeakers: \n\nRachel Sung, Mitacs Specialist, Innovation York, VPRI\nSatinder Brar, Professor, James and Joanne Love Chair in Environmental Engineering, Department of Civil Engineering, Lassonde School of Engineering\nJanine Marchessault, Professor, Department of Cinema & Media Arts, School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design\n\nThis workshop will be recorded and saved in our archive ( https://www.yorku.ca/researchcommons/events/archived/ ). For a list of upcoming workshops, please find our program here ( https://www.yorku.ca/researchcommons/program/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/collaborative-research-and-funding-all-about-mitacs/
