SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub | Caring Under Constraints: Social workers’ identity at the crossroads of compliance and rebellion
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Unionville Library on March 26 at 7 p.m. for a special in-person Scholars’ Hub presentation with Farshid Shams, Associate Professor of Strategy and Organization Studies, Faculty of Liberal Arts and Professional Studies. Professor Shams will draw on a recent study examining the routine activities of social workers in an Ontario-based mental health and addiction counselling organization and explore how these frontline practitioners make sense of who they are as they navigate restrictive organizational requirements while striving to maintain their professional autonomy.\n
