SUMMARY:Online Workshop: Developing Effective Supervision Strategies
DESCRIPTION:Online Workshop: Developing Effective Supervision Strategies: Staying Well and Fostering Excellence with Professor Dr. Michele Jacobsen, Werklund School of Education, The University of Calgary\nMichele Jacobsen is a distinguished researcher and educator specializing in design for learning, technology integration, and innovative teaching in higher education.\nWhether you are a seasoned supervisor or new to the role, this online webinar offers practical strategies and evidence-based insights to enhance your approach, support student success, and cultivate a culture of well-being in academia.\nThe online workshop draws on data shared by Canadian supervisors about their experiences being supervised and learning how to be a good supervisor on the job.\nDate: Tuesday, March 4th, 2025\nTime: 2:00pm-3:15pm EST\nLocation: via Zoom online\nRegistration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_moLhAuq3TJO-3ukU7aOI0g#/registration ) (click link)\nFor more information reach out to Tracy Bhoola, Program Manager of the Graduate Supervision Support Hub tbhoola@yorku.ca ( mailto:tbhoola@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/online-workshop-developing-effective-supervision-strategies/
