TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:City of Toronto Green Jobs Hackathon: Shape Toronto’s Future!
DESCRIPTION:Green Jobs Hackathon: Shape Toronto’s Future!\nThe City of Toronto has set an ambitious goal to achieve net zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2040 through their TransformTO Net Zero Strategy. To make this vision a reality, Toronto needs passionate and creative thinkers like YOU to help tackle an urgent challenge:\nThe Challenge:\nToronto is forecasting a talent shortage in the green jobs sector. How can we attract more students to pursue careers in these fast-growing, game-changing fields?\nWhen: Wednesday, Feb. 19, 2025, from 10:00 am – 4:15 pm\nWhere: Career Centre Presentation Room, Rm. 103 McLaughlin College\nWhy You Should Join:\n\nDive into a real-world challenge that impacts Toronto’s future.\nCollaborate with like-minded students and meet new friends.\nGain insights and network with City of Toronto representatives.\nShowcase your ideas and compete for exciting cash prizes!\nEnjoy a free lunch and an unforgettable experience.\n\nWhether you’re a hackathon pro or a first-timer, this is your chance to make a difference. Let’s create a greener, brighter Toronto-together!\nTo register and for more information, please visit https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4635\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/city-of-toronto-green-jobs-hackathon-shape-torontos-future/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
LOCATION:103 McLaughlin College
END:VEVENT
