SUMMARY:The Harriet Tubman Institute’s Black History Month 2025: Racial Justice and Labour
DESCRIPTION:Date: February 13, 2025\nTime: 12-2pm EST\nLocation: Nat Taylor Cinema (Room 102, Ross North bldg., 4700 Keele Street, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3)\nIn-person registration: https://research.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=252717 ( https://research.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=252717 )\nOnline registration: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/hRGIOj4wTdCeXEloC-qj7Q ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/hRGIOj4wTdCeXEloC-qj7Q )\nEvent Overview\nHow do labour movements advance racial justice, and how can workers, unions, and advocates create more equitable workplaces for Black and racialized workers? This panel discussion will explore the ongoing struggles and successes of labour organizing in the fight for racial justice.\nBringing together labour leaders and advocates, this conversation will highlight key examples of successful policy changes, legislative efforts, and workplace reforms that serve as models for future action. Panelists will also discuss the importance of cross-sector solidarity, particularly in supporting migrants, gender-diverse workers, and other marginalized communities who are at heightened risk of workplace discrimination and exploitation.\nIn addition, the discussion will address the personal cost of this work, reflecting on how Black labour organizers and advocates prioritize self-preservation while fighting for systemic change.\nPanelists\n\nLisa Skeete (CUPE 4400)\nTiana Reid (YUFA)\nUsha Viswanathan (YUFA & Glendon’s Race Equity Caucus – CERREC)\nCrystal Garvey (OPSEU)\nPatrick Teed (CUPE 3903)\n\nModerator: Bianca Beauchemin (Executive Committee Member, The Harriet Tubman Institute)\nThis event is part of the Harriet Tubman Institute’s Black History Month 2025: Labour Movements & Organizing series. Open to students, faculty, community members, and the public, this panel offers a critical space to reflect on the connections between racial justice and labour activism. Join us for a thought-provoking discussion on the future of equitable work environments and the power of collective organizing.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-harriet-tubman-institutes-black-history-month-2025-racial-justice-and-labour/
ORGANIZER;CN=The Harriet Tubman Institute:MAILTO:tubman@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Black History Month
LOCATION:Nat Taylor Cinema (Ross North 102) York University @ 4700 Keele St
END:VEVENT
