TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Level Up | Law school: Tips on how to get accepted and succeed
DESCRIPTION:Thinking about going to law school or studying for the Law School Admissions Test (LSAT)? Hear from two York alumni who have recently graduated from law school and are now successful lawyers working in the Toronto area.\nLearn about:\n• Tips for navigating law school admissions\n• What law school is really like, including highs and lows of being a law school student\n• Advice on securing an articling placement\n• The value of mentorship and networking\n• Realities of working as an early career associate\nFeatured alumni speakers:\n\nSam Dobbin, JD ’22, Associate, Osler, Hoskin & Harcourt LLP\nElnaz Nejadabbasi, BA ’18, Real Estate and Corporate Lawyer, Hummingbird Lawyers LLP\n\nThe discussion will be followed by an opportunity for the audience to ask questions.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/level-up-law-school-tips-on-how-to-get-accepted-and-succeed/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/levelupoct8_ebanner_1200.png
END:VEVENT
