TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Black and Bold: Education, Empowerment, and Excellence
DESCRIPTION:Founders College, LA&PS and Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) will be hosting its Black and Bold event under the theme “Education, Empowerment & Excellence” as we explore the evolution of education throughout the years and the Black experiences in the education system. How has education evolved? How has Black peoples’ access to education changed? What will future access to education look like? How can education foster Black excellence and empowerment? Is education inclusive enough? These are some of the questions we will explore as we connect the past, present and future.\nRegister here ( https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0AqCHG88_PJLgjxun3I3p05UQjlMMlZORlZTREczWjk2S1NRRktCSUFWVy4u ) to reserve your spot.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-and-bold-education-empowerment-and-excellence/
ORGANIZER;CN=Black Excellence at York University:MAILTO:beyu@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,BE-YU,Bethune College,Black History Month,Calumet College,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Colleges,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,Graduate Program in Political Science,International,LA&amp;PS Advancement,Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,Libraries,Markham Campus,Osgoode Hall Law School,School of Continuing Studies,School of Medicine,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Schulich School of Business,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre
LOCATION:305 Founders College @ 4700 Keele St
