SUMMARY:Experience Grad York: Biotechnology (Graduate Diploma) Biotechnology Management (MBM)
DESCRIPTION:The Master’s in Biotechnology Management focuses on how modern biotechnology management is performed and surveys the scientific, ethical, and societal contexts. The program is designed to appeal to students who hold a Bachelor of Science degree in Biology, Biological Sciences, Biotechnology, Life Science, or a related discipline, and have little to no work experience in Biotechnology.\nThe Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology addresses an unfilled need in the Canadian Biotechnology Industry. Recently, enormous stress has been put on Canadian society, and the biotechnology industry has been leaned on heavily to bring forward high-value strategies and pharmaceutical options with many job openings remaining unfilled. The Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology is designed to increase the available pool of trained talent for the biotechnology industry and to strengthen the biotechnology ecosystem.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy.\nLearn more about our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/experience-grad-york-biotechnology-graduate-diploma-biotechnology-management-mbm/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Markham Campus
LOCATION:Online Zoom
