SUMMARY:8th Annual Book Celebration – Department of Social Science
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Social Science invites you to join us for our 8th Annual Book Celebration! This will be an informal, social meet-up with drinks and light food. We are very excited to celebrate our colleagues’ achievements and prolific production.\nDate: Thursday, February 6th, 2025\nTime: 1 p.m.\nLocation: 752 Resource Room, Ross Building South\nThis year’s celebration features the following new publications:\n\nNaked Fieldnotes: A Rough Guide to Ethnographic Writing, Edited by Denielle Elliott & Matthew J. Wolf-Meyer\nFaith in Rights: Christian-Inspired NGOs at Work in the United Nations by Amélie Barras\nThe Planning Moment: Colonial and Postcolonial Histories, Edited by Sarah Blacker, Emily Brownell, Anindita Nag, Martina Schlünder, Sarah Van Burden & Helen Verran\nLaw, Humans and Plants in the Andes-Amazon: The Lawless of Life by Iván Darío Vargas Roncancio\n\nWe look forward to seeing you there!\nThe Research and Communications Committee,\nDepartment of Social Science\nFaculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/8th-annual-book-celebration-department-of-social-science-2/
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/8th-Annual-Book-Celebration-Poster-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
