SUMMARY:OMNI-RÉUNIS Super Spreader Seminar Series
DESCRIPTION:OMNI-RÉUNIS Super Spreader Seminar Series first installment for 2025 is here!\nThis time, Dr. Gelan Ayana presents his research on “Community-based approach to one-health: AI for community-based early detection of zoonotic diseases.” We look forward to your attendance on:\n📆Thursday, January 30 from\n⏰10:30 to 11:30 a.m.\nIf you’re at York University’s Keele Campus, we invite you to join us at our lab located at the Petrie Science & Engineering Building (PSE), Room 018, 140 Campus Walk  REGISTER HERE ( https://tinyurl.com/7yfd4md7 ), and feel free to share this invitation with your colleagues, networks and other researchers.\nShould you have any questions, please contact Nolan Holder, OMNI-RÉUNIS Program Manager, at nholder@yorku.ca.\n
