TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:The Goldfarb Gallery × Jane Street Speaks February Showcase
DESCRIPTION:For our February Showcase, we join forces with Jane Street Speaks to present an all-star lineup of emerging rappers, singers, and spoken word poets from the Jane Finch community. Hosted by Jane Street Speaks founder, Nathan Baya, with musical sets by DJ EnzoMezu (formerly known as Kappa Mezu), this event features performances by hip hop artists Cocanina and S!shaalong with spoken word poetry by Faduma Mohamed. This program reflects The Goldfarb Gallery and Jane Street Speaks’ joint commitment to spotlighting the talents and achievements of up-and-coming artists from the Jane Finch neighbourhood. This event also includes an open mic, giving emerging artists a platform to share their work, enabling them to build and cultivate new audiences.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-goldfarb-gallery-x-jane-street-speaks-february-showcase/
CATEGORIES:Equity, People &amp; Culture,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp;PS Addressing Anti-Black Racism,LA&amp;PS Community Hub,Students
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Nathan-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
