SUMMARY:Black Histories Wikipedia Edit-a-thon
DESCRIPTION:Representation matters. Not just on screens and pages, but in the information and data we share. Join us in the Library Collaboratory to celebrate Black History Month by learning to edit Wikipedia. Anyone can make a difference by helping to improve coverage of Black histories online.\nLearn to edit Wikipedia pages if you have never before or join for the community if you are a more experiend editor. Optional training will be provided. This event is a drop-in event.\nThis event is part of a larger series organized by library and archives staff and students at Toronto Metropolitan University, Toronto Public Library, University of Toronto and York University. Check the Black Histories Editathon webpage ( https://bhetoronto.my.canva.site/ ) to find out about more events happening in the month of February.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-histories-wikipedia-edit-a-thon/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Black History Month,Libraries
LOCATION:Scott Library, 4700 Keele Street
