SUMMARY:Sketching in the Third Dimension: VR Storyboarding with Gravity Sketch
DESCRIPTION:Virtual information worlds can be used to create engaging multisensory experiences. Join this workshop to learn how to prototype your own three-dimensional world in virtual reality using the 3D design platform Gravity Sketch and a Meta Quest headset in ways that engage spatial thinking. Explore how the libraries’ collections can be used to inspire virtual space design. Once finished, turn your prototype into a storyboard that communicates the experience. Good experiences do more than just put us in a space; they enhance our awareness of that space and the implications of our presence in it.\n \nBy the end of this workshop, you will be able to:\n\nExplain why spatial thinking matters and how it is engaged in virtual environments.\nCreate a 3D prototype of a virtual world using Gravity Sketch.\nUse the library’s visual collections to inspire 3D space design.\nApply a workflow to reformat your prototype into a storyboard.\nRecognize the library support available (equipment, training, collections, resources) for creating a virtual reality project.\n\n \nNote: This is an interactive workshop where participants will engage in hands-on collaborative activities using a VR headset. Space is limited. Sign up early to reserve your spot.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sketching-in-the-third-dimension-vr-storyboarding-with-gravity-sketch/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Scott Library, 4700 Keele Street
END:VEVENT
