SUMMARY:Indigenous Resources and Citations
DESCRIPTION:Researching Indigenous topics is undeniably complex. Identifying authentic Indigenous voices among numerous colonial narratives can be a daunting task, and processing this material can take an emotional toll. By learning how to navigate these resources thoughtfully, you can respectfully and ethically incorporate Indigenous knowledge into your assignments and research.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-resources-and-citations-2/
