SUMMARY:Ritual of Reuse: Reimagining Game Controller Lifecycles for Life-Centered Futures Workshop
DESCRIPTION:We use gaming controllers almost every day, but the environmental and social impacts of their life-cycle are often ignored. From material extraction to labour exploitation, internet pollution, and discarded e-waste, the consequences of gaming controllers are deep-rooted and felt universally by humans, non-humans, and ecosystems. Using a Life-Centred lens, this participatory design workshop incorporates an immersive role-playing game with a burial ritual for deceased technology, and provides an opportunity to collectively take apart and recycle our gaming controllers while contributing to a more sustainable future. The workshop is hosted by Thalia Godbout, Laurel Green, Rachel Remesat, and Omar Shabbar.\nDate: Friday, March 14, 2025\nTime: 1:00 – 4:00 p.m.\nLocation: Transmedia Lab, 103 ACW (Accolade West Building)\nFree: Register HERE ( https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScdchEgU6u5L5_5nrUe2jc3eA3k4ec1msGWblNaGlDdz9qj0A/viewform )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ritual-of-reuse-reimagining-game-controller-lifecycles-for-life-centered-futures-workshop/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Transmedia Lab, 103 Accolade West Building, York University @ 89 York Blvd, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/ritualofreuse.jpg
END:VEVENT
