SUMMARY:Black Talk Real Talk – Markham Campus
DESCRIPTION:This event will be hosted by York Universities’ Black Excellence team. The purpose of this event is to celebrate and highlight the diverse African diasporic languages that have deeply influenced Western subcultures. Through highlighting the rich linguistic heritage and its impact on music, fashion, art, and everyday language, we aim to foster a greater understanding of how African diasporic communities have shaped global cultural landscapes.\nHow do I register through Experience York?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Career Centre” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nSelect “Workshops & Webinars”\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\nEvent Link: https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4620\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-talk-real-talk-markham-campus/
CATEGORIES:Black History Month,Markham Campus
LOCATION:Markham Campus Room 2050
