SUMMARY:The Gathering of Green: Nurturing Resilence Through Love, Care & Justice
DESCRIPTION:The Gathering of Green Threads: Nurturing Resilience Through Love, Care, & Justice\nJoin us for a two-day care conference aimed at building resilience within racialized communities through loving and caring practices. Hosted by Many Green Hands, this event will feature yoga, arts and crafts, music, journaling, workshops on love and care, and a special conversation with Professor Ola Mohammed.\n📅 Dates:\n\nJanuary 24th (3:00 PM): Collective Day (Open to All)\nJanuary 25th (12:00 PM): Dedicated to Women, Femme, and Trans Folks\n\n📍 Location: HNES 140, 141, 142, and the Student Lounge\nThis safe and nurturing space centers QTBIPOC lived experiences and supports racialized youth in fostering collective liberation and self-care. Don’t miss this opportunity to connect, heal, and grow!\n💚 Free Admission | All are Welcome!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-gathering-of-green-nurturing-resilence-through-love-care-justice/
ORGANIZER;CN=Many Green Hands at York University:MAILTO:manygreenhandsyu@gmail.com
