SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | Breaking into Accounting Careers
DESCRIPTION:Join us for in-person and informal mentoring session at the Alumni & Career Lounge, York Lanes (opposite the Bookstore). This session we will discuss navigating accounting and CPA pathways, interview prep and networking tips to land a job in accounting firms.\nAlumni Mentors:\n\n\n\nJamie Herman (Bcom ’08), Partner, Fruitman Kates LLP\nMeharleen Gaudh (BCom ’21), Senior Consultant, Real Estate Tax, KPMG\n\n\n\nNote: Spaces are limited, RSVP today ( https://forms.office.com/r/X47P94u7da ).\nEvent Details:\nDate: Tuesday, Jan. 28\nTime: 5:30 p.m. – 7 p.m.\nLocation: Alumni & Career Lounge, York Lanes (opposite the Bookstore)\nLight food and refreshments will be provided.\n\nLearn more about the Mentor Circles Program and explore a wide range of sessions on various career fields and industries through engaging discussions with our experienced alumni.\nIf you have any questions about this event or Mentor Circles, please email Issa Abdi Jamaa, Alumni Engagement Officer at issajama@yorku.ca ( mailto:issajama@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-breaking-into-accounting-careers/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,Students
LOCATION:4700 Keele Street, York Lanes, 80 York Lanes Blvd., North York, ON, M3J 1P3
