SUMMARY:Globally Networked Learning (GNL) Virtual Info Sessions
DESCRIPTION:The GNL info sessions are open to all York faculty members and staff who are interested in innovative pedagogies that combine internationalization, experiential education, and co-teaching a course with an international partner.\nPlease note this is a virtual Zoom meeting and registration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/76XYDx0RRcui18TTy_HJZA#/registration ) is required. Please visit our website ( https://yorkinternational.yorku.ca/gnl/ ) for more information.\nIn this session, we will cover:\n\nWhat and why GNL\nGNL examples by York course leaders \nPedagogy of GNL or Collaborative Online Intercultural Learning (COIL),\nHow-to break-out rooms: addressing participants’ GNL course design and Qs&As\nGNL Award $1000 to support piloting your GNL initiatives  ( https://yorkinternational.yorku.ca/gnl/ )\n\n
