SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | How to Succeed in Medical School Admissions
DESCRIPTION:Join us for in-person and informal mentoring session at the Alumni & Career Lounge, York Lanes (opposite the Bookstore).\nAlumni Mentors: \n\nAreeba Chaudhary (BSc ’23), MD candidate at Temerty Faculty of Medicine – University of Toronto\nMohamed Elghobashy (BSc ’23), MD candidate at Temerty Faculty of Medicine – University of Toronto\n\nFocus of this Mentor Circles session: Crafting a strong application for medical school admission, interview techniques, and MCAT strategies.\nRegister now ( https://forms.office.com/r/X47P94u7da ) as SPACED ARE LIMITED!\nLight food and refreshments will be provided.\nThe Mentor Circles Program at York University connects students with experienced alumni to discuss career-related interests, industries, and experiences. These informal mentoring sessions provide valuable insights and networking opportunities, empowering students to navigate their academic and career paths while developing leadership and interpersonal skills. Please visit HERE ( https://www.yorku.ca/alumniandfriends/mentor-circles/ ) to explore a wide range of Mentor Circles sessions on various career fields and industries through engaging discussions with our experienced alumni.\nIf you have any questions about this event or Mentor Circles, please email Issa Abdi Jamaa, Alumni Engagement Officer at issajama@yorku.ca ( mailto:issajama@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-how-to-succeed-in-medical-school-admissions/
ORGANIZER;CN=Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumnievents@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Health,Faculty of Science,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies
LOCATION:4700 Keele Street, York Lanes, 80 York Lanes Blvd., North York, ON, M3J 1P3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Mentor-Circles-1.png
END:VEVENT
