SUMMARY:Mass Vaccination Challenges: Lessons from Canadian First Nations and Remote Communities Symposium
DESCRIPTION:CIFAL York, Y-EMERGE, ADERSIM, and Mathematics for Public Health, Fields Institute are very pleased to host the first Vaccine for First Nations and Remote Communities Symposium.\nThe Symposium aims to address the unique challenges and lessons learned surrounding mass vaccination in First Nations and remote communities. Considering unique conditions of these communities, mass vaccination had its unique challenges and successes.\nThis symposium is a knowledge sharing, capacity building, and networking event that brings together healthcare professionals, community leaders, policymakers, and researchers to discuss strategies for improving mass vaccination policy, planning, and practice. Through collaboration and shared insights, we seek to build a more resilient healthcare framework that meets the specific needs of First Nations and remote communities in Canada.\nMore Information: https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/vaccine-symposium/\nRegistration: https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/vaccine-symposium-registration/\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mass-vaccination-challenges-lessons-from-canadian-first-nations-and-remote-communities-symposium/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Online at Zoom Webinar: Register for the link at: www.yorku.ca/research/yemerge/lectures
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/MassVaccinationPoster1-scaled.jpg
