SUMMARY:World Music Festival 2025
DESCRIPTION:York University’s World Music Festival is a cross-cultural celebration spotlighting musical traditions around the world.\nProduced by Professor Mike Cadó ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/mike-cado/ ) this global sonic tour presents a sampling of several international cultures represented in York’s world music program.\nThe festival packs two concerts into one day – Thursday, March 13, 2025\nMaps and Directions ( http://maps.info.yorku.ca/keele-campus/ )\nTHURSDAY, MARCH 13\n12:30 p.m. – West African Drumming (Ghana) – Kwasi Dunyo and Larry Graves, Ensemble Director\n7:30 p.m. – Balkan Ensemble, Irene Markoff ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/irene-markoff/ ), Ensembe Director\nLOCATION: Tribute Communities Recital Hall  ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ )\nFREE ADMISSION\n
