SUMMARY:Mountains beyond Mountains: the challenges for non-state actors to contribute to climate governance
DESCRIPTION:\nThis hybrid panel will explore issues surrounding the role of non-state actors in the fight against climate change. The movement from state-centred regulation towards transnational regulatory models that transcend national borders forces us to de-construct and re-construct our understandings of the role of the state versus those outside the state such as corporations and NGOs.\nModerator and Panelists:\nHassan Ahmad, assistant professor, Osgoode Hall Law School\nBarnali Choudhury, professor, Osgoode Hall Law School & Director, Jack and Mae Nathanson Centre on Transnational Human Rights, Crime and Security\nKonstantia Koutouki, professor, Université de Montréal\nBenjamin Richardson, professor, University of Tasmania\nVanisha Sukdeo, assistant professor, Queen’s University\n\nREGISTER ( https://machformext.osgoode.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=407128 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mountains-beyond-mountains-the-challenges-for-non-state-actors-to-contribute-to-climate-governance/
CATEGORIES:Osgoode Hall Law School
LOCATION:Faculty Common Room - 2027, Osgoode Hall Law School @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
