SUMMARY:KPMG Women in Deals Conference 2025
DESCRIPTION:Our KPMG GTA team is thrilled to invite your students to apply to our upcoming Women in Deals Conference!\nThis in-person conference offers a unique opportunity for students to gain valuable insights from accomplished women in KPMG’s Deal Advisory practice, as well as participate in engaging discussions, informative sessions, and industry networking.\nPlease note that this event is specifically designed for candidates who self-identify as Women and are in their 2nd to 4th year of study within an undergraduate or masters program at an accredited Canadian educational institution.\nWe would really appreciate your support in posting this opportunity with your career center. I have attached a copy of the posting for your reference as well as a poster you can share.\nPlease see conference details below:\nDate: Friday, February 28th, 2025\nTime: 10:00AM – 6:00PM EST\nLocation: Downtown Toronto (exact address to be shared with invited attendees)\nDress code: Business Casual\nTarget audience: Candidates who self-identify as Women and are in their 2nd – 4th  year of study within an undergraduate or masters program at an accredited Canadian educational institution.\nThe application deadline is Sunday January 19th at 11:59 PM EST.\nThe posting is now LIVE and all applications must include a video submission, cover letter, resume and an electronic copy of their most recent transcript. Further details on the video submission can be found on the posting.\nHow do I register?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Employer Events” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/kpmg-women-in-deals-conference-2025/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
