SUMMARY:BMO Resume and Interview Tips
DESCRIPTION:In preparation for our 2025-2026 recruitment season, and to help better support your learning and growth, we are offering a series of virtual sessions led by our BMO Capital Markets Canadian Campus Recruitment Team. Business representatives will be present.\nThis is the fourth of four virtual sessions.\n \nResume and Interview Tips for CM Campus\n\nDate: Friday January 31, 2025\nTime: 12:00PM – 12:45PM ET\nDuring this virtual session, we’ll provide you general Resume and Interview Tips to prepare you for applying to our roles. We will also share a brief overview of CM Campus Programs, our recruitment timelines, process, and eligibility requirements. You will then get a chance to ask any questions you have.\nEvent Eligibility\n· You are a student at an accredited Canadian University, currently enrolled in an undergraduate program with a graduation date of December 2026 and onwards,\n· A proven record of academic excellence and\n· A demonstrated interest in finance\nThis session will be 45 minutes in length. Please come prepared with your questions.\n\nHow do I register?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Employer Events” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/bmo-resume-and-interview-tips/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
