TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:York Dances 2025: Fragments of Existence
DESCRIPTION:York Dances 2025: Fragments of Existence features the new choreographic works of 29 third year BFA majors performed by students engaged in all levels of York’s programs in Dance. Contradiction is in the zeitgeist and these emerging artists are exploring incongruity in a multitude of ways. Their compelling questions are palpable in the devising of dances ranging from expressive solos to vibrant large ensemble works. These creators are engaged in processes stemming from various conceptual underpinnings including the loss of potential, liberation, morphing/awakening, burnout, and what lies beyond the box. In addition to conducting their own creative processes, the students lead every facet of the production of York Dances, supported by faculty at every level of creation, performance, and production.\nArtistic Director and 3rd year Choreography Course Director: Tracey Norman\nWork/Study Team: Sanvi Chugh, Alyssa Levac, Hana Yeung (Pui Wan, Yeung )\nYork Dances: Fragments of Existence\nSeries A: Shattered – Thursday, March 27 & Friday, March 28 at 7:00 pm\nfeatures 14 new choreographic works by third year BFA dance students.\nSeries B: Subsistence – Thursday, March 27 & Fri, March 28 at 8:30pm\nfeatures 15 new choreographic works by third year BFA dance students.\nLOCATION: McLean Performance Studio ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/mclean-performance-studio/ ) (244 Accolade East Building)\nTICKETS: Advance (until March 23rd) $12.00 | Regular: $17.00\nBOX OFFICE  ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/index.asp )\nPhoto by: Colleen Wiebe\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-dances-2025/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:McLean Performance Studio | 244 Accolade East @ 4700 Keele St, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/yde2025.jpg
END:VEVENT
