SUMMARY:VCP presents DANCE COLLECTIVE
DESCRIPTION:The VCP Dance Collective is made up of a team of dancers of varying style and skill levels who, through a rotating choreographer system, are given the opportunity to challenge themselves by creating and teaching choreography in their preferred style for fellow members.\nThis year’s recital is a robust showcase of talent that spans various genres of dance including hip hop, jazz, K-pop, musical theatre, ballroom, tap, lyrical, and contemporary.\nDirected by Shreyas Batra\nFeaturing Choreography and Performances by the Dance Collective\nStage Managed by Lakshika Khurana\nJan. 23-26, 2025\nThur-Sat @ 7:30pm\nSun @ 2:30pm\nFred Thury Studio Theatre, 258 Vanier College\nTo reach the theatre, take the stairs or elevator on the east side of Vanier College to the second floor.\nPay-What-You-Can-Afford Tickets\nSuggested Pricing: General $25 | VCP Alumni $20 | Students $15 | VCP Current Company $10\nAvailable online or CASH ONLY at door\nEmail: vcp@yorku.ca\nFacebook: @VanierCollegeProductions\nInstagram: @vancproductions\nWebsite\n
