SUMMARY:OMNI-RÉUNIS Super Spreader Seminar Series
DESCRIPTION:OMNI-RÉUNIS Super Spreader Seminar Series final instalment for the fall and 2024 is here!\nThis time, Chigozie Ugwu presents her research on “Bayesian Spatial Analysis of Socioeconomic Influences on Mpox in the African Region: Implications for a One Health Approach.” We look forward to your attendance on:\n📆Thursday, Dec. 19 from\n⏰10:30 to 11:30 a.m.\nIf you’re at York University’s Keele Campus, we invite you to join us at our lab located at the Petrie Science & Engineering Building. REGISTER HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEkd-2srzkjGteOzIptOadJ155G9CX5U1uP )🔗, and feel free to share this invitation with your colleagues, networks and other researchers.\nShould you have any questions, contact Nolan Holder, OMNI-RÉUNIS program manager, at nholder@yorku.ca.\nWe hope to see you there!\n
