SUMMARY:How to Make Career Decisions for Students with Disabilities Webinar
DESCRIPTION:This webinar is for York students with disabilities only.\nAre you feeling stuck with your career decision making and not sure how to move forward? Attend this webinar to learn steps for making informed career decisions and how a growth mindset is essential for your personal and career success. If you require accessibility needs to access this webinar, please contact the Career Centre as soon as possible so we can assist you with accessing this webinar career@yorku.ca ( mailto:career@yorku.ca )\n** PLEASE NOTE THIS WILL BE AN ONLINE WEBINAR**\nTo participate in a webinar, you will need a computer (with speakers or headphones), internet access, and Zoom desktop application (Zoom) installed in your computer. You will receive the URL of the webinar with the meeting id in a reminder email after you have registered for the event. On the day of the event, you will join the webinar and ask your questions via chat.\nHow do I register?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Career Centre” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nSelect “Workshops & Webinars”\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/how-to-make-career-decisions-for-students-with-disabilities-webinar/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
