SUMMARY:Teaching Kitchen Cooking Class
DESCRIPTION:Looking to boost your brain health through food? You’ve come to the right place!\nThis event is a collaboration with The Centre for Sexual Violence, Support & Education for 16 Days of Activism. Join us for a meaningful and educational event!\nLearn how to make delicious Vietnamese spring rolls. Our executive chef and dietitian will guide you through the entire process, sharing their tips and tricks along the way.\nDuring this in-person event, you’ll have the opportunity to get hands-on experience and enhance your culinary skills. Immerse yourself in the vibrant flavors as you prepare this delicious recipe.\nWhether you’re a beginner or an experienced cook, this event is perfect for anyone looking to expand their culinary knowledge. Don’t miss out on this chance to learn, have fun, and connect with fellow food enthusiasts.\nMake sure to bring your own takeout container to take any leftovers with you!\nIf you have been prescribed an Epi Pen, bring it with you to the event.\nThis event is exclusively for York University students.\nDate: Tuesday, Dec. 3\nTime: 2 to 3 p.m.\nLocation: Ross Building, South 166\nMark your calendars and register now! ( https://TKSpringRollsKeele.eventbrite.com ) We can’t wait to see you there!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-kitchen-cooking-class/
