SUMMARY:5th Annual Dahdaleh Institute Global Health Graduate Scholar Symposium
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 5th Annual Global Health Graduate Scholars Symposium to learn more about some of the groundbreaking research being conducted at the Dahdaleh Institute. This year, six accomplished Dahdaleh graduate scholars will share the progress of their funded research projects in line with the Institute’s three themes (planetary health, global health and humanitarianism, and global health foresighting). The exciting presentation lineup includes:\n\nAna Cardoso – Fighting for Tomorrow: Colonization of the Future(s) and International Climate Politics at the End of the World(s)\nBrian Waters – Seasonal Variation of Urban Water Security in Freetown, Sierra Leone\nHanie Fard – Transnationalized Environmental Obligations of Foreign Investors\nLiam Michaud – Securitizing Risk: The Legal Determinants of Health Among People Who Use Drugs\nMichael De Santi – Linking Water Quality to Health Risks Using Machine Learning and Quantitative Microbial Risk Assessment in the Kyaka II Refugee Settlement\nValerie Lawson – Healthcare Access: An Analysis of the National Health Insurance Scheme in Accra, Ghana\n\nRegister below and join us on Dec. 11 at 10:30 a.m. share.hsforms.com/1lqMdQTUKRam5iudapuuc_A3t7a5 ( https://share.hsforms.com/1lqMdQTUKRam5iudapuuc_A3t7a5 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/5th-annual-dahdaleh-institute-global-health-graduate-scholar-symposium/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Dahdaleh Institute for Global Health Research @ Suite 2150 88 The Pond Rd, Dahdaleh Bldg., YorkU Keele Campus
END:VEVENT
