SUMMARY:Community Safety Month Tabling – Glendon
DESCRIPTION:With November being Community Safety Month, York University’s Community Safety Department is hosting Community Safety Month Activities on November 25-29 which focuses on promoting safety awareness, fostering community engagement, and providing resources and support to address safety concerns. During this week, a range of activities and workshops are organized to engage students, faculty, and staff members on topics related to personal, community, and environmental safety.\nA few of the events include:\n\n\n\nTabling at all three campus locations, to provide more information on the department and tips on how to maintain personal safety.\n\nGlendon – Tuesday, Nov. 26 at 10 a.m. at The Centre of Excellence (north corridor and lobby area).\n\n\n\n\n\n
