SUMMARY:Africa is Not a Country Seminar Series 2 on Environmental Genocide
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change at York University presents its second seminar, “Environmental Genocide: A Discussion of the Human and Environmental Costs of Oil in Nigeria,” as part of the Africa Is Not a Country: Seminar Series.\nThe series aims to address the absent, inadequate, skewed, and inaccurate representation of Africa and African issues in global discourse.\nSeminar Series 2: Environmental Genocide: A Discussion of the Human and Environmental Costs of Oil in Nigeria\nDate and Time: Wednesday, Nov. 27, noon to 2 p.m.\nGuest Scholars\nKathryn Nwajiaku-Dahou, director of politics and governance, ODI Global\nProfessor Engobo Emeseh, head of the School of Law, University of Bradford, U.K.\nIsaac “Asume” Osuoka, Social Action International\nHow to Attend Online\nRegister here: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_DRPuhJmvTderRzNiWcXm0w.\nEVERYONE WELCOME!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/africa-is-not-a-country-seminar-series-2-on-environmental-genocide/
