SUMMARY:Digital Media Graduate Program Virtual Open House – PhD
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2018, the joint graduate program in digital media is a unique partnership between the Department of Computational Arts ( https://computationalarts.ampd.yorku.ca/ ) and the Department of Electrical Engineering & Computer Science (EECS).  ( https://lassonde.yorku.ca/eecs/ ) Our students have access to the courses, faculty and scholarly resources of both departments.\nOur interdisciplinary program treats computation and code as an expressive medium open to creative and experimental applications bridging art and science. Students in the program work across a range of current and emerging digital media from experimental games and interactive installations to digital fabrication, data visualization, live coding, performance and sound.\nWe invite students to join us for an admissions information session:\nVirtual PhD Information Session\nDate: Dec. 3\nTime: 10:30 to 11:30 a.m.\nRSVP for the Zoom event ( https://forms.office.com/r/PHv7KXc7QS ).\nGraduate Digital Media students will benefit from:\n\ncompetitive funding packages at the MA, MSc and PhD level;\n\n\nhands-on experience using a broad range of digitally supported media;\n\n\ninterdisciplinary training combining computational science and artistic practices;\n\n\nteaching opportunities for PhD Candidates, research assistant work opportunities for MA/MSc and PhD candidates;\n\n\nstrong support for external scholarship application success;\n\n\nflexible course offerings across specializations and access to comprehensive research/training spaces; and\n\n\nthe potential to contribute to scholarly dialogue and community-building through conferences, arts festivals, exhibition and publishing opportunities.\n\n \nOngoing faculty research ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/digitalmedia/about-us/our-faculty/ ) areas include: immersive installations, mixed reality, digital fabrication, experimental gaming, autonomous agents for computer games and virtual world applications, human-centred computing, data visualization, live coding, wearable computing, distributed performance, sound and intelligent environments.\n \nApplication deadlines\nInternational students: Dec. 15, 2024\nDomestic students: Jan. 15, 2025\n \nYou can find more information as well as application instructions though York’s Faculty of Graduate Studies ( https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/apply-now/ ) web page. You can find further program information here ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/digitalmedia/ ).\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/digital-media-graduate-program-virtual-open-house-phd/
ORGANIZER;CN=Graduate Program in Digital Media:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Graduate Program in Digital Media
LOCATION:Register for Zoom Info
END:VEVENT
