SUMMARY:AMPD-Sensorium Graduate Symposium
DESCRIPTION:The AMPD-Sensorium Graduate Symposium is a dynamic platform where emerging researchers across AMPD and beyond share their innovative work through concise presentations, fostering an environment of collaboration and dialogue. All are welcome to come and explore the intersections of knowledge as participants co-create insights that challenge conventional boundaries and inspire future directions in their fields. This year, the Graduate Symposium will coincide with the Wendy Michener Memorial Lecture featuring speaker danah boyd ( https://www.danah.org/ ).\nDecember 13th, 2024\n9:15 a.m. – 5:30 p.m.\nJoseph G. Green Studio Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/joseph-g-green-studio-theatre/ )\nFree Admission\nRSVP HERE ( https://ampd.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=208420 ) to reserve your spot\nSYMPOSIUM SCHEDULE\nMORNING\n9:15 – 9:45 a.m. – Coffee Reception\n9:45 – 11:15 a.m. – Session 1: Lightning Presentations of Graduate Research\n11:15 – 11:30 a.m. – Break\n11:30 – 12:30 a.m. – Session 2.1: Collaborative Presentations\nDienye Amajor and Luke Kuplowsky,\nSarah Grace Grothaus and Vladimir Kanic,\nDaniella Sanader and Erica Stocking\nAFTERNOON\n12:30 a.m. – 1:45 p.m. – Lunch\n1:45 – 2:45 p.m. – Session 2.2: Collaborative Presentations\nNava Waxman and Sebastian Oreamuno,\nNick Fox-Gieg and Robert Appleton,\nSophia Hershfield and Michael Trommer\n2:45 – 3:00 p.m. – Break\n3:00 – 4:30 p.m. – Michener Lecture with danah boyd\n4:30 – 5:30 p.m. – Closing Reception\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ampd-sensorium-graduate-symposium/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Joe G. Green Theatre, Centre for Film and Theatre @ York University, 4700 Keele Street, Toronto, ON
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/gradsymposium.jpg
END:VEVENT
