SUMMARY:Interdisciplinary Studies Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Interdisciplinary Studies? We invite you to attend our program information session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/96094842741?pwd=qsQs1IydhXo2RWGkFAaVdhsZUWmGLZ.1 )\nThe Master’s in Interdisciplinary Studies—one of the first formalized graduate programs in Canada—enables highly motivated students to study within three distinct disciplines in order to deeply explore a particular problem or phenomenon. Students have the option to propose a research project and choose scholarly lenses from an intriguing range of interdisciplinary fields. The student’s unique area of inquiry may combine the fine arts, sciences, health, social sciences, engineering, humanities, law and more.\nTo learn more about our graduate program, please visit our website ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/interdis ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/is-info-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies
LOCATION:Online Zoom
END:VEVENT
