SUMMARY:EUC PhESSA Research Day: Precarity, Care and Repair
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change invites you to our PhD in Environmental Studies Students Association (PhESSA) Research Day!\nPlease come and learn about the exciting work our colleagues and students are doing.\nIf you’re coming for lunch and are not  a presenter, please send a quick RSVP to esphd@yorku.ca ( mailto:esphd@yorku.ca ).\nThank you and see you there! Tim Quick and Clara Gomez Garcia (PhESSA) and Cate Sandilands (ES PhD Program Coordinator)\nES PhD Research Day: Precarity, Care, and Repair\nProgram Schedule, HNES 140\n8:45                     Welcome and opening remarks\n9:00 – 10:45     Panel #1: Precarity and Extraction\nNilanjala Ganguli: Sex for resilience: Understanding how climate-vulnerable populations use transactional sex to respond to shocks and stressors\nZachary Dark: The Discourse of Critical Minerals: Insights from the Canadian Prairies\nIsaac Thornley: No De-Risking the Neoliberal Fetish: TMX and the Politics of Social License\nElham Akbari: Narratives of Housing Crisis: Precarity and Resilience in Toronto’s High-Rises\n10:45 – 11:00   Break\n11:00 – 12:30   Panel #2: Approaches to Care in Research Methodologies\nLaurence Butet-Roch: Remediating toxic images: a journey towards representational justice and attuned methodologies\nMaureen Owino: Activist Research – Putting Theory into Practice\nCole Swanson: Such Beautiful Skeins: Methodological Meditations on Art, Science, and Anthropocenic Others\n12:30 – 1:00     Lunch\n1:00 – 2:00        Keynote Speaker\nStuart Schussler, ES PhD 2023\nCaring for Each Other, Caring for Society: On the Reproductive Labour of Organizing\n2:00 – 2:15        Break\n2:15 – 4:00        Panel #3: Art, Design, and Aesthetics of Care\nSayeh Dastgheib-Beheshti: Rethinking Design Thinking\nTim Quick: Gregory Bateson’s Aesthetic Epistemology\nKarl Petschke: “The Speed That Tears Us Away”: Ethics and Aesthetics in Bypassed Landscapes\nPhyllis Novak: Down and Dirty: Earthwork as Socially Engaged Art and Care Practice for Eco-social Movement and Justice\n4:00                     Closing remarks\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/euc-phessa-research-day-precarity-care-and-repair/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies
LOCATION:Health, Nursing &amp; Environmental Studies (HNES 140) @ York University
END:VEVENT
