TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:MES Research Presentations
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) is delighted to present the research of MES graduates, now PhD students, Kelly Gingrich and Cole Weber!\nKelly Gingrich, MES, is a ﬁrst year Environmental Studies PhD Student in EUC. She is studying environmental and climate change education as preﬁgurative, participatory and place-based practices,\nwith a particular interest in post-capitalist economic transitions towards degrowth and climate justice. Her doctoral research is at the intersection of degrowth and climate education.\nCole Weber, MES, is also a ﬁrst year Environmental Studies PhD Student in EUC. He is a long time activist in tenant struggles. His MES major paper argues that housing research does not adequately theorize economic and political power. The paper analyzes public documents and archival materials on state intervention in rental housing in Canada from 1941-1995.\nThis is an in-person event only at the Health Nursing & Environmental Studies (HNES) Building, Rm 138, York University.\nEVERYONE WELCOME!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mes-research-presentations/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:HNES 138
