SUMMARY:Investing in the Future – Unlocking Potential: Financial Innovations and Open Banking
DESCRIPTION:A CI Financial – Schulich Panel and Networking Event\nDate and time: Nov. 19 between 5 and 8 p.m.Location: Schulich Building, Room G101 for the panel and McEwen Building Atrium for the networking reception\nPanellists:\n\nKambiz Vatan-Abadi, chief innovation officer at CI Financial and president UDP at CI Direct Investing;\nMatthew Wilcox, head of deposits and investments at Neo Financial; and\nRoy Kao, board member at Fintech Candence and Open Finance Network Canada, and advisory board member at Open Banking Expo.\n\nModerator: Prof. Pauline Shum Nolan\nAgenda:\n5 to 5:30 p.m. – Registration & Networking – McEwen Building Atrium5:30 to 7 p.m. – Panel Session – G1017 to 8 p.m. – Networking and Reception – McEwen Building Atrium\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/investing-in-the-future-unlocking-potential-financial-innovations-and-open-banking/
ORGANIZER;CN=Schulich School of Business:MAILTO:admissions@schulich.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Schulich School of Business
