SUMMARY:Supporting Scholars at York: Preventing, Mitigating, and Responding to Scholarship Harassment
DESCRIPTION:Across universities and disciplines, scholars face diverse forms and sources of harassment related to their research or teaching. Join York faculty members and representatives from university offices for information and conversation about how to contend with these concerns and support academic freedom.\nThis event is open to all York full-time faculty members interested in finding out about scholarship harassment, what might be done to prevent it and what recourse and resources are available if it occurs. \nWe will hear from 3 colleagues who have experienced scholarship harassment from various sources and using various means:\n\nChristine Till, Department of Psychology, Faculty of Health\nJake Pyne, School of Social Work, Faculty of LA&PS\nVidya Shah, Faculty of Education\n\nThere will also be representatives from university offices for discussion on the following topics:\n\nOnline harassment\nResearch supports\nLegal and complaints process\nSupport for grad students\n\nTuesday, November 12, 9:00 – 10:30 am, In-person, Keele Campus (Location TBD)\nRSVP Link.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/supporting-scholars-at-york-preventing-mitigating-and-responding-to-scholarship-harassment/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty Affairs, EPC:MAILTO:FacAffairs@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, People &amp; Culture
LOCATION:Keele Campus, York University @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
