SUMMARY:In-Person Tour of the Allan I. Carswell Observatory
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a tour night at Allan I. Carswell Observatory every Wednesday from 5 to 7 p.m. During this tour, you will get a chance to look at and learn about the 60-centimetre telescope, the one-metre telescope and the control room at the observatory, and get all your astronomy questions answered. The one-metre telescope is the largest telescope on any Canadian university campus.\nTickets are free but required to attend. Find all the updated event information and registration links are on the Observatory website: yorku.ca/science/observatory.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/in-person-tour-of-the-allan-i-carswell-observatory/
