TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Student Nurses’ Voices Speaker Series
DESCRIPTION:Session 1: Grassroots-to-Global\nThe world’s nurses have been enduring ceaseless challenges from overwhelmed health-care systems, resulting in anxiety, depression, post-traumatic stress and escalating burnout, as well as increased threats, hostility and violence. These have been further exacerbated by the most recent COVID-19 pandemic that strained the frontline nurses worldwide. Even as nurses have been appreciated and widely trusted for this service, the prevalent absence of nursing’s public voice contributes to the fact that nurses continue to be undervalued. Of course, student nurses – the future of nursing worldwide – are keenly aware of these challenges. With their voices, student nurses can bring contemporary perspectives from the inherent global and digital awareness characteristic of their generation.\nThis Student Nurses’ Voices Speaker Series will continue its innovative global multimedia outreach to prepare and engage nurses. This series aims to focus on the future of nursing by engaging student nurses to become empowered leading public storytellers and to share their stories of healing advocacy, resilience and collaboration for a healthy world – as thought leaders across the global public space and to the listening ears of everyone.\nThis session, join us to hear from student nurses from the West Visayas State University, York University and the University of Stirling.\nRegister here: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_LhYRbv_8RiugaqwkN2hAmg#/registration.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/student-nurses-voices-speaker-series/
ORGANIZER;CN=CIFAL York:MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
