SUMMARY:Ask a Nurse Drop-by Tabling Session
DESCRIPTION:Consult a healthcare professional\nStudents juggle a lot, from academics and work to family and friends. It can be hard to prioritize your own health and well-being at the same time.\nAsk a Nurse is a confidential service for York students. Speak to Public Health Nurses from Student Counselling, Health & Well-being about your health-related questions, without an appointment. There is a lot of health-related information online and it can be difficult to tell what’s reliable. Our goal is to answer your questions, find solutions and connect you to the most helpful resources. Come see us in-person or get in touch online ( https://students.yorku.ca/health/ask-a-nurse )!\n*This tabling session will focus on discussing vaccine availability for COVID-19 and the flu at Shoppers Drug Mart.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/295-905-404-944/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being:MAILTO:schw@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,Ask a Nurse,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Health Education &amp; Promotion,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
LOCATION:York Lanes Mall, 80 York Blvd, North York, ON M3J 1P3
END:VEVENT
