SUMMARY:Pura Vida Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:In May 2024, 25 York University students travelled to Costa Rica to take part in the PANF 3030/5030 Global Eco-Arts Residency Course. This 10-day intensive course comprised a series of workshops, gallery tours, creative class-based exercises, and participation in a local community festival at York University’s Las Nubes Eco-Campus and surrounding areas. Through these experiences, students were introduced to themes of environmental and community-based art, food sovereignty, site-specific art, and the ethics of community engagement. The Pura Vida exhibit highlights some of the student-created art that was inspired by this course and the Las Nubes Eco-Campus in Costa Rica. It also includes artwork created by students who participated in the Environmental Arts and Food Sovereignty course offered in the previous year.\nExhibition: October 28 – November 8\nOpening Reception: November 6 (5:30 p.m. – 7:00 p.m.)\nLocation: Gales Gallery ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/gales-gallery/ ), 105 Accolade West, Keele Campus\nGallery Hours: 10:00 a.m. – 4:00 p.m.\nFree Admission\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sensorium-presents-resonant-futures-pura-vida-exhibition/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Gales Gallery, 105 Accolade West Building (ACW), York University @ 89 York Blvd., Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/pure.jpg
END:VEVENT
