SUMMARY:Grammar On! Workshop 3: A Tense Time
DESCRIPTION:Workshop 3: A Tense Time\nDo you feel tense when you think about time? Then make time this week to come talk about the 13 ways of Looking at Time in English sentences! In this Thursday’s Grammar On!, you’ll not only learn how to time-travel in your academic essays, but you’ll also discover that the past and present are both “simple” and “perfect”\nWe often think of academic writing conventions as limitations to our writing and of grammar as a series of scary rules about “what-not-to-do.” But academic writing conventions can serve as guidelines in producing an effective piece of writing, and grammar is an awesome tool you can use to write more effective sentences and increase your range of syntactical choices.\nCome join Dunja on Thursdays at 11:30am in the Writing Centre’s Grammar On! series of online workshops. The workshop is open to all students who want to learn to construct elegant and effective academic sentences that say what you want them to say and do what you want them to do.\nNo RSVPs. Just click to join!\nJoin Now\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grammar-on-workshop-3-a-tense-time/
ORGANIZER;CN=Writing Centre:MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca, dbaus@yorku.ca, lapswrit@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Student Success,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-International,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,LA&amp;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/person-takes-notes-with-pen-and-paper-while-l_James-Robertson-9.jpg
