SUMMARY:York Collegium for Public Ethics and McLaughlin College Panel – The 2024 U.S. Elections: Harris vs. Trump
DESCRIPTION:The 2024 U.S. elections are coming down to the wire. How did things get to this point? Who is likely to win? When should the results be known? These and other questions will be addressed in a live panel, consisting of: Robert Drummond, Professor Emeritus, Department of Politics and former dean of the Faculty of Arts; and Nathaniel Denaro, a juris doctor candidate at Osgoode Hall Law School whose graduate studies focused on the evolution of the American working class. The chairperson is Philip MacEwen, co-editor of the Canadian Journal of Practical Philosophy and director of the York Collegium for Public Ethics.\nJoin us on Wednesday, Oct. 30 from noon to 1:30 pm in 140 McLaughlin College (Senior Common Room), or join via Zoom at: yorku.zoom.us/j/96880704520?pwd=KjdYyR45bED9QG3NGhyoZdBpEOGQyM.1.\nNote: this event is being organized and hosted by McLaughlin College and the York Collegium for Public Ethics.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-collegium-for-public-ethics-and-mclaughlin-college-panel-the-2024-u-s-elections-harris-vs-trump/
ORGANIZER;CN=McLaughlin College:MAILTO:nfemia@yorku.ca, vcarneva@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS Department of Philosophy
LOCATION:140 McLaughlin College
