SUMMARY:Grand Opening of the Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery of York University
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating the Grand Opening of the Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery\nWe are excited to announce the grand opening of the Joan and Martin Goldfarb Gallery on Wednesday, Nov. 13, from 7 to 10 p.m. This momentous occasion honours the generous contributions of Joan and Martin Goldfarb, longtime supporters of the arts at York University.\nThe new stand-alone gallery, designed by internationally acclaimed architect Siamak Hariri, features a stunning butterfly-shaped design with three distinct exhibition spaces and a multifunctional pavilion. This space will serve as a vital hub for art presentations, performances and workshops, enhancing community engagement and promoting the artistic vision of York University.\nThe opening will showcase three inaugural exhibitions:\n\nPlains Horizon by Lori Blondeau, featuring stones collected from the gallery’s site, alongside a poignant painting by her mother;\nManual Assembly, a group exhibition with works by nine artists exploring themes of accumulation and assemblage, including El Anatsui and Jeneen Frei Njootli; and\nAbstract Legacies, which highlights the significance of York’s art collection, showcasing pieces donated by the Goldfarbs.\n\nIn addition to the exhibitions, attendees will enjoy remarks and a special performance by Lori Blondeau, as well as refreshments.\nRSVP to confirm your attendance here: thegoldfarbgallery.ca/project/rsvp ( https://thegoldfarbgallery.ca/project/rsvp/ ).\nWe invite everyone to join us in celebrating this pivotal moment in the University’s artistic journey.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grand-opening-of-the-joan-and-martin-goldfarb-gallery-of-york-university/
ORGANIZER;CN=Art Gallery of York University:MAILTO:agyu@yorku.ca
