SUMMARY:CineSiege 2024
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nIn its 22nd year, CineSiege is an annual showcase screening of outstanding productions created in the previous year by undergraduate students in the Department of Cinema and Media Arts at York University ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/department-of-cinema-and-media-arts/ ). CineSiege features a juried selection of short films, chosen by industry leaders in Canadian film and media.\nWe hope you can join us to celebrate the next generation of filmmakers! All nominated films in 3rd and 4th year are also eligible for craft awards i.e. Best Cinematography, Best Sound Design, etc.\nCineSiege 2024\nTuesday, November 19, 2024\n7:00 PM – 10:30 PM\n(Please arrive at 6:30 PM, as the show will start promptly at 7:00 PM)\nParadise Theatre ( https://paradiseonbloor.com/ ): 1006c Bloor Street West Toronto, ON M6H 1M2\nFREE Admission \nTICKETS \n\n\n\n\nDirector Name\n\n\nFilm Title\n\n\nCategory Nominated\n\n\n\n\nAna Iacovleva\n\n\nChained\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nFelicia Donkor\n\n\nChildish\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nDaniela Norouzian & Cassie Serapion\n\n\nFrom Me To You\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\nPatrick  Malette\n\nLimerence\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nNatalie Singh\n\n\nPursuance\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nZav Jenabian\n\n\nThe Colour Blue\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nMattia  Salvatore\n\n\nTi Voglio, Bene, Pape\n\n\nBest 1st Year Film\n\n\n\n\nSamuel Jean\n\n\nJe M’apelle Syrup\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nSkye Rooney-Pedersen\n\n\nAn Apple a Day\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nElla Kennedy\n\n\nI’m Becoming My Mother\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nRyan Raake\n\n\nBlossom\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nRyan Buraphacheep\n\n\nRed Blvd\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nAria Van Allen\n\n\nMelody: The Melleny Melody Story\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nChristine Sawka Fraser\n\n\nWe Still Need The Village\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nSebastian Xavier Lennox\n\n\nThe Competitive World of Ballroom Dance\n\n\nBest 2nd Year\n\n\n\n\nHannah Lane\n\n\nJust On