SUMMARY:Africa Is Not a Country Seminar Series
DESCRIPTION:“Africa Is Not a Country” is a hybrid seminar series that aims to address the absent, inadequate, skewed, and inaccurate representation of Africa and African issues.\nJoin us for our maiden seminar themed: Genocides on the Margins, from Tigray to Congo to Sudan\nSeminar speakers include:\n\nTaiwo Bello, PhD (assistant professor, Oklahoma State University);\nNisrin Elamin, PhD (assistant professor, University of Toronto);\nMaereg Adhanom, PhD (environmentalist and international development expert); and\nGertrude Mianda, PhD (professor, York University-Glendon).\n\nTo attend, please register here: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_CS4YXaJ7Rt2XQniVXdOs5w.\nYou can also attend in person at the Black Community Space (HNES 248) located in the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change.\n \n
