SUMMARY:[Scholarly Skills Webinar] The Road to Defence: Demystifying & Preparing for your Final Defence & Oral Exam
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies will be hosting a series entitled Scholarly Skills. Join us for our next workshop!\nSince starting your graduate studies, you’ve probably heard about ‘the defence’ and the ‘oral exam’ and wondered what exactly they are. In this next installment of the Faculty of Graduate Studies’ Scholarly Skills Series, Associate Dean, Academic Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith, will demystify this important final milestone. Discussion regarding the goal and structure of the final defence and its’ oral exam will be followed by what to expect and how best to prepare. You’ll then hear from recent graduates who successfully defended their work at an oral exam where they’ll share their top tips. Bring us your questions and we will be happy to address them.\nDate: November 26, 2024\nTime: 12:00pm (1-hour workshop)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required. Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_0GJECwZRSq2pNA341FMpVA )\n
