SUMMARY:Open Forum: Anti-Racism On Screen
DESCRIPTION:with Marjorie Beaucage and Lisa Myers\nFriday, October 29, 2024\n7:00 P.M.\nBachir/Yerex Screening Room (4th Floor)\nFree Admission | Reception to Follow\n401 Richmond Street West ( https://maps.app.goo.gl/ykSnxMi3fiGbRbNX6 )\nMarjorie Beaucage is a Métis filmmaker and activist whose films include Bingo, Ntapueu… I am telling the truth, and Coming in Stories: Two Spirit in Saskatchewan.\nLisa Myers is an Anishnaabe artist, curator, cook and filmmaker, whose works include Blueprints for a Long Walk, Straining and absorbing, and Shore Lunch.\nOpen Forum is a monthly series of conversations about putting anti-racism on screen, co-presented by York’s Cinema and Media Arts, Vtape, CFMDC, Reel Asian International Film Festival and OCADU.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/open-forum-anti-racism-on-screen-in-conversation-with-nick-fernandes/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
