SUMMARY:The Filipino Diaspora in Canada: Celebrating Successes and Addressing Persistent Challenges  
DESCRIPTION:The Philippine Consulate General in Toronto and York University jointly invite you to a public forum celebrating the 75th anniversary of the diplomatic relations between the Philippines and Canada this year.\n\nThe Filipino Diaspora in Canada: Celebrating Successes and Addressing Persistent Challenges  \nDate and Time: Monday, Oct. 28, 7 to 9:30 p.m. (doors open at 6:30 p.m.)\nVenue: Tribute Communities Recital Hall and CIBC Lobby, York University\n\nThe forum features a panel of distinguished Filipino Canadians who will share their journeys towards professional leadership positions in various fields. The discussion will address the role of family, community, education and mentorship in navigating career success. In addition to reflecting on their successes, the panel will also consider what Filipino identity now means in the Canadian context, and the barriers and challenges still faced by the community.\n\nInvited leaders:\n\n\nRechie Valdez, minister for small business, Government of Canada;\n\n\nFlordeliz (Gigi) Osler, senator, Senate of Canada, Canadian Senators Group, Manitoba;\n\n\nSteve A. Coroza, justice of the Court of Appeal for Ontario;\n\n\nAna Serrano, president of OCAD University; and\n\n\nGlenda Bonifacio, dean of Lakehead University.\n\n\nRSVP at go.yorku.ca/filipino-forum.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-filipino-diaspora-in-canada-celebrating-successes-and-addressing-persistent-challenges/
ORGANIZER;CN=York International:MAILTO:goglobal@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:International
LOCATION:Accolade East Building, Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
END:VEVENT
