SUMMARY:Navigating Your Job Search in Canadian Politics (By Request – Job Search Workshops)
DESCRIPTION:Navigating Your Job Search in Canadian Politics!\nAre you studying Canadian Politics and aiming for a career in government or related organizations? If so, this workshop is designed for you! The Career Centre will provide essential information on how to effectively search for jobs in Federal, Provincial, and Municipal governments. This session is packed with valuable resources and practical tips to help you successfully navigate the job search process and reach your career goals.\nNote: This is a hybrid session. You can choose to join us in person or attend online via Zoom\nHow do I register?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Career Centre” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nSelect “Workshops & Webinars”\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n
