SUMMARY:ScaryFest presented by the Friends of Markham Museum
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a spooktacular time at Scaryfest 2024 as the Markham Museum transforms its 25-acre site into a Halloween haven! The York University Markham Campus team will be hosting a fang-tastic booth filled with Halloween-themed activities to engage and educate the community about our programs. Stop by to chat with us and learn all about our new campus (if you dare). \nScaryfest is a family event perfect for kids 10 and under. Come in costume, explore the site and enjoy a cauldron full of family-friendly activities. Entrance is by timed ticket; please pick the entrance time slot that works best for you and guarantee your spot today! Children under 24 months are admitted free and do not require tickets. \nFor more info on the event, visit Markham.ca. Don’t forget to arrive in costume! \nVisit Markham’s website to learn more about Milliken Children’s Festival. \nDate & Time \nSaturday, Oct. 26\nSunday, Oct. 27 \n11 a.m. to 6 p.m.  \nLocation \nMarkham Museum – 9350 Markham Road, Markham \nAdmission \n$14 per person. Children 24 months and under admitted free. All rides and activities included in admission. Some exceptions apply. Purchase tickets here now.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scaryfest-presented-by-the-friends-of-markham-museum/
CATEGORIES:Markham Campus
LOCATION:9350 Markham Road
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Scaryfest-2023-Web-500-x-250.jpg
