SUMMARY:Celebration of Women in Computing
DESCRIPTION:CAN-CWiC is the premiere Canadian computing conference for young women and non-binary people in technology.\nThis annual event has been offered since 2011 and features networking, learning, sharing and mentoring. CAN-CWiC embodies the mission of encouraging curiosity and awareness for the digital innovations that change the community and world around us, bringing together leaders in research, education and industry from across Canada.\nGet inspired by stories from women who have been there and done that and how they succeeded. This year, for the first time in its history, the conference is being hosted at a university campus – at York University, with Maleknaz Nayebi from Lassonde’s Department of Electrical Engineering & Computer Science serving as the conference Chair.\nVisit cscan-infocan.ca/celebration-of-women-in-computing to register.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/celebration-of-women-in-computing/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp; Culture
LOCATION:Second Student Center Conference Room (2nd floor)
