SUMMARY:Victorian Studies Network at York’s 16th Annual Symposium – Victorian Studies at York: A Closer Look
DESCRIPTION:Faculty and graduate students from all departments are invited to attend. The cross-disciplinary scope of the program – history, law, commerce and empire, bee-keeping, publishing and pedagogy – is especially inviting.\nFor 16 years, the Victorian Studies Network at York has been connecting researchers and enhancing connections among graduate students, post-docs and faculty. Our goal is to facilitate interdepartmental and interdisciplinary work, to enrich our personal and collective experience of research in the field and to showcase York as a centre for Victorian studies.\nLunch and refreshments will be served.\nRSVP to Professor Lesley Higgins at 19higgins55@gmail.com.\nAll faculty, postdocs and grad students are welcome.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/victorian-studies-at-york-a-closer-look/
