SUMMARY:Level Up | Working abroad: Alumni panel and Q&A
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in taking your career globally? This upcoming panel discussion features successful early career alumni from Europe and the United States discussing their international careers and advice for interested alumni and students. The moderated discussion will cover how the panelists secured work after graduation, discussing the challenges, benefits, learnings and tips for grads looking to find work outside of Canada.\nFeaturing alumni speakers:\n\nAlamgir Khandwala CPA (BAS ’17), Revenue Accounting Manager, Uber, representing San Francisco, United States\nJenny Chong (BCOM ’07), Founder, The Essential Project Manager, representing London, England, United Kingdom\nCheyenne Duz (BSc ’11), Sustainability Ratings Senior Manager, EcoVadis.Representing Paris, France\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/level-up-working-abroad-alumni-panel-and-qa-2/
