SUMMARY:Level Up | Med School: Tips on how to get accepted and succeed
DESCRIPTION:Thinking about going to medical school or studying for the Medical College Admission Test (MCAT)? This event will feature intimate conversations with two successful York alumni, Brian Serapio (BSc ’18), Psychiatry Resident, University of Toronto and Clarelle Gonsalves (BSc ’18), Paediatrics Resident, Hospital for Sick Children/University of Toronto, who have recently graduated from medical school and are now excelling as doctors. Learn tips for navigating medical school admissions, the highs and lows of being a medical school student and takeaways from being an early career doctor.\n \n
