SUMMARY:Managing the People Side of Change
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Organizational Learning and People Excellence, Human Resources\nThe discipline of change management is well practiced in organizations today. Successful organizational change is rooted in the ability to facilitate individual change one person at a time. In the current context of constant change, people managers need change management knowledge and skills to ensure they lead their teams towards adaptive and constructive change when change is expected and when it’s not. This session features certified change management practitioners and leaders who share the highest standards in change management methods and the skills and tools needed to apply to the people side of change.\nIntended Audience: York U Employees\nFormat: Virtual Event\nClosed Captioning Available\nRegister here\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/managing-the-people-side-of-change/
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
