SUMMARY:Exploring Black Men’s Mental Health Challenges 
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will focus on the different challenges affecting Black men in our society, ranging from navigating societal expectations, to addressing men’s mental health topics. This workshop will be led by the Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) program, under the leadership of their Student Success Mentor Leads, and will be facilitated by Byron Gray, Manager of York University TD Community Engagement Centre. There will also be an honorary presence of Greg N. Leslie, a registered Social Worker, Psychotherapist and Consultant.\nIntended Audience: All students are welcome; Black males are encouraged to attend\nFormat: In-person event\nLocation: EUC’s Black Community Space in room HNES 248\nRegister here\n
