SUMMARY:Well-being Week Art Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Faculty of Health: Calumet & Stong Colleges\nThis art exhibit emphasizes and advocates for the importance and diversity of well-being practices, as well as the connection between well-being, art and expression. The exhibition will give attendees a space to reflect, be mindful, be empathetic towards themselves and others, and give artists a space to express themselves and be supported and celebrated.\n\nCommunity members will be given an opportunity submit their art for adjudication, prizes of $300, $200 & $100 will be given to top 3 winners. Sponsored by the William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\n\n\nIntended Audience: All York community\nFormat: In-person event\nLocation: Samuel J. Zacks Gallery (Stong College Room 109)\nCall for Proposals\nReception Information\n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/well-being-week-art-exhibition/
CATEGORIES:Advising,Calumet College,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre,Well-being,Well-being Week
END:VEVENT
