SUMMARY:Empowering Health and Wellness: The Well-being Strategy Launch featuring Georgette Reed
DESCRIPTION:Presented by the Well-being Strategy Team\nJoin us online for the highly anticipated launch of our Campus Well-being Strategy, a comprehensive initiative designed to promote health and wellness throughout our University community. This virtual event is a key milestone in our commitment to fostering a supportive and thriving campus environment.\n\nWe are thrilled to welcome Georgette Reed, a certified track & conditioning coach, former Olympian, health & wellness, mental health and productivity expert with 43 years of experience. Georgette will share the positive lessons, values and virtues of sport through relevant and humorous anecdotes in an inspirational and genuinely enthusiastic and optimistic manner.\n\nSponsored by the William and Nona Heaslip Foundation\n\n\nIntended Audience: All York community\nFormat: Virtual event\nClosed Captioning Available\nRegister here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_AxrrpbFXSZOvLarI0wWpqA )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/empowering-health-and-wellness-the-well-being-strategy-launch-featuring-georgette-reed/
CATEGORIES:Advising,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre,Well-being,Well-being Week
END:VEVENT
