TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Campus Sustainability Month – BioBlitz
DESCRIPTION:Do you love capturing nature? Help us take a snapshot of York’s biodiversity! For Campus Sustainability Month, join our BioBlitz event by using the iNaturalist app to catalog and geotag plants, animals and insects across our beautiful campus. Whether you’re exploring a heritage woodlot, the arboretum or one of our scenic ravines, every observation counts on either the Keele or Glendon Campus! 🍃\n💡 How to Participate:\n1️⃣ Download the iNaturalist app.\n2️⃣ Create an account.\n3️⃣ Search “York University BioBlitz” under the Projects tab and join.\n🎉 Upcoming Walks\n🔹 Oct. 10, 2:30 to 3:30 p.m.: Walk with Prof. Gordon Fitch at Arboretum Lane; meet behind the Bergeron Building.\n🔹 Oct. 22, 9:30 to 11 a.m.: Walk with Prof. Alex Mills at Arboretum Lane; meet behind the Bergeron Building.\n🔹 Oct. 23, 2 to 3:30 p.m.: Walk with Professor Laura McKinnon; at the Glendon Manor entrance (Glendon College).\n🔹 Oct. 24, 1 to 2 p.m.: Walk with Valerio Larivera; meet at York Boulevard and Keele Street, by the York sign at the main entrance of the University.\n✨ Prize Alert: The student with the most observations in iNaturalist wins a $50 YUcard cash prize! 💳\nGet involved and be part of this exciting journey to explore and capture York’s rich biodiversity. 🌱💚\nFor more information, email sustainability@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/campus-sustainability-month-bioblitz/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Sustainability:MAILTO:sustainability@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Sustainability
END:VEVENT
