TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Trump’s Mail-In Voting Opposition and Canadians’ Trust in the System
DESCRIPTION:Join Cary Wu, Associate Professor and York Research Chair, Faculty of Liberal Arts and Professional Studies and Andrew Dawson, Associate Professor of Sociology, Glendon Campus on Oct. 23 at 12 p.m. for a discussion on Donald Trump’s vigorous attacks on voting by mail. His relentless assault on the integrity of mail-in balloting has cast a shadow over the confidence of American voters. Our recent investigation suggests that Trump’s false claims also had reverberations across the border, influencing how some Canadians view mail-in ballots.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-trumps-mail-in-voting-opposition-and-canadians-trust-in-the-system/
