TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Teaching Kitchen: No Bake Energy Bites at Keele Campus
DESCRIPTION:Looking to boost your brain health through food? You’ve come to the right place!\nJoin us for an exciting and interactive Teaching Kitchen event at Keele Campus! Learn how to make delicious no bake energy bites with Fair Trade ingredients to celebrate Fairtrade Month. Our executive chef and dietitian will guide you through the entire process, sharing their tips and tricks along the way.\nDuring this in-person event, you’ll have the opportunity to get hands-on experience and enhance your culinary skills. Immerse yourself in the vibrant flavors as you prepare this easy and packed with energy bites.\nWhether you’re a beginner or an experienced cook, this event is perfect for anyone looking to expand their culinary knowledge. Don’t miss out on this chance to learn, have fun, and connect with fellow food enthusiasts.\nMake sure to bring your own takeout container to take any leftovers with you!\nThis event is exclusively for York University students.\nMark your calendars and register now. We can’t wait to see you there!\nDate: Wednesday, Oct. 9\nTime: 2 to 3 p.m.\nLocation: Grad Lounge – Ross Building South – Room S166\nRegister now!  ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/teaching-kitchen-no-bake-energy-bites-at-keele-campus-tickets-1012785587957 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-kitchen-no-bake-energy-bites-at-keele-campus/
ORGANIZER;CN=Food Services:MAILTO:food@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp; Promotion,Students,Sustainability,Well-being
LOCATION:Grad Lounge in Ross Building South
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/IMG_6681-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
