SUMMARY:G.I.V.E – Gospel Inter-Varsity Explosion 2024
DESCRIPTION:Imagine the power of 200 voices raised in chorus. Now imagine that power expressed through gospel music.\nG.I.V.E. aims to strengthen connections between post-secondary gospel choirs, highlight our gospel courses, welcome prospective students, and create a supportive, uplifting environment. The event takes place in the world class Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre, accompanied by a full rhythm section.\n\nFEATURING\nHumber Gospel Choir (HGC) – Conductor: Natalie Stewart\nUniversity of Toronto Faculty of Music Gospel Choir (UTFMGC) – Conductor: Darren Hamilton\nYork University Gospel Choir (YUGC) – Conductor: Natalie Stewart\nYork University Gospel Ensemble (YUGE) – Course Director: Corey Butler\nGuest Conductor/Coordinator: Karen Burke\nMUSICANS\nCorey Butler – Music Director | Keys\nStephen Lewis – Hammond Organ\nEthan Groves – Drums\nRandal Hall – Bass\n\nLocation: Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/sandra-faire-and-ivan-fecan-theatre/ )\nAdmission: $20 | $15 students\nBox Office: TICKETS ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/b_otix.asp?cboPerformances=2154&cboEvent=995 )\nMaps and Directions\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/g-i-v-e-gospel-inter-varsity-explosion-2024/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre, 110 Accolade East Building @ 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/gospelchoir.jpg
END:VEVENT
