TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:The 39th Annual Meeting of the Canadian Econometrics Study Group (CESG)
DESCRIPTION:The 39th Annual Meeting of the Canadian Econometrics Study Group (CESG) will be held in Toronto from Oct. 25 to 27. The meeting is organized by the Department of Economics at York University. The theme of the meeting is: Inequality Measures and Econometric Modelling and our keynote Speakers are Marc Henry (Penn State University) and Francesca Molinari (Cornell University).\nThe local organizers – I. Archakov, A. Djogbenou, J. Jasiak, P. Rilstone, R. Sufana, P. Tuvaandorj and J. Zhao – gratefully acknowledge the support of York University’s Office of the Vice-President Research & Innovation, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies, and Department of Economics, as well as the Social Sciences & Humanities Research Council of Canada, the Canadian Economics Association’s Analysis Group, the Society for Nonlinear Dynamics & Econometrics, the Fields Institute and York University’s Catalyzing Interdisciplinary Research Cluster project “Digital Currencies.”\nFor more information about the event, visit caneconometrics.ca/annualMeeting/current/details.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-39th-annual-meeting-of-the-canadian-econometrics-study-group-cesg/
ORGANIZER;CN=Department of Economics:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Economics
END:VEVENT
