SUMMARY:Diversity and Inclusion Career Day: Mastering Leadership Coaching
DESCRIPTION:As a part of the Diversity and Inclusion Career Day, join us for an informative session on learning how to be a good coach and how coaches save impact and/or change lives? This session, facilitated by Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) Student Success Mentor Leads, dives into a brief overview of the BE YU program, followed by a quick icebreaker to get our day started. To finish our session off, we will be hosting a leadership workshop titled Leadership Coaching, focusing on the core components of coaching, what BE YU offers in terms of coaching for leaders, and how to find your coaching style.\nHow do I register?\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Career Centre” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nSelect “Workshops & Webinars”\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n
