SUMMARY:Exploring AI Security in Markham: York University, the City’s First University, Engages in Critical Discussions
DESCRIPTION:In the ever-evolving landscape of artificial intelligence (AI), the security implications of its applications have become a major focus for industries and academic institutions alike. On Thursday, Sept. 26, from noon to 2 p.m., Computek College is hosting a highly anticipated event, “AI’s Impact on Cybersecurity: What You Need to Know,” at the Toronto Marriott Markham, organized by the Markham Board of Trade.\nThis event is dedicated to exploring AI’s growing impact in the cybersecurity landscape and its increasing relevance in the business world. The luncheon will bring together industry leaders, innovators, and experts to discuss the latest advancements in AI technology and their applications across various sectors, focusing on the intersection of AI and cybersecurity.\nAmong the distinguished speakers, Arash Habibi Lashkari, a York University professor, will deliver an insightful talk and serve as a panel member. York University, a leader in technological research and education, plays a vital role in advancing the conversation on AI security. The University is particularly proud to have its Markham Campus represented at this prestigious event. As the first university and a hub of innovation and academic excellence in Markham, York University’s Markham Campus is at the forefront of the city’s educational and research initiatives, making it a key player in addressing emerging challenges in cybersecurity.\nThis event and York University’s involvement underscore the institution’s leadership in education, especially cybersecurity, and its role in preparing the next generation of leaders and innovators to tackle the challenges of an AI-driven future.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/exploring-ai-security-in-markham-york-university-the-citys-first-university-engages-in-critical-discussions/
ORGANIZER;CN=Markham Board of Trade (MBOT):MAILTO:smartins@markhamboard.com
CATEGORIES:Markham Campus
END:VEVENT
