SUMMARY:Moccasin Identifier: Learn about the Land Through Art Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join the team from Moccasin Identifier, from Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation, to learn about the traditional Indigenous\nlands that the new Markham campus is on through an art workshop. Learn more about traditional footwear and contribute to ongoing development of land-based art and learning on our new Markham campus at York University, as supported through York University’s Academic Innovation Fund, and our partners.\nDate: Monday, October 21, 2024\nTime: 2:30 p.m. – 5:00 p.m.\nAddress: York University Markham Campus – 1 University Boulevard | L6G 0A1\n2nd floor, near the Indigenous Circle, exit at Level 2 Entrance (outside).\nAn indoor space is available in case of rain.\nRegistration: Please register HERE ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/moccasin-identifier-learn-about-the-land-with-an-art-stencilling-workshop-tickets-999385347477?aff=oddtdtcreator ) as spots are limited.\nFor more information please contact Rebecca Caines at (rcaines@yorku.ca ( rcaines@yorku.ca ))\n
