SUMMARY:Diversity and Inclusion Career Day
DESCRIPTION:Session 1: Mastering Leadership Coaching \nTime: 10 to 10:45 a.m.\nPresenter(s): Becoming YU Team \nWhat does it mean to be a good coach? How can coaches save and/or change lives? This session, facilitated by Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) Student Success Mentor Leads, dives into a brief overview of the BE YU program, followed by a quick icebreaker to get our day started. To finish our session off, we will be hosting a leadership workshop titled Leadership Coaching, focusing on the core components of coaching, what BE YU offers in terms of coaching for leaders and how to find your coaching style. Register here: experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4308 ( https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4308 ).\nSession 2: Taking Up Space \nTime: 10:45 to 11:30 a.m.\nPresenter: Harriett Brempong\nIn this session, we will be discussing imposter syndrome. Join us to explore how to confidently “take up space” in your professional life. We’ll address overcoming self-doubt, crafting a strong professional image and using effective communication to assert your presence. Empower yourself to thrive and shine in your career. Register here: experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4309 ( https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4309 ).\nSession 3: Launching your Tech Career: Tools and Opportunities\nTime: 11:30 a.m. to noon\nPresenter: Madison Edwards, TECHNATION Canada\nDiscover essential tools to boost your career readiness for tech and tech-adjacent jobs. This session is designed to guide Black students through the landscape of tech and tech-adjacent opportunities, offering insights into building essential skills, accessing training and navigating industry challenges. Learn how TECHNATION’s Career Ready Program (a student work placement program SWPP) can support your career growth. Register here: experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4310 ( https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4310 ).\nSession 4: Employer Meet and Greet: Diversity & Inclusion Recruitment Event    \nTime: 1 to 3:30 p.m.\nMeet face-to-face with employers committed to equity, diversity and inclusion. During this event, you’ll have the opportunity to connect with organizations hiring for part-time, summer, internship and full-time positions after graduation while learning about their organization’s culture, hiring practices, and how you can apply for full-time positions after graduation and summer jobs/internships in 2025. Register here: experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4288 ( https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4288 ).\nSession 5: Indigenous Student & Employer Networking Session\nTime: 4 to 5 p.m.\nFollowing the Employer Meet & Greet Diversity & Inclusion Recruitment Event, CISS welcomes you to meet and mingle with employers and recruiters from various organizations in Canada in an intimate, casual setting. Enjoy some light refreshments and have fun getting to chat with different companies about your top career interests and what opportunities might be coming up at various organizations.\nRegister here: experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4311 ( https://experience.yorku.ca/entityRedirect.htm?eventId=4311 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/diversity-and-inclusion-career-day-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
