SUMMARY:How to prepare a successful President’s University-Wide Teaching Award file – Zoom information session
DESCRIPTION:The President’s University-Wide Teaching Award is a prestigious and unique award that encourages nominations from any member of the York University community, including the faculty member and teaching assistants themselves, their current and past students, their teaching assistants and their colleagues.\nJoin us for a panel discussion on preparing a winning President’s University-Wide Teaching Award file, moderated by Mehraneh Ebrahimi, Senate Award Committee Chair. Panellists include past Chairs and longtime Senate Awards Committee members, professors Robert Kenedy and Shayna Rosenbaum. Learn about the file preparation process and gain insights into the adjudication procedures.\nDate: Wednesday, Oct. 9\nTime: noon to 1:30 p.m.\nZoom link: yorku.zoom.us/j/2705198327\nAward call link: yorku.ca/secretariat/wp-content/uploads/sites/107/2024/09/Presidents-University-Wide-Teaching-Awards-Criteria-2025-1.pdf ( https://www.yorku.ca/secretariat/wp-content/uploads/sites/107/2024/09/Presidents-University-Wide-Teaching-Awards-Criteria-2025-1.pdf ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/how-to-prepare-a-presidents-university-wide-teaching-award-nomination/
