SUMMARY:2024 DARE Celebration Event
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies (LA&PS) is celebrating this year’s cohort of students who received the Dean’s Award for Research Excellence (DARE) this summer, with a special event on Tuesday, October 8 from 1:00 p.m. until 3:00 p.m. at the Scott Library’s Collaboratory.\nEach year, undergraduate students selected for the Dean’s Award for Research Excellence (DARE) receive $5,000 and the unique opportunity to work with a LA&PS faculty member on a designated research project. This year’s DARE Research Poster Session and Celebration features diverse projects from students enrolled in the programs that cross the entire spectrum of LA&PS.\nThe event does not require registration and is open to all.\nLearn more\n
