SUMMARY:Experience Grad York – Gender, Feminist & Women’s Studies
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Gender, Feminist & Women’s Studies? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEpfuCtqz4uHtAS6EUoVl-2_E4pBUHDxEoG )\nFounded 1991, the Gender, Feminist and Women’s Studies (GFWS) program is one of the largest Gender Studies programs in the world. One of our primary goals is to develop and apply a feminist analytical perspective to teaching and research on women and gender as they intersect with sexuality, race, ethnicity, class, ability and age. The program is interdisciplinary – drawing widely from the humanities, social sciences, environmental studies, fine arts, education and law.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/experience-grad-york-gender-feminist-womens-studies/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies
