SUMMARY:Robarts 40th Anniversary Lecture featuring M. NourebeSe Philip
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to attend the 40th anniversary Robarts Lecture, featuring the poet, novelist, playwright, and essayist M. NourebeSe Philip, who is launching a new edition of her acclaimed book-length poem Zong!  M. NourebeSe Philip is known for experimenting with literary form and their commitment to social justice, notably in Ontario. Through the innovative use of fugal and counterpointed repetition, Zong! becomes an anti-narrative lament that stretches the boundaries of the poetic form, haunting the spaces of forgetting and mourning the forgotten. Zong! has been disseminated in three dramatic performances by theatrical directors and excerpts of Zong! have been used in six different visual arts installations by different artists in five countries. This event is co-presented by Sensorium and the Department of Theatre, Dance and Performance.\nDate: September 12, 2024\nTime: 4:00 p.m. – 5:00 p.m.\nFollowed by a reception and book signing from 5:00 – 6:00 p.m.\nLocation: Joseph G. Green Studio Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/joseph-g-green-studio-theatre/ ), 151 Centre for Film and Theatre\nReception: Fireside Lounge, 150 Cente for Film and Theatre\nRSVP: to robarts@yorku.ca\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/robarts-40th-anniversary-lecture-featuring-m-nourebese-philip/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Joe G. Green Theatre, Centre for Film and Theatre @ York University, 4700 Keele Street, Toronto, ON
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/M.-NourebeSe-Philip.jpg
END:VEVENT
