SUMMARY:National Day for Truth and Reconciliation Film Screening Glendon Campus (Hebron Relocation + Honour to Murray Sinclair)
DESCRIPTION:Please join us in honouring National Day for Truth and Reconciliation 2024.\nWe will be hosting a film screening of two short films: Hebron Relocation (15 minutes) and Honour to Murray Sinclair (29 minutes), followed by a brief reflection and discussion with Amy Gaukel, senior executive officer in the Division of Equity, People & Culture.\nHebron Relocation\nThrough touching conversations with community members, Andersen guides us with care as she learns about their stories of relocation and reflects on what it has meant for their families. By weaving together intimate stories from her community with rare footage that gives us a glimpse of community life during this upheaval, Andersen provides a heartfelt look at a difficult past that has changed the lives of Labrador Inuit forever.\nHonour to Murray Sinclair\nAs the Chair of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission, Senator Murray Sinclair was a key figure in raising global awareness of the atrocities of Canada’s residential school system. The honouring of Senator Sinclair reminds us to honour the lives and legacies of the tens of thousands of Indigenous children taken from their homes and cultures, and leaves us with a profound feeling of hope for a better future.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/national-day-for-truth-and-reconciliation-film-screening-5/
CATEGORIES:ND4TR
LOCATION:A100 - Centre of Excellence, Glendon Campus - York University @ 2275 Bayview Ave, North York, ON M4N 3M6, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/23062-ND4TR_Events-Banner-5-scaled.jpg
