SUMMARY:Theatre@York presents People, Places, and Things
DESCRIPTION:Emma was having the time of her life. Now she’s in rehab. Her first step is to admit that she has a problem. But the problem isn’t with Emma, it’s with everything else. She needs to tell the truth. But she’s smart enough to know that there’s no such thing. When intoxication feels like the only way to survive the modern world, how can she ever sober up?\nPeople, Places, and Things\nby Duncan Macmillan\nDirected by Andrew Moodie\nProduced and Designed by Production/Design students\nActed by 4th year Acting students\nPerformance Schedule\nMarch 22, 2025 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview)\nMarch 23, 2025 – 7:30 p.m. (Preview)\nMarch 25, 2025 – 7:30 p.m. (Opening)\nMarch 26, 2025 – 1:00 p.m. | 7:30 pm\nMarch 27, 2025 – 7:30 p.m.\nMarch 28, 2025 – 1:00 p.m. | 7:30 pm\nMarch 29, 2025 – 2:00 p.m. (Closing)\nLocation: Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/sandra-faire-and-ivan-fecan-theatre/ ), Accolade East Building.\nTickets\nPreview Tickets (March 22 & 23):  $ 10.00\nRegular Tickets: $ 20.00\nOnline advance ticket purchasing highly recommended. Purchase tickets HERE ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/index.asp ).\n\n
