SUMMARY:The Entrepreneurial Strategy: How entrepreneurship can bolster community and economic development
DESCRIPTION:Sustainable Economic Growth and Prosperity Speaker Series\nThe United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) provide a comprehensive framework for addressing global challenges and achieving sustainable development. This webinar will explore how the SDGs can be the foundation for economic development, growth and prosperity. Presenters will explore how the SDGs can be integrated into day-to-day activities to effectively create positive economic, social and environmental impacts in their communities. The series will cover various topics that play a role in sustainable economic development, including entrepreneurship; equity, diversity and inclusion; supply chain management; import/export; water management; and community development.\nSpeaker: Dana Abou Shackra, entrepreneurship programs specialist\nRegister: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_g2V224fKQfWHpQsx4lRwWA#/registration.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-entrepreneurial-strategy-how-entrepreneurship-can-bolster-community-and-economic-development/
