DESCRIPTION:Join this webinar to explore the further education landscape and gain tips on how to research graduate programs, post-degree college programs, skilled trades, and potential schools of interest. You will also be introduced to online resources and York’s campus support to help you succeed. In collaboration with the Faculty of Graduate Studies (FGS) and York’s Writing Centre.\n** PLEASE NOTE THIS WILL BE AN ONLINE WEBINAR**\nTo participate in a webinar, you will need a computer (with speakers or headphones), internet access, and a Zoom desktop application (Zoom) installed on your computer. After registering for the event, you will receive the webinar URL and meeting ID in a reminder email. On the day of the event, you will join the webinar and ask your questions via chat, or, you can participate via telephone at 1.647.558.0588\nHow do I register?\n\n\nTo register for this event, follow the steps below:\n\nLog-in to Experience York ( https://experience.yorku.ca/home/home.htm )\nSelect “Career Centre” in the menu on the left-hand side of the page\nSelect “Workshops & Webinars”\nNavigate to the event you want to register for in the events calendar\nSelect the event and click the “Register for the event” button in the event listing\n\n\n\n
