SUMMARY:SmartTO & MathWorks Coffee, Bagels & Tech
DESCRIPTION:Come grab a coffee, have a bagel and learn about rapid prototyping with our partner, MathWorks.\nMathWorks, the maker of MATLAB and Simulink software – which are widely used in engineering globally for design, analysis and simulation – provides 12 months of free access to all of their software (up to 10 licences per startup) and engineering support to our startup members.\nIn this session, you’ll learn how MATLAB and Simulink are used in the development of algorithms, including implementation and testing on hardware. Our demonstration will emphasize how to design, simulate and test a complex system that incorporates multiple domains such as mechanical, electrical and hydraulic – that are typically isolated across different software platforms and thus not simulated in a common framework. This, in turn, accelerates the pace of product development.\nDuring our presentation, we’ll demonstrate how to:\n\ndesign and optimize the control system, and simulate the control system and plant model together;\ngenerate code for hardware-in-the-loop testing and rapid prototyping, and demonstrate how you can test your models in real-time with actual hardware; and\ndevelop and deploy MATLAB algorithms and Simulink models as digital twin.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/smartto-mathworks-coffee-bagels-tech/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of the Vice President Research and Innovation:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
