SUMMARY:Geographic Information Systems (GIS) Day 2024
DESCRIPTION:Attention all secondary school educators (Grades 9 to 12)!\nJoin us for an engaging and informative day dedicated to all things GIS! Whether you’re a seasoned expert or just beginning your journey with Geographic Information Systems, this event has something for everyone. Dive into exciting discussions, hands-on workshops and insightful presentations, all designed to enhance your understanding and application of GIS.\nConnect with fellow educators and GIS enthusiasts, and learn from industry experts in a fun and interactive environment. This is more than just a learning opportunity – it’s a celebration of the transformative power of GIS.\nMark your calendar for GIS Day on Nov. 20 at Keele Campus. We warmly invite you to bring your students along for a day of discovery and inspiration. Stay tuned for a detailed agenda, which will be shared closer to the event.\nDon’t miss out on this chance to expand your knowledge, network with peers and celebrate the impact of GIS.\nRegister here: eventbrite.ca/e/geographic-information-systems-gis-day-2024-tickets-965041032707.\nFor any questions, contact Brittany at eucapply@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/geographic-information-systems-gis-day-2024/
