SUMMARY:Advancing YU Women and Black Students’ Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Are you considering joining Advancing YU? Are you a Black or woman-identifying student? You may seek guidance and mentorship from esteemed alumni with a similar lived experience. Or want to enhance your professional development skills as an upper-year student (with 54+ credits)? If that resonates with you, and you’re a student at LA&PS Colleges, you’re invited to join the Advancing YU team and alumni on Oct. 2nd from 12-2 pm in VC 001 to learn more about the Advancing YU program. You will learn about the program requirements, receive critical advice and feedback on your application, and hear from program alumni. During this event, students will also have an opportunity to network and mingle with LA&PS staff and esteemed alumni. Light refreshments will be provided; please bring a resume if you’re interested in the program.\nRegister Now\n
