SUMMARY:Theatre, Dance & Performance Studies VIRTUAL Info Session (MA, PhD) – FA25 Admissions
DESCRIPTION:If you are interested in applying to the MA or PhD program in Theatre, Dance & Performance Studies, please join us for our admissions (FA25) information session on Monday, Nov. 4 at 3:30 p.m. The session will take place online, via Zoom. Registration is required.\nTo register, please select the following link: yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0kduuhpjkuGNfU3WS2kfFT56usidhis8Vl.\nAttendees will have the chance to learn about the admissions process, including application requirements, deadlines and selection criteria. We will also address any specific questions you may have about program structure, funding options and support services available to students. This session is an excellent opportunity to gain insights into how our programs can align with your academic and career goals.\nWe encourage you to bring any questions you have about the programs or the application process, as the graduate program director, Marlis Schweitzer, and graduate program assistant, Julia Kenny, will be available to provide detailed answers and guidance. For any inquiries in the meantime, please contact the Graduate Program Office at gradthea@yorku.ca ( mailto:gradthea@yorku.ca ).\nRefreshments and snacks will be provided.\nWe look forward to virtually meeting you!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tdps-info-session-ma-phd-fa25-admissions-2/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp; Performance Studies,Recruitment,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
