SUMMARY:Experience Grad York – Theatre, Dance & Performance Studies
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Theatre, Dance & Performance Studies? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEvd-yppzkvHNWsKlRuzMfKxMTA9NnjWAgV )\nThe MA and PhD programs in Theatre, Dance, and Performance Studies emphasize our collective interest in theatre, dance, performance, and cultural politics. Students explore performances across a broad range of periods and cultural contexts, both on stage and in everyday life, to highlight the cultural, political, material and ideological dimensions of performance practices. Specializations include: Canadian Theatre & Cultural Politics; Postcolonialism & Globalization; Critical Pedagogy & Community Engagement; Embodiment & Cultural Memory.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/experience-grad-york-theatre-dance-performance-studies/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp; Performance Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Online Zoom
