SUMMARY:Anita McBride Mentorship Event – Call for MES Alumni Mentors
DESCRIPTION:Attention master of environmental studies (MES) alumni!\nThe Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) invites you to participate at our upcoming Anita McBride Mentoring Workshop on Oct. 29 from 9 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.\nThe Anita McBride Mentoring Workshop is an annual event for MES students and alumni, consisting of a panel presentation and speed networking sessions. We invite alumni from various sectors and fields of work to participate as mentors during the second half of the event. Connect with first-year MES students about how to navigate their time in the program, how to identify the career pathways that exist post-graduation, as well as share tips on navigating the current labour market.\nJoin us in supporting MES students as they navigate their academic and professional journeys. RSVP via this form by Oct. 1 to indicate your interest in joining us a mentor. ( https://euc.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=242425 )\nWe look forward to your participation in this rewarding opportunity to contribute to the success of our MES community.\nFor more information, contact Joanne Huy, alumni engagement officer, at johuy@yorku.ca ( mailto:johuy@yorku.ca ).\n–\n McBride is the former director of the FES Office of Student & Academic Services. She began working at the Faculty in 1972 and retired in 1999.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/anita-mcbride-mentorship-event-call-for-mes-alumni-mentors/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies
LOCATION:Health, Nursing &amp; Environmental Studies (HNES 140) @ York University
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/FES_students122222-scaled-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
