SUMMARY:Mature Student Orientation (In-Person Session)
DESCRIPTION:Join us on this transformative journey, where we empower you to thrive as a mature student.\nResiliency, Resources & Reflection: Navigating University Life as a Mature Student\nThis orientation session focuses on building resilience and thriving strategies specifically tailored for mature students. We will explore the five-factor model of resilience, practical techniques, campus resources and self-reflection to empower you on your academic journey.\nLearning outcomes:\n\nLearn Diana Brecher’s five-factor model of resilience and how it contributes to flourishing as a mature student.\nDiscover various campus resources that support your well-being and academic success.\nExplore positive reflection techniques to enhance resilience and personal growth. Learn how to seamlessly integrate resilience and resources into your university life\n\nRegister Now!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mature-student-orientation-in-person-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=ACMAPS:MAILTO:acmaps@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Ad