SUMMARY:Resonant Futures: Sensorium x Vector Fest Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Sensorium: Centre for Digital Art and Technology ( https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/ ) is proud to partner with InterAccess ( https://interaccess.org/ ) as an exhibition site for the 2024 Vector Festival. Resonant Futures showcases work by Sensorium members that explores the intersection of technology and new media artwork, focusing on disintegration, decomposition and obsolete technology.\nThe works featured include:\n𝘚𝘶𝘯 (𝘓𝘪𝘴𝘵𝘦𝘯) | Sana Akram\n𝘔𝘢𝘨𝘪𝘤 𝘓𝘦𝘢𝘱𝘵 | Nick Fox-Gieg\n𝘏𝘰𝘭𝘰𝘯𝘪𝘤 𝘊𝘩𝘰𝘳𝘶𝘴 | Grace Grothaus, Kwame Kyei-Boateng, Eyal Assaf, Ilze Briede\n𝘙𝘶𝘪𝘯 | Mary Bunch, Dolleen Tisawii’ashii Manning\nOpening Reception: Friday, July 12, 5-9 pm\nExhibition Hours: Saturday, July 13 – Friday, July 19 – 12-5 pm\nLocation:  Joan and Martin Goldfarb Centre, ( https://maps.info.yorku.ca/2010/06/joan-martin-goldfarb-centre-for-fine-arts/ ) CFA 326\nFREE Admission\nImage credit: Sana Akram\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/resonant-futures-sensorium-x-vector-fest-exhibition/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/vector.jpg
END:VEVENT
