SUMMARY:2024 MYPAC Walking Tour at The Well
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we discover new and exciting Toronto hotspot The Well!\nThis free walking tour explores the recently constructed, integrated, mixed-use project in downtown Toronto’s King West area. Chris Edey, York University professor and executive with RioCan, will take us through the vast property and teach us about its origins and construction. Following the tour, let’s enjoy some food and drink together at one of the many restaurants that The Well has to offer. Register now!\nMYPAC Walking Tour at The Well\nWhen: 📅Friday, Sept. 6 at 4 p.m.\nWhere: 📍486 Front St. W., Toronto, M5V 0V2\nCost: Free with optional 💲pay-your-own-way food and drink\n🔗Registration is required: euc.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=246636.\n\nAbout MYPAC\n\n\nThe MES York Planning Alumni Committee (MYPAC) was formed in 2004 by several York U alumni, students and faculty members. MYPAC’s initiatives include the following:\n\n\nhost the annual MYPAC social;\n\n\nmanage the MYPAC mentorship program;\n\n\nraise money for student initiatives and events; and\n\n\nsupport speaking programs.\n\n\nIf you have any questions about MYPAC initiatives, email mypac.executive@gmail.com\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2024-mypac-walking-tour-at-the-well/
ORGANIZER;CN=MES @ York Planning Alumni Commitee:MAILTO:mypacexecutive@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:486 Front St W, Toronto, Ontario M5V 0V2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/The-Well-2023-117-1-scaled.jpg
