SUMMARY:York University Black Alumni Network (YUBAN) Drop-in Mentoring Session
DESCRIPTION:Join the York University Black Alumni Network (YUBAN) for an exclusive drop-in mentorship and support session! Following our successful Black Grad celebration, we’re thrilled to offer additional hands-on support to new students and recent graduates seeking more time with YUBAN.\nWhether you need assistance with career and interview skills, navigating the workforce, or exploring specific fields, our team is dedicated to helping you succeed! Explore the diverse topics our YUBAN members are experienced in below:\n\nFikayo Aderoju (BA ’22) – Public Speaking, Content Marketing, Non-Profit Work, Career Development\nJoannes Yimbesalu (MA ’20) – International Development, Workforce Development, Community Engagement, Youth Development\nVictoria Medley-Perkins (BA ’20) – Disability Management, Student Affairs/Housing, Equity, Diversity, Inclusion, Indigeneity and Anti-Racism (EDII-A) Work, Post Graduate Work Permit (PGWP) Navigation\nAishah Imran (BA, BPA ’22) – Economics, Public Policy, Fraud Analyzation, Student Advising\nKobe Cargill (BSc ’23) – Personal Training, Student Success Advisor, Data Management, Intercultural Communication\n\nDate: July 18\nTime: 6-8 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\nDon’t miss out—register now! We look forward to seeing you there!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/yuban-drop-in-mentoring-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=Office of Alumni Engagement:MAILTO:alumni@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
LOCATION:Zoom Session
