SUMMARY:Restaurant Brands International Summer Virtual Group Coffee Chats
DESCRIPTION:Restaurant Brands International is hosting a series of virtual group coffee chats where students can connect with past Campus Program alumni to learn more about the organization, culture and various entry-level positions and programs offered. RBI is known for their coffee chat culture, which they start early in the recruitment process.  \nCoffee chats are an informal way for RBI employees to connect with top talent before the applications are live for both internships and full-time roles. The Coffee Chat series will be hosted over 4 weeks, with chats scheduled from June 17 to July 12.\nWhat You Need & How to Apply:  \n\nCurrently enrolled at an accredited Canadian college or university, in one of the following programs: \n\nUndergraduate degree – ideally in business administration, economics, sociology, psychology, supply/operations management, or hospitality management with an expected graduation by August 2025 or 2026 (Junior or Senior student). \n\n\nPlease submit a current copy of your resumé. \n\nLearn more: https://careers.rbi.com/global/en/urstudent. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/rbi-summer-virtual-group-coffee-chats/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advising,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Faculties,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students
END:VEVENT
