SUMMARY:Addressing and Responding to Sexual Harassment and Discrimination
DESCRIPTION:In this interactive session, participants will become familiar with the legislation and policies that define sexual harassment and gain a general understanding of why sexual harassment continues to be pervasive in our society. Attendees will examine various scenarios aimed at obtaining strategies and sharing best practices on how to identify, prevent and respond to instances of sexual harassment on campus.\nRegister on YU Learn: yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=1249.\nFor more information, visit: 2024 Summer Workshops – Centre for Human Rights, Equity and Inclusion (yorku.ca) and YU Learn | Employee Learning & Development at York University.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/addressing-and-responding-to-sexual-harassment-and-discrimination/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Pride Month
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
END:VEVENT
