SUMMARY:Mass Evacuation and First Nations
DESCRIPTION:Governance, Science & Technology of Mass Evacuations Speaker Series\nMass Evacuation and First Nations\nFeaturing:\n\nTara K. McGee, professor, University of Alberta;\nJennifer Jesty, emergency resiliency manager, Union of Nova Scotia Mi’kmaq;\nMaia Foster-Sanchez, Stronger Together: Evacuation Partnerships; and\nMichelle Gervais, Stronger Together: Evacuation Partnerships.\n\nModerated by Eric Kennedy, York University.\nVirtual Session 2 | Tuesday, June 18, 2 to 3 p.m. EDT; 3 to 4 p.m. ADT; 11 a.m. to 12 p.m. PD.\nRegister: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_SOz-LHPcRl2WNRIRGJ8MAQ#/registration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_SOz-LHPcRl2WNRIRGJ8MAQ#/registration ).\n
