SUMMARY:Pride 2024 Opening Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Join the Centre for Human Rights, Equity & Inclusion for the York University Pride 2024 Opening Ceremony on Tuesday, June 4 from 1 to 2:30 p.m. at the Vari Hall Rotunda.\nThe ceremony will feature opening remarks followed by the unfurling of the Pride flag. Attendees can enjoy free treats – provided by the Office of the Vice-Provost Students – snap a selfie with York’s mascot, Yeo, and learn about 2SLGBTQIA+ resources and services available at York. Engage in the conversation on social media using #YUPride and share what a campus free of homophobia and transphobia looks like, feels like and sounds like to you.\nAll York community members are welcome.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/pride-2024-opening-ceremony/
