SUMMARY:Sound and Sense: Jewish Music @ York –  David Eisenstadt
DESCRIPTION:The Koschitzky Centre for Jewish Studies ( https://www.yorku.ca/cjs/ ) and the Department of Music in the School of the Arts, Media, Performance and Design  ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/ ) present Under the Radar: Notable Canadian Jewish Musicians.\nWhat do The Diamonds, Jerry Gray & The Travellers, Moe Koffman, Marc Jordan, Sophie Milman and Howard Shore have in common? All are chaptered in David Eisenstadt’s first book -Under The Radar – 30 Notable Canadian Jewish Musicians. 24 other talented performers are also featured. Join us for a fun evening where David will discuss his insights about many of the performers and share some of their music.\nDavid Eisenstadt is a Public Relations Consultant who at the outset of the Covid pandemic began a hobby writing columns about Canadian Jewish musicians. Writing for various online publications, the columns morphed into a special collection – two books (Under The Radar – 30 Notable Canadian Jewish Musicians AND Musicians Under The Radar – 36 Notable Canadian Jewish Performers).\nThe “Sound and Sense: Jewish Music @York” series is supported by the Azrieli Foundation.\nSunday, May 26, 2024\nZoom \n7:00 pm\nReserve your spot HERE ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/under-the-radar-notable-canadian-jewish-musicians-tickets-891636898967?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sound-and-sense-jewish-music-york-david-eisenstadt/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Online event via Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/book.jpg
