SUMMARY:Carbon Pricing, Federalism and the Future of Canadian Climate Policy
DESCRIPTION:The Sustainable Energy Initiative at the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change presents:\nCarbon Pricing, Federalism and the Future of Canadian Climate Policy\nWebinar\nFriday, May 24, 12:30 to 2 p.m. Eastern\n(2 p.m. NFLD; 10:30 a.m. Mountain; 9:30 a.m. Pacific)\nDespite the growing evidence of the impacts of a changing climate, including last summer’s record wildfires, Canadian climate policy, and especially carbon pricing, has become a focal point for intensifying federal-provincial conflicts and political challenges at the federal and provincial levels.\n \nJoin us for a discussion on the future of Canadian climate policy, featuring leading researchers from across Canada.\nSpeakers will include: \nAngela Carter: Canada Research Chair in Equitable Energy Governance and Public Policy, Memorial University of Newfoundland and Labrador, St. John’s\nPierre Olivier Pineau: Research Chair in Energy Sector Management, HEC, Montreal.\nMark Winfield: Professor and SEI Co-Chair, Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change, York University, Toronto.\nKeith Brownsey:  Professor, Economics, Justice and Policy Studies, Mount Royal University, Calgary.\nGeorge Hoberg: Professor, School of Public Policy and Global Affairs, UBC, Vancouver\nChair: \nRuna Das, Associate Professor, Interdisciplinary Studies, Royal Roads University, Victoria.\nREGISTER HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJArcOirrDsoHNdnbNgluxRW0KaEYnCDARIU ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/carbon-pricing-federalism-and-the-future-of-canadian-climate-policy/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
