SUMMARY:Mitacs GRI Information Session
DESCRIPTION:Interested in hosting a student for research during summer 2025? York International and Mitacs will be hosting an information session to answer faculty members’ questions about the Mitacs GRI 2025 submission process.\nRegister: yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0pdeygrz4uG9J2KErnY16olwCyR1bOkM5d.\nMitacs Globalink Research Internship is a competitive initiative for international undergraduates from the following countries and regions: Australia, Brazil, Chile, China, Colombia, France, Germany, Hong Kong, India, Mexico, Pakistan, South Korea, Taiwan, Tunisia, Ukraine, the United Kingdom and the United States. From May to October of each year, top-ranked applicants participate in a 12-week research internship under the supervision of Canadian university faculty members in a variety of academic disciplines, from science, engineering and mathematics to the humanities and social sciences. Mitacs Globalink Research Internships can offer students an international experience like no other. Canada features excellent academic institutions, outstanding research facilities, cutting-edge industry innovation and unparalleled undergraduate training opportunities.\nThe Globalink Research Internship (GRI) call for faculty project submissions for the summer of 2025 is now open. To submit your project, visit globalink.mitacs.ca/#/prof.\nThe deadline for submissions is June 4 at 1 p.m. PT.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mitacs-gri-information-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=York International:MAILTO:goglobal@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculties,International,Research &amp; Innovation,Teaching &amp; Learning
LOCATION:Virtually via Zoom
END:VEVENT
