SUMMARY:2024 Critical Social Science Perspectives in Global Health Research Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The Dahdaleh Institute for Global Health Research invites all to attend the fifth annual Critical Social Science Perspectives in Global Health Research Workshop on Tuesday, April 30.\nParticipants will engage with the research community at York University to generate new insights, foster collaboration, and discover new research opportunities in global health research with critical social science perspectives that uses social science theory and methodology with social justice aims in global health. It is transdisciplinary, participatory, experimental, or experiential. It seeks greater effectiveness, equity, and excellence in global health by engaging directly with global public health actors, structures, and systems to transform global public health.\nThis year, Professor Cary Wu (Department of Sociology, York University) will be delivering the keynote presentation titled “A triple trust penalty? The majority-minority gap in subjective wellbeing.”\nLearn more and register: yorku.ca/dighr/events/2024-cpgh-workshop-2.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2024-critical-social-science-perspectives-in-global-health-research-workshop-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=Dahdaleh Institute for Global Health Research:MAILTO:dighr@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,International,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,Lassonde School of Engineering,Osgoode Hall Law School,Research &amp; Innovation,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Students
LOCATION:Hybrid, link will be sent after RSVP form is submitted
