SUMMARY:Ipsos Private Event for Graduating Students – Apply by April 15,
DESCRIPTION:Ipsos would like to extend an invitation to our upcoming private event tailored for currently graduating students from bachelor’s degree or higher programs in analytical or insights-focused fields, such as economics, marketing, psychology, sociology, statistics, or similar business or liberal arts programs.\nThe event is scheduled for April 26th, from 10 am to 2 pm, and will be held at our Toronto Office. We are excited to offer attendees the opportunity to learn more about Ipsos, our culture, and the career opportunities we have available, including our Summer Internship and Early Career positions (links for your reference, other positions available are posted on our career page). Lunch will be provided during the event, and there will also be a networking session with our hiring teams at the end of the day. We believe this event will be an excellent opportunity for students to engage with our professionals and learn more about potential career paths at Ipsos.\nAs we have a limited capacity, we would like to ensure we connect with the best talent coming out from your programs.\nIf interested please submit you  resume to Mara.Correch@ipsos.com by Monday April 15, 2024, EOD. We will extend the invitation directly to them. \nIf you are not the appropriate contact for this matter, please direct me to the appropriate individual who can assist us. We look forward to potentially collaborating with your institution and meeting the talented students you recommend.\nLastly, we wanted to share the?Why Work at Ipsos? ( https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HwUcWpYLJJc )page which showcases many of the great reasons to work at Ipsos!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ipsos-private-event-for-graduating-students-apply-by-april-15/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
LOCATION:Off-campus
