TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Osgoode’s Internationally Trained Lawyers Day (OITLD)
DESCRIPTION:We’re celebrating Osgoode’s 10th annual Internationally Trained Lawyers Day!\nOsgoode’s Internationally Trained Lawyers Day (OITLD) is a unique opportunity that brings together diverse, internationally trained talent with experienced members of the Canadian legal community to discuss tips and strategies on how to make your international training stand out in the Canadian legal landscape.\nDesigned for lawyers and law graduates from around the globe, as well as those navigating the process of accreditation or licensing independently, OITLD provides comprehensive insights into the unique paths and partnerships available to help you thrive in the Canadian legal profession.\nThis year, as we celebrate a decade of empowering internationally trained legal professionals, we’ve extended our event to span two enriching days! Mark your calendars for Tuesday, May 28 and Wednesday, May 29.\nJoin us in person for the full day or register to be part of our morning sessions online. Here’s a glimpse of what you can expect. ( http://osgoodepd.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/OITLD24-Agenda.pdf )\nRegister today to save your spot!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/osgoodes-internationally-trained-lawyers-day-oitld-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=Osgoode Professional Development:MAILTO:OsgoodePD@osgoode.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Osgoode Hall Law School
LOCATION:Moot Court, Room 1005 | Osgoode Building | Keele Campus | York University
END:VEVENT
