TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:In a ‘Land of Hope’: Documents on the Canadian Jewish Experience, 1627-1923 – Pierre Anctil and Richard Menkis in Conversation with David S. Koffman
DESCRIPTION:Join us in conversation with esteemed historians Pierre Anctil and Richard Menkis about their new primary source reader, In a “Land of Hope”: Documents on the Canadian Jewish Experience, 1627-1923. This book represents the world’s first effort to present an expansive portrait of Canadian Jewish life using original documents. It draws from archives coast to coast to coast, selecting a wide host of subjects and voices in multiple languages, from the earliest days of Jewish presence in what would become Canada to the inter-war era of immigration restriction. Anctil and Menkis will be interviewed by York’s David S. Koffman. Open Q-and-A to follow. A discount code for the book will be shared.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/in-a-land-of-hope-documents-on-the-canadian-jewish-experience-1627-1923-pierre-anctil-and-richard-menkis-in-conversation-with-david-s-koffman/
ORGANIZER;CN=Israel and Golda Koschitzky Centre for Jewish Studies:MAILTO:cjs@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
