SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub | Elusive Desires and the Aesthetics of Difference
DESCRIPTION:Who gets written out of dominant representations of the suburbs? Focusing on her curatorial projects and research in the Toronto suburb of Markham, York assistant professor Marissa Largo discusses the potential of aesthetics to show us other ways of being in the world that consider racial, class, gender, and sexual difference with an ethic of care. Join Marissa on April 18 at 7 p.m. for Scholars’ Hub at the Markham Public Library, Markham Village Branch, to learn more.\n\n
