SUMMARY:(Online) Black Students Careers Community: Ace That Interview! (Job Search Workshops)
DESCRIPTION:Workshop 4: Ace That Interview!\nInterviews are not only a chance for an employer to find out about you… But for you to find out about them! Are you the right fit for each other? In this session:\n\nWe’ll go through different types of interviews\nDiscuss common questions and build answers\nReview the STAR technique\nTalk about presenting yourself professionally in interviews.\n\n—\nThroughout the 23/24 academic year, we’ll be running career development workshops for Black students. These sessions are designed to be fun, safe, inclusive spaces, through the lens of systemic factors that affect our career decisions – designed to help you to develop your own career success.\nAll sessions can be booked through Experience York.\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Career Centre calendar.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/online-black-students-careers-community-ace-that-interview-job-search-workshops/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
