SUMMARY:York U Motion Media Studio: Worldbuilding with Sound
DESCRIPTION:York U Motion Media ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/motion-media-studio/ ) is excited to host this outstanding opportunity to learn from an expert panel, and explore the ways sonic world-building can elevate your artistic work.\nDate: Thursday, April 18, 2024\nTime: Panel (6:00 – 7:30 p.m.) | Social Mixer ( 7:30 – 9:00 p.m.)\nLocation: York U Motion Media Studios is located at Cinespace Film Studios ( https://maps.app.goo.gl/XWb48cU4V1ubZTdu9 ) ( 777 Kipling Ave, Etobicoke, ON M8Z 5Z4)\nRSVP for access: yumms@yorku.ca ( mailto:yumms@yorku.ca )\nFeaturing award-winning sound artists and scholars.\nDebashis Sinha (moderator), distinguished composer and sonic artist at TMU.\nHector Centeno Garcia (panelist), accomplished digital media artist.\nDr. Rebecca Caines (panelist), esteemed scholar investigating the intersection of new media and sound art. \nBy uniting individuals with unique approaches to constructing narrative through sound, we hope to engage an audience, encompassing students, scholars, artists, podcasters, and producers.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-u-motion-media-studio-worldbuilding-with-sound/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:777 Kipling Ave, Toronto M8Z 5Z4
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/sound.jpg
END:VEVENT
