SUMMARY:ONxpress (Recruitment Session)
DESCRIPTION:Dive into the heart of Canada’s largest transit project and discover a world of opportunities with ONxpress Operations Inc. As we embark on transforming the Greater Toronto and Hamilton Area’s transit system, they’re on the lookout for passionate, innovative minds to join their team. Whether you’re just starting your career or looking for a new challenge, this webinar is your gateway to making a significant impact.\nWhy Attend?\nExplore Diverse Roles: Learn about the various positions ONxpress Operations Inc. is hiring for, including Cybersecurity, Revenue Vehicle Maintenance, Fixed Asset Management, Mobilization, Train Service Controllers, Train Crew, HR, Legal, and Finance. Find out how each role contributes to their mission and how you can fit into our grand vision.\nMeet the Team: Hear directly from the leaders and team members about what it’s like to work on this groundbreaking project. Discover our culture of innovation, inclusion, and teamwork.\nGet Insider Insights: Gain valuable insights into ONxpress’s hiring process and what they’re looking for in candidates.\nAsk Your Questions: Have your queries answered in a live Q&A session. Whether it’s about the roles, the project, or life at ONxpress, we’re here to provide clarity.\n\nAbout the Speaker\nChloe, ONxpress’s esteemed Diversity, Inclusion, Equity & Belonging Lead and Early Careers Program Lead, will guide you through the webinar. With over 12 years of talent acquisition experience, including 4 years dedicated to campus recruitment, Chloe has a wealth of knowledge and insights to share. She’s passionate about nurturing talent and creating opportunities for growth and development within ONxpress Operations Inc.\nJoining Chloe is Bhumika Bhandari, a recent addition to the ONxpress team as a Talent Acquisition Coordinator. A proud graduate of the University of Waterloo with a degree in Honours Psychology and Business, Bhumika brings over a year of experience in the recruitment industry, with a focus on both experienced and campus recruitment. She is deeply committed to advancing Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) within the workplace and hiring practices. Bhumika is eager to partner on more DEI and Campus initiatives, bringing her fresh perspectives and innovative ideas to ONxpress Operations Inc.\nTogether, they will provide invaluable insights into the opportunities at ONxpress, sharing their expertise on talent acquisition, DEI, and how these practices shape the future of the workplace.\nDon’t Miss This Chance\nWhether you’re a current student or graduating soon, this webinar is your first step toward a rewarding career with ONxpress Operations Inc. Be part of a project that’s not just about enhancing transit but also about creating sustainable, inclusive communities.\nRegister now to secure your spot and discover how you can contribute to a historic project while advancing your career. We look forward to welcoming you to the ONxpress family!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Employer Events calendar.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/onxpress-recruitment-session/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
LOCATION:Online
END:VEVENT
