TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:CIBC Breaking Barriers – Diversifying Capital Markets Summer 2025 – Register by Mar 24
DESCRIPTION:\nThe Capital Markets Early Talent team at CIBC is hosting our Breaking Barriers: Diversifying Capital Markets Summer 2025 Early Talent Recruitment Event, with the aim to increase applications to our summer programs from talent segments who are currently under-represented in Capital Markets. Priority will be made for students who self-identify as one or more under-represented communities, for example, people of colour, including members of the Black community, Indigenous peoples (i.e., First Nations, Inuit or Métis peoples), persons with disabilities, members of the LGBTQ+ community and women. This event will be held on April 4th 2024, in person at our CIBC office in Toronto. This is an invite-only event and you will need to receive confirmation from the Campus team at CIBC to attend.\nAre you currently enrolled in an undergraduate program and are interested in learning more about a career at CIBC Capital Markets? Are you interested in learning more about our inclusive culture here at the bank? This is your chance to connect with CIBC professionals across Global Investment Banking, Corporate Banking and Global Markets during an in-person networking event to learn if it’s the right fit for you. Through this event, you will learn more about our culture, the business, people networks, and how we will support you during your student term as well as Summer 2025 student opportunities & recruitment timelines.\nYou will have the opportunity to experience our state-of-the-art global headquarters at CIBC Square while networking with industry professionals. You’ll engage with members of the Capital Markets business, campus recruiters and members of our Inclusion team.\nIf you cannot attend this event in-person, please sign up for the virtual option here.\nIf you are selected to attend this event, you will receive an invitation to the email address you provide us, along with additional information about the event. Please note that space is limited, and selection is first come first served.\nImportant information\nYou are enrolled in an undergraduate degree with a graduation date no sooner than April 2026 and are looking for a Summer 2025 internship.\nLocation: This event will be held in-person at CIBC in Toronto.\nEvent applications will close on March 24th 2024 at 11:59PM EST. Please monitor your email address for an invitation from the CIBC team.\nRegister using this link – https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/campus/job/Toronto-ON/Campus-Event–Breaking-Barriers—Diversifying-Capital-Markets-Summer-2025–April-4th-2024-_2406592 ( https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/campus/job/Toronto-ON/Campus-Event--Breaking-Barriers---Diversifying-Capital-Markets-Summer-2025--April-4th-2024-_2406592 )\nHow you’ll succeed\nMeet Industry Leaders  ?  Network with our experienced professionals across Capital Markets and gain career insights from our representatives to help prepare you for your next student opportunity at CIBC.\nNetworking  ?  Have opportunities to build your network and connect with members of the Capital Markets Early Talent Team.\nCommunication  ?  Leverage your communication skills through active listening and learning, providing feedback and asking questions.\nWho you are\nYou love to learn. You’re passionate about growing your knowledge. You have a strong sense of curiosity.\nYou’re goal oriented. You’re motivated by accomplishing your goals and delivering your best to make a difference.\nYou’re passionate about people. You find meaning in relationships and surround yourself with a diverse network of partners. You connect with others through respect and authenticity.\nValues matter to you. You bring your real self to work and you live our values – trust, teamwork, and accountability.\nWhat CIBC Offers\nAt CIBC, your goals are a priority. We start with your strengths and ambitions as an employee and strive to create opportunities to tap into your potential.\nWe work to recognize you in meaningful, personalized ways including a competitive compensation, a banking benefit*, wellbeing support, and additional offers such as employee and family assistance programs and MomentMakers, our social, points-based recognition program.\nOur spaces and technological toolkit will make it simple to bring together great minds to create innovative solutions that make a difference for our clients.\n*Subject to program terms and conditions\nWhat you need to know\nCIBC is committed to creating an inclusive environment where all team members and clients feel like they belong. We seek applicants with a wide range of abilities and we provide an accessible candidate experience. If you need accommodation, please contact Mailbox.careers-carrieres@cibc.com\nYou need to be legally eligible to work at the location(s) specified above and, where applicable, must have a valid work or study permit.\n\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Employer Events calendar.\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/cibc-breaking-barriers-diversifying-capital-markets-summer-2025-register-by-mar-24/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
LOCATION:Online
