SUMMARY:CIBC Breaking Barriers – Diversifying Capital Markets Summer 2025 (Diversity and Inclusion Event)
DESCRIPTION:The Capital Markets Early Talent team at CIBC is hosting our Breaking Barriers: Diversifying Capital Markets Summer 2025 Campus Event, with the aim to increase applications to our summer programs from talent segments who are currently under-represented in Capital Markets. Priority will be made for students who self-identify as one or more under-represented communities, for example, people of colour, including members of the Black community, Indigenous peoples (i.e., First Nations, Inuit or Métis peoples), persons with disabilities, members of the LGBTQ+ community and women. This event will be held on Wednesday, April 3rd, 2024 from 4:00PM – 5:30PM EST virtually via Microsoft Teams. This is an invite-only event and you will need to receive confirmation from the Capital Markets Early Talent team at CIBC to attend.\nAre you currently enrolled in an undergraduate program and are interested in learning more about a career at CIBC Capital Markets? Are you interested in learning more about our inclusive culture here at the bank? This is your chance to connect with CIBC professionals across Global Investment Banking, Corporate Banking and Global Markets during an virtual networking event to learn if it’s the right fit for you. We’ll share with you insider perspective on the Capital Markets business and how you can prepare for applications and interviews. You’ll hear from a panel of Analysts & Associates from Global Markets, Investment Banking and Corporate Banking as they share key information on their career journeys and what student opportunities look like at CIBC.\nIf you are selected to attend this event, you will receive an invitation to the email address you provide to us along with additional information about the event. Please note that space is limited and selection is first come first served.\nImportant information\nYou are enrolled in an undergraduate degree with a graduation date no sooner than April 2026 and are looking for a Summer 2025 internship\nThis event will be hosted virtually via Microsoft Teams. If you are selected to attend, you will receive an email with the Microsoft Teams link.\nEvent sign-ups will close Monday, April 1st at 11:59PM EST.\nRegistration link – https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/campus/job/Ontario-VIRTUAL/Campus-Event–Breaking-Barriers—Diversifying-Capital-Markets-Summer-2025–April-3rd-2024—Virtual-_2406501 ( https://cibc.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/campus/job/Ontario-VIRTUAL/Campus-Event--Breaking-Barriers---Diversifying-Capital-Markets-Summer-2025--April-3rd-2024---Virtual-_2406501 )\nHow you’ll succeed\nMeet Industry Leaders  ?  Network with our experienced professionals across Capital Markets and gain career insights from our representatives to help prepare you for your next student opportunity at CIBC.\nNetworking – Have opportunities to build your network and connect with members of the Capital Markets Early Talent Team.\nCommunication – Leverage your communication skills through active listening, giving feedback and asking questions.\nWho you are\nYou have demonstrated interest in Capital Markets. You are a passionate, accomplished and success-oriented individual who has a keen interest in pursuing a career in the financial services industry demonstrated through school courses, clubs and/or related work experience.\nYou love to learn. You’re passionate about growing your knowledge. You have a strong sense of curiosity.\nYou’re goal oriented. You’re motivated by accomplishing your goals and delivering your best to make a difference.\nYou’re passionate about people. You find meaning in relationships and surround yourself with a diverse network of partners. You connect with others through respect and authenticity.\nValues matter to you. You bring your real self to work and you live our values – trust, teamwork, and accountability.\nWhat CIBC Offers\nAt CIBC, your goals are a priority. We start with your strengths and ambitions as an employee and strive to create opportunities to tap into your potential.\nWe work to recognize you in meaningful, personalized ways including a competitive compensation, a banking benefit*, wellbeing support, and additional offers such as employee and family assistance programs and MomentMakers, our social, points-based recognition program.\nOur spaces and technological toolkit will make it simple to bring together great minds to create innovative solutions that make a difference for our clients.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Employer Events calendar.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/cibc-breaking-barriers-diversifying-capital-markets-summer-2025-diversity-and-inclusion-event/
