SUMMARY:Anthropology Annual General Lecture: The Management of Colonial Luggage
DESCRIPTION:The Management of Colonial Luggage with distinguished lecturer Ghassan Hage\nThe Oxford English dictionary defines luggage as: 1) suitcases or other bags in which to pack personal belongings for travelling and 2) past experiences or long-held ideas and opinions perceived as burdensome encumbrances. Each of these definitions belongs to a different dimension of life. An ethnographic investigation of the first takes us into the material culture of physical mobility, what we carry, and how we carry it, as we move from one place to another. The second takes us into the psychological and affective culture that is part of our existential mobility, what we carry as we are moving through life.\nJoin Ghassan Hage at the Anthropology Annual General Lecture ( https://www.yorku.ca/laps/anth/experience/lecture-series/anthropology-annual-lecture/ ) for a presentation on how these two ethnographies resonate, intersect and speak to each other when researching post-colonial culture.\nGhassan Hage is professor of Anthropology and Social Theory at the University of Melbourne, Australia. His most recent works include: Decay (Duke: 2021), The Diasporic Condition (Chicago: 2021) and The Racial Politics of Australian Multiculturalism (Sweatshop: 2023).\nRegistration\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/anthropology-annual-general-lecture-the-management-of-colonial-luggage/
ORGANIZER;CN=Department of Anthropology:MAILTO:updanth@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Open to the Public,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Vanier College
LOCATION:Downtown Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Anthropology_Annual_Lecture_Eventbrite-1-scaled.jpg
