SUMMARY:Publishing your research data in a data repository
DESCRIPTION:Data is deposited into a repository towards the end of its lifecycle when it is ready for sharing and publication. Publishing your data in a trusted data repository can provide the necessary curation and storage conditions to key your data secure and ensure your data is discoverable to a wide audience. Increasingly, many journal publishers and funding programs encourage the sharing and depositing of research data in a recognized data repository.\nBy the end of this workshop, you’ll be able to:\n• Understand the guiding principles of data sharing and publishing\n• Learn how to prepare your data for sharing and long-term preservation and access\n• Access and select trusted data repositories including York’s generalist data repository York U Dataverse\nIt is recommended that registrants attend the RDM workshop “Create a Data Management Plan (DMP) for Your Research Project ( https://yorku.libcal.com/event/3778934 )” prior.\nRegister at: https://yorku.libcal.com/event/3779524 ( https://yorku.libcal.com/event/3779524 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/publishing-your-research-data-in-a-data-repository/
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
