SUMMARY:Building Bridges: Advancing a community-centric approach to safety 
DESCRIPTION:Join York’s Executive Director of Community Safety, Orville Wallace, for a panel discussion with community leaders and experts to learn more about adopting a community-centric approach to safety.\nDavid Mitchell, former assistant deputy minister in the Youth Justice Division of the Ontario Ministry of Children, Community & Social Services; Devon Jones, founding director of the Youth Association for Academics, Athletics & Character Education; Louis March, founder of the Zero Gun Violence Movement; and Yukimi Henry, executive director of Community Support & Services at York, will come together to share their diverse perspectives and experiences for an engaging and informative discussion.\nAs York moves away from the current law enforcement model that governs its security services and transitions to the community-centric model for safety that was recommended in the Security Services Review final report, community insights, collaboration and honest discourse are a critical component of the path ahead.\nLearn more and register here ( https://www.yorku.ca/safety/upcoming-opportunities-and-learning/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/building-bridges-advancing-a-community-centric-approach-to-safety/
