UID:MEC-6bb604663d5d74f1431ff8a4995f9fd7@events.yorku.ca
DTSTART:20240328T190000Z
DTEND:20240328T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20240312T200300Z
CREATED:20240312
LAST-MODIFIED:20240312
PRIORITY:5
SEQUENCE:4
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Mindful Painting
DESCRIPTION:Studies have shown that most people who try art as a form of therapy or stress relief have experienced significant reductions in their cortisol levels when doing so. Painting allows for emotional release because it stimulates the creative side of your mind while focusing your attention in one place, which can lower anxiety. In this way, the creative outlet improves your mental health significantly.\nJoin the Health Ed team in taking advantage of the benefits of art therapy and taking a break to paint and connect with like-minded students. \n To register, click here ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=303572 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mindful-painting-3/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being:MAILTO:schw@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Event Planners Network,Faculties,Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Support Groups,Teaching &amp; Learning,Well-being
LOCATION:Bennett Centre W319 @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
