SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | Unlocking corporate success – exploring career paths to one of the Big Four, featuring Puneet Gandotra (BCom ‘21)
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Mentor Circles featuring Puneet Gandotra (BCom ’21, PAcc ’22) as he shares his experiences as a York U alumnus and mentors you on: \n\nfinding career opportunities at one of the Big Four; \nhow to successfully write the CPA Common Final Exam (CFE); \nmaking connections and networking. \n\nGandotra graduated from York University with a bachelor of commerce specializing in accounting. He followed up with a graduate diploma in professional accounting from York and he successfully wrote his CPA CFE in September 2022. He is currently an auditor in the Financial Institutions team at KPMG Canada and he is passionate about giving back to his alma mater by mentoring students and coming out to alumni events to share his experiences. He is currently taking a course offered by KPMG Canada in partnership with Simon Fraser University, which explores the integration of data analytics in his audit role. \nLight food and refreshments will be served. \nDate: Tuesday, March 19 \nTime: 1-2:30 p.m. \nLocation: Alumni & Career Lounge, York Lanes (opposite Bookstore) \nIf you have any questions about this event, email Issa Abdi Jamaa, alumni engagement officer, at issajama@yorku.ca.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-unlocking-corporate-success-exploring-career-paths-to-one-of-the-big-four-featuring-puneet-gandotra-bcom-21/
