SUMMARY:Mentor Circles | Insider tips on successful medical school admission featuring Areeba Chaudhry (BSc ‘23)
DESCRIPTION:Join our upcoming Mentor Circle session featuring Areeba Chaudhry (BSc ‘23) as she shares her experiences as a YorkU alum, and mentors you on: \n\nNavigating medical school admissions \nFinding research opportunities and mentorships \nMaking connections and networking \n\nAreeba Chaudhry recently graduated from York University’s Biomedical Science program and is a recipient of the 2023 Faculty of Science Gold Medal. She is currently a first-year medical student at the University of Toronto and a proud alumna of York University. During her time at York University, Areeba developed a deep passion for research and mentorship. She was a devoted student researcher, Peer Mentor, PASS Leader, President’s Ambassador, and member of the Science Student Caucus.  \nTuesday March 12, 2024 | 11:30 a.m. – 1:00 p.m.  \nLocation: Alumni & Career Lounge, Yorklanes (Opposite Bookstore) \nLight food and refreshments will be served. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-insider-tips-on-successful-medical-school-admission-featuring-areeba-chaudhry-bsc-23/
