SUMMARY:A Student’s Guide to Nutrition
DESCRIPTION:For students, post-secondary is a period of self-discovery and exploration. This is a period of growing independence and an opportunity for you to begin accepting personal responsibility and making independent decisions, including what you eat.  \nDuring this time, have you ever found yourself wondering…  \n\nWhat is a “Calorie”  \nWhat is a “Macronutrient” and how much of each should I be eating?\nWhat about vitamins/minerals?  \nIs there any truth to this diet?\n\nIf so, join the Health Education & Promotion team as they introduce the basics of nutrition, navigate macronutrients, and discuss various diets.  \nRegister now! \nAll our workshops require York University authentication (passport York). Please login into your zoom account prior to clicking the meeting link. \n  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/a-students-guide-to-nutrition/
