SUMMARY:Michael Garron Hospital?s Student Open House (Networking Event)
DESCRIPTION:Michael Garron Hospital is hosting a Student Open House for nursing, allied health and medical radiation technology students on Tuesday, March 19, 2024.\nAll nursing, allied health and medical radiation technology (MRT) students are welcome to attend!\nJoin us to learn about working at MGH and visit the Ken and Marilyn Thomson Patient Care Centre (Thomson Centre), one of Ontario’s newest hospital facilities. The Thomson Centre opened in 2023 and provides eight floors of modern and bright care spaces.\nThe Student Open House will encourage you to:\n\nExplore MGH’s current and future job opportunities\nMeet and network with department leaders and the Human Resources team\nLearn what staff like best about working at MGH\nLearn how MGH supports staff in all stages of their career development\n\nPlease see the attached event flyer that can be shared with your networks.\nEvent Details\nLocation: Michael Garron Hospital, T1 Auditorium (located in the new Ken and Marilyn Thomson Patient Care Centre)\nAddress: 825 Coxwell Avenue – The closest entrance to the auditorium is the Sammon Entrance.\nDate and time: Tuesday, March 19, 2023, 12 p.m. to 1 p.m.\nComplete this registration form to confirm your attendance or go to tehn.ca/StudentOpenHouse.\nIn the meantime, we encourage you to discover why working at MGH isn’t one thing, it’s everything. Learn more about MGH’s nursing careers or allied health and MRT careers.\nIf you have any questions about this event, please email hr@tehn.ca. We look forward to meeting you on March 19!\nAbout Michael Garron Hospital\nNestled in the heart of East Toronto, MGH is a vibrant community teaching hospital serving more than 400,000 people in 22 distinct neighbourhoods. With a 90-year history and more than 2,900 staff, MGH is a full-service hospital with strong community and research partners, including the University of Toronto. MGH is an equal opportunity employer and fosters an inclusive and diverse work environment.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Employer Events calendar.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/michael-garron-hospitals-student-open-house-networking-event/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
LOCATION:Off-campus
