SUMMARY:POSTPONED: CHREI’s Annual Inclusion Week feature presentation ‘Reengaging the Significance of Listening’
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: This event has been postposed until further notice.\nRe/Engaging with Listening: Experiences of recognition, respect, and understanding in service of community building \nFeaturing the work of Angela Easby and Evadne Kelly, this panel tackles key questions about listening by examining themes of embodiment, the stakes and the risks associated with listening, the fear of listening and how it connects to the fear of change, and the importance of the heart in listening. It will bring focus to the mediums of dance and digital storytelling.\nKey questions:\n\nHow does our assessment of what is at stake in a moment of listening impact our experience and quality of listening?\nHow do social behaviours of discomfort, such as resistance to uncertainty, hamper people’s ability to perceive, act on or acknowledge their perceptions of injustice? How are these patterns of behaviours systemically enabled by hierarchized power and knowledge relations?\n\nThis is an online event. Register here: yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_8_yUiHuKQ62FhCyIAmTBjA ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_8_yUiHuKQ62FhCyIAmTBjA ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/chreis-annual-inclusion-week-feature-presentation-reengaging-the-significance-of-listening/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Human Rights, Equity &amp; Inclusion:MAILTO:chrwkshp@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion
LOCATION:This is an Online event. Register here:  https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_8_yUiHuKQ62FhCyIAmTBjA 
END:VEVENT
