SUMMARY:Scholarly Skills Webinar:  Publishing Your Work
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies will be hosting a series entitled Scholarly Skills. Join us for our next workshop!  \nSo, you’ve done your research and you’re ready to share your results with the world… now what? Publishing your work is a crucial part of academic conversation, and an important step for graduate students and junior scholars. But, it can be daunting.\nPlease join our panel of distinguished writers and mentors as we tackle some of the most common concerns, worries, and questions about academic publishing. From choosing a journal and working with your co-authors to finding your scholarly voice and responding to reviewers, we’ll take you through the process from start to finish. We’ll also talk about predatory journals and how to write for a public audience.\nPanelists:\nAlice MacLachlan, Philosophy (FGS)\nRaymond Mar, Psychology (Health)\nKeith O’Regan, Writing Department (LAPS)\nMike Zryd, Cinema and Media Arts (AMPD)\nDate: October 2, 2024\nTime: 12:00pm (1-hour workshop)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_cNKEEwjPTd2PmESOWagvOA )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholarly-skills-workshop-5/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Glendon Maîtrise en affaires publiques et internationales (MAPI),Glendon Masters in Public &amp; International Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French and Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Theatre,Graduate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp; Performance Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,Markham Campus
