SUMMARY:(In-person and Online) Black Students Careers Community: Writing Your Best Job Application (Including Resumes and Cover Letters – Job Search Workshops)
DESCRIPTION:Workshop 3: Writing Your Best Job Application (Including Resumes and Cover Letters)\nIn this session, we’ll help you to build your whole job searching profile so you can stand out! Including:\n\nBuilding a job search strategy to maximise your chances of finding opportunities suited to you\nHow to build/optimise a great resume\nHow to write your best cover letter\nDiscovering basic skills to thrive in the professional world.\nTransferring your skills from the academic world to the professional world.\nArticulating your skills to make you stand out.\nRevisiting LinkedIn and updating your experience and posts.\n\n—\nThroughout the 23/24 academic year, we’ll be running career development workshops for Black students. These sessions are designed to be fun, safe, inclusive spaces, through the lens of systemic factors that affect our career decisions – designed to help you to develop your own career success.\nAll sessions can be booked through Experience York.\nThe sessions will be:\nThurs Oct 3rd, 2023, 2-4pm\n\nWorkshop 1: Kick-Off and LinkedIn Networking\n\nThurs Feb 1st, 2024, 2-4pm\n\nWorkshop 2: Conquering Imposter Syndrome and Exploring Your Career Options\n\nThurs March 7th, 2024, 1:30 – 4pm\n\nWorkshop 3: Writing Your Best Job Application (Including Resumes and Cover Letters)\n\nWeds April 30th , 2024, 2-4pm\n\nWorkshop 4: Ace That Interview!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Career Centre calendar.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-students-careers-community-writing-your-best-job-application-including-resumes-and-cover-letters-job-search-workshops/
