TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Mentor Circles: Choosing your own career path post-graduation
DESCRIPTION:Join our upcoming Mentor Circle session featuring Fikayo Aderoju (BA ‘22) as he shares his experiences as a Black International York U alumnus, and mentors you on:\n\nMarketing yourself\nMaking connections and networking\nCharting your own path\n\nFikayo is an award-winning entrepreneur who has reached over 10 million individuals on various media platforms. He is the CEO of BFG Group and founder of Project Impacting Lives, the largest youth-led care product distributor in Canadian history. With an admirable dedication, the initiative has successfully distributed over 10,000 care products across Ontario to individuals in need. Additionally, Fikayo serves as the Chair of York University’s Black Alumni Network (YUBAN), contributing significantly to the university’s community and empowerment initiatives. \nLight food and refreshments will be served. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circles-unlocking-success-journey-to-black-excellence-and-international-student-success-and-careers-post-graduation/
