SUMMARY:Toronto Community Crisis Service Information and Recruitment Event (Networking – Employer Event)
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Community Crisis Service is expanding and looking for new mental health workers to join our teams!\nThe Toronto Community Crisis Service (TCCS) provides a community-based, client centred, trauma-informed response to non-emergency mental health crisis calls and wellness checks. The TCCS is delivered in partnership with community-based organizations including Gerstein Crisis Centre, Canadian Mental Health Association (CMHA) Toronto Branch, TAIBU Community Health Centre, 2-Spirited People of the 1st Nations, and Findhelp 211 I Central.\nJoin us at an Information and Recruitment Event on March 6th at Metro Hall (55 John St.) to learn about the skills and qualifications required to become employed as a mental health worker with the Toronto Community Crisis Service. The event will feature a panel of current Toronto Community Crisis Service staff who will share information about their career journeys and learnings on the job. Attendees will also have opportunities to connect directly with employers to ask questions and apply for available positions with the Toronto Community Crisis Service. Don’t forget to bring your resume!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo know more for this event, login to Experience York and access the Career Centre calendar.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/toronto-community-crisis-service-information-and-recruitment-event-networking-employer-event/
