SUMMARY:Elaborated Images as De Colonial Praxis
DESCRIPTION:Presentation by Laurence Butet-Roch and Deanna Del Vecchio.\n\n\nDate: Wednesday, Feb. 28\nTime: 11:30 a.m. to 1 p.m.\nLocation: 626 Kaneff Tower, York University\nRSVP here.\nElaborated images, created through participant intervention on photographs, actively disrupt static notions of meaning. \nIn this presentation, we will situate the practice; explaining what the method consists of, its lineage and contributions to visual participatory methodologies.\nDrawing on the projects of several social documentary photographers (Bieke Depoorter, Patrick Waterhouse, Nigel Poor, Wendy Red Star and Laurence Butet-Roch), we will elucidate the decolonial potentials of this photographic praxis.\nWe’ll conclude with an outline of practical and logistical considerations to keep in mind when using the method, all in the hopes of inspiring more researchers to adopt it in their projects.\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/elaborated-images-as-de-colonial-praxis/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Feminist Research:MAILTO:cfr-coor@yorku.ca
