SUMMARY:Fledgling Sensory and Rehabilitative Infrastructures: Cochlear Implantation and Feedback Networks in Pakistan and Turkey
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Michele Friedner and Fulden Arisan (University of Chicago)\nMonday, March 4, 3 to 5 p.m. (EST)\nRegister via Eventbrite to receive the Zoom link for this webinar.\nThis is the third webinar talk in the Technoableism Seminar Series supported by the Institute for Technoscience and Society, York University’s Critical Disability Studies, Science and Technology Studies, and Health and Society programs. Coined by critical disability studies and STS scholar Ashley Shew, technoableism forms a narrative about disability that speaks to empowering disabled people, while also reinforcing harmful ableist tropes that cement beliefs around what kinds of bodies are deemed valuable.\nIf you are having any issues accessing the link or registration for either talk, please contact techno@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fledgling-sensory-and-rehabilitative-infrastructures-cochlear-implantation-and-feedback-networks-in-pakistan-and-turkey/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
END:VEVENT
