SUMMARY:Facilitating Listening Circles: Advanced Training and Essential Skills
DESCRIPTION:The RELATIONAL CULTURE WORKSHOP SERIES ( https://www.yorku.ca/vpepc/wp-content/uploads/sites/310/2024/02/Relational-Culture-series-at-York-flyer.pdf ) are series of learning opportunities to enrich our skills for working with each other at York.\nFACILITATING LISTENING CIRCLES: ADVANCED TRAINING AND ESSENTIAL SKILLS\nWEDNESDAY, FEB 21, 9:30 am -1:30pm\n& TUESDAY MAR 26, 1-3:30pm, online\nBy Pat Lewis & Kaleigh Mrowka, International Institute for Restorative Practices Canada.\nThis highly-interactive 2-part training is intended to teach the skills and considerations for becoming\nskilled facilitators of Listening Circles, which are ‘safe spaces’ for individuals to share their thoughts,\nperspectives and experiences surrounding a challenge or harm to their community.\nRSVP ( https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=GBNTNBFw1E-H8KQ4FsSb0HN5RtPxCUZJrPhfwaSGEh9UN1paR1VHREZaRjZWRzNNTkhRWlRJQjJQMi4u )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/facilitating-listening-circles-advanced-training-and-essential-skills/
CATEGORIES:Equity, People &amp; Culture,Well-being
END:VEVENT
