SUMMARY:York Dances 2024: Era of Oddities
DESCRIPTION:York Dances: Era of Oddities features new choreographic works by 29 BFA Dance majors performed by dance students in and connected to the York dance program. Era of Oddities is an evening of performance that unapologetically celebrates our identity, investigates the nuances of the self, and considers the future of our world through the lens of performance.\nAs they take on multiple roles in the creation and production of this show, these passionate artists consider how we generate an inclusive, yet positive community where our voices can be heard as well as uplifted.\nArtistic Director and Course Director: Syreeta Hector\nWork/Study Supervisor: Jennifer Jimenez\nDATES:\nTuesday, March 26: Series A – 7:00 PM | Series B – 8:30 PM\nWednesday, March 27: Series A – 7:00 PM | Series B – 8:30 PM\nThursday, March 28: Series A – 7:00 PM | Series B – 8:30 PM\nSeries A: Back Then\nSeries B: Later On\nLOCATION: McLean Performance Studio ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/mclean-performance-studio/ ) (244 Accolade East Building)\nTICKETS: Advance (until March 18th) $12.00 |Regular: $17.00\nBOX OFFICE  ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/index.asp )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-dances-2024-era-of-oddities/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:McLean Performance Studio | 244 Accolade East @ 4700 Keele St, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/eraofoddities.jpg
