SUMMARY:Discovering Careers as a Mature Student (Career Conversations | Networking Event – Employers Event)
DESCRIPTION:Brought to you in partnership between the Career Centre and the Atkinson Centre for Mature & Part-time Students (ACMAPS).\nConnect with accomplished professionals who were mature students at York University! Meet alumni who are currently enjoying their careers and get the inside scoop on what it’s really like to work in the field. During this panel, professionals will share their personal stories about breaking into the field, how their career paths took them from graduation to where they are now, and what knowledge, skills and experience helped them succeed in their jobs. The panel discussion will be followed by an open forum where students will have an opportunity to ask the panellists their own questions.\nRegistration is required. Please register via the Experience York link: experience.yorku.ca/events.htm?evtId=2699. \n\nLog into Experience York with your PPY account.\nClick on “CAREER CENTRE” on the left-hand side of the navigation menu.\nSelect “EVENTS & WORKSHOPS.”\nNavigate to the event date and click on it.\nSelect the red button that says, “Register for this event” on the top right-hand side. \nThe Zoom link for the event is available and will be resent to you as a reminder 24 hours before the event.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/discovering-careers-as-a-mature-student-career-conversations-networking-event-employers-event-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=ACMAPS:MAILTO:acmaps@yorku.ca
