SUMMARY:BRIDGING THE GAP: Student Panel Discussion on Israel/Palestine
DESCRIPTION:BRIDGING THE GAP\nISRAEL/PALESTINE STUDENT PANEL DISCUSSION\nWe are a group of York University students and alumni, both Palestinian/Arab and Israeli/Jewish, who want to change the way the conversation about Israel/Palestine is happening at York University. We believe that, as fellow students who have a connection to this land, we all deserve human dignity and an honest conversation. We have established an Israel/Palestine student dialogue group on campus for the purpose of sharing multiple perspectives in a respectful manner.\nYork University Professor Randal Schnoor (Religious Studies) will moderate a public panel discussion with outstanding student leaders of BRIDGING THE GAP to explore Israeli and Palestinian views of the current situation in Israel/Palestine, student motivations for starting this dialogue group, views on the current campus climate, challenges and opportunities for dialogue. A question and discussion period with the audience will follow. Come to learn more about this new and important initiative at our university.\nMonday, Feb. 12\n2:45 p.m.\n137 South Ross Building\nRegistration link: forms.gle/rb63U8zBcjZczmnS7.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/bridging-the-gap-student-panel-discussion-on-israel-palestine/
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities
LOCATION:Ross S137
END:VEVENT
