SUMMARY:Mixer, Play-through and Tetris (2023) Screening
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Thursday, January 23 in the Sensorium Flex Space for an afternoon celebrating gaming history and preservation. The event will feature a welcome session & mingle with refreshments, a  game play-through to immerse yourself in the amazing history and enduring fun of Tetris, and a screening of the acclaimed film Tetris (2023), based on true events around the race to license and patent the video game Tetris from Russia in the late 1980s during the Cold War. The mixer and playthrough will begin at 3:00 pm, and the screening will begin at 4:00 pm.\nThis is the first event in the Save Play Series, a collaborative initiative that invites participants to engage creatively and conceptually with the genre of video games and re-imagine what preservation can mean in this context.\nThe Save Play Series is sponsored by Sensorium: Centre for Digital Arts and Technology, Digital Media at York, and AMPD\nDate: Thursday, January 23, 2025\nTime: 3:00 p.m. – 6:00 p.m.\nLocation: Sensorium Flex Space ( https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/flex-space/ ) (326 CFA)\nFree Admission\nPlease RSVP HERE ( https://ampd.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=210496 ) if you would like to attend.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mixer-play-through-and-tetris-2023-screening/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sensorium Flex Space, 326 Joan and Martin Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts (CFA)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/tetris-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
