SUMMARY:Sensorium Writing Club
DESCRIPTION:Want to join a writing group with other researchers to fight procrastination and make consistent progress? Sensorium is partnering with the Graduate Film Student Association to host bi-monthly writing sessions every other Wednesday. These sessions provide a structured and focused environment in the Sensorium Loft where Graduate students, faculty, and visiting researchers can come together, set aside distractions, and achieve their writing goals, whether it’s for a dissertation, essay, book chapter, or poetry.\nThe Sensorium Research Loft ( https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/research-loft/ ) is located on the 4th floor of the Joan and Martin Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts.\nThe Loft is wheelchair accessible.\nFREE\nUPCOMING DATES \nWednesday, February 28, 2024 (1pm – 3pm)\nWednesday, March 13, 2024 (1pm – 3pm)\nWednesday, March 27, 2024 (1pm – 3pm)\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sensorium-writing-club-feb28/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Sensorium Loft, 4th Floor of Goldfarb Centre for Fine Arts @ 86 Fine Arts Rd
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/writingworkshop.jpg
END:VEVENT
