SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Still I rise: The resistance work of Black mother learners in Toronto
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Stephanie Fearon, Assistant Professor, of Black Thriving and Education in the Faculty of Education on Feb. 21 at 12 p.m. for Scholars’ Hub. Dr. Fearon will explore the resistance practices of Black Caribbean mothers attending community-based adult learning programs in Toronto. She will draw on visual and Black oral storytelling traditions to challenge widely held notions of leadership.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-still-i-rise-the-resistance-work-of-black-mother-learners-in-toronto/
