SUMMARY:Zotero for collaborative research projects
DESCRIPTION:Zotero ( https://www.zotero.org ) is a free, open-source tool to manage and track bibliographic citations. This series of live workshops are designed to take participants beyond the basics of using Zotero to having it serve as a fully-fledged research partner.\nBy the end of this live workshop, participants will understand how to:\n\nshare a Zotero collection with a specific group of colleagues, or with the public;\nsuccessfully locate existing and shared Zotero collections;\ncollaborate with colleagues to build and share a directory of sources; and\nunderstand how Zotero stores content in the context of pay-walled or subscription-based resources.\n\nRegister at: yorku.libcal.com/event/3778360 ( https://yorku.libcal.com/event/3778360 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/zotero-for-collaborative-research-projects/
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
