SUMMARY:WORD, SOUND, POWER: An Annual Celebration of Black Artistic Expression
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to immerse yourself in the ultimate celebration of Black artistry, where words, sounds and power collide in a night to remember.\nCome join us for an unforgettable evening at the Tribute Communities Recital Hall as we celebrate the rich and diverse world of Black artistic expression. This annual event promises to be a vibrant showcase of talent, creativity and cultural pride.\nMark your calendars for Wednesday, Feb. 7 at 5:30 p.m. (EST), and join us for an evening that will ignite your senses and uplift your spirits. The Tribute Communities Recital Hall provides the perfect setting for this cultural extravaganza, with its intimate and welcoming atmosphere.\nWhether you are a lover of art, a supporter of diversity or simply looking for a memorable night out, you don’t want to miss this.\nThis is a free event and all are welcome to attend.\nReserve your spot HERE ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/word-sound-power-an-annual-celebration-of-black-artistic-expression-tickets-776624443617 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/word-sound-power-an-annual-celebration-of-black-artistic-expression-2/
ORGANIZER;CN=The Jean Augustine Chair in Education, Community and Diaspora:MAILTO:jachair@edu.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,BE-YU,Black History Month,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Faculty of Education,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Student Accessibility Services
LOCATION:Accolade East Building, Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/wordsound.jpg
END:VEVENT
