SUMMARY:World Music Festival – CANCELLED
DESCRIPTION:York University’s World Music Festival is a cross-cultural celebration spotlighting musical traditions around the world.\nProduced by Professor Mike Cadó ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/mike-cado/ ) this global sonic tour presents a sampling of several international cultures represented in York’s world music program.\nThe festival packs four concerts into one day: Thursday, March 14, 2024\nMaps and Directions ( http://maps.info.yorku.ca/keele-campus/ )\nTHURSDAY MARCH 14\n11:30 am – West African (Ghana) – Kwasi Dunyo, Ensemble Director\n1:30 pm – Cuban Ensemble – Rick Lazar ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/rick-lazar/ ), Ensemble Director\n3:15 pm – Caribbean Ensemble –  Gareth Burgess ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/gareth-burgess/ ), Ensemble Director\n7:30 pm – Balkan Ensemble, Irene Markoff ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/irene-markoff/ ), Ensembe Director\nLOCATION: Tribute Communities Recital Hall  ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/world-music-festival-2024/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/worldmusicfest.jpg
