SUMMARY:Scholarly Skills Webinar: Navigating the Ethics Approval Journey in Graduate Studies – Balancing the seriousness with the opportunities
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies will be hosting a series entitled Scholarly Skills. Join us for our next workshop!  \nIn this, the next installment of the Dean’s Scholarly Skills Brown Bag Workshop Series,  Associate Dean, Academic and National Girls/Women’s health researcher Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith will lead discussion regarding what grad students need to understand and do as they approach this important graduate studies milestone. Key aspects of the Research Ethics Protocol Form for Graduate Student Theses or Dissertations, found here ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/wp-content/uploads/sites/184/2021/03/td-2.pdf ),  will be demystified with a particular emphasis on working with human participants. From understanding risk assessment, the outlining of goals, objectives, participant criteria and recruitment, proposed methodologies and data analysis, come and gain valuable information about how walking through your ethics application helps to tighten and clarify your proposed area of inquiry in ways that will set you up for success!\nDr. van Daalen-Smith will be joined by the Senior Manager and Policy Advisor of the Office of Research Ethics, Alison Mrakus-Collins who will answer participant questions while providing guidance to avoid the pitfalls leading to delays in ethics approvals. Participants are invited to access the form, with the link provided above, so you can understand what is required and walk through items together with us as you listen.\nDate: Monday, February 12, 2024\nTime: 12:00pm (1-hour workshop)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN__BWtY2YjQaCrwViPQGKC9A )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholarly-skills-workshop-4/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Glendon Maîtrise en affaires publiques et internationales (MAPI),Glendon Masters in Public &amp; International Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administration,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduate Program in Cinema &amp; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Engineering,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate Program in Education–Leadership &amp; Community Engagement,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp; Computer Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp; Applied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program in Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Physics &amp; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Science