SUMMARY:Navigating Queer Resources (Online Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:It is no secret that 2SLGBTQIA+ folks can face some unique barriers and challenges in university life. From struggling to find a safe community to trying to find queer-friendly resources to support health and wellness, it can feel like a lot to navigate. This workshop is meant to simplify this process for queer folk and allies here at York.\nJoin the Health Education & Promotion team as we examine the unique barriers and stigma faced by the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, discuss the importance of holistic wellness by utilizing the wellness wheel framework, and discover many of the queer-friendly resources available both on and off campus pertaining to: \n\nqueer-informed mental health support; \n\n\nfinding community and homelessness support;\n\n\nphysical health-care, including gender-affirming care and queer-friendly primary care providers; and \n\n\nsexual health support.\n\n To register, click here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMkc-GhqD4rEtd5M2IMDHLjxqvEGYFBJ13c ).\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than one minute to complete): forms.office.com/r/AhNyJRd7ea. \n This form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/navigating-queer-resources-online-workshop-2/
