SUMMARY:Mentor Circles: The glamour and grit of balancing a full time career & parenthood
DESCRIPTION:During the month of January, we are celebrating National Mentoring Month in the lounge with the launch of a new program, Mentor Circles. This exciting, new in-person opportunity is designed to bring together alumni and students interested in mentoring or career opportunities.\nIf you would like to participate in any of the sessions please email Issa Jamaa at issajama@yorku.ca.\nEver dreamed of planning events? Join featured alumni mentor, Jenny Evans (BA ’07) on Jan. 29, as she shares her experiences of balancing a full time job and parenthood.\nJenny has worked in the events space for 15 years. In the past five years, her life has been defined by constant change. As a mother of two she has had to also adjust to an entirely different work environment since the pandemic. Jenny is happy to share the glamour and grit of her journey and provide advice for mentees.\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mentor-circle-the-glamour-grit-and-evolution-of-my-event-planning-career-the-balance-of-parenthood/
