TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Cannabis: Misconceptions & Safer Practices
DESCRIPTION:Using cannabis (weed, pot) is a personal choice, but it can have short- and long-term effects on your health.   \nWe review types of cannabis forms (edibles, inhalants , topicals), provide guidance on understanding dosage size, packaging labels interaction with other substances, and discuss common myths about cannabis.   \nWe also look at safety considerations and provide harm-reduction guidelines to lower health associated health risks and dependency and interaction with other substance use (e.g. alcohol).    \nPlease note the purpose of this workshop is for general education only. We do not condone or promote any particular lifestyle choice. Please consult a healthcare professional for guidance and support. \n To register, Click here! ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEkduitrj8sG9OTDH95Q3lvd6FCeZF7l2ow )\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete): https://forms.office.com/r/GntveLeWeR \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/cannabis-misconceptions-safer-practices/
