SUMMARY:Introduction to Reproductive Health (Online Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:According to the WHO, reproductive health implies that people are able to have a satisfying and safe sex life and that they have the capability to reproduce and the freedom to decide if, when, and how often to do so.  \nAt Health Education & Promotion we aim to support the WHOs goals through educating and spreading awareness on reproductive health topics, in order to provide students with the tools needed to make decisions that support their reproductive health in ways they see fit. \nJoin the Health Education & Promotion team as we explore the following topics: \n\nUnderstanding the conception process & bust common myths \nUnderstanding the menstruation process \nExplore contraceptive options \nLearn about reproductive health care services and resources available to students \n\nTo register, Click here! ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMvc-mvpj8tGtydSAevsR5389GFd2L22pd6 )\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete): https://forms.office.com/r/uCzYvdKmz3 \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/introduction-to-reproductive-health-online-workshop-3/
