SUMMARY:Plant-based Nutrition (Online)
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop we will discuss why some students may choose a plant-based diet. We will also debunk some of the common misconceptions surrounding plant-based diets.   \nWhat does a well-rounded plant-based diet look like? How hard is it to meet all of your essential nutrient needs? Does plant-based always mean “healthy”?  \n Learn to navigate marketing/labeling pitfalls to maximize your student budget, too.\nPlease note this workshop is for general education only. We do not condone or promote any particular diet or lifestyle. Please consult a physician or registered Dietitian to support your specific needs.  \nTo register, click here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJwsc-GrqTsjGdAt4U35PWCLFWY4EWI_ydcM ).\nAll our online workshops require York University authentication (Passport York). Please login into your zoom account prior to clicking the meeting link.     \nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete): forms.office.com/r/XeMPn7Mj5d.  \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/plant-based-nutrition-online/
