SUMMARY:Experience Grad York: Social Anthropology
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Social Anthropology? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register\nWe are a dynamic intellectual community of scholars and students committed to theoretically informed, empirically grounded, and socially relevant research. Our faculty expertise spans a world of topics, theories, and innovative methodologies through which we teach and produce knowledge that critically illuminates the social and cultural life of the past, the present, and projects about the future.\nThe program focuses on the social/cultural anthropology of contemporary societies. The program is ideally suited to students who are independent thinkers and who value flexibility.\nJoin our session to learn more!\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsnews@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsnews@yorku.ca ).\n
