SUMMARY:Navigating Mental Health Resources
DESCRIPTION:Navigating Mental Health Resources at York University \nTransitioning to university is challenging enough. The quality of your health and well-being impacts everything from managing your stress, making time for your loved ones and still working towards your academic success. Join the Health Education & Promotion team to: \n\nLearn what mental health is and why it is important to consider your mental well-being as a student. \nDiscuss the barriers students face when accessing mental health support and destigmatize the topic of mental health.  \nLearn about what mental health services and well-being supports are available and accessible to students.   \n\nTo register, click here ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=294749 ).\nAll our online workshops require York University authentication (Passport York). Please login into your Zoom account prior to clicking the meeting link.   \nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than one minute to complete): forms.office.com/r/U3A1m9F3cR. \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
