SUMMARY:A Student’s Guide to Meal Planning (In-Person)
DESCRIPTION:Meal Planning for Students on a Budget  \nAre you interested in learning about strategies to use going grocery shopping? Do you find yourself not having enough time to meal prep for the week?   \nDuring this one-hour session, Health Education and Promotion will take you on a grocery shopping trip where they will break down ways to shop on a budget while showing students how to understand nutrition labels. Afterwards, we will go over meal planning and how students can fit meal prep in their busy schedules.  \nTo register, click here ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=294749 ).\nAll our online workshops require York University authentication (Passport York). Please login into your Zoom account prior to clicking the meeting link.   \nBefore attending the presentation, fill out our anonymous pre-test form (it takes less than one minute to complete): forms.office.com/r/JdnkbH1Rwh. \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body\n
