SUMMARY:Intersectional Futures: We Have Always Been Here featuring Samra Habib
DESCRIPTION:Samra Habib is a Pakistani Canadian photographer, writer and activist. They are most noted for Just Me and Allah, a photography project they launched in 2014 to document the lives of LGBTQ Muslims, and We Have Always Been Here, a memoir of their experience as a queer-identifying Muslim, published in 2019 by Penguin Random House Canada.\n
