SUMMARY:Scholarly Skills Webinar: Starting From Scratch! First steps in a major research project
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies will be hosting a series entitled Scholarly Skills. Join us for our next workshop!  \nThwarted by your thesis? Daunted by an approaching dissertation? The first steps in a major research project can seem overwhelming at first. Join FGS Dean Alice MacLachlan and a panel of experienced experts from across York as we discuss everything from outlining a proposal, managing data and sources, to sketching early drafts and avoiding disorganization and burnout. Bring us your questions and your concerns, and we will be happy to address them.\nPanelists include:\n– Dawn Bazely, Professor, Biology\n– Alison Crosby, Associate Professor and Chair, Gender, Sexuality and Women’s Studies\n– Scott McLaren, Associate Librarian and Graduate Faculty Member in History and Humanities\nDate: Monday, January 22, 2024\nTime: 12:00pm (1-hour workshop)\nLocation: Virtual Workshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_nSKZU4cHTfOe7uiGrAJ_hQ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholarly-skills-workshop-3/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
