SUMMARY:Alumni Career Chat: Kyle Wong, Physiotherapist & National Manager, Clinical Talent Ambassador at CBI Health (Networking – Employers Event)
DESCRIPTION:Shifted to an online event.\nBrought to you in partnership between the Career Centre and the Office of the Dean, Faculty of Health.\nAlumni Career Chats are designed to assist York students and new graduates in making connections, building their professional network, and gaining industry insights.\nMeet Kyle Wong, Physiotherapist & National Manager, Clinical Talent Ambassador at CBI Health!Kyle graduated from the Bachelor of Applied Science, Kinesiology and Exercise Science program in 2008 and then went to the University of Toronto and completed the Master of Physical Therapy program. Upon graduating, Kyle started his career journey at CBI Health and has worked at the organization for over 13 years. Aside from his PT role, Kyle has been a GTA Recruiter, Clinic Manager, Regional Manager, and now National Manager. Kyle has transferred his passion for patient care and management to helping fellow clinicians find great career opportunities within rehab at CBI Health. Kyle looks forward to connecting with future clinicians at this Alumni Career Chat!\nRegistration: Experience York ( http://careers.yorku.ca/online-system/ ), open to Kinesiology students only\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/alumni-career-chat-kyle-wong-physiotherapist-national-manager-clinical-talent-ambassador-at-cbi-health-networking-employers-event/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Faculty of Health
LOCATION:Online (Register through Experience York)
