SUMMARY:Pre-Exam Wellness Event
DESCRIPTION:For many folks, the festive month of December brings about increased feelings of comfort and joy.\nHowever, for university students, the month of December can present differently.\n\nRather than viewing festive light, you might find yourself in the library studying under bright florescent lights.\nInstead of gathering with friends and family, you are solitary trying to complete that last assignment.\nRather than having feelings of comfort and joy, you might be feeling increased feelings of stress and anxiety.\n\nExam season is difficult, but with the right tools and supports you can make it through and have a happy new year.\nJoin Health Education & Promotion for our December Pre-Exam Wellness Event. In this event, we will discuss exam anxiety, explore ways to reframe mindset and engage in mindful practices, including journaling, painting and jewelry making.\nPlease follow this link to register ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=291198 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/pre-exam-wellness-event/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being:MAILTO:schw@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Faculties,Glendon,Health Education &amp; Promotion,International,LA&amp;PS Colleges,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,Learning Skills Services,Markham Campus,Research &amp; Innovation,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Support Groups,The Centre,Well-being
LOCATION:Bennett Centre W319 @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
