SUMMARY:ChatGPT: One Year Later, A Roundtable Discussion
DESCRIPTION:INSTITUTE FOR TECHNOSCIENCE & SOCIETY\nChatGPT: One Year Later, A Roundtable Discussion\nHybrid event: Zoom and In Person in the Lassonde Research Centre (LRC), Room 102\nRegistration link: bit.ly/1yearchatgpt ( https://bit.ly/1yearchatgpt ).\nDirections to reach LRC102 will be provided upon registration.\nThursday, Nov. 30, noon to 1:30 p.m.\nConvening on Nov. 30, the one-year anniversary of ChatGPT’s launch, this roundtable brings together a diverse group of scholars to reflect on the promises and perils of generative artificial intelligence (AI) in the context of higher education. Turning their eyes to the future, each of our panellists will bring forward a topic or concern they see as being under-explored, laying the groundwork for future conversations and collaborations as we continue to make our way in this new educational landscape.\nPanellists\n\nDr. Sava Saheli Singh\nAssistant Professor of Digital Futures in Education\n\nDr. Kelly Bergstrom\nAssistant Professor, Department of Communication & Media Studies\n\n\n\nRyan Collis\nDoctoral Candidate, Graduate Program in Education\n\nSee the ITS News & Events page for more information, at yorku.ca/research/its/events ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/its/events/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/chatgpt-one-year-later-a-roundtable-discussion/
