SUMMARY:Paalam Dance Salon
DESCRIPTION:Featuring works by Ann Ariyadasa, Ramya Raghavan and Niroshehaa Ragunathan with Marilyn Yogayrajah.\nJoin us work-in-progress dance performances and for conversations with chai and snacks.\nRegister at: eventbrite.ca/e/paalam-a-reimagining-south-asian-dance-salon-tickets-748138090167?aff=oddtdtcreator ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/paalam-a-reimagining-south-asian-dance-salon-tickets-748138090167?aff=oddtdtcreator ).\nGardeners of Stories\nArpita Bajpeyi, Vridhhi Chaudhry and Meera Kanageswaran, the salon’s organizers, invite you to Paalam: A Reimagining South Asian Dance Salon Series. This November, they are featuring works by international and Toronto-based artists whose art explores stories we don’t typically encounter in South Asian dance: experiences of life on tea plantations, queerness, postpartum depression and much more.\nPaalam has been made possible by the generous support of the Centre for Drama, Theatre & Performance Studies at the University of Toronto, the York Centre for Asian Research and the Institute for Dance Studies at CDTPS.\n
