SUMMARY:The Stories Around Us: Mental Health Narratives of South Asian Women
DESCRIPTION:The Stories Around Us: Mental Health Narratives of South Asian Women | Book Launch webinar\nRana Khan, editor of The Stories Around Us\nNamrta Mohan, psychotherapist, speaker and clinical supervisor\nKripa Sekhar, executive director, South Asian Women’s Centre\nPlease register for this event at this link ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_xPOjahteRn2hUA6oNOWbhw ).\nRana Khan is an author, poet, ESL teacher and community educator. She shares her own story of mental health issues, and those of nine other South Asian women, in an anthology titled The Stories Around Us.\nNamrta Mohan holds a master degree in psychology, and is a registered psychotherapist, speaker and clinical supervisor, with more than 15 years of experience in the field of mental health.\nKripa Sekhar is the Executive Director of the South Asian Women’s Centre (SAWC) and former co-chair for the Metropolitan Action Committee on Violence Against Women and Children (METRAC).\nThis event is organized by the York Centre for Asian Research and the Office of Women’s Health Research Chair in Mental Health (OWHC).\nFor more information, email ycar@yorku.ca ( mailto:ycar@yorku.ca ).\n
