SUMMARY:Graduate Writing Series – Part 4: Communicating Your Big Ideas
DESCRIPTION:Oftentimes developing your own ideas is a challenging process. Communicating those ideas is a crucial skill in connecting your research to varied audiences. The purpose of this workshop is to help graduate students develop the skills needed to communicate their complex ideas and research to diverse audiences outside of their discipline and even outside of academia.\nThis workshop is part four of a five part series on graduate writing skills, hosted by LA&PS Colleges in collaboration with The Writing Centre. All LA&PS MA and PhD students are welcome to attend.\nRegister Here\n
