SUMMARY:Social Exclusion of Roma, Indigenous People and Irregular Migrants
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nThis talk explores how Canada’s approach to social inclusion for indigenous and vulnerable populations could inform Greek policymakers seeking to address the challenges faced by marginalized groups, such as Roma, migrants, and undocumented people, with a focus on bridging the gap between equitable principles and actual societal standing.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRegister Here\n\n\n\n
