SUMMARY:Ready, Set, GROW! Lunch & Learn Series: Green Excellence – Conflict Resolution
DESCRIPTION:This session will equip participants to master workplace conflict resolution. Strategies such as addressing issues immediately and openly, setting clear expectations, building active listening skills, will be covered with the aim of improving co-worker relationships. This session will establish how to address employee differences of opinions, objectives, or styles, including establishing common grounds for the most effective collaboration.  \nThis session will be facilitated by the Prince’s Trust Foundation. Prince’s Trust Foundation “help equity-deserving youth and veterans to secure meaningful employment through training and mentorship. They partner with employers and community organizations to provide free skill-building programs and mentoring that prepares you for the transforming world of work.” \nThe Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) is excited to announce its partnership with Green Career Centre to host York University’s inaugural Green Career Fair on January 18th, 2024! To support the YorkU community in preparation for the career fair, EUC will be hosting Ready, Set, GROW! Lunch & Learn Series. This professional development series will run from Oct 26th to Dec 5th on alternating Tuesdays and Thursdays during the lunch hour (12PM or 1PM) as a hybrid format open to the community (in-person seating limited). RSVP to tap into our workshops and learn more on how you can become green career ready for the workforce!   \n
