SUMMARY:Department of English presents Derek McCormack
DESCRIPTION:Department of English presents Derek McCormack\nWEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 8TH, 2023\n1:00pm-2:30pm\nVanier College, Room 119\nDerek McCormack will speak to the AP/CWR 4610: Senior Prose Workshop about queer experimental fiction, art writing, fashion, and independent publishing.\nThis talk will include a short reading by Derek but will mostly comprise a free-flowing Q&A.\nDerek McCormack is the author of twelve works of fiction, most recently Castle Faggot (Semiotext(e)). He has also written for Art Forum, Bomb, Fanzine, among other publications. He is one of Canada’s most unique stylists and an indispensable voice in our national literature.\nFurhter\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/department-of-english-presents-derek-mccormack/
ORGANIZER;CN=Meaghan McCue:MAILTO:mmccue@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of English
LOCATION:Vanier College, Room 119
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/McCormack-D.-photo-e1699368683341.png
END:VEVENT
