SUMMARY:Discovering Open Education at York University
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in learning more about open educational resources (OER) and how they can be incorporated into the classroom? Join Charlotte de Araujo, assistant professor, Faculty of Science, and Stephanie Quail, acting director of the Libraries’ Open Scholarship Department on Thursday, November 23 from 2:30pm to 4:00pm via Zoom for a workshop on foundational OER and open education topics. During this session, attendees will learn about the following topics:\n\nWhat are OER?\nOpen licensing basics\nAccessibility considerations and OER\nCommon OER creation tools, H5P & Pressbook\n\nRegister for the Zoom session ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0oc-qupz4pH9Uwt1l36aBOzKUZSd-tjBNK#/registration )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/discovering-open-education-at-york-university/
ORGANIZER;CN=York University Libraries:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Libraries
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
