SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: Emergency management for all: Meeting the needs of the whole community during disasters
DESCRIPTION:Canada’s culturally diverse communities are occasionally impacted by disasters. When disasters strike, there is the potential for racially and culturally diverse communities to have their needs overlooked. This presentation will discuss “emergency management for all”, analyzing how the needs of communities are met, or not met, during emergencies.\nJoin Dr. Jack L. Rozdilsky, Associate Professor of Disaster and Emergency Management on Nov. 8 at 12 p.m. for Scholars’ Hub @ Home.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-emergency-management-for-all-meeting-the-needs-of-the-whole-community-during-disasters/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Glendon Alumni &amp; Friends
