SUMMARY:Allan I. Carswell Observatory Haunted Hydrogen Halloween
DESCRIPTION:What mysterious substance makes up our universe? Hydrogen is the spooky element behind it all, changing forms inside stars and even making ghostly nebulae.\nJoin the York University Allan I. Carswell Astronomical Observatory on Tuesday, October 31st, 6-9PM, for some Halloween fun and to learn more!\nBOOK YOUR TICKET\nDate: Tuesday, October 31, 2023\nTime: 6:00PM – 9:00PM\nLocation: Allan I. Carswell Observatory (Petrie Science & Engineering Building, 3rd floor)\nThis session will go ahead regardless of weather conditions. Guests will be shown into the 1-m, as well as the 60-cm, domes from inside the Observatory. Domes will not open under rain and/or overcast conditions. Free Halloween candy to kids upon exit.   \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/allan-i-carswell-observatory-haunted-hydrogen-halloween/
