SUMMARY:MABOUNGOU: Being in The World (film screening & artist panel)
DESCRIPTION:A Special Tubman Talks and Department of Dance Event\nOn Wednesday November 1st, The School of the Arts, Media, Performance and Design (AMPD) will host a screening of the 2023 biographical documentary MABOUNGOU: Being in the World (48 minutes) followed by a discussion panel featuring Governor General’s Performing Arts Award-winner Zab Maboungou ( https://ggpaa.ca/award-recipients/2020/maboungou,-zab.aspx ) and three internationally renown dance artists – Isaac Akrong ( https://isaacniiakrong.com/about ), Florent Nikiéma ( https://christoph-winkler.com/en/people/florent-nikiema/ ), and Pulga Muchochoma ( https://www.pulgadance.com/ ). This special event is a collaboration between the Department of Dance ( https://dance.ampd.yorku.ca/ ) and the Harriet Tubman Institute ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/tubman/ ), addressing how colonial pasts inform the present experience of dance artists of African descent working in the diasporas.\nPanel Moderator: Collette ‘Coco’ Murray ( http://www.misscocomurray.com/about-coco.html ), arts educator and doctoral student in Dance\nWednesday, November 1, 2023\n7:00 pm to 9:30 pm\nMcLean Performance Studio\n244 Accolade East Building (2nd Floor)\nSeating is limited. Register for your free ticket HERE ( https://ampd.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=185234 )\nThe McLean Performance Studio is fully accessible.\nSponsored by PUBLIC ( https://linktr.ee/publicjournal ): journal of art, culture and ideas.\nThis event will be presented in English and French.\nPRODUCTION COMPANY\nMouvement Perpétuel ( https://mouvementperpetuel.net/about-mp ) is an award-winning Montreal-based independent film, video, and new media production company specializing in arts programming. Co-directors Marlene Millar and Philip Szporer create impressionistic dance-media films, arts documentaries and multi-channel video installations. MABOUNGOU: Being in the World has received critical success at dance and film festivals around the world since its release in 2023.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/maboungou-being-in-the-world-film-screening-artist-panel/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:McLean Performance Studio | 244 Accolade East @ 4700 Keele St, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/filmstill.jpg
END:VEVENT
