SUMMARY:UNHack 2023: Design Solutions – Impact Lives
DESCRIPTION:Note: This a paid event and participants who complete the event will be refunded the $10 registration fee upon submitting their reflection survey by Nov. 1.\nAre you an undergrad student in a post-secondary school?\nIf so, you’re invited to join us for an unforgettable weekend, where we will work together to try and solve some of the world’s greatest challenges.\nUNHack – focused on “UN Sustainable Development Goals” is calling all aspiring change-makers.\nWhether you’re in engineering, business, science, health, environmental studies, humanities, or more, join other like-minded students and solve some of the world’s most important problems. Over the weekend, you will collaborate on addressing global challenges, and form teams, to follow our structured design thinking approach.\nDuring the weekend, you will be led through our structured design sprint:\n\nDiscover your passion and enrich your university experience\nConnect with like-minded people and make new friendships\nExplore career opportunities and grow your professional network\nLearn about real-life challenges and develop critical skills\nBuild a business case, and create a pitch\n\nYou will have access to Mentors, Workshops, Startup Founders and co-founders and will be provided with networking opportunities to connect and learn.\nWho can apply?\nThe event is open to all undergraduate university and college students who have an interest and passion for making an impact in their community and beyond.\nPrizes valued in excess of $2,000.\nSchedule (Location: Bergeron Building)\n\nCheck in: Friday, Oct. 27 at 5:30pm\nOpening Ceremony: Friday, Oct. 27 from 6 to 9 p.m.\n\nTeam formation and problem identification\n\nSaturday, Oct. 28 from 9:30 a.m. to 9 p.m.\n\nSolution Development, Solution Validation and Making a Business Case\n\nClosing Ceremony: Sunday, Oct. 29 from 9 a.m. to 4 p.m.\n\nStudents practise pitching and receiving feedback; invited teams will make a pitch and be awarded prizes.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/unhack-2023-design-solutions-impact-lives/
CATEGORIES:Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Faculties,Lassonde School of Engineering,Schulich School of Business
LOCATION:Bergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence @ 11 Arboretum Ln, North York, ON M3J 2S5, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/https___cdn.evbuc_.com_images_573472569_225829800867_1_original.jpg
END:VEVENT
