SUMMARY:Study Integrative Arts at York University
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE EVENT\nEver wonder if there is a bachelor program can allow one to discover their own artistic journey? Look no more and sign up for our Integrative Arts program (BA) info session to discover the freedom to blend various art forms, from music to visual arts, and chart your unique path in the world of Arts. Focusing on the intersection of arts, entrepreneurship, and technology, you will learn through collaboration inside and outside the classroom.  \nBuild your unique curriculum by pursuing personal interests across AMPD programs, including course options from Cinema & Media Arts, Digital Media, Dance, Music, Theatre, and Visual Art & Art History.  \nThe event is led by Emilia White, an assistant professor and program coordinator of Integrative Arts in the Department of Computational Arts.  \nDecember 6, 2023\n10:00 am to 11:00 am (EST)\nRegister HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9LpfBfhgQsiAmk6FS1_iIw#/registration )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS\nEmilia White (she/they) is an assistant professor and program coordinator of Integrative Arts in the Department of Computational Arts. Formerly, Emilia taught at the University of Michigan Stamps School of Art & Design. Emilia boasts a BFA in Theatre & Original Works and an MFA in Studio Arts. Currently, her research delves into female embodiment and motherhood, using humor to approach the grotesque. They’re working on a witty video animation called “40 Year Old ZIT” about aging and a DIY publication titled “The Ugly Placenta” on maternal health. \nEmilia’s art has graced venues across North America, Taiwan, and Indonesia, including Collar Works and the Museum of Contemporary Art Detroit. They’ve also co-curated The Performance Laboratory in Detroit and were part of the political arts collective Taring Padi in Indonesia. Born in Northern California, Emilia is a proud parent of two wonderful kids. \nMeet Lan Vu the International Recruitment Officer for the York University School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design (AMPD). Lan holds a master’s degree in education from Canada, where she was once an international student herself. With 15 years of experience in student advisory roles, Lan has been a guiding light for countless students navigating their educational journeys.  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/study-integrative-arts-at-york-university/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/integrativearts.jpg
END:VEVENT
