SUMMARY:Study Creative Technologies at York University
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE EVENT\nAn exciting exploration of York University’s Creative Technologies program (BFA) awaits you. Join Dr. Caines to learn how our students apply creativity, collaboration, and entrepreneurship to address real-world problems in fast-changing industries, such as the ethics of disruptive technologies, web3, the development and application of artificial intelligence, and more. \nNovember 13, 2023\n1:00 pm to 2:00 pm (EST)\nRegister HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_XWpfnzj8TiefjgYORo9ErQ )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS\nDr. Rebecca Caines ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/rebecca-caines/ ) is a versatile professor, artist, and writer, specializing in community engagement, project management, interdisciplinary creativity, sound, and mobile devices. She creates art, collaborates with industry partners in health, education, and technology, and publishes in academic journals. Currently, she’s the Project Lead for a new Creative Technologies program at York University, offered exclusively at York’s new Markham Campus starting September 2024. Her courses cover project facilitation, digital culture, and topics like sound, artificial intelligence (AI), and live event technology. \nMeet Lan Vu the International Recruitment Officer for the York University School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design (AMPD). Lan holds a master’s degree in education from Canada, where she was once an international student herself. With 15 years of experience in student advisory roles, Lan has been a guiding light for countless students navigating their educational journeys.  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/study-creative-technologies/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/creativetech.jpg
END:VEVENT
