SUMMARY:Audition Monologue Workshop for Theatre at York University
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE EVENT\nIn this Audition Monologue Workshop, participants will explore how to prepare for an Acting audition, which is an essential part of the actor’s craft. The workshop will explore: (1) Breaking down text; (2) Personalizing text; and (3) Audition technique. \nParticipants should come with a short monologue from a play (2 minutes or less) that they’re ready to explore. \nDecember 8, 2023\n8:00 am to 9:00 am (EST)\nRegister HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_PFZV6Y3eT1-PSJqN86R1CA )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS\nJamie Robinson ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/jamie-robinson/ ) is a versatile artist and professor at York University. He’s directed for CBC Gem, Canadian Stage, and more, and has acted at the Stratford Festival of Canada. Jamie teaches Acting/Directing at York University, where his research explores Canada’s casting practices. He’s also the co-chair of York U AMPD’s committee for Decolonization, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion (DEDI). \nMeet Lan Vu the International Recruitment Officer for the York University School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design (AMPD). Lan holds a master’s degree in education from Canada, where she was once an international student herself. With 15 years of experience in student advisory roles, Lan has been a guiding light for countless students navigating their educational journeys.  \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/audition-monologue-workshop-for-theatre/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/theatre.jpg
END:VEVENT
