SUMMARY:Class of 2023 EUC Fall Convocation Reception Lunch
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change is hosting a special reception in Stong College’s Master’s Dining Hall (basement level) ( https://map.concept3d.com/?id=1200#!w/43.77276,-79.50879,0;43.77153,-79.51204,0;0 ) to celebrate our Class of 2023 grads and to meet the friends and family who join them at Convocation.\nWe are thrilled to invite you, your family, and friends to celebrate your extraordinary accomplishments. All EUC community members are welcome to attend our Faculty Reception on Friday October 13 at 12:30 p.m. Eastern Time.\nPlease register here (by Oct 6) to let us know that you plan to join us at the special event before your Convocation Ceremony. ( https://euc.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=199309 )\n Here is how we’re making this event special in a number of ways:\n\nLight refreshments will be served;\nRemarks from Dean Alice J. Hovorka;\nA photobooth for selfies and a photographer will be available to capture your special moment;\nAnd of course, spend a bit more time with your professors, classmates and EUC staff.\n\nCan’t make the lunch?\n\nNot to worry. EUC will have a table on-site at the reception tent. We look forward to seeing you after your ceremony!\n\nFor those NOT ATTENDING convocation:\n\nWe will miss you and look forward to welcoming you the next time you are back on campus. The convocation ceremony will be live-streamed via https://www.yorku.ca/convocation ( https://www.yorku.ca/convocation/ ).The ceremony starts at 3:30pm ET.\n\nStay Connected:\n\nFollow us on social media @YorkUEUC ( https://twitter.com/YorkUEUC ), connect with us on LinkedIn ( https://www.linkedin.com/in/yorkueuc/ ) and join our LinkedIn group ( https://www.linkedin.com/groups/6715378/ ).\nIf you are interested in sharing your graduation story for our marketing efforts, please get in touch for more details!\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/class-of-2023-euc-fall-convocation-reception-lunch/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:101 Stong College (MDR)
