SUMMARY:Level Up: Becoming an Entrepreneur: Young alumni panel and Q&A
DESCRIPTION:Have you dreamed about starting your own business or becoming an entrepreneur? Attend our upcoming virtual alumni entrepreneurship panel and Q&A and learn valuable advice for launching and growing a start-up business. This panel will feature three award-winning alumni who have launched successful start-ups as entrepreneurs:\n\nSuzanna Alsayed (BA ’16, BA ‘17, MDEM ’20), Founder & CEO, Evolutz Inc. and 2022 York Top 30 Alumni Under 30 recipient.\nNick Di Scipio (BEng ‘23), Founder & CEO, Pantheon Prototyping\nFaridah Yagboyaju (IBBA ’22), Program Manager, Bell Canada, Founder, MErai and 2023 York Top 30 Alumni Under 30 recipient.\n\nPanelists will discuss:\n\n\n\nTheir career journeys, including starting their companies as students and recent grads.\nThe highs and lows of running a start-up.\nAdvice for starting a company, touching on a variety of topics including: marketing, funding, resilience and the importance of mentorship.\n\n\n\nRegistration is required in advance. Attendees will have the opportunity to ask questions during the Q&A portion of the panel discussion.\nDate: Tuesday, Oct. 17, 2023 | 12 p.m. ET\nFormat: Zoom webinar\nHost: Prakash Amarasooriya, (BSc ’15), Learning Solution Architect, TD; CEO and Founder, Kashamara Productions\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/level-up-becoming-an-entrepreneur-young-alumni-panel-and-qa/
