SUMMARY:Calumet & Stong Colleges Spirit Day Event: Friendly Competition with Outdoor Activities
DESCRIPTION:York University will be celebrating Spirit Day on October 4, 2023. Spirit Day takes place once a year, during which time the York community is invited to participate in festivities where we celebrate and recognize the people who continue to make this University a success, including our students, faculty and staff.\nFriendly Competition with Outdoor Activities\nThe purpose of this activity is to promote teamwork, physical fitness, and camaraderie through friendly competition. Participants will form teams and compete in various outdoor games or challenges. This activity fosters a sense of community and teamwork. It encourages individuals to come together, build bonds, and work toward common goals in a positive and healthy manner.\nLocation: Grassy Field to the south of Stong College, across from entrance to Stong Residence: https://maps.app.goo.gl/oPfCMBxHsWhhtxaR6Time: 11:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/calumet-stong-colleges-spirit-day-event-friendly-competition-with-outdoor-activities/
ORGANIZER;CN=Calumet &amp; Stong Colleges (CCSC):MAILTO:
