SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home | Unpacking and understanding the importance to a Land Acknowledgement: It is not just a script
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Ruth Green, Associate Professor and Special Advisor to the Dean’s Office on Indigenous Issues on March 20 at 12 p.m. to learn a bit about the history of the York University Land Acknowledgement and what it really means to the people that wrote it. Dr. Green will share about the Dish with One Spoon and the Two Row wampum as she discusses responsibilities of peace, friendship and mutual respect.\n
