SUMMARY:Outdoor Experience Treetop Trekking
DESCRIPTION:Challenge yourself to new heights. Travelling by bus, participants will head to Stouffville Treetop Trekking, where they will enjoy three hours of ziplining and aerial games through the trees. From suspension bridges and Tarzan swings to balance logs, the activities are suitable for a wide range of abilities with no experience necessary. A safety orientation and all equipment will be provided upon arrival.\nThis Outdoor X trip runs on Friday, Oct. 27. It is a total of five hours. We will be leaving the Tait McKenzie Centre at 10 a.m. The price includes transportation, access to the park, all equipment and a snack.\nThose attending must have proper footwear, such as running or hiking shoes. Please do not arrive in open-toed shoes, Crocs, slides or anything with a heel. The event takes place rain or shine (with the exception of lightning in the area), so please dress according to the weather. We recommend comfortable, athletic layers (no jeans). Please bring an elastic to tie back long hair and avoid any loose articles of clothing that may get caught in the ropes. Water and a snack will be provided part way through the trip, but please bring a reusable water bottle and any other snacks you may want.\nFor more information or to register, visit the Outdoor Experience Program website.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/outdoor-experience-treetop-trekking/
