SUMMARY:2023 Canadian Jewish Literary Awards
DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to announce that the 2023 Canadian Jewish Literary Awards ceremony will take place on Oct. 15 at 2 p.m. at the Tribute Communities Recital Hall, Accolade East Building, York University.\nThis year’s honorees are:\nBiography/Memoir: Moshe Safdie for If Walls Could Speak: My Life in Architecture\nChildren and Youth: Heather Camlot for The Prisoner and the Writer\nFiction: Lori Weber for The Ribbon Leaf\nHistory (The Irving Abella Award): Doris Bergen for Between God and Hitler: Military Chaplains in Nazi Germany\nHolocaust: Josef Lewkowicz for The Survivor: How I Survived Six Concentration Camps and Became a Nazi Hunter\nJewish Thought and Culture: Sara Ronis for Demons in the Details: Demonic Discourse and Rabbinic Culture in Late Antique Babylonia\nPoetry: Gary Barwin for The Most Charming Creatures\nScholarship: Derek Sayer for Postcards from Absurdistan: Prague at the End of History\nYiddish: Rebecca Margolis for Yiddish Lives On: Strategies of Language Transmission\n***\nSpecial Achievement Award: Michael Posner for Leonard Cohen, Untold Stories\nSpecial Citation: Simon-Pierre Lacasse for Les Juifs de la Révolution tranquille : regards d’une minorité religieuse sur le Québec de 1945 à 1976\n \nRSVP: eventbrite.com/e/2023-canadian-jewish-literary-awards-tickets-719279342877?aff=oddtdtcreator.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2023-canadian-jewish-literary-awards/
ORGANIZER;CN=Israel and Golda Koschitzky Centre for Jewish Studies:MAILTO:cjs@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies
LOCATION:Accolade East Building, Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/230914-YorkCJS-CJLA2023-FB-01-scaled.jpg
