SUMMARY:DARE Celebration Event
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies (LA&PS) is celebrating this year’s cohort of students who received the Dean’s Award for Research Excellence (DARE) this summer, with a special event on Wednesday, October 4 from noon until 2 pm at the Scott Library’s Collaboratory.\nEach year, undergraduate students selected for the Dean’s Award for Research Excellence (DARE) receive $5,000 and the unique opportunity to work with a LA&PS faculty member on a designated research project. This year’s DARE Research Poster Session and Celebration features diverse projects from students enrolled in the programs that cross the entire spectrum of LA&PS.\nThe event does not require registration and is open to all.\nLearn more\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/dare-celebration-event-158/
ORGANIZER;CN=LA&amp;PS Dean's Office:MAILTO:lapsdo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,LA&amp;PS Addressing Anti-Black Racism,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Open to the Public,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-International,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Vanier College
LOCATION:Collaboratory, Scott Library (Second Floor) @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 2S5
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/DARE-cover.jpg
END:VEVENT
