SUMMARY:Teaching and Learning with Hong Kong Canadian Youth: Some Reflections
DESCRIPTION:With Amardeep Kaur, Canadian Studies, University of Toronto\nDr Kaur will provide an overview of the Hong Kong-Canadian astronaut family and their experience with transnational circular migration. She will also offer insights into the unique challenges and opportunities that arise when working with Hong Kong Canadian youth.\nThis is the inaugural event of the YCAR Hong Kong Studies Group Lecture Series 2023–24.\nAll faculty, undergraduate and graduate students are welcome.\nFor more information about the Hong Kong Studies Group, click this link. ( https://ycar.apps01.yorku.ca/hong-kong-studies-group/ )\n
