SUMMARY:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Interdisciplinary Studies?
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Interdisciplinary Studies? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJcocuusqTktH9TqoDAERbouB0QomcpyhJCx )\nThe Master’s in Interdisciplinary Studies—one of the first formalized graduate programs in Canada—enables highly motivated students to study within three distinct disciplines in order to deeply explore a particular problem or phenomenon. Students have the option to propose a research project and choose scholarly lenses from an intriguing range of interdisciplinary fields. The student’s unique area of inquiry may combine the fine arts, sciences, health, social sciences, engineering, humanities, law and more.\nTo learn more about others sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsnews@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsnews@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/are-you-thinking-of-pursuing-your-graduate-education-in-interdisciplinary-studies/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
