SUMMARY:AMPD Industry Talks: Film Directing with Sharon Lewis
DESCRIPTION:YORK UNIVERSITY MOTION MEDIA STUDIO\nin collaboration with\nOYA BLACK ARTS COALITION (OBAC)\npresent\nIndustry Talks Series\nHosted by SARAH BAY-CHENG Dean, York University School of the Arts Media Performance & Design (AMPD) \nGuest Speaker SHARON LEWIS, Film Director\nDate: Friday, January 26, 2023\nTime: 6 p.m. to 8 p.m.\nLocation: York U Motion Media Studio (777 Kipling Ave, Toronto M8Z 5Z4 ( https://goo.gl/maps/TmtstHtA5Pr2WgFG8 ))\nFree event.\nRegistration required for entry.\nRSVP: yumms@yorku.ca ( mailto:yumms@yorku.ca )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS \nDr. Sarah Bay-Cheng\nDr. Sarah Bay-Cheng ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/sarah-bay-cheng/ ) is Dean & Professor, School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design at York University. Her research focuses on the intersections of media and performance, including four books & more than 75 articles and essays. Current research focuses on data in cultural arts policy and history.\nSharon Lewis\nSharon Lewis ( https://www.thesharonlewis.com/ )‘ directing work has been well received on premium broadcasters such as HBO, NBC, Hulu, Netflix, Amazon, STARZ, FX and every Canadian broadcaster platform. Sharon is well known in the screen industry for her directing flair, distinct cinematic voice, and her ability to inspire award-winning performances from her actors.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ampd-industry-talks-with-sharon-lewis/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/industrytalks4.jpg
END:VEVENT
