SUMMARY:AMPD Industry Talks: Filmmaking with Naomi Jaye
DESCRIPTION:YORK UNIVERSITY MOTION MEDIA STUDIO\nin collaboration with\nOYA BLACK ARTS COALITION (OBAC)\npresent\nIndustry Talks Series\nHosted by JOHN GREYSON Associate Professor, Cinema and Media Arts \nGuest Speaker NAOMI JAYE, Filmmaker \nDate: Friday, November 24, 2023\nTime: 6 p.m. to 8 p.m.\nLocation: York U Motion Media Studio (777 Kipling Ave, Toronto M8Z 5Z4 ( https://goo.gl/maps/TmtstHtA5Pr2WgFG8 ))\nFree event.\nRegistration required for entry.\nRSVP: yumms@yorku.ca ( mailto:yumms@yorku.ca )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS \nJohn Greyson \nJohn Greyson ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/john-greyson/ ) is a filmmaker, video artist, writer, activist, and educator whose productions have won accolades at festivals throughout the world. He joined the full-time faculty in York University’s Department of Cinema & Media Arts in 2005.\nNaomi Jaye \nNaomi Jaye ( http://www.filmfatales.org/directors/naomijaye#:~:text=Filmmaker%20Naomi%20Jaye%20has%20a,only%20Yiddish%20language%20narrative%20film. ) is known for her cinematic scale, unconventional storytelling, and striking visual execution. Her works include Miriam’s World, MRI, and The Water being mounted at the Harbourfront Centre Theatre 2023.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ampd-industry-talks-with-naomi-jaye/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
