SUMMARY:AMPD Industry Talks: Photography & Videography with Elijah De Los Santos
DESCRIPTION:YORK UNIVERSITY MOTION MEDIA STUDIO\nin collaboration with\nOYA BLACK ARTS COALITION (OBAC)\npresent\nIndustry Talks Series\nHosted by INGRID VENINGER Director, Motion Media Studio\nGuest Speaker ELIJAH DE LOS SANTOS Director & CEO, Of the Saint Productions\nDate: Friday, October 27, 2023\nTime: 6 p.m. to 8 p.m.\nLocation: York U Motion Media Studio (777 Kipling Ave, Toronto M8Z 5Z4 ( https://goo.gl/maps/TmtstHtA5Pr2WgFG8 ))\nFree event.\nRegistration required for entry.\nRSVP: bminor@yorku.ca ( mailto:bminor@yorku.ca )\nABOUT THE SPEAKERS \nIngrid Veninger \nIngrid Veninger ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/ingrid-veninger/ ) is a writer, director, producer, full- time faculty at York University and Director of the Motion Media Studio at Cinespace. She has produced 15 feature films with premieres at TIFF, Rotterdam, Locarno, Busan, Whistler, Rome, Hot Docs and Karlovy Vary with retrospectives of her work at the Canadian Film Institute in Ottawa and FemCine in Chile.\nElijah De Los Santos\nElijah De Los Santos ( https://www.themom3ntnet.com/about ), aka Of The Saint, is a visionary photographer/videographer celebrated for amplifying stories worldwide, leaving an indelible mark on Toronto’s creative scene bridging art and emotion.\n
