SUMMARY:Navigating Queer Resources
DESCRIPTION:It is no secret that 2SLGBTQ+ folks can face some unique barriers and challenges in university life. From struggling to find a safe community to trying to find queer-friendly resources to support health and wellness, it can feel like a lot to navigate. This workshop is meant to simplify this process for queer folk and allies here at York! \nJoin the Health Education and Promotion Team as we examine the unique barriers and stigma faced by the 2SLGBTQ+ community, discuss the importance of holistic wellness by utilizing the wellness wheel framework, and discover many of the queer-friendly resources available both on and off campus pertaining to: \n\nQueer informed mental health support \n\n\nFinding community and homelessness support \n\n\nPhysical health care including gender affirming care and queer-friendly primary care providers \n\n\nSexual health support \n\nTo register, click here! ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=260029 ) \nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete): https://forms.office.com/r/AhNyJRd7ea \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
