TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Navigating Mental Health Resources (Online Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:Transitioning to university is challenging enough. The quality of your health and well-being impacts everything from managing your stress, make time for your loved ones, and still work towards your academic success. Join the Health Education & Promotion team to learn the following:\n\nWhat is mental health and why it is important to consider your mental wellbeing as a student. \n\n\nDiscuss the barriers students face when accessing mental health support and destigmatize the topic of mental health.  \n\n\nLearn about what mental health services and well-being supports are available and accessible to students.   \n\nAll our online workshops require York University authentication (passport York). Please login into your zoom account prior to clicking the meeting link.   \n  To register, click here.\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete): https://forms.office.com/r/U3A1m9F3cR \nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body. \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/navigating-mental-health-resources-online-workshop/
CATEGORIES:Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Event Planners Network,Markham Campus,Stong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students
END:VEVENT
