SUMMARY:Black Students Careers Community Workshop 1: Kickoff and LinkedIn Networking (Community Workshop)
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Black Student Careers Community!\nHosted by the Jasmine Morton (career educator) and the Career Centre, in partnership with various teams within York University, we will be hosting a series of career development workshops through the ’23/’24 academic year for Black students. These will be safe, inclusive spaces, designed to help you develop your own career success. Workshops throughout the year will include:\n\nNetworking and effectively using LinkedIn\nWriting your best job applications, including resumes and cover letters\nPreparing and aceing interviews\nHow to thrive professionally with awareness of systemic issues\nExploring career decisions and opportunities\nLooking at ‘imposter syndrome’\n\nWe also have a LinkedIn group for our careers community! Moderated by Jasmine, she will share events, you can share your successes, ask any quick questions and generally support each other.\nBlack identifying students can join here ( https://www.linkedin.com/groups/14307873/ )\nYou can also book a 1:1 chat with Jasmine at the Career Centre through Experience York!\nTo register for this event, login to Experience York and access the Employers Events calendar.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/black-students-careers-community-workshop-1-kickoff-and-linkedin-networking/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Co-op &amp; Career Centre
LOCATION:Ross Building S802
END:VEVENT
