TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Beginner’s Knitting Class with Health Education & Promotion
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that the rhythm of knitting releases serotonin, the chemical that helps regulate anxiety, happiness, and mood? So much so in fact that it’s comparable to meditating! Knitting also helps in being more mindful by promoting focus on breathing, clearing thoughts, and taking time to be in the moment. Join the Health Education and Promotion team to boost your mental health, connect with likeminded students, and learn a new life skill you didn’t know you were missing. In this workshop you will learn to knit a drink coaster. Why a coaster you may ask? This particular knitting pattern is one of the simplest you can get so it’s perfect for beginners!  \nTo register, Click here! ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=272985 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/beginners-knitting-class-with-health-education-promotion/
