SUMMARY:Special Event During the UN 2023 SDG Summit: Addressing Global Water Insecurity
DESCRIPTION:Join us virtually on Monday, Sept. 18 at 3:30 p.m. ET for a special event for the UNITAR Global Water Academy, co-presented by York University, UNITAR and United Nations University, during the UN SDG Summit, with a panel titled “Addressing Global Water Insecurity: Harnessing the Power of Big Data, Novel Technologies and International Collaboration.”\nFeaturing water experts from around the world – live from UN Headquarters – this panel will create a dialogue on how new technologies, large open-access databases, and inclusive international collaborations hold the potential to identify the extent and causes of global water insecurity, particularly in regions where data and resources can be limited.\nFor more information and to register, visit yorku.ca/research/WaterInsecurityPanel ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/WaterInsecurityPanel ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/special-event-during-the-un-2023-sdg-summit-addressing-global-water-insecurity/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/AddressingGlobalWaterInsecurityPanel.png
END:VEVENT
