SUMMARY:Taking Effective Breaks
DESCRIPTION:Have you just started classes and already running out of steam? Have you felt lower energy levels and increased brain fog? Is it harder to pay attention to lectures and readings?\nWell, taking breaks can help with re-energizing yourself, but what you do during those breaks can really make a difference.\nIn this in-person workshop you’ll learn about the benefits of passive and active leisure and create your own leisure plan, which will include practical ways to engage in self-care and enhance your energy levels. Learn self-care strategizes that support limited time and budget especially during exam season.\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form ( https://forms.office.com/r/Q4dEwNB48T ) (it takes less than 1 minute to complete).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/taking-effective-breaks-5/
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being
LOCATION:N110 Bennett Centre
END:VEVENT
