SUMMARY:Mindful Painting & Art Session
DESCRIPTION:Studies have shown that most people who try art as a form of therapy or stress relief have experienced significant reductions in cortisol levels when doing so. Painting allows for emotional release because it stimulates the creative side of your mind while focusing your attention in one place, which can lower anxiety.\nIn this way, the creative outlet improves your mental health significantly. Join the Health Ed team in taking advantage of the benefits of art therapy and taking a break to paint and connect with likeminded students.\nPlease register in advance!  ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=255348 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mindful-painting-art-session/
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being
LOCATION:N110 Bennett Centre
END:VEVENT
