TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Improving your Relationships with Social Media
DESCRIPTION:We are constantly and unconsciously consuming messages from the media, which can manifest insecurities and impact our self-esteem in ways that we may not even be aware of.\nIn this in-person workshop we will work to develop critical skills on decoding and dissecting some of the harmful marketing tactics used by companies and social media influencers. We hope to:\n\nDebunk the world of social media, celebrity culture and advertising\nHow to reduce appearance-focused conversations and comparisons\nHow social media can be catered to empower self-acceptance\n\nOur goal is that audiences learn how to utilize social media in a safe, supportive, and empowering way.\nWe hope to see you there! Please register in advance now.  ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=254382 )\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form ( https://forms.office.com/r/4dVNUVntzh ) (it takes less than 1 minute to complete).\nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/improving-your-relationships-with-social-media/
LOCATION:N110 Bennett Centre @ Room N102
END:VEVENT
