SUMMARY:Navigating Mental Health Resources
DESCRIPTION:Transitioning to university is challenging enough. The quality of your health and well-being impacts everything from managing your stress, make time for your loved ones, and still work towards your academic success.\nJoin the Peer Health Educator Team for this in-person workshop to learn how to:\nWhat is mental health and why it is important to consider your mental wellbeing as a student.\n\nDiscuss the barriers students face when accessing mental health support and destigmatize the topic of mental health.\nLearn about what mental health services and well-being supports are available and accessible to students.\n\nWe hope to see you there! Please register in advance.  ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=254002 )\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form ( https://forms.office.com/r/U3A1m9F3cR ) (it takes less than 1 minute to complete).\nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n
