SUMMARY:Navigating Physical Health Resources
DESCRIPTION:The quality of your physical health and well-being impacts everything from managing your stress, make time for your loved ones, and still working towards your academic success. However, it can sometimes be challenging to know which resources are out there to help you upkeep your physical health as students!\nJoin the Peer Health Educator Team for this in-person workshop, as they guide you through:\n\nIntroducing what OHIP and UHIP are.\nHighlighting what you can do when you are feeling sick.\nGuide you through the student accessible primary care resources available.\nAnd guide you through further on campus resources for maintaining your physical health!\n\nWe hope to see you there! Please register in advance ( https://forms.students.yorku.ca/view.php?id=253157 ).\nBefore attending the presentation, please fill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form ( https://forms.office.com/r/3p5VSyfbpd ) (it takes less than 1 minute to complete).\nThis form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n
