SUMMARY:Film Screening: Stolen Children: Residential School Survivors Speak Out & Truth and Reconciliation: The Legacy of Residential Schools in Canada
DESCRIPTION:Stolen Children: Residential School Survivors Speak Out\n2015, 19min\nThis CBC documentary looks at how the Residential School system affected survivors, and their children and grandchildren through personal interviews.\nTruth and Reconciliation: The Legacy of Residential Schools in Canada\n2016, 30min\nThis program examines the history, legacy and current impacts of the Residential School experience in Canada. From the establishment of the early Residential Schools to the work of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission, this film shines a light into this dark chapter of Canadian history.\nWritten and directed by multiple award winning Métis filmmaker Matt LeMay, this poignant documentary features interviews with Phil Fontaine, Shawn Atleo, Dr. Marie Wilson, Dr. Mike Degagne, and Martha Marsden.\nTo register for these film screenings visit, https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRfilmscreenings ( https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRfilmscreenings ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-films-documentaries-stolen-children-residential-school-survivors-speak-out/
CATEGORIES:ND4TR
LOCATION:Sound &amp; Moving Images Library (SMIL), Room 124 Scott Library
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/23062-ND4TR_Events-Banner-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
