SUMMARY:Film Screening: Muffins for Granny
DESCRIPTION:Muffins for Granny\n2006, 1h28m\nDirected by Nadia McLaren Muffins for Granny is a remarkably layered, emotionally complex story of personal and cultural survival. McLaren tells the story of her own grandmother by combining precious home movie fragments with the stories of seven elders dramatically affected by their experiences in residential school. McLaren uses animation with a painterly visual approach to move the audience between the darkness of memory and the reality that these charismatic survivors live in today.\nTo register for this film screening, visit https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRfilmscreenings ( https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRfilmscreenings ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-films-documentaries-muffins-for-granny/
CATEGORIES:ND4TR
LOCATION:Junior Common Room (012)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/23062-ND4TR_Events-Banner-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
