SUMMARY:National Day for Truth and Reconciliation at York University
DESCRIPTION:Susan Dion, Associate Vice-President Indigenous Initiatives will host a community panel— Speaker Reflections—featuring the voices of staff reflecting on their learning journey through engaging in various forms of media. The panel discussion will be followed by a ceremonial fire and light refreshments at Skennen’kó:wa Gamiig for those attending in person. Participants will be offered a tobacco tie and invited to offer it to the ceremonial fire.\nThe event will be live streamed online and recorded for all community members to participate remotely.\nTo register for the event, visit https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRspeakerreflections ( https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRspeakerreflections )\nTo view this event online please, visit https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRspeakerreflectionslivestream ( https://yorku.ca/go/ND4TRspeakerreflectionslivestream )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/national-day-for-truth-reconciliation-at-york-university/
CATEGORIES:ND4TR
LOCATION:Helliwell Centre, Osgoode Hall Law School, York University @ Ignat Kaneff Building, 4700 Keele Street, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3
