SUMMARY:The Allan I Carswell Observatory Grand ReOpening
DESCRIPTION:This reopening celebrates the finish of a grand renovation project at the observatory, including new robotic domes and more! In addition, starting on September 6th, we will be resuming in-person public tours of the Observatory every Wednesday (except holidays) evening after sunset. To join the tour, come to the 3rd floor of the Petrie Science and Engineering building (PSE) from 8-10pm, and walk to the blue Observatory doors. All regular tours will be listed on the observatory website with FREE Eventbrite tickets at: https://www.yorku.ca/science/observatory/\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/this-reopening-celebrates-the-finish-of-a-grand-renovation-project-at-the-observatory-including-new-robotic-domes-and-more-in-addition-starting-on-september-6th-we-will-be-resuming-in-person-publi/
ORGANIZER;CN=Allan I. Carswell Astronomical Observatory:MAILTO:observe@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Bethune College,Faculty of Science,Glendon
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/DSC00191-1024x683-1-scaled.jpg
