SUMMARY:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Financial Accountability?
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Financial Accountability? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJIvdOCtpjMvHNBzOFryBO7wQ3pOjiYULHqg )\nFounded in 2009, The MFAc is the only program of its kind in the world, which consists of four dynamic and interrelated conceptual cornerstones: (1) Corporate Ethics; (2) Regulative Standards and Legislative Requirements; (3) Effective Information Systems; and (4) Transparency in Reporting (the program’s ultimate goal). Students are well equipped with the tools and knowledge required to deal innovatively with complex organizational, ethical, legislative and financial realities in their careers.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsnews@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsnews@yorku.ca ).\n
