SUMMARY:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Art History & Visual Culture?
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Art History & Visual Culture? We invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0pfuiorDssGtV7B8QXUaTevKY9bTrshQrY )\nThe Graduate Program in Art History is designed to meet contemporary Canadian needs in the areas of art and architectural history, critical theory and writing, visual culture, and the gallery and museum field. The objective of the program is to prepare candidates for careers in art history and academia, as well as in publishing, curatorial practice, museology and arts administration. Part-time students, especially those with experience in the discipline, are encouraged to apply.\nTo learn more about other sessions being offered during our Experience Grad York week, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ).\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsnews@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsnews@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/are-you-thinking-of-pursuing-your-graduate-education-in-art-history-visual-culture/
