SUMMARY:Anchor YorkU Community Presentation
DESCRIPTION:Anchor YorkU is a concrete demonstration of how York University can contribute in impactful ways to the surrounding communities. This event has not been held for a few years, but it’s back and it’s a great opportunity to meet in-person and do the following:\n\nshare the achievements and impact of Anchor YorkU, 2021-23;   \ndiscuss and confirm important next steps for Anchor YorkU;   \nre-engage more broadly with Anchor YorkU; and \nbring the community and the University together in shared Anchor YorkU planning.\n\nThe formal part of the meeting will take place from 2:30 to 4 p.m., with informal conversation and networking to follow. Those who have been actively working on Anchor YorkU look forward to seeing everyone at the end of August.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/anchor-yorku-community-presentation/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Finance &amp; Administration,Vice Provost Academic
LOCATION:519 Kaneff Tower @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
