SUMMARY:Special Virtual Event UN HLPF: Humanitarian responses to emerging water crises as a result of extreme climatic events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event during the High-Level Political Forum on Sustainable Development and inaugural event from the UN Global Water Academy at York University! 🌍🚰 \n📅 Date: July 14th ⏰  \nTime: 10 AM \n📍 Location: Zoom Webinar  \nPanel topic: Humanitarian Responses to Emerging Water Crises \nLearn from global experts as they discuss humanitarian challenges and solutions to the freshwater crisis caused by extreme climatic events. Don’t miss this opportunity to be part of the conversation and contribute to sustainable water solutions! \nFor more details and to RSVP, click here: https://bit.ly/3rrEevk  ( https://bit.ly/3rrEevk )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/special-virtual-event-un-hlpf-humanitarian-responses-to-emerging-water-crises-as-a-result-of-extreme-climatic-events/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Slide1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:York University
CLASS:PUBLIC
UID:MEC-e64a98242922f7799ec4a0ad6999924f@events.yorku.ca
DTSTART:20230714T140000Z
DTEND:20230714T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20230712T202500Z
CREATED:20230712
LAST-MODIFIED:20230712
PRIORITY:5
SEQUENCE:2
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Humanitarian Responses to Emerging Water Crises as a Result of Extreme Climatic Events
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Friday, July 14, 2023 at 10 a.m. ET for a special inaugural event from the UN Global Water Academy during the High-Level Political Forum on Sustainable Development with a panel entitled, “Humanitarian responses to emerging water crises as a result of extreme climatic events.”\nExtreme climatic events, including heatwaves, droughts, and storms, are increasing in frequency and intensity over the past few decades, with consequences for freshwater. Extreme climatic events have been associated with changes in freshwater availability and degradation of water quality, including elevated concentrations of nutrients, contaminants of emerging concern, and potential for algal blooms, some of which may be toxic. As humans and wildlife rely on freshwater for life, alterations in the freshwater supply in response to extreme climatic events can have catastrophic impacts, particularly during humanitarian crises.\nBringing together four renowned experts who work at the heart of humanitarian solutions through technology, engineering, global governance, and advocacy, this virtual panel aims to explore the humanitarian responses, challenges, and solutions to alleviating the freshwater crisis, particularly in the face of global environmental degradation and extreme climatic events.\nRegister for the panel here: https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_eQBQe37mRmyVjYZdEk4-xw#/registration ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_eQBQe37mRmyVjYZdEk4-xw#/registration )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/humanitarian-responses-to-emerging-water-crises-as-a-result-of-extreme-climatic-events/
CATEGORIES:Research &amp; Innovation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Slide1-2-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
