SUMMARY:Nellie Library Pop-Up Book Sale
DESCRIPTION:Hello everybody,\nHappy summer! Picture this: sitting in the shade on a warm day with a cool drink and a compelling book that you bought from the Nellie Langford Rowell Library at a huge discount. Make this vision a reality by visiting our Pop-Up Book Sale!\nThe Nellie has a lot of new(ish) fiction for sale. We carry works by Jane Austen, Paul Auster, Douglas Adams, and Agatha Christie, as well as massive collections of mysteries, thrillers, and fantasies. We also sell memoirs and religious/spiritual materials, along with non-fiction and theory commonly used in GSWS courses, including texts from Monique Wittig, bell hooks, Donna Haraway, and Virginia Woolf.\nBooks range in price from 50¢ to $2, and we only accept cash. Let’s get to reading everybody! We hope to see you there.\nWarm regards,\nThe Nellie Team\nnlrowell@yorku.ca\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/nellie-library-pop-up-book-sale-3/
ORGANIZER;CN=Nellie Langford Rowell Library:MAILTO:nlrowell@yorku.ca
