SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: How do children remember? Insights from research about memory and brain development
DESCRIPTION:Join Thanujeni Pathman, Associate Professor, Department Of Psychology July 26 at 12 p.m. for Scholars’ Hub @ Home.\nThis presentation examines what we know about children’s memory and the factors that support memory development, including changes that are occurring in the brain as kids get older. Learn about the sophisticated memory abilities in young children when they were tested in naturally occurring situations. Viewers will also learn about the implications of this type of child development research for forensic settings (e.g., eyewitness testimony) and education.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-childrens-memory-in-the-wild/
