SUMMARY:York U Motion Media Studio and Shooting the Set present Salted
DESCRIPTION:Green Screen meets the new Neo-Realism!\nJoin us for a sneak preview screening of six new short films, collectively created by 30 AMPD students in our YUMMS “Shooting the Set” summer intensive course.\nGrads and undergrads worked together as actors, writers, DOPs, editors and directors to create this anthology series of original stories, linked by the thematic of salt.\nDATE: Friday, June 16, 2023\nTIME: 2:30 PM\nLOCATION: York U Motion Media Studio at CineSpace ( https://goo.gl/maps/aDYUJkqGvEmadC5h7 ) (777 Kipling Ave, Toronto M8Z 5Z4) – Enter Through Security Gate 4 Security\nFREE ADMISSION\nRSVP REQUIRED: bminor@yorku.ca ( mailto:bminor@yorku.ca )\nFEATURED FILMS \nGarlic Olive Oil and Salt\nPlacebo\nLittle Aggressions\nDigging for Sunshine\nBon Appetit\nOn Me\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-u-motion-media-studio-and-shooting-the-set-present-salted/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/movie.jpg
