TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Departments of English and Humanities present Patricia Park
DESCRIPTION:8 June 2023 via Zoom\n2:30pm-3:30pm\nPatricia Park is the novelist of Re Jane, a modern-day reworking of Charlotte Brontë’s Jane Eyre with a Korean-American Jane, and the new YA novel, Imposter Syndrome & Other Confessions of Alejandra Kim. She’s a tenured professor of creative writing at American University. She’s written for the New Yorker, the New York Times, the Guardian, and others.\nJoin us for a discussion run by Patricia Park regarding her novel Re Jane. She will read from her novel, discuss how she reimagined Brontë’s Victorian Gothic text for 21st-century readers, and answer questions about creative writing and rewriting.\nPlease email Professor Natalie Neill at nneill@yorku.ca for Zoom link.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/departments-of-english-and-humanities-present-patricia-park/
ORGANIZER;CN=Meaghan McCue:MAILTO:mmccue@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of English,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/books-ona-a-shelf.jpg
END:VEVENT
