SUMMARY:CISS Members Strawberry Beading event – Indigenous students prioritized
DESCRIPTION:The York Centre for Indigenous Student Services (CISS) invites all self-identifying Indigenous students to the 2023 Strawberry Beading Workshop, hosted by event facilitator Marissa Magneson.\nBead a strawberry pin or earrings and get to know fellow Indigenous students. Event details below:\n \n[This workshop is currently full.]\n\nOpen to Indigenous CISS members and Indigenous York Students\n12 spots for in-person event with an hybrid option, see RSVP email address for details on the latter.\nMonday, June 12 at noon to 3 p.m.\nSkennen’kó:wa Gamig\nRSVP by June 1 to nancyj9@yorku.ca for location confirmation\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ciss-members-strawberry-beading-event-indigenous-students-prioritized/
CATEGORIES:National Indigenous History Month
