SUMMARY:Water Security, Climate Change & Resilience: Sharing Experiences from the UN Water Conference with Our Community & Partners
DESCRIPTION:Members of OneWATER will share their experiences from the recent UN Water Conference, held earlier this year in New York. It will be a great opportunity to gain insights into the current challenges and innovative solutions in the field of water security, climate change, and resilience. OneWATER researchers are excited to showcase their work in the water field and exchange valuable knowledge with community and partners.\nThe event is organized by Sapna Sharma (Science), Marina Freire-Gormaly (Lassonde), and Sylvie Morin (Science) in collaboration with the OneWATER Institute ( https://www.yorku.ca/research/onewater/ ), Women & Inclusivity in Sustainable Energy Research (WISER) ( http://wseresearch.com/ ), and CIFAL York. ( https://www.yorku.ca/cifal/ )\nBe sure to register by June 10th : https://research.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=178059 ( https://research.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=178059 ) \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/water-security-climate-change-resilience-sharing-experiences-from-the-un-water-conference-with-our-community-partners/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Science,Lassonde School of Engineering
