SUMMARY:Meet-and-Greet: Artist Zeelie Brown
DESCRIPTION:Students and faculty are encouraged to attend a meet-and-greet with Visiting Artist-in-Residence Zeelie on May 18th at 10:30am in HNES 138.\nZeelie’s artistry stems from her upbringing in rural Alabama. She creates Black and queer refuges called ‘soulscapes’ – blending sound, performance, installation, wilderness and more to provide solace and challenge systemic oppressions.\nZeelie Brown is being hosted by Professor Andil Gosine ( https://euc.yorku.ca/faculty/andil-gosine/ ). Zeelie will be collaborating with the EUC community to create a quilt to explore the intersections of Black and Queer identities and nature, and will be shared at Dr. Gosine’s keynote lecture ( https://ssaaes.org/2023/04/03/keynote-plenary-panel-for-2023-conference/ ) at the Sexuality Studies Association conference as part of Congress @ York on May 29th.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/meet-and-greet-artist-zeelie-brown/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:HNES 138
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Zeelie-Brown-Photo-e1683555914720.png
END:VEVENT
