SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: BEEc and the York Bee Collection: Globally Recognized Research at York University
DESCRIPTION:Join Laurence Packer, Professor, Department of Biology, Faculty of Science and Victoria MacPhail, PhD, Coordinator, Centre for Bee Ecology, Evolution, and Conservation on May 18 at 12 p.m. for Scholars’ Hub.\nIn this presentation, viewers will learn about the research undertaken by the Centre for Bee Ecology, Evolution and Conservation (BEEc), a network of faculty, staff, and students based at York University investigating topics on the genetic through ecosystem level. A particular focus will be on bee diversity: why and how York has one of the world’s best collections of bees on the planet.\n \n
