SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: From the workplace to the kitchen: Understanding the influence of masculinity on behaviour
DESCRIPTION:Our next Scholars’ Hub @ Home will take place on May 3 at 12 p.m. with Luke Zhu, Associate Professor, Organizational Behaviour and Industrial Relations, Schulich School of Business.\nThis presentation explores the impact of masculinity on behaviour, from workplace aggression to unhealthy eating habits. Drawing from research about gender stereotypes and precarious manhood theory, this presentation will provide viewers with a deeper understanding of how masculine norms can shape our actions and the underlying cognitive processes. Additionally, practical solutions for addressing these issues will be discussed.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-from-the-workplace-to-the-kitchen-understanding-the-influence-of-masculinity-on-behaviour/
