SUMMARY:Earth Day at the Farm: Downsview Earth Day
DESCRIPTION:We welcome one and all to join us for Earth Day. Come and get your hands in the dirt and spend time with your neighbours. Bring a snack to share and your water bottle.\n \nHosted by Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change Professor Jose Etcheverry and Masters of Environmental Science student Codrina Ibanescu, President of Rural Urban Learning Association, this event is in partnership with our colleagues at the Toronto Black Farmers and Growers Collective and Downsview Park.\nWe welcome one and all to join us for Earth Day. Come and get your hands in the dirt and spend time with your neighbours. Bring a snack to share and your water bottle.\nThe day’s itinerary includes: tree planting, bird watching, trishaw rides, guided nature walks, and the opportunity to learn and connect with our education staff, vendors and more\nSee the Downsview Park event ( https://downsviewpark.ca/events/earth-day-downsview-park ) website for more information, and see eventbrite.ca ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/earth-day-jour-de-la-terre-tickets-568679384347 ) to register for this free event!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/earth-day-at-the-farm/
CATEGORIES:Earth Month,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change
LOCATION:Parc Downsview Park
