SUMMARY:13th Annual Glendon Graduate Student Conference
DESCRIPTION:13th Annual Glendon Graduate Student Conference in Translation Studies – April 14th and April 15th at York University, Glendon Campus.\n“TRANSLATION  and UNHEARD VOICES”\nTwo keynote speakers! Dr. Janis Cole, from Gallaudet University, and Dr. Anthi Wiedenmayer, from Aristotle University of Thessaloniki. For the conference program and other details, please visit: https://www.glendon.yorku.ca/transconf/ ( https://www.glendon.yorku.ca/transconf/ )\nYou may attend in person or online. For information and registration, click here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/13th-annual-glendon-graduate-student-conference-in-translation-studies-tickets-602883369387 ( https://www.eventbrite.com/e/13th-annual-glendon-graduate-student-conference-in-translation-studies-tickets-602883369387 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/13th-annual-glendon-graduate-student-conference/
LOCATION:A100 - Centre of Excellence @ 2275 Bayview Ave, North York, ON M4N 3M6, Canada
END:VEVENT
