SUMMARY:Transition Tuesdays
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a history of academic accommodations such as an Individualized Academic Accommodation Plan (IEP)?  Are you a student with a learning disability/disorder, chronic health or mental health condition, attention disorder (ADD or ADHD), brain injury, physical or mobility disability, sensory disability or impairment (Deaf, deafened, hard of hearing, Blind, low vision, partially sighted), on the Autism spectrum, and/or from the neurodiverse or diverse ability community?\nTransition Tuesdays will answer questions about the academic accommodation process, introduce students to key campus supports and support a successful transition to York.\nStudents and their parents, or other support persons, are welcome to attend.\nThis session will take virtually (via Zoom). To take part please complete this Meeting Registration Form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEoduCgrzgtHtHtMAjtmSl48N9AHIT5b--Q ).  A Zoom link will be sent to the email address provided as soon as you submit the form.\nQuestions? Contact eechoi@yorku.ca\nWe strive to make our events fully accessible.  Please email eechoi@yorku.ca if you require American Sign Language (ASL) interpreting.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/transition-tuesdays-3/
CATEGORIES:Student Accessibility Services
