SUMMARY:Classrooms to Careers: Rebranding Disability Through Achievement with Lime Connect
DESCRIPTION:This webinar is part of the Career Centre’s week-long webinar series Classrooms to Careers for Students with Disabilities ( http://careers.yorku.ca/classrooms-to-careers ).\nJoin Lime Connect to learn tips on how to disclose your disability to an employer during an interview or when you start work. You will also learn how Lime attracts, prepares, and connects university students with disabilities for internships and full-time careers with corporate partners. Lime Connect is a global not-for-profit organization that’s rebranding disability through achievement. Facilitated by Karen Kelsey, Relationship Manager, Canada Lime Connect.\nRegistration through Experience York ( http://careers.yorku.ca/experienceyork ) is required. If you require accessibility needs to access this webinar, please contact the Career Centre as soon as possible so we can assist you with accessing this webinar. Email us at career@yorku.ca\nIn partnership with Student Accessibility Services.\n
