SUMMARY:Grand Community Iftar
DESCRIPTION:The York University community is invited to join us on the evening of Thursday April 6th, from 6 – 9pm for a Community Iftar Banquet for charity, hosted by the Keele & Glendon Muslim Student Associations in partnership with Student Life: The Centre for Student Community & Leadership Development.\nTickets are $25, and can be bought here: https://yuscld.ticketleap.com/iftar/ ( https://yuscld.ticketleap.com/iftar/ )\nProceeds from ticket sales will be donated towards earthquake relief in Türkiye & Syria by way of Human Concern International.\nAll are welcome & invited, including folks from all faiths, to join & enjoy the fundraising efforts, as well as an array of guest speakers & performers for an evening of unity, solidarity & celebration of the beauty of Islam.\nGuest speakers, du’a, breaking of the fast & Maghrib prayer to be observed. Followed by dinner.\nIf you would like to attend but are unable to financially, or have any questions, please email: Urshian Khalid (urshkhal@yorku.ca). No one will be turned away.\nSpeakers include: \n\nHassam Munir @hassam.history\nLabibah Salim @labibah.salim\nAhmed Adan @wordsof1der\nIman Dirie @signediman\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grand-community-iftar/
