SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: Ecological futures and energy infrastructure across continental North America
DESCRIPTION:Investment in the North American energy infrastructure will have a major impact on our ability to protect the global ecosystem for decades to come. As such, North American pipeline projects have become particularly controversial among climate justice advocates given their implications for carbon emissions, Indigenous land use and notably the way they lock in particular ecological futures.\nJoin us for this special Earth Day presentation with Anna Zalik, Associate Professor in the Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change who will be examining the disputes over Canadian pipelines delivering natural gas.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/scholars-hub-home-ecological-futures-and-energy-infrastructure-across-continental-north-america/
