TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Not a Checkbox: Engaging in a Culture of Equitable Teaching (Decolonization, Equity, Diversity & Inclusion in Teaching & Learning Community of Practice 2023 Conference)
DESCRIPTION:As academic institutions move towards post-pandemic teaching and learning, the return to “normal” has reinforced and reproduced issues of power and privilege in the academy, such as ableism, racism, and classism. In this call for collaborators, we ask learning communities at York to consider how we can engage in a culture of equitable teaching that intervenes and disrupts the flow of “normalcy.”\nEquity is not a checkbox to be completed. It is a relational process of engaging in different social relations. In this collaborative conference, together, we will ask how we can cultivate safe and caring conditions in our learning spaces, structures, policies, and processes. How do we co-create flexible and adaptable strategies and systems that accommodate diverse learning needs and ways of being? What can we learn from listening to and sharing our experiences around DEDI (Decolonizing, Equity, Diversity, and Inclusion)?\nConference Dates:\nMonday, May 15th – Tuesday, 16th 2023\nConference is free and open to all those who teach at York University.\nPre-register your interest in attending this event by completing this form ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=973157 ).\nConference is free and open to all those who teach at York University. It will be held in a hybrid format, with options for attending and participating both in-person and virtually.\nRegistration deadline: May 1st, 11:59.\nConference Dates: Monday, May 15th – Tuesday, 16th 2023\nConference is free and open to all those who teach at York University. It will be held in a hybrid format, with options for attending and participating both in-person and virtually.\nRegistration deadline: May 1st, 11:59.\nClick here to register to attend this conference. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=973157 )\nClick here to view the detailed conference schedule.\nClick here to join our Community of Practice. ( https://teachingcommonsforms.apps01.yorku.ca/forms/view.php?id=829047 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/not-a-checkbox-engaging-in-a-culture-of-equitable-teaching-decolonization-equity-diversity-inclusion-in-teaching-learning-community-of-practice-2023-conference/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/notfinal.jpg
END:VEVENT
