SUMMARY:The Department of English presents John Edwards
DESCRIPTION:The music of the Blackfriars’ Theatre\n27 March 2023\n11:30am – 12:30pm\nRoom VC 104\nThe King’s Men’s use of the more exclusive Blackfriars’ Theatre (where admission prices were up to a whopping 2 shillings!) meant that a more discerning audience was going to demand more sophisticated and ‘court’-eous entertainment than the bloody heads and rustic jigs of the Globe Theatre. John Edwards discusses the importing of court masque instruments, vocal music techniques, and dance numbers into plays for the Blackfriars after 1600.\n
