SUMMARY:Crisis and Struggle in Sri Lanka: One Year On
DESCRIPTION:Register at: www.tinyurl.com/30mar2023 ( http://www.tinyurl.com/30mar2023 )\nOne year after Sri Lanka’s political and economic crises, we bring together a panel of academics, journalists and activists to discuss the continuing challenges and possibilities for political change.\nSwasthika Arulingam | Attorney at Law; President of the Commercial and Industrial Workers Union, Sri Lanka\nMythri Jegathesan | Associate Professor, Department of Anthropology, Santa Clara University\nThiruni Kelagama | Lecturer in South Asian Studies, University of Oxford\nMahendran Thiruvarangan | Senior Lecturer in English Literature, Department of Linguistics & English, University of Jaffna\nJayadeva Uyangoda | Professor of Political Science (Retd.), University of Colombo\nThis event is part of the Demos, Democratization and Democracy in South Asia series at York University and is presented by Jamhoor and the York Centre for Asian Research.\nCo-sponsored by: Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies; Department of Anthropology; Department of Politics; Department of Social Science; Department of Sociology; Faculty of Arts, Media, Performance and Design; Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change; Graduate Program in Communication and Culture; Office of the Vice-President, Research & Innovation.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/crisis-and-struggle-in-sri-lanka-one-year-on/
ORGANIZER;CN=York Centre for Asian Research:MAILTO:ycar@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Political Science,International,LA&amp;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp;PS Students All,Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Virtually via Zoom
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Jamhoor_30032023web-scaled.jpg
