SUMMARY:The Queer Comics Symposium
DESCRIPTION:York University’s Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies and the Departments of English and Humanities proudly present\nThe Queer Comics Symposium\nFeaturing:\nProfessor Michelle Ann Abate ( https://english.osu.edu/people/abate.30 ) (Ohio State University), author of Tomboys: A Literary and Cultural History ( https://tupress.temple.edu/books/tomboys ) (Temple University Press)\nProfessor Justin Hall ( https://portal.cca.edu/people/jhall/ ) (California College of the Arts), cartoonist and editor of No Straight Lines: Four Decades of Queer Comics (Fantagraphics)\nProfessors Alison Halsall ( https://profiles.laps.yorku.ca/profiles/ahalsall/ ) and Jonathan Warren ( https://profiles.laps.yorku.ca/profiles/jwarren/ ) (York University), editors of The LGBTQ+ Comics Studies Reader ( https://www.upress.state.ms.us/Books/T/The-LGBTQ-Comics-Studies-Reader ) (University Press of Mississippi)\nA screening of the award-winning documentary, No Straight Lines: The Rise of Queer Comics (dir. Vivian Kleiman, Compadre Media)\n \nFriday, 28 April 2023\n12-3 PM: Lecture and Panel Discussion, York University, Accolade Building East, Room 005 ( https://map.concept3d.com/?id=1200#!ct/29093?s/ )\n6-10 PM: Lecture and Screening, Buddies in Bad Times Theatre ( https://buddiesinbadtimes.com/ ), 12 Alexander Street, Toronto ( https://goo.gl/maps/nBT7PChk6gRqh18h6 )\nQueries may be directed to Professors Alison Halsall (ahalsall@yorku.ca ( mailto:ahalsall@yorku.ca )) and Jonathan Warren (jwarren@yorku.ca ( mailto:jwarren@yorku.ca )).\n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-queer-comics-symposium/
