DESCRIPTION:To celebrate Earth Month, the York community is invited to participate in campus tree planting at Glendon (April 12) and Keele campus (April 13)! This event will help create positive change – a greener campus with restored ecosystems to help mitigate climate change.\nNOTE: Limited number of spots for tree planting. Please indicate in the registration link below if you would like to participate in Glendon AND/OR Keele tree planting events. The Office of Sustainability/Regenesis will contact registrants a few days prior to the event to provide more details.\nThis event is sponsored by the UNFCCC’s Youth Climate Report ( https://unfccc.int/topics/education-youth/resources/youth/youth-climate-report ). A special thank you to the City of Toronto and Facility Services at York University for their help in making this event possible.\nREGISTER HERE: https://sustainability.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=25602 ( https://sustainability.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=25602 )\n \n\n          \n \n
