TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Is Democracy Broken?
DESCRIPTION:\n \nOur next edition of the Glendon Global Debates: “Is Democracy Broken?” will be held on April 4, 2023, at 7 PM, featuring The Honourable Elizabeth Dowdeswell, Lieutenant Governor of Ontario.\nREGISTER NOW\n \nThe Panelists\nClare Hutchinson \nFormer Senior gender advisor with the United Nations Department of Peacekeeping & Power Corp Fellow, Glendon College\nSusan Pond\nFormer NATO executive & BMO Senior Fellow, Glendon College\nEmily Laxer \nAssociate Professor, Sociology, York University’s Glendon Campus & York Research Chair in Populism, Rights, and Legality\nEvent Description\nDifferent phenomena are affecting the faith in and the functioning of democracies: growing inequalities (and the failure of reforms to address them); the rise of social media and their detrimental effects on public discourse; and the growing tendency of political parties across the spectrum to exploit divisions, whether real or perceived.\nDo these contemporary shifts in political activity and discourse suggest that democracy is broken, or is it just frayed?\nThis event will be hybrid and bilingual.\nQuestions? Please contact gouellet@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/is-democracy-broken/
CATEGORIES:Glendon,Glendon Alumni &amp; Friends,Glendon Continuing Education,Glendon Current Students,Glendon International Studies &amp; Business Administration Dual Degree,Glendon Masters in Public &amp; International Affairs
LOCATION:BMO Skyroom - York Hall A300 @ Glendon Campus, York University - 2275 Bayview Ave., Toronto @ M4N 3M6
END:VEVENT
