SUMMARY:York Dances 2023: Convergence
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Dance presents\nYork Dances 2023: Convergence\nYork Dances 2023: Convergence features new choreographic works of 27 third year BFA majors performed by students engaged in all levels of York’s programs in Dance. Convergence dances are born of our celebration of being together, our respect and sometimes struggle for individuality, and our dedication to the positive power of community.In addition to steering their own creative processes, the students led every facet of the production of York Dances, supported by faculty at every level of creation, performance, and production. The two series will feature 27 new works staged in the McLean Performance Studio March 30 and 31, at 7pm and 8:30pm.\nCourse Director: Maxine Heppner\nWork/Study Team: Christian Sears, Jordyn Bartholomew\nWork/Study Supervisor: Jennifer Jimenez\nYork Dances 2023: Convergence\nMarch 30-31, 2023\n7:00 pm – Series A\n8:30 pm – Series B\nMcLean Performance Studio ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/mclean-performance-studio/ ), 244 Accolade East Building\nAdmission: $12 until March 26, 2023 / $17 Regular\nBox Office: 416-736-5888 | ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice/ )\n \n
