SUMMARY:“Imaging Imaginations” Storytime for children ages 2 to 6 and their caregivers
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of National Reading Month, please join us for a morning of childrens’ stories, songs, and rhymes at the gallery. AGYU welcomes parents of children between 2 and 6 to attend this special Storytime event guided by a Registered Early Childhood Educator.\nOn Saturday, March 25, families are welcome to visit our current exhibition, Meleko Mokgosi: Imaging Imaginations, and enjoy a reading of children’s literature expanding on themes in the exhibition. A sample of select titles include: Amazing Grace by Mary Hoffman, Please Louise by Slade Morrison and Toni Morrison, The Dot by Peter H. Reynolds, Mix it Up by Hervé Tullet, and more.Coffee, tea, and light refreshments will be served in the gallery lobby.\n
