SUMMARY:World Music Festival (2023)
DESCRIPTION:York University’s World Music Festival is a cross-cultural celebration spotlighting musical traditions around the world.\nProduced by Professor William Thomas ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/william-thomas/ ) this global sonic tour presents a sampling of several international cultures represented in York’s world music program.\nThe festival packs three concerts into one day: Thursday, March 16, 2023\nMaps and Directions ( http://maps.info.yorku.ca/keele-campus/ )\nTHURSDAY MARCH 16\n12:30 PM – West African (Ghana) – Kwasi Dunyo and Larry Graves ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/larry-k-graves/ ), Ensemble Directors\n2:00 PM – Escola de Samba – Rick Lazar ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/rick-lazar/ ), Ensemble Director\n4:30 PM – Caribbean Music Ensemble –  Gareth Burgess ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/gareth-burgess/ ), Ensemble Director\nLOCATION: Tribute Communities Recital Hall  ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ )\nTICKETS: $5\nBox Office ( https://music.ampd.yorku.ca/box-office/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/world-music-festival-2023/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/worldmusicfest.jpg
END:VEVENT
