TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Inclusion Week Series March 6-10 2023
DESCRIPTION:Inclusion Week Series March 6-10, 2023 – Centre for Human Rights, Equity and Inclusion (yorku.ca) ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-series-march-6-10-2023/ )\n\n\nINCLUSION WEEK 2023 – Reclaiming Social Justice in EDI \n\n\n\n\nMarch 6-10, 2023 \n \nCHREI’s annual Inclusion Week is just around the corner, and we want to tell you about our exciting line-up of speakers and events. This year CHREI has partnered across the York campus, and we are excited about these collaborations. Visit our website often for additional information and remember to register early! \n \n\nWhat does Social Justice have to do with it? \n\n\n              A fireside chat with guest speakers who will explore the (dis)connections between EDI and Social Justice \n\nDate: Mar. 7th 11AM – In person panel event  \nGuest panelists: Prof. Susan Dion, AVP Indigenous Initiatives, York \n      Remi Warner, Dir. of Human Rights Services, TMU,  \n      Rania El Mugammar, Artist+Anti-Oppression Consultant,  \n      Prof. Jessica Vostermans, CDS, York \nIn-person Registration here  Register early!\n            (Bring your questions, enjoy refreshments and giveaways) \n              Registration to access streaming \n \n\nReclaiming the Transformative Roots of DEDI/EDI\n\nDate: Mar. 8th 11AM – Online Event \nOur keynote speaker Kike Ojo-Thompson will reflect on: \nWhat does DEDI have to do with social justice movements? \nWhat are the tensions between DEDI and social justice movements?\nAre DEDI and social justice movements compatible or contradictory?  \n \nThis is an online event, please register early \n \nOur exciting line-up continues in the week with CHREI and SCLD workshops: \n\nA Long Overdue Conversation: Oppression and Privilege Mar. 6th 11am on Zoom (registration link) \nAdvancing Organizational Change to foster belonging Mar. 10th on Zoom (registration link) \n\n \nCHREI has partnered with the Campus Community to bring you events throughout the week. Our Partners: \n\n\n\nAmnesty International YU – Poetry Readings highlighting decolonization\nAthletics & Recreation – Keynote\nGlendon College – Interactive event\nAMPD – Sensorium Exhibit with Prof. Joel Ong\nSchulich School of Business – Fireside chat on tensions of EDI with corporate frameworks\nThe Centre – Community of practice discussion with EDI educators\nProf. Jessica Vostermans’ Graduate Class – Alternative Campus Tour\n\n\n \nVisit our website for more details: \nhttps://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-series-march-6-10-2023/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInclusion Week Series March 6-10, 2023 – Centre for Human Rights, Equity and Inclusion\n\n\nWatch this space. More events and details coming soon. The Centre for Human Rights, Equity & Inclusion, in collaboration with partners across York University invites everyone to be a part of this year’s Inclusion Week series. This year’s events are being led in partnership with Amnesty International YU, Athletics & Recreation, Sensorium at the School […]\n\n\nrights.info.yorku.ca\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/inclusion-week-series-march-6-10-2023/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Human Rights, Equity &amp; Inclusion:MAILTO:chrwkshp@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion
LOCATION:Zoom @ zoom link
