SUMMARY:Connections: Leveraging my Liberal Arts Degree
DESCRIPTION:Students in the Humanities and Social Sciences: your degree is your ticket to success!\nCome to our first in-person speed-mentoring event since 2020!\nMeet successful York graduates who started out by earning a Liberal Arts degree, and who are now enjoying successful and fulfilling careers in business, government, and the not-for-profit sector.\nThis event is a chance for students to learn about career paths, receive advice and have their questions answered by people who have gone before them.\nBrowse our Mentor Bios ( https://www.yorku.ca/laps/connections/mentors/?wpv_view_count=361154&wpv-connections-event-date=0&wpv_filter_submit=Submit ) to see the alumni who participated in past events. Some of them will be back!\nRegister\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/connections-leveraging-my-liberal-arts-degree/
ORGANIZER;CN=Dean's Office - Advancement:MAILTO:mgmitrov@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp;PS Department of Communication &amp; Media Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of English,LA&amp;PS Department of Equity Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of French Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of History,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS Department of Languages, Literatures &amp; Linguistics,LA&amp;PS Department of Philosophy,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS School of Gender, Sexuality and Women's Studies,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
LOCATION:Convention Centre, Second Student Centre @ 4700 Keele St, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
