SUMMARY:What does Black History Month mean to you?
DESCRIPTION:February is Black History Month, a time to focus on the contributions and achievements of Black Canadians. Black Excellence at York University (BE YU) Peer Leads will examine what Black History Month means to them during this session, while highlighting Black leaders they admire and their accomplishments. Participants will also get a chance to discuss what Black History Month means to them and/or the Black leaders they admire. To reserve your spot, please complete our registration form ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJwtd-6hqzkqH9Sppr96AWe4Zjs14Gqhxs3P ).\nThis session is open to all students at York and students who identify as Black are encouraged to attend.\n
