SUMMARY:Globally Networked Learning: Faculty Info Session
DESCRIPTION:\nThe Globally Networked Learning (GNL) ( https://yorkinternational.yorku.ca/gnl/ ) approach engages faculty and students from different locations around the world to participate in collaborative class discussions, joint lectures, assignments and/or research projects through innovative pedagogies and the use of online communication and information technologies. In addition to innovative pedagogical approaches, GNL promotes and facilitates intercultural communication and global learning for both faculties and students.\nYork University faculty members who will integrate GNL in their courses will have access to many supports, including York International, the Teaching Commons, University Information Technology (UIT), and the York Libraries along with resources from the partner university. To further assist York faculty members to co-develop resources for their GNL course and support GNL initiatives, there is also an award of $1,000.\nThe GNL award application ( https://yorkinternational.yorku.ca/gnlapplication/ ) deadline for Fall 2023 & Winter 2024 terms is February 28, 2023.\n \n
URL:https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0odeCgpz0oGdA1Y0S4s12NqK1s4VTc7649
ORGANIZER;CN=York International:MAILTO:goglobal@yorku.ca
