SUMMARY:Faculty Concert Series: Al Henderson Quintet
DESCRIPTION:Acclaimed jazz composer, bassist, arranger and York University music Professor Al Henderson leads his ensemble as part of the Department of Music’s Faculty Concert Series. The Al Henderson Quintet brings a collection of original compositions to the Tribute Communities Recital Hall at York’s Keele campus February 14.\nJoining Henderson onstage are Nic Vasiliou (piano), Sam Ruttan (drums), Alex Dean (saxophones) and Pat LaBarbera (saxophones). The concert will feature a selection of Henderson’s original compositions and arrangements.\nHenderson has been a seminal force on the Canadian jazz scene for more than 30 years. He has earned critical acclaim and legions of fans as leader of his own bands – the Al Henderson Septet, Quintet and Quartet – and co-founder and co-leader of the groundbreaking group, Time Warp. He has also performed as sideman with many leading jazz artists including Diana Krall, Jane Bunnett, Arnett Cobb, Hank Crawford, Slim Gaillard, Jimmy Knepper and Flip Phillips.\nAs a composer, Henderson has created a large and distinctive repertoire of original works. More than 60 of his compositions have been recorded by his bands as well as other eminent artists such as Don Pullen, Jane Bunnett, Shox Johnson & the Jive Bombers, Alex Dean and Richard Whiteman. His accolades include the Jazz Report’s Composer of the Year designation and the prestigious SOCAN Award for Original Jazz Composition.”… Al Henderson is the real thing, a composer in the tradition of Duke Ellington and Charles Mingus, whose works have distinctive energy and melodic and harmonic character,” said jazz writer Stuart Broomer (Toronto Life).\nAdmission: $20 | $15 (students and Seniors)\nTICKETS ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/b_otix.asp?cboPerformances=1982&cboEvent=926 )\nMaps & Directions ( https://map.concept3d.com/?id=1200#!m/325781 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/faculty-concert-series-al-henderson-quintet-150/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ Accolade East Building 83 York Boulevard, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/alhenderson.jpg
END:VEVENT
