SUMMARY:Nellie Library Book Club Event
DESCRIPTION:The Nellie Langford Rowell Library is pleased to invite all students to our inaugural Book Club meeting where we will discuss the novel Split Tooth by Tanya Tagaq. The Nellie Library would appreciate your participation in examining the work of Tagaq, an Inuk throat singer, songwriter, storyteller, and visual artist from Nunavut.\nSplit Tooth relays the experiences of a girl growing up in Nunavut in the 1970s. In a blend of fiction, memoir, and Inuit legend, presented through poetry and prose, Tagaq depicts a community that struggles with violence, alcoholism, and poverty, but brims with love and tradition that continues to light the way despite any hardships.\nAdmission to the event is free. Refreshments will be served.\nCome prepared for an engaging discussion about this haunting and tender exploration of an Inuit community in the 1970s. We promise a great time and we look forward to seeing you there.\nRegistration\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/nellie-library-book-club-event/
ORGANIZER;CN=Nellie Langford Rowell Library:MAILTO:nlrowell@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp;PS Department of Communication &amp; Media Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of Economics,LA&amp;PS Department of English,LA&amp;PS Department of Equity Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of French Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of History,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS Department of Languages, Literatures &amp; Linguistics,LA&amp;PS Department of Philosophy,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS Nellie Library,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Gender, Sexuality and Women's Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Human Resources Management,LA&amp;PS School of Information Technology,LA&amp;PS School of Public Policy &amp; Administration,LA&amp;PS School of Social Work,LA&amp;PS SNACK,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-International,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,LA&amp;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
