SUMMARY:2023 Goldfarb Lecture in Visual Arts: Meryl McMaster
DESCRIPTION:The McMichael is pleased to present a special artist’s talk by Meryl McMaster, Canadian artist of nehiyaw (Plains Cree), British and Dutch Ancestry, who explores the self in relation to land, lineage, history, culture and more-than-human world.\nMcMaster’s work is predominantly photograph based, incorporating the production of props, sculptural garments and performance forming a synergy that transports the viewer out of the ordinary and into a space of contemplation and introspection.\nCoinciding with the survey of the artist’s work in the exhibition Bloodline featured at the gallery from February 4 to May 28, 2023 the talk will be introduced by Sarah Milroy, McMichael Chief Curator and the exhibition’s curator.\nWednesday, March 1, 2023\n5:00 PM\nThe McMichael Canadian Art Collection  ( https://mcmichael.com/event/2023-goldfarb-lecture-in-visual-arts-meryl-mcmaster/?utm_campaign=GoldfarbYorkU&utm_medium=email&utm_source=eVite )\n(10365 Islington Ave, Kleinburg, ON L0J 1C0) \nDeparture from Campus\nThe bus will depart York University Keele campus at 3:30 pm from the front of Centre for Fine Art (CFA).\nReturn to Campus\nThe bus will be depart the McMichael at 7:15 pm to head back to York University Keele campus.\nREGISTER NOW\nSeating is limited (36 seats available)\nOffered in partnership with the Department of Visual Art and Art History of\nYork University.\n________________________________________\nGenerously supported by the Joan and Martin Goldfarb.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2023-goldfarb-lecture-in-visual-arts-meryl-mcmaster/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:McMichael Canadian Art Collection:10365 Islington Ave, Kleinburg, ON L0J 1C0
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/y.jpg
END:VEVENT
