SUMMARY:Improving Your Relationship with Social Media
DESCRIPTION:We are constantly and unconsciously consuming messages from the media, which can manifest insecurities and impact our self-esteem in ways that we may not even be aware of. In this workshop, we will work to develop critical skills on decoding and dissecting some of the harmful marketing tactics used by companies and social media influencers. We hope to:\n\nDebunk the world of social media, celebrity culture and advertising\nDiscuss how to reduce appearance-focused conversations and comparisons\nShow how social media can be catered to empower self-acceptance\n\nOur goal is that audiences learn how to utilize social media in a safe, supportive, and empowering way.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\nBefore attending the presentation:\n\nLog into your Zoom account (with your Passport York credentials) prior to clicking the meeting link.\nFill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete). This form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/improving-your-relationship-with-social-media-2/
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being
LOCATION:Zoom
