SUMMARY:Supporting Peers in Distress
DESCRIPTION:Supporting Peers in Distress aims to provide students with the skills needed to recognize, respond, and refer other peers with mental health concerns. The learning objectives of this session include: Helping participants gain a better understanding of the type of mental health concerns that York University students face, creating safer online spaces for fellow classmates, colleagues and/or friends to disclose mental health concerns and recognizing the unique ways to respond to potential distress or crisis in an online environment.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\n
