SUMMARY:Film Screening and Q&A: The Price of Cheap
DESCRIPTION:Join the free screening and conversation about modern slavery in the fashion industry, Jan. 26 at York University\n\n\n“A powerful film that shows how the pressure on foreign manufacturers to produce clothes at unsustainable prices results in modern slavery of the vulnerable – especially young girls.” – Robin Wright, Actor, Director, Activist\n\nAdmission is free to this event, but we ask that you bring a donation of non-perishable food or basic need items to be provided to the York Federation of Students – Food Support Centre, which provides support for students experiencing food insecurity.\n\nThe event is sponsored by muuvment.com and York University’s Business and Society Program, Green Campus Cooperative, and the International Development Studies Program.\n\nRegister here: https://bit.ly/3X3b8xi\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/film-screening-and-qa-the-price-of-cheap/
