SUMMARY:Countdown to Congress Launch Event
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a sneak peak of Congress 2023, including a preview of live musical and Indigenous dance performances to be featured in York’s Arts@Congress programming. We’ll also share details about opportunities for York students to get involved and offer a “taste of Congress” with some fun and light refreshments.\nCongress 2023: ‘Reckonings & Re-imaginings’\nYork University is hosting the 2023 Congress of the Humanities and Social Sciences this year from May 27-June 2, in partnership with the Federation for the Humanities and Social Sciences ( https://www.federationhss.ca/en ). Congress is the largest academic gathering in Canada, and one of the largest in the world. This year’s theme ‘Reckonings and Re-imaginings ( https://www.federationhss.ca/en/congress-2023-reckonings-and-re-imaginings )‘ is a call to action to ignite positive change on the biggest social and environmental issues of our time.  \nFormat: This event will be held in person and via livestream\nLink to Livestream: https://youtu.be/G5JshK418eI ( https://youtu.be/G5JshK418eI )\nRSVP by Monday, January 23: http://go.yorku.ca/countdowntocongress ( http://go.yorku.ca/countdowntocongress )\n
URL:http://go.yorku.ca/countdowntocongress
ORGANIZER;CN=Congress:MAILTO:congressac@yorku.ca
