SUMMARY:Mid-Career Conversations: Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DEI) as Competitive Advantage 
DESCRIPTION:Mid-Career Conversations were created with alumni like you in mind — alumni who have several years of experience and are now considering (or have already made) an important transition.\nEach event will focus on a specific mid-career transition and feature a fellow alumni speaker sharing their own personal story and experiences. There will be the opportunity to ask questions and then move into virtual breakout rooms to discuss your own unique situations and ambitions.\nJoin Julia M. Satov (BA’11, MEd’14) Global Director of Diversity & Inclusion at Litera on Jan. 19 at 12pm.\nIn this session Julia will share: \n\nher journey towards becoming a Global DEI Leader \nunderstanding how industries have radically shifted and responded to the markets’ demand for DEI to become a powerful skillset for professionals \nHow you create DEI as a Business Imperative \nHow to combat imposter syndrome and leverage your own diversity, the diversity of your colleagues as a superpower\n\nRegister here \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/mid-career-conversations-diversity-equity-and-inclusion-dei-as-competitive-advantage/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/486a8865-a97d-4743-ade3-dad8ee45b103.png
END:VEVENT
