SUMMARY:Femicide, Intersectionality and the Media. Centering Black and Indigenous women, girls & gender-diverse victims
DESCRIPTION:In person webinar sharing featuring the following panelist:\n\nDr. Tope Adefarakan, Black Femicide Canada Council\nElisha Corbett, Native Women’s Association of Canada\nDr. Myrna Dawson, Canada Feminicde Observatory for Justice & Accountability\n\nModeration: Nneka MacGregor\nOpening Remarks: Minister Marci Ien\n \nTo register, please email thecentre@yorku.ca\nAdditionally, for folks who attend York University and wish to view the webinar, York University’s Centre for Sexual Violence Response, Support & Education, WomenatthecentrE’s longstanding community partner, will also be broadcasting the webinar in Room 125 Bergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence!\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/femicide-intersectionality-and-the-media-centering-black-and-indigenous-women-girls-gender-diverse-victims/
ORGANIZER;CN=The Centre for Sexual Violence Response, Support &amp; Education:MAILTO:thecentre@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:The Centre
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/TheCentre-16DaysofActivism-Digital_Calendar-Banner-8.png
END:VEVENT
