SUMMARY:2022 Ian P. Howard Memorial Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Sabine Kastner\nThe Centre for Vision Research is thrilled to be hosting Dr. Sabine Kastner, from the Princeton Neuroscience Institute at Princeton University as its speaker at the 2022 Ian P. Howard Memorial Lecture. This event will take place on Tuesday, November 22nd at 2 p.m. in the Senate Chambers, N940 Ross. All are welcome.\nThis talk honours Ian P. Howard, the founder of York University’s Centre for Vision Research.\nDr. Kastner will discuss “The Neural dynamics of the primate attention network.”\nThe selection of information from our cluttered sensory environments is one of the most fundamental cognitive operations performed by the primate brain. Dr. Kastner will highlight the large-scale network mechanism that acts as a ‘spotlight’ that can be flexibly shifted around the visual scene to focus our visual attention.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/2022-ian-p-howard-memorial-lecture/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Vision research:MAILTO:cvr@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Bethune College,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Health,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Psychology,Research &amp; Innovation,Stong College
LOCATION:Senate Chamber - N940 Ross Building @ York University, Toronto, ON M3J, Canada
END:VEVENT
