SUMMARY:Ernest C. Mercier Lecture in Entrepreneurial Science with Molly Shoichet
DESCRIPTION:The Lassonde School of Engineering and the Schulich School of Business invite you to attend the Ernest C. Mercier Lecture in Entrepreneurial Science on Monday, December 5.\nWe are honoured to welcome Dr. Molly Shoichet, a University Professor at the University of Toronto who served as Ontario’s first Chief Scientist in 2018, to present the lecture Research to Reality: from Asking the What If to Clinical Testing.\nDr. Shoichet is the recipient of many prestigious distinctions and the only person to be inducted into all three of Canada’s National Academies of Science of the Royal Society of Canada, Engineering and Health Sciences. Don’t miss this incredible opportunity to learn from an expert in the study of polymers for drug delivery and tissue regeneration.\nThe lecture will be held in person, and we encourage guests to engage in the Q&A session and the networking reception following the lecture.\nRegister ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/ernest-c-mercier-lecture-in-entrepreneurial-science-with-molly-shoichet-tickets-466304418067 )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ernest-c-mercier-lecture-in-entrepreneurial-science-with-molly-shoichet/
CATEGORIES:Lassonde School of Engineering
LOCATION:McEwen Auditorium, Seymour Schulich Building @ Seymour Schulich Bldg, 111 Ian MacDonald Blvd, North York, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
END:VEVENT
