SUMMARY:YUGAN Annual Lecture + 60 Years of Geography @ York Celebration
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change and the York University Geography Alumni Network (YUGAN) invites you to the YUGAN Annual Lecture on Tuesday, Nov 29 from 3-6pm ET at the Second Student Centre.\nJoin us for a fun evening, gather with friends old and new as we welcome a distinguished researcher to share their research and celebrate 60 years of Geography @ York!\nThe talk “Reimagining Capitalism? or Enacting Post-Capitalist Practices?” will be presented by Katherine Gibson who is a Professorial Research Fellow in the Institute for Culture and Society at Western Sydney University and the 2022 Gough Whitlam and Malcolm Fraser Visiting Professor of Australian Studies, Harvard University. A reception to follow.\nDetails\nDate: Tuesday, November 29, 2022 | 3pm ET\nLocation: York University Second Student Centre – 15 Library Ln, North York, ON M3J 2S5\nTickets: FREE – but RSVP required\nEvent Schedule:\n3:00-4:30pm ET – Lecture by Kathy Gibson\n4:30-6:00pm ET – Reception – Refreshments and beverages will be provided.\nFor more information, contact Joanne Huy, Alumni Engagement Officer at (416)-736-2100 x 44633 or at eucalum@yorku.ca.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/yugan-annual-lecture-60-years-of-geography-york-celebration/
