SUMMARY:York University Wind Symphony
DESCRIPTION:The York University Wind Symphony presents James Bonney’s composition “Chaos Theory” featuring guitarist, and York U. alumna, Melanie Jag. The concert includes works by composers Yasuhide Ito, Kevin Day, Gustav Holst, Julie Giroux, Brian Balmages, John Mackey and William Thomas.\nWilliam Thomas, Conductor\nMelanie Jag, Electric Guitar\nSunday, December 4, 2022\n3:00 PM\nTribute Communities Recital Hall ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/tribute-communities-recital-hall/ ) \nADMISSION\nTickets: $20\nStudents | Seniors: $15\nBox Office: 416-736-5888 | ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice ( https://secure1.tixhub.com/yorku/online/index.asp )\nMELANIE JAG\nMelanie Jag is a jazz/pop guitarist with a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in Music from York University. Throughout her time at York, Melanie gained proficiency in the traditional application of Jazz and its presence in music of all genres and contexts. Outside of her studies, Melanie is also a freelance guitarist who has worked with artists and producers in Canada and the US. Her work as a guitarist ranges from accompanying vocalists to adding melodies over beats, integrating her own flavour to her compositions while maintaining the artist’s vision. Melanie can be found on social media (@MelanieJag) producing content that showcases her creativity and putting her own twist on the latest trends in music.\n\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-university-wind-symphony-6/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall Accolade East Building, York University @ 4700 Keele Street
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/wind-events-banner.jpg
END:VEVENT
