SUMMARY:Nutrition Basics: Plant-Based Diets
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop we will discuss why some students may choose a plant-based diet. We will also debunk some of the common misconceptions surrounding plant-based diets.\nWhat does a well-rounded plant-based diet look like? How hard is it to meet all of your essential nutrient needs ? Does plant-based always mean “healthy”?\nLearn to navigate marketing/labeling pitfalls to maximize your student budget too!\nPlease note this is presentation is created and delivered by Peer Health Educators. The purpose of this workshop is for general education only. We do not condone or promote any particular diet or lifestyle. Please consult a certified dietician to support your specific needs.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\nBefore attending the presentation:\n\nLog into your Zoom account (with your Passport York credentials) prior to clicking the meeting link.\nFill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete). This form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/nutrition-basics-plant-based-diets/
