SUMMARY:Food & Mood: From Gut Health to Mental Heatlh
DESCRIPTION:How does the food you consume affect your grades and your ability to handle life’s challenges and stressors?   This peer-led workshop aims to help educate students on the relationship to nutrition and food choices in how it impacts well-being and our ability to manage stress.\nDid you know 90% of serotonin (aka our happy hormone) receptors are in your gut? In the relatively new field of nutritional psychiatry our gut health and food choices can play a huge impact on positively or negatively affect our mood.\nThis practical workshop shares tips on mood boosting food and nutritional hacks with simple and practical recipes on a student budget.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\nBefore attending the presentation:\n\nLog into your Zoom account (with your Passport York credentials) prior to clicking the meeting link.\nFill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form ( https://forms.office.com/r/mS4Y4utWcQ ) (it takes less than 1 minute to complete). This form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/food-mood-from-gut-health-to-mental-heatlh/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Well-being Week
LOCATION:Zoom
