SUMMARY:Substance Usage: Cannabis 101
DESCRIPTION:Using cannabis (weed, pot) is a personal choice, but it can have short- and long-term effects on your health.\nOur peer-led workshop focuses on debunking cannabis myths.\nWe review types of cannabis forms (edibles, inhalants , topicals) and understanding dosage size, understanding packaging labels interaction with other substances. We also look at safety considerations and provide harm-reduction guidelines to lower health associated health risks and dependency and interaction with other substance use (e.g. alcohol).\nPlease note this is presentation is created and delivered by Peer Health Educators. The purpose of this workshop is for general education only. We do not condone or promote any particular lifestyle choice. Please consult a professional counsellor if you are looking for individual support.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\nBefore attending the presentation:\n\nLog into your Zoom account (with your Passport York credentials) prior to clicking the meeting link.\nFill out our anonymous Pre-Test Form (it takes less than 1 minute to complete). This form helps us ensure our presentation meets the needs of the student body.\n\n
