SUMMARY:Camp d’anticipation
DESCRIPTION:Glendon’s camp d’anticipation will take place over three days (including two overnights) and is designed to give students in grades 10 and 11 (and, if necessary, grade 12) a taste of what university is like and what their journey to university might look like. This activity will give high school students a clearer picture of what to expect in university, both academically and in terms of student life.\nParticipants will have the opportunity to customize their day by choosing from interactive program workshops, career development workshops, as well as workshops with various themes that will practice their current skills and transferability to their university studies.\nDuring camp d’anticipation, students will also have the opportunity to interact with current Glendon students and ask them any questions they may have about their program of study, the transition from high school to post-secondary education, and student life.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/camp-danticipation/
ORGANIZER;CN=Glendon:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Glendon,Glendon Continuing Education
LOCATION:Glendon (détails à venir)
