SUMMARY:FSc Scientists on Science Symposium: Where is the pandemic heading?
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a Scientists on Science Symposium organized by the Faculty of Science and moderated by Vivian Saridakis, Associate Dean of Research & Partnerships.\nDate: Monday, October 17, 2022\nTime: 1:30 PM – 3:00 PM (Presentations, followed by a panel discussion)\nLocation: Lumbers Building (LUM) 306 & Zoom\nTo register, visit: yorku.ca/science/Oct17symposium ( http://www.yorku.ca/science/Oct17symposium )\nZoom Details\nZoom Link: https://yorku.zoom.us/j/93545541338?pwd=NWNYcHgzUTdPQTdaeEdiTHRxT0JVUT09 ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/93545541338?pwd=NWNYcHgzUTdPQTdaeEdiTHRxT0JVUT09 )\nMeeting ID: 935 4554 1338\nPasscode: 142320\nEvent Schedule\n1:30 pm – Welcome remarks by Dean Rui Wang\n1:35 pm – Jane Heffernan: “Immunity and COVID-19”\n1:50 pm – Jude Kong: “Using AI to improve public health preparedness and response to outbreaks”\n2:05 pm – Seyed Moghadas: “Not over yet: COVID-19 and the continuing uncertainty”\n2:20 pm – Huaiping Zhu: “Monkeypox: no need to panic!”\n2:35 pm – Q & A\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fsc-scientists-on-science-symposium-where-is-the-pandemic-heading/
