SUMMARY:Sex on the Couch – 2SLGBTQIA+ Edition 
DESCRIPTION:Let’s talk about all things sex! Our peer health educators and community support team are here to help you navigate the world of 2SLGBTQIA+ sexual health as safely and comfortably as possible.\nJoin us for a community dialog regarding sexual health, consent, healthy relationships, Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs), and practices for safer sex. You are welcome to ask your questions as anonymously as you like, and no question is too strange or silly.\nWhat is a Safer Space? \nA safe space is a supportive and affirming environment for lesbian, gay, bisexual, trans/transgender, queer, two-spirted, non-binary (2SLGBTQIA+) students. While we can never ensure that any space is going to be “safe” and affirming one hundred percent of the time, a safe space is a place, group, or community that is intentionally working to affirm our 2SLGBTQIA+ community. We encourage curiosity and respect everyone’s lived experience. We strive our best to create an online space where you can ask your question to the degree of privacy you prefer. If there are any additional accommodations you specifically require in order to attend this event, please contact us.\nTo reserve your spot, please complete our registration form.\nWhat questions would you like answered?\nLet us know in our Pre-Event Question Submission Form.\nAll responses shared within this form will remain completely anonymous. The goal of this form is to let the facilitators know what topics you would like to cover to ensure our conversations meet student needs.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sex-on-the-couch-2slgbtqia-edition/
CATEGORIES:Health Education &amp; Promotion,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
