SUMMARY:The Shape of ME | RE-IMAGINING FAMILY
DESCRIPTION:A three-hour story workshop unpacking family history through play, featuring mask painting, music and food, and community. To make it more fun, you may bring a favourite family photograph with you!\nFilmmaker and Story Workshop Facilitator, Shabnam Sukhdev will lead you through the engaging process of mask painting and improvisational performance.\nIn the workshop, food and conversation will become important channels of connecting with other participants, unraveling what family means to each of us.\nAll members of the York family are invited to this free event. Space is limited so please register at: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/the-shape-of-me-reimagining-family-tickets-431075417177 ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/the-shape-of-me-reimagining-family-tickets-431075417177 ).\nThis workshop is presented with support from Theatre and Performance Studies and the York Centre for Asian Research at York University.\n
