SUMMARY:Register Open! One Health Modelling for EIDs course with OMNI-RÉUNIS/Fields Institute – Fall 2022/Winter 2023 (deadline October 17)
DESCRIPTION:OMNI-RÉUNIS ( https://omni-reunis.ca/courses-one-health-modelling-for-emerging-infectious-diseases/ ) and Fields Institute for Research in Mathematical Sciences ( http://www.fields.utoronto.ca/ ) have partnered up to launch a two-part course on One Health Modelling for Emerging Infectious Diseases in Fall 2022 and Winter 2023. The online course is free and open to all students, researchers, and professionals interested in learning more about One Health Modelling for Emerging Infectious Diseases\nCheck out the OH Course Poster and Schedule ( https://secureservercdn.net/104.238.68.196/p3b.ab6.myftpupload.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/OH-Modelling-Course-Poster-Schedule_2022_2023-1.pdf ) along with the course syllabus (Part 1: Fall 2022 ( https://secureservercdn.net/104.238.68.196/p3b.ab6.myftpupload.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/OneHealthCourse-Part1_OMNI-REUNIS-Fields-Institute_Fall-2022.pdf ) & Part 2: Winter 2023 ( https://secureservercdn.net/104.238.68.196/p3b.ab6.myftpupload.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/OneHealthCourse-Part2_OMNI-REUNIS-Field-Institutes_Winter-2023.pdf )) for more details! Course Description: http://www.fields.utoronto.ca/activities/22-23/one-health-I ( http://www.fields.utoronto.ca/activities/22-23/one-health-I )\nThe course schedule includes both synchronous and asynchronous classes to give students the opportunity to self-pace their learning and access resources and support as needed. Instructors will be available during contact hours for questions and support. Upon registration, students will receive further details.\nOMNI-RÉUNIS instructors include:\n\nWoldegebriel Assefa Woldegerima, Assistant Professor at the Department of Mathematics, York University\nMarina Freire-Gormaly, Assistant Professor in Mechanical Engineering Department at the Lassonde School of Engineering at York University\nJulien Arino, Professor and Faculty of Science Research Chair in Fundamental Science with the Department of Mathematics at the University of Manitoba\nKatie Clow, Assistant Professor in One Health in the Department of Population Medicine at the Ontario Veterinary College, University of Guelph\nRebecca Tyson, Associate Professor in Mathematical Biology at the University of British Columbia\n\nDeadline to Apply: October 17, 2022\nRegistration open for Part 1 only (October 11, 2022 – January 27, 2023): Please register and you will receive the zoom link in the registration confirmation email: https://www.fields.utoronto.ca/cgi-bin/register?form_selection=one-health-I ( https://www.fields.utoronto.ca/cgi-bin/register?form_selection=one-health-I )\nIf you have any questions, please contact Natasha Ketter, Program Manager, OMNI-RÉUNIS.\nWe look forward to receiving your application!\n \n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/register-open-one-health-modelling-for-eids-course-with-omni-reunis-fields-institute-fall-2022-winter-2023-deadline-october-17/
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Health,Faculty of Science,Glendon Mathematics,Graduate Program in Health,Lassonde School of Engineering
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/omni-reunis-logo_acronym-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
