SUMMARY:York Circle: The aftermath: Where do we stand living with COVID for two years
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nPlease join us on Oct. 29, 2022 at 10am for part one of our virtual York Circle lecture series, where we welcome Jennifer Steeves as the new Academic Chair for the 2022-2023 season. As associate vice-president research (AVPR), she will moderate sessions as some of York’s leading faculty members present on a wide variety of interesting topics related to this year’s theme The Pandemic: COVID’s Impact on Canada’s health care system.\nThis session’s theme is The aftermath: Where do we stand living with COVID for two years.\nIn this panel discussion, three York faculty members will discuss the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on different areas in health care. This series will showcase York’s leading faculty members engaging in lively panel discussions and Q&A.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVisit yorku.ca/alumniandfriends/york-circle ( https://www.yorku.ca/alumniandfriends/connect/events/york-circle/ ) for more information.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-circle-the-aftermath-where-do-we-stand-living-with-covid-for-two-years/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/202210-yorkcircle-header.png
END:VEVENT
