SUMMARY:Community Safety Day at Glendon Campus
DESCRIPTION:\nYork’s Community Safety Department ( https://www.yorku.ca/safety/ ) offers comprehensive safety and security services to our community members and visitors. Our mission is to ensure that York continues to be a safe and welcoming place to study, work and live.  We approach campus safety through a community-centric, holistic and intersectional lens, where everyone plays a role in safety and where your contributions and initiatives play a vital role in promoting safety.  \nCommunity engagement is a cornerstone of safety. Join members of the Community Safety Department for Community Safety Days on Keele and Glendon campuses. \nTuesday, October 18, 2022, in Vari Hall, Keele Campus from 9:30 a.m. – 3:30 p.m. and  \nThursday, October 20, 2022, Centre for Excellence-Glendon Campus from 9:30 a.m. – 1:30 p.m. \nWe take your safety seriously and we want you to do the same. We encourage you to download the York Safety App  and get immediate access to all the University’s safety resources. \nWe look forward to seeing you on Community Safety Days. \n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/community-safety-day-at-keele-campus-414/
CATEGORIES:Finance &amp; Administration
LOCATION:A100 - Centre of Excellence, Glendon Campus - York University @ 2275 Bayview Ave, North York, ON M4N 3M6, Canada
END:VEVENT
