SUMMARY:Smyth Dialogues SHELTER IN PLACE: A CONVERSATION ON COMMUNITY, CONNECTION AND REFUGE
DESCRIPTION:How do we understand refuge and create it for ourselves and our communities? Join us for the 2022 Smyth Dialogues with award-winning authors Billy-Ray Belcourt and David Chariandy as they discuss refuge, safety, and our connections and disconnections with family, community and culture.\nHosted by Lily Cho, Associate Dean, Global & Community Engagement, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies, this event will feature two of Canada’s most noteworthy writing talents engaging in a lively panel discussion around the idea of refuge. There will also be a Q&A session.\nBilly-Ray Belcourt\nDavid Chariandy\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nYou have the option to attend this event virtually via Zoom (7 pm start for speakers’ panel) or in person (6 pm start, includes reception) at York’s Keele campus.\nClick below for registration options.\nMore info\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/smyth-dialogues-shelter-in-place-a-conversation-on-community-connection-and-refuge/
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,LA&amp;PS Addressing Anti-Black Racism,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Career and Employer Events,LA&amp;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp;PS Department of Communication &amp; Media Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of Economics,LA&amp;PS Department of English,LA&amp;PS Department of Equity Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of French Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of History,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS Department of Languages, Literatures &amp; Linguistics,LA&amp;PS Department of Philosophy,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp;PS Employee Research Workshops,LA&amp;PS ESLOLC,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS Future Students,LA&amp;PS IEP Bridging Program,LA&amp;PS Internship Information Sessions,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS Multimedia Language Centre,LA&amp;PS Nellie Library,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Open to the Public,LA&amp;PS Resume &amp; Cover Letter Workshops,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Gender, Sexuality and Women's Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Human Resources Management,LA&amp;PS School of Information Technology,LA&amp;PS School of Public Policy &amp; Administration,LA&amp;PS School of Social Work,LA&amp;PS SCOLAPS,LA&amp;PS SNACK,LA&amp;PS Student Success,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,LA&amp;PS Vanier College Productions,LA&amp;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
