TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Sensorium Lunchtime Seminar with Juma Parriri
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our first Lunchtime seminar of the season Monday Oct 3rd 2022 with:\nHemispheric Encounters Postdoctoral Scholar/Artist‎‏‏‎ ‎‏‏‎Juma Pariri ‎‏ (with Translation by Anna Agazzi)\nMonday Oct 3rd, 2022\n12pm – 1pm \nIn person at CFT 301, Centre for Film and Theatre. ACE, York University\nOR\nOnline  ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0vcOmtpjMoGdYwGaJ4VSOSaniRRldjT6eB )\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the meeting.\nJuma Pariri ( https://www.artseverywhere.ca/author/jumapariri/ ) is a postdoctoral researcher working with the SSHRC-funded Partnership, Hemispheric Encounters. Juma seeks to listen and learn from plant secrets. They move in the friction between the arts of the body, undisciplined pedagogy, and the Indigenous struggle for environmental justice. They are part of the social movements Retomada Kariri and the Indigenous Cariri of Poço Dantas-Umari Association. Among others, they activate the platformAGITPORN! – POR NO a la desigualdad, for social decolonization!, to learn from indigenous ancestors about anti-monocultural sexualities, cuisines and crops, and the audiovisual springboard United against colonization: many eyes, only one heart for collective creation of other symbolic forms of self-representation of the people from first nations of Abya Yala. Their current postdoctoral project is called Indigenous perforMAGICAL ACTivations against the farce of colonial representation.\nMore Information about Juma’s work : https://www.artseverywhere.ca/author/jumapariri/\nMore information available at: https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/lunchtime-seminar-series/ ( https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/lunchtime-seminar-series/ )\nJointly organized by Hemispheric Encounters, the Department of Theatre, and Sensorium: the Centre for Digital Art and Technology at the School of the Arts Media Performance and Design. The talk will be held during Ecoscenography Studio, a course run by Professor Ian Garrett.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sensorium-lunchtime-seminar-with-juma-parriri/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
LOCATION:Centre for Film and Theatre - Conference Room #301 @ 4700 Keele St, Toronto, ON M3J 1P3, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/juma.jpg
END:VEVENT
