SUMMARY:Modern Greek Studies Association Symposium
DESCRIPTION:The 27th MGSA Symposium ( https://mgsasymposium.org/ ) will take please in-person at York University between October 13-16, 2022. The MGSA Executive Board, the Program Committee and the Local Arrangements Committee will welcome Canadian scholars and members from around the world to take part in an enriching intellectual exchange about Toronto’s vibrant Greek Canadian community and its history. The MGSA symposium is the oldest and largest of its kind in the world. It provides a unique forum for current research and new ideas. Over the years it started welcoming graduate students, often giving them their first exposure to the field as well as to disciplines outside of their own.\nIf you are interested in registering to attend the conference, please visit: go.yorku.ca/MGSARegistration2022  ( https://mgsa.press.jhu.edu/membership/conference )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/modern-greek-studies-association-symposium/
