SUMMARY:8-Count: Delightful moments of dance cinema
DESCRIPTION:A cinematic exploration of how the art of screendance and storytelling continues to evolve post-pandemic. FFDN is thrilled to make our silver screen debut with the newest addition to our festival’s mainstage programming 8-Count: Delightful moments of dance cinema.\nJoin us for two live cinema screenings at the Betty Oliphant Theatre (Sep 23, 7:30 PM), a charming venue with a Victorian facade, or the stunning Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre at York University (Sep 24, 2:00 PM). Each screening will be followed by a moderated artist chat with select 8-Count filmmakers and artists, sharing insight into their creative process and vision of what it means to make dance on film.\n8-Count screenings will showcase the following short films, in no particular order:\nTRAX (an Excerpt)\nOur Bodies Back\nAUTOCORRECT\nThe Child Within\nSlipping\nInklings\n..Savannah?\nSep 23 @ 7PM EST – Betty Oliphant Theatre ( https://www.nbs-enb.ca/en/venue-rentals/betty-oliphant-theatre ) at The National Ballet School\nSep 24 @ 2PM EST – Sandra Faire and Ivan Fecan Theatre ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/sandra-faire-and-ivan-fecan-theatre/ ), York University\nEach screening will be followed by a post-show panel discussion featuring artists from the films and moderated by Associate Professor, Patrick Alcedo. \nAll tickets ( https://www.ffdnorth.com/programs/8-count?/tab/find-tickets ) are $15 (plus HST and fees). General admission.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/8-count-delightful-moments-of-dance-cinema/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/8count.jpg
