SUMMARY:Start of semester Communication tips for TAs
DESCRIPTION:Are you TAing for the first time and …? Are you a TA that wants to learn some tips for effective communication with students and course directors? \n\n\n\nCome on out to discuss strategies for communication including how to give an engaging introduction to students in your first lab or seminar, tips for writing professional emails, and use of inclusive language in the classroom, with Dr. Hovig Kouyoumdjian, Associate Dean, Curriculum and Pedagogy, and Dr. Lisa Robertson, Assistant Professor in Biology.\n\nDate: Thursday September 22, 2022\nTime: Noon-1pm EST\nLocation: Zoom\nRegistration: https://science.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=450380\nZoom Link: https://yorku.zoom.us/s/96931136495\n\nThis workshop is open to all graduate students and post-docs in the Faculty of Science. No previous TA experience is required.\n\n\n\nIf you have any questions, concerns, or just want to chat about teaching & learning, I would love to hear from you at ashleynk@yorkuca. \n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/start-of-semester-communication-tips-for-tas/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Science:MAILTO:fscomms@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Science
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
