SUMMARY:Scholars’ Hub @ Home: New names, old places: What memorializing teaches us about who we are and who we might be
DESCRIPTION:This webinar invites us to consider what our practices of naming, renaming, and memorializing teach us about our collective values and identities. Dr. Shah explores the importance of context, history, dialogue, and complicity in this process of raising our collective critical consciousness.\nRegister ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_FkAAOiNGSbq40ZGyt_ORzQ )\n
