SUMMARY:Moving Forward: Making the Most of Your International Student Experience
DESCRIPTION:International students face special challenges, including making the transition to life in Canada, and learning to feel part of the York community. Come join us for this special hour to learn tips and tricks from York graduates who were international students themselves.\nOur panelists, all in senior positions, will share resources that supported them during their time at York and talk about what a difference their York degree has made in their life and career:\n\nAnna Boateng, BA, International Development Studies ’06, Economics ‘07\n\nVice President, Client Services at BMO Capital Markets\n\nHasnain Versi, BA, Business Economics ‘00\n\nPresident & CEO at ISM – a Kyndryl Company\n\nKamika McLean, BA, Political Science and Law & Society ‘02\n\nGeneral Counsel & Corporate Secretary at KSS HoldCo Inc.\nHosted by Lily Cho, Associate Dean, Global & Community Engagement. Includes Q&A Session.\n \nRegistration\n
