SUMMARY:Looking Forward: Preparing to Apply to Graduate School in 2025
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education and want to get a head start on the preparation? We invite you to attend our virtual program session. RSVP | yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_re_TfXd8Tu281MSk44sfWQ )\nThis session will go over how to best prepare for graduate school applications when you still have a few years to go before formally applying. We’ll talk about application requirements and how you can start, or continue, to meet and exceed them.\nThis session is meant for folks who are currently in their undergraduate program, and plan on applying to graduate studies at least two years in the future if not more.\nYou are also welcome to attend if you are no longer in an undergraduate program, but still do not plan on applying to graduate studies for at least two years in the future if not more.\nIf you are interested in applying for a graduate program starting in September 2023, we invite you to check out any of the Faculty Admissions sessions being held during Experience Grad York: yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ )\nTo learn about more sessions being offered, visit yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy ( https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ). \nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsnews@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsnews@yorku.ca ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/looking-forward-prepping-to-apply-to-graduate-school-in-2025/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Earth &amp; Space Science,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,Markham Campus
LOCATION:Online Zoom
