SUMMARY:Department of English presents JASON LOO — The Pitiful Human-Lizard
DESCRIPTION:Department of English presents Jason Loo\nMonday, July 25 from 2:30 to 3:30 p.m. \n**Please email James Papoutsis for Zoom link — james.papoutsis@gmail.com ( mailto:james.papoutsis@gmail.com )\nJason Loo is a Toronto-based cartoonist and comic creator behind Toronto’s own pretty decent superhero comic series The Pitiful Human-Lizard. He is also the co-creator of the Eisner Award-winning digital comic series Afterlift with Chip Zdarsky for ComiXology Originals. His other notable works include The All-Nighter, Star Wars Adventures, Razorblades, and various Marvel comics like X-Men Unlimited and Lucky the Pizza Dog.\nJason Loo will be presenting the creative process behind his Toronto-based comic series the Pitiful Human-Lizard and its contribution to the history of Canadian superhero comics.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/department-of-english-presents-jason-loo-the-pitiful-human-lizard/
ORGANIZER;CN=Meaghan McCue:MAILTO:mmccue@yorku.ca
