SUMMARY:Domestic Graduate Admissions at York
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a Graduate Admissions Session for Domestic Applicants – learn more about York University and our graduate admissions process. This session is intended for applicants who are in one of the following categories: a Canadian citizen, permanent resident, or an Indigenous person who is covered by the Jay Treaty.\nThis session will run about an hour, and will cover “Why York”, eligibility, requirements, financial information, how to apply, and more.\nPlease note that during these sessions we will not be able to answer any questions about Schulich School of Business programs, or Osgoode Law School programs. For all other master’s programs, doctoral programs, and graduate diplomas, this is the session for you!\nRegistration is required. To RSVP or learn more, visit  https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEscOquqTwtH9HK_CiZaZfgyx7RBWLH7OcP ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEscOquqTwtH9HK_CiZaZfgyx7RBWLH7OcP )\nLearn more about our graduate programs at https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs ( https://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nFor any questions, please email us at FGSNEWS@YORKU.CA ( mailto:FGSNEWS@YORKU.CA ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/domestic-graduate-admissions-at-york-11/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Visual Art
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Online Seminar via Zoom
