TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Intersectional Futures Speaker Series – Wapahtowak: They See Each Other
DESCRIPTION:Jack Saddleback bares raw stories with humorous musings to uplift spaces for identities like his, a Cree two-spirit, transgender gay man. Weaving experiences of personal resilience, community compassion, and societal shifts in his keynote, Jack inspires the future lens needed to create an intersectional holistic society. Where we see Wapahtowak (pronunciation: wah-pah-taw-walk): They See Each Other thriving.\nHosted by Student Community & Leadership Development, and the Centre for Indigenous Student Services.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/intersectional-futures-speaker-series-wapahtowak-they-see-each-other/
ORGANIZER;CN=Student Community &amp; Leadership Development:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Bethune College,Calumet College,Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,LA&amp;PS Founders College,LA&amp;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp;PS New College,LA&amp;PS Vanier College,National Indigenous History Month,Pride Month,Provost,Special Themes,Stong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp; Well-being,Students,Teaching &amp; Learning
END:VEVENT
