SUMMARY:Ambe Daga Wiijiiwishin: An Indigenous Walk on Campus
DESCRIPTION:The Centre for Indigenous Knowledge and Languages & The Department of Indigenous Initiatives Presents…\nAmbe Daga Wiijiiwishin: An Indigenous Walk on Campus\n(“Come with Me”: An Indigenous Walk on Campus)\nJoin us for a walk to reflect on Indigenous History Month as we explore Indigenous spaces on campus. All students, staff, and faculty are welcome.\nOn this walk, we will listen to Indigenous voices and learn about Indigenous spaces at York. Some notable stops along the walk include Ahqazhu, Skennen’kó:wa Gamig, and the Centre for Indigenous Student Services.\nRain or shine! Please dress for the weather.\n \nDate: Wednesday, June 29\nTime: noon to 12:45 p.m.\nStarting/Ending point: Meet outside Vari Hall.\n Kindly RSVP to: cikl@yorku.ca\nThis will be a collaborative event hosted by the Centre for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages and the Department for Indigenous Initiatives.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ambe-daga-wiijiiwishin-an-indigenous-walk-on-campus/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages:MAILTO:cikl@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:National Indigenous History Month,Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Vari Hall
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/june-29-INDIGENOUS-WALK-AT-YORK-POSTER-revised-01.png
END:VEVENT
