SUMMARY:Instage- Interview Preparation Webinar
DESCRIPTION:Approach your next interview or networking event with increased confidence. Learn how you can influence the first impression you make and show your best self while answering employers’ questions.\nDuring this webinar, you will have access to InStage and practise interview skills. InStage is a cloud-based experiential learning tool designed to make it fun for students to build career skills. You can practice for job interviews, classroom presentations, business pitches, and more! After each practice session, you will receive a detailed progress report that shows your rate of speech, filler words usage (e.g. um, like and so), volume, and much more.\n** PLEASE NOTE THIS WILL BE AN ONLINE WEBINAR **\nTo participate in an online webinar, you will need a computer (with speakers or headphones), internet access, and Zoom desktop application (Zoom) installed in your computer. You will receive the URL of the webinar with the Zoom Meeting ID in a reminder email after you have registered for the event. On the day of the event, you will join the webinar and ask your questions via chat.\nDeadline to Apply: July 14 at 10 a.m.\nFor more information about this event and to register, login to Experience York. ( http://experience.yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/instage-interview-preparation-webinar/
ORGANIZER;CN=Career Centre:MAILTO:career@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre
