TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Creating and Maintaining Positive Space (REDI)
DESCRIPTION:This is a “101” session that will explore gender and sexual diversity, as well as homophobia and transphobia specific to the campus experience. Learn about using inclusive language, being a supportive ally, campus resources, and creating safer spaces on campus for gender and sexually diverse students, staff, and faculty. This session will be in English. It will also be delivered in French on June 15 from 1 to 2:30 p.m. ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=329 ).\nSign up on YULearn ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=299 ).\nIn recognition of Pride month, this session is part of REI’s Summer REDI Mini-Series on Gender and Sexuality Inclusion. ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/redipd-summer/ ) York community who attend three REDI sessions and an online REDI tutorial are eligible for a REDI Certificate.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/creating-and-maintaining-positive-space/
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Pride Month
END:VEVENT
