SUMMARY:Addressing and Responding to Sexual Harassment (REDI)
DESCRIPTION:In this interactive session, participants will become familiar with the legislation and policies that define sexual harassment and gain a general understanding of why sexual harassment continues to be pervasive in our society. Attendees will examine various scenarios aimed at obtaining strategies and sharing best practices on how to identify, prevent, and respond to instances of sexual harassment on campus.\nSign up on YU-Learn: https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulearn/learning_opportunity.php?id=300\nThis session is part of the Summer REDI mini-series on Gender and Sexuality Inclusion ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/redipd-summer/ ). Those who complete three REDI sessions and an online tutorial are eligible for a REDI certificate.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/addressing-and-responding-to-sexual-harassment-redi/
ORGANIZER;CN=Centre for Human Rights, Equity &amp; Inclusion:MAILTO:chrwkshp@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Pride Month
END:VEVENT
