TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Corporate Rules and Big Energy
DESCRIPTION:Join the York Sustainable Energy Initiative (SEI) ( https://sei.info.yorku.ca/ ) for the launch event of EUC Adjunct Professor Bruce Campbell’s ( https://theconversation.com/profiles/bruce-campbell-697607 ) new book Corporate Rules: The Real World of Business Regulation in Canada (James Lorimer & Co 2022). Our panel of contributing authors will focus on the environmental, health and safety regulation of Big Energy in Canada, looking at the cases of federal climate change and energy policy, the Alberta oil industry and the tar sands, and nuclear energy. SEI Co-Chair and contributing author (Institutionalizing Regulatory Capture as Regulatory Practice) Professor Mark Winfield will moderate.\nSpeakers\nJason MacLean is an assistant professor at the Faculty of Law at the University of New Brunswick and an adjunct professor at the School of Environment and Sustainability at the University of Saskatchewan.\nTheresa McClenaghan is executive director and counsel for the Canadian Environmental Law Association.\nNathan Lempers is an adjunct professor in the Department of Political Science at the University of Waterloo. He is a Former Postdoctoral Fellow at the University of Ottawa’s Smart Prosperity Institute.\nMark Winfield (Moderator) is a professor at the Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change, and co-chair of the Sustainable Energy Initiative at the Faculty.\nBruce Campbell is an adjunct professor at the Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change and former executive director of the Canadian Centre for Policy Alternatives.\nWilliam K. Carroll is a professor emeritus in the Department of Sociology at the University of Victoria.\nEveryone is welcome! Registration is required on eventbrite ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/yorkus-euc-and-sei-present-corporate-rules-and-big-energy-tickets-326765483357 ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/corporate-rules-and-big-energy/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Research &amp; Innovation
LOCATION:Zoom Webinar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:York University
CLASS:PUBLIC
UID:MEC-1be9573be51135cd5be1e191f44e09f8@events.yorku.ca
DTSTART:20220517T150000Z
DTEND:20220517T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20220429T153100Z
CREATED:20220429
LAST-MODIFIED:20220429
PRIORITY:5
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Tips for Learning @ York U for Transfer Students
DESCRIPTION:Students transferring to YorkU from college or another university face different challenges and experiences than those coming straight from high school. This workshop, called Tips for Learning @ YorkU, is designed to help transfer students better understand the keys to mastering university-level learning and put you on the path to academic success. This session is brought you by the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-Time Students (ACMAPS) in collaboration with Learning Skills Services.\nRegistration details:  https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMuc-2gqjMsE9fJyF0JbmNmGtUCmWFyGYnq ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMuc-2gqjMsE9fJyF0JbmNmGtUCmWFyGYnq )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/tips-for-learning-york-u-for-transfer-students/
ORGANIZER;CN=ACMAPS:MAILTO:acmaps@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Students
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
