SUMMARY:NAOSH Week: Student Counselling, Health & Well-being – YU Matter: Self-Care in the Workplace
DESCRIPTION:Open to all York University Community Members\nIn support of North American Occupational, Safety and Health (NAOSH) Week, Student Counselling, Health & Well-being will be providing a session on self-care.\nThis session is open to all members who are interested in learning more about self-care in the workplace, self-assessments, and taking away some practical skills to manage stress. Facilitated by Student Counselling, Health & Well-being (SCHW), participants will be given tools and resource to evaluate and support their own journey to better self-care.\nTo register, please click here ( https://dohs.apps01.yorku.ca/machform/view.php?id=82049 ).\n
