SUMMARY:Indigenous Perspectives: Relationships and Responsibilities to Plants
DESCRIPTION:Join us this Earth Day, Friday April 22 at 1 p.m. for an incredible discussion with Joseph Pitawanakwat of Creators Garden hosted by Deborah McGregor over Zoom! Pitawanakwat will be discussing our obligations to the Earth and to the plants, not just for one day, but every day. We have obligations to grow our relationship with plants throughout the year, through the whole cycle of life, and uphold our responsibilities to these plants. Join us via the zoom link below, and we can’t wait to see you there!\nSee Creators Garden https://www.facebook.com/CreatorsGarden/ ( https://www.facebook.com/CreatorsGarden/ ) for more of Pitawanakwat’s work around plants.\nhttps://yorku.zoom.us/j/2336397616 ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/2336397616 )\nMeeting ID: 233 639 7616\nFor more information or questions, please contact the Indigenous Environmental Justice Project at theiejproject@gmail.com ( mailto:theiejproject@gmail.com ) or via social media, at:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/theiejproject/ ( https://www.instagram.com/theiejproject/ ) on Instagram\nhttps://www.facebook.com/theIEJproject ( https://www.facebook.com/theIEJproject ) on Facebook\nhttps://twitter.com/theIEJproject ( https://twitter.com/theIEJproject ) on Twitter\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/indigenous-perspectives-relationships-and-responsibilities-to-plants/
