SUMMARY:Hack ITE York U
DESCRIPTION:IN-PERSON EXPERIENCE\nREGISTRATION ( http://eventbrite.ca/e/319168310007 )\nHack ITE York is going to be ITE’s first official hackathon ever. Over 36 hours with more than 50 of the top graduate and undergraduate technical talent from Lassonde School of Engineering, they will create, code and collaborate to build their projects and solve the most difficult sustainable mobility challenges.\nThis is not a coding hackathon! You will be able to work on various aspects without needing to code. Coding is completely optional.\nOur leading sponsor is Frank Stronach, the creator of Magna International who will be proving challenges and parts of his new vehicle SARIT for you to work on.\nLocation: SANDBOX (Bergeron 2nd floor)\nTime: Friday (5 to 11 p.m.), Saturday (9 a.m. to 11 p.m.), Sunday (9 a.m. to 5 p.m.)\nTheme: Transportation and Micromobility\nPrizes: Cash prizes, as well as giveaways, will be announced later\nTeam Formation: You can register as a team or make one during team formation happening on Friday\nSkills and Experience required: Everyone is welcome no matter what your previous experience or skills are\nPrice: Early-bird (15 spots) $5, Early General Admission (15 spots) $10, General Admission (20 spots) $15\nThis event is exclusive to York University students. You will be eligible for a stipend if you have not participated in previous hackathons and have not been enrolled in C4\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/hack-ite-york-u/
ORGANIZER;CN=ITE York University Student Chapter:MAILTO:ite@my.yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Lassonde School of Engineering
LOCATION:Bergeron Centre for Engineering Excellence @ 11 Arboretum Ln, North York, ON M3J 2S5, Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/Hack-ITE-York-U-2.png
END:VEVENT
