SUMMARY:Celebrate Earth Day with York U – hosted by the Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Thursday, April 21 for a special evening event in honour of Earth Day 2022 and learn how York U’s Faculty of Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) is making positive change for people and the planet.\nThe event will include:\n\nA welcome address from EUC’s Dean Alice J. Hovorka ( https://euc.yorku.ca/faculty/alice-j-hovorka/ ), who will share how our newest faculty at York U is mobilizing knowledge for a just and sustainable future.\nA keynote address from one of our prestigious Top 30 under 30 alumn ( https://www.yorku.ca/alumniandfriends/top30/ )i, Elijah (Eli) Bawuah (BA’18, MES’21), who will share how his experiences at York U and in EUC shaped his career journey.\nA student experience panel, moderated by our Experiential Education Coordinator, Aren Sammy, with three of our current students discussing their Changemaker experiences.\nA moment of reflection to bring all attendees together for a united community pledge to right the future in honour of Earth Day 2022.\n\nAll are welcome | Registration is required. Click here to register ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEpcO2przkuHdDLP4QcF1f-rOn_V1uTbn8- )\nThis event will be hosted virtually on Zoom Webinar. All registrants will receive the access link prior to the event.\n \n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/celebrate-earth-day-with-york-u-hosted-by-the-faculty-of-environmental-urban-change/
