SUMMARY:Nat Taylor Films presents TABIJA (THE WHITE FORTRESS)
DESCRIPTION:In a rundown Sarajevo suburb, Faruk is an orphan who lives with his ill grandmother and spends his days foraging for scrap metal and dabbling in petty crime. One day he meets Mona, a timid teen from a politically powerful and affluent family. As Mona dreams of escaping the overbearing toxicity of her home life, she seeks refuge and opens herself up to Faruk, a boy from a world entirely different than her own.Celebrate a new year of cinema by joining York University’s AMPD Grad Film Department for an exclusive screening of Igor Drljača’s feature film TABIJA (THE WHITE FORTRESS) (Berlinale 2022, 2022 Oscar selection for Bosnia & Herzegovina), plus a post-screening zoom Q&A with the filmmaker after on April 15th!Attendance is FREE! (RSVP’ing is encouraged to ensure that a seat is available upon arrival. Once we have reached max capacity in our RSVP, pre-registration for the event will be closed to ensure that the event adheres to COVID-19 safety guidelines and protocols.)\nNat Taylor Cinema\nN102 Ross Building (Campus Walk)\nToronto, ON M3J 2S5\nTIME: 7:00 PM\nRSVP HERE ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/nat-taylor-films-presents-tabija-the-white-fortress-tickets-308965974547 )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/nat-taylor-films-presents-tabija-the-white-fortress/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
