SUMMARY:(Dis)Content Futures?: The politics of insecurity and inequality in Africa
DESCRIPTION:RCPS Global Public Sociology Conversations Series, in Collaboration with Founders College, African Studies, and the Canada Research Chair in Youth and African Urban Futures presents: (Dis)Content Futures?: The politics of insecurity and inequality in Africa on Wednesday, April 6.\nPanel includes: Chair/Provocateaur: Dr. Pablo Idahosa, Head of Founders College at York University. Yousif Hassan: Scholar, Entrepreneur, and Software Engineer in Toronto. Dr. Aminata C. Mbaye, Post-doctoral Research Fellow at Queen’s University. Dr. Thomas K. Tieku, African-Canadian international relations and negotiation expert and Associate Professor of Political Science at King’s University College. Bahlelisiwe Luhlanga, Teaching Assistant at York University and PhD Candidate in Political Studies. Dr. Temitope Oriola, Joint Editor-in-Chief of African Security journal and Associate Professor at the University of Alberta.\nJoin Zoom meeting\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/discontent-futures-the-politics-of-insecurity-and-inequality-in-africa/
