TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Grammar On!!! Week 8: Verb that Noun!
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nGrammar On! Week Eight We often think of grammar as a series of scary rules about “what-not-to-do”, but, in reality, grammar is a tool that you can use to write more effective sentences and increase your range of syntactical choices. Come join Dunja this Thursday at 10:30am in the Writing Centre’s Grammar On! series of workshops. The workshop is open to all students who want to learn to construct effective and beautiful sentences that say what you want them to say. Grammar On! Verb that Noun! Are you in the habit of disguising perfectly good verbs in those bloated drag-your-sentence-to-a-slow-and-heavy-crawl nouns called nominalizations? Come to this week’s Grammar On! and learn how to quicken the pulse and the pace of your sentences. Come learn how to verb that noun! No RSVPs. Just show up!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nZoom link \n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grammar-on-week-8-verb-that-noun/
ORGANIZER;CN=Writing Centre:MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca, dbaus@yorku.ca, lapswrit@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
LOCATION:Zoom Webinar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/pexels-tima-miroshnichenko-6913193_James-Robertson-4-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
