TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Applying to Graduate School
DESCRIPTION:Curious to learn about Indigenous graduate programs and the process of applying for graduate studies? Join us for a discussion on selecting and applying to Indigenous graduate programs. Our session is open to all students but is specifically designed for Indigenous students and those interested in applying to programs in Indigenous studies. We will share our experiences, advice and answer your questions about graduate programs (MA and PhD) at York and beyond.\nPanellists: \nDr. Brock Pitawanakwat\nAssociate Professor in the Department of Humanities and the Coordinator of the Indigenous Studies Program at York University\nLance Morrison\nHonours BA Indigenous Studies, MA Candidate in Interdisciplinary Studies at York University, Indigenous Studies instructor at Fleming College\nDr. Nathalie LaCoste Ling\nPhD Religious Studies at University of Toronto, and Coordinator for York University’s Centre for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages\nRegistration: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0vduCorz8qE9bZntm-wwDyKunM3b8YWMRK ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJ0vduCorz8qE9bZntm-wwDyKunM3b8YWMRK )\nQuestions? cikl@yorku.ca ( mailto:cikl@yorku.ca )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/applying-to-graduate-school/
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp; Career Centre,Research &amp; Innovation,Students
END:VEVENT
