SUMMARY:MFA22 Thesis Exhibitions: Michelle Peraza
DESCRIPTION:aquí y allá: una manera de ser (here and there: a way of being): MFA Thesis Exhibition by Michelle Peraza\nMFA Thesis Exhibitions\nSchool of Arts, Media, Performance & Design (AMPD) presents thesis work by MFA candidates from the Graduate Program in Visual Arts. Artists include Abraham Oghobase, Jasmine Canaviri, Andrew Harding, Catherine Hois, Michelle Peraza, Shawn Grey, Jessie Kitchen and Lisa Cristinzo.\nExhibitions are scheduled throughout the month of April in the Gales Gallery ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/gales-gallery/ ) and Special Projects Gallery ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/special-projects-gallery/ ).\nMichelle Peraza, artist\nGales Gallery ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/gales-gallery/ )\nApril 18 – 22, 2022\nFREE\nGallery Hours: 9am-4pm (Mon-Fri)\naquí y allá: una manera de ser (here and there: a way of being) is the MFA exhibition of Michelle Peraza. The project explores figurative and non-figurative representations of her LatinX family through drawing and painting. Its intention is to probe, contest, address, and resist their colonial history to contribute to resilience, empowerment, and a nuanced LatinX identity in a visual format.\n\n\n \n
