SUMMARY:United Nations World Water Day: Career Networking with Professionals in the Water Sciences
DESCRIPTION:Clean drinking water is recognized as a human right by the United Nations, yet marginalized communities are denied access to it. Student voices are essential in progressing and solving water issues, including through a variety of career opportunities. Join us on March 25 from noon to 1 p.m. to get involved in the conversation and network with professionals in the water sciences!\nGuest Speakers:\nJennifer Winter – Ministry of Environment, Conservation Park\nAndrew Drake – Department of Fisheries and Oceans\nArnab Shuvo (York University alumni) – Data manager at Center for Limnology, University of Wisconsin-Madison\nNatasha Tucker – Plastic Oceans, NGO\nRegistration is required.\nPlease register here: https://forms.gle/ARQfRUCdUJVCy3LN7 ( https://forms.gle/ARQfRUCdUJVCy3LN7 )\nZoom link for the event: https://yorku.zoom.us/j/96306118104?pwd=dTRna0VXTTltT25pMUtjTE1nTGszdz09 ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/96306118104?pwd=dTRna0VXTTltT25pMUtjTE1nTGszdz09 )\n
