SUMMARY:York Dances 2022: coordinates
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Dance presents\nYork Dances 2022: coordinates – series x & series y\nYork Dances 2022: coordinates features the new choreographic works of 31 third year BFA majors performed by students engaged in all levels of York’s programs in Dance. This will be the Department’s first live performance in over two years and the artists are delighted to share their works with an in-person audience. coordinates explores how we navigate our spaces, relationships, identities, communities, and our place in the ecosystem. As we continue to experience a sense of collective disorientation, these young voices act as a compass, pointing us to what is most imperative in this moment. In addition to steering their own creative processes, the students led every facet of the production of York Dances, supported by faculty at every level of creation, performance, and production. The two series feature 31 world premieres staged in the McLean Performance Studio, April 6, 7 and 8, at 7pm and 8:30pm.\nArtistic Director and Course Director: Tracey Norman\nWork Study Team: Emily Bakker, Hannah Kimbell, Emily Weaver\nWork Study Supervisor: Jennifer Jimenez\nYork Dances 2022: coordinates\nApril 6-8, 2022\n7:00 pm – series x features 15 new choreographic works by third-year students\n8:30 pm – series y features 16 new choreographic works by third-year students\nMcLean Performance Studio ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/facilities/mclean-performance-studio/ ), 244 Accolade East Building\nAdmission: $10 until April 5, 2022 / $15 Regular\nBox Office: 416-736-5888 | ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice/ )\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-dances-2022-coordinates/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/coordinatesbanner.jpg
