TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:York University Graduate Colloquium: World Fictions of Friendship in Critical Times
DESCRIPTION:“It’s like no self. No I. Non-existence”: Friendship and Family in Contemporary Fiction\nKeynote address by Prof. Doris Hambuch\n\n\n\nFriday, March 18 at 10 a.m. \nFor the link and schedule, please contact Marie-Christine Leps at mcleps@yorku.ca ( mailto:mcleps@yorku.ca ).\nDoris Hambuch is an associate professor of Literature and Film Studies at United Arab Emirates University, and president of the Canadian Comparative Literature Association. Her publications focus on Caribbean literature, ecocriticism, film analysis, trans-cultural feminism, and polyglot art practices.\nFocusing on friendship in times of war and exile, Hambuch’s address investigates transculturation and its impact on the more-than-human through selected film and fiction by A. Roemer, X. Guo, J. Fares, and J. Alvarez. The study offers an ecocritical perspective as timely expansion of a discourse on friendship from Emerson to Derrida.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/york-university-graduate-colloquium-world-fictions-of-friendship-in-critical-times/
ORGANIZER;CN=Graduate Program in English:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Humanities
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
END:VEVENT
