DESCRIPTION:You are invited to register for the second online community consultation town hall for the Security Services Review scheduled for March 29 from 5 p.m. to 6:30 p.m.\nTown hall participants will have opportunities to provide input during the event and hear from other members of the community. To prepare for the town hall participants are encouraged to read the consultation brief ( https://www.yorku.ca/safety/wp-content/uploads/sites/78/2022/03/2022-02.22-Security-Services-Review-Consultation-Brief-FINAL-Eng-KT.pdf ) and refer to the guided questions to help provide concrete feedback/recommendations for action.\nAll participants are expected to engage in the session in a respectful and collegial manner. Any violation of conduct rules will result in participants being removed from the town hall.\nQuestions and comments shared by participants during the town halls will be captured saved and used for internal purposes only. All microphones and cameras will be turned off during the town hall. If you would like to provide input by speaking into your microphone so that you can be heard by all participants, this can be accommodated by using the Q&A function in Zoom. Please know that by turning on your microphone and speaking at the event, you are consenting to the potential sharing of your comments in a group setting.\nRegister Today! ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_j1VJgzENTmWaHnhOqAuBzg )\nTo learn more, visit the Security Services Review website ( https://www.yorku.ca/safety/security-review/ ).\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/security-services-review-consultation-town-hall-2/
CATEGORIES:Finance &amp; Administration
