SUMMARY:World Music Festival (2022)
DESCRIPTION:York University’s World Music Festival is a cross-cultural celebration spotlighting musical traditions around the world.\nProduced by Professor William Thomas ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/william-thomas/ ) this global sonic tour presents a sampling of several international cultures represented in York’s world music program.\nThe festival packs six free concerts into two days: March 10-11, 2022\nMaps and Directions ( http://maps.info.yorku.ca/keele-campus/ )\nTHURSDAY MARCH 10\n11:00 AM – Cuban Ensembles – Rick Lazar ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/rick-lazar/ ), Ensemble Director\n1:30 PM – Escola de Samba – Rick Lazar ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/rick-lazar/ ), Ensemble Director\n2:30 PM – West African (Ghana) – Kwasi Dunyo and Larry Graves ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/larry-k-graves/ ), Ensemble Directors\n7:00 PM – Caribbean Music Ensemble –  Gareth Burgess ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/gareth-burgess/ ), Ensemble Director\nFRIDAY MARCH 11\n1:00 PM – Celtic Ensemble – Sherry Johnson ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/sherry-johnson/ ), Ensemble Director\n7:30 PM – Balkan Music Ensemble – Irene Markoff ( https://ampd.yorku.ca/profile/irene-markoff/ ), Ensemble Director\nTICKETS:\nLivestream (Sliding Scale: $5-$25)\nIn-Person (Free – Box Office ( https://facilities.ampd.yorku.ca/boxoffice/ ) Registration Required)\nBox Office ( https://music.ampd.yorku.ca/box-office/ )\n \n \n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/world-music-festival-2022/
