SUMMARY:PhESSA Research Day
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to PhESSA Research Day on March 17 from 9 a.m. to 12:30 p.m.\n9 to 9:15 a.m. – Welcoming Remarks\n9:15 to 9:35 a.m. – Content Analysis of Environmental Advocacy at a Global Scale · Nyssa van Vierssen Trip\n9:35 to 9:55 a.m. – Visual Polyphony: Transforming the Representation of Environmental Issues · Laurence Butet-Roch\n9:55 to 10:15 a.m. –  Considering Issues of Quality in Urban Political Ecology · Hillary Birch\n10:15 to 10:35 a.m. – The Radical Lair: Dramaturging a Disabled Revolutionary Romanticism\nThrough Theatrical Trauma Magic · Sarah Erik Sackville-McLauchlan\n10:35 to 10:45 a.m. – Break\n10:45 to 11:30 a.m. – Navigating Indigenous-Informed Methods as a Settler · Benjamin Kapron & Clara Fraser\n11:30 to 11:50 a.m.am – A food system analysis of dietary consumption, food availability, and food access for food security in northern Ghana – Balikisu Osman\n11:50am to noon – Preview of UnderCurrents vol. 21 – Memories and Futurities · Benjamin Kapron\nNoon to 12:30 p.m. – Closing Remarks & Virtual Social\nEveryone is welcome!\nZoom link to the meeting: https://yorku.zoom.us/s/97420015801 ( https://yorku.zoom.us/s/97420015801 )\nAny inquiries can be directed to brian.dorin@gmail.com ( mailto:brian.dorin@gmail.com )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/phessa-research-day/
