TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Ukraine, Putin, and the Impact on International Security
DESCRIPTION:\n\nJoin the Glendon community on Zoom to discuss the Russia-Ukraine crisis with Susan Pond, former NATO executive.\n\n\n\n\nThis event will be hosted in English. There will be a Q-and-A session. \nSpeaker Biography\nFor 30 years, Ms. Pond has been an agent for change, promoting peace and security and the transformation of international institutions. As a member of the international staff, she completed NATO assignments in Brussels, Kyiv and Norfolk, providing recommendations on the implementation of the alliance’s core tasks.\nShe served as head of the Partnership for Peace section, preparing nations to take on the responsibilities of the Washington Treaty and developing cooperation agreements with nations such as Afghanistan and Ukraine. Working as head of the NATO Liaison Office in Kyiv, Ms. Pond advised on the development of a program of cooperation to support the transformation of the Ukrainian defence and security forces.\nRegister here: https://bit.ly/3vqBaQk ( https://bit.ly/3vqBaQk )\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/ukraine-putin-and-the-impact-on-international-security/
ORGANIZER;CN=Glendon:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Glendon
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/RUSSIA-UKRAINE-TALK-_v3.png
