TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:Black History: In March and forever after?
DESCRIPTION:Now that the month where Black History is both celebrated and prescribed is over, what are the lenses through which we can understand its pasts and its presents? Where are they, and how are they celebrated and understood, not just in North America, but throughout different parts of the world where people of African descent reside? Join Professor Pablo Idahosa, Head of Founders College, for a discussion about some of these meanings, and why the month needs to be understood through multiple lenses, places and histories.\nProfessor Pablo Idahos\nRegistration\n \n \n \n
