SUMMARY:Social for Good: Building Mental Health Support Networks for Youth in the Digital Space
DESCRIPTION:\nJoin us for a round table conversation with a group of trailblazing mental health advocates.\n\nPanelists include Dr. Kojo Sarfo, Steven Sharpe Jr., Wynnikka Matthews and York University’s Dr. Agnes Berthelot-Raffard, assistant professor in the School of Health Policy and Management at the Faculty of Health.\n\n\n\nThe panelists will:\n\n\n• Share lived experiences centered around mental health and well-being and address stigmas and barriers to access/support.\n\n\n• Lean into the power of internal resilience, touching on external support systems.\n• Share information on Black student mental health research and online resources.\n\n\n• Offer helpful perspectives and strategies to encourage better mental health and well-being. Touching on the need for online support systems, particularly when local communities are not a viable resource.\n\n\n\nThis live event will be streamed on Unsinkable’s Facebook & Twitter platforms on Feb. 27 at 7 p.m. EST\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/social-for-good-building-mental-health-support-networks-for-youth-in-the-digital-space/
CATEGORIES:Black History Month,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion
