SUMMARY:Scholar’s Hub @ Home | Law in the time of COVID: Pandemics, protest and emergencies
DESCRIPTION:Featuring Professor Allan Hutchinson, Osgoode Hall Law School\nThis talk will explore how law has been affected by the pandemic and the Emergency Powers Act specifically. What are its implications on Canadian civil liberties in the current situation? How does it empower the federal government? What are the powers available to federal and provincial governments?\nRegister: https://bit.ly/3BNrlwP\n
