SUMMARY:Grammar On! Workshop #Four – Let’s Get Active!
DESCRIPTION:We often think of grammar as a series of scary rules about “what-not-to-do”, but, in reality, grammar is a tool that you can use to write more effective sentences and increase your range of syntactical choices. Come join Dunja this Thursday at 10:30 a.m. in the Writing Centre’s Grammar On! series of workshops. The workshop is open to all students who want to learn to construct effective and beautiful sentences that say what you want them to say. Grammar On! Workshop #Four Let’s Get Active! (And, of course, Passive, too, but with a Purpose.) Unsure about when to use Active Voice or Passive Voice in your academic essays? Come to this Thursday’s Grammar On! and learn how to use voice with purpose and confidence! No RSVPs. Just show up!\nJoin Zoom meeting\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grammar-on-workshop-four-lets-get-active/
