SUMMARY:Las Nubes Summer Study Abroad Info Session
DESCRIPTION:Don’t miss the unique opportunity to earn credits through courses taught by York’s faculty!\nOur courses take a community-based approach by developing collaborative projects that provide learning opportunities with an emphasis on experiential education, building on our long-standing relationships with diverse communities and groups in Southern Costa Rica, including women’s organizations, agricultural cooperatives and producers, environmental protection and social justice groups, and Indigenous communities, among others.\nCourses are open to all York University undergraduate (3rd and 4th year) and graduate students.\nImportant Dates & Registration Instructions\nStep 1: Attend an information session and check your eligibility All students are welcome to attend our sessions. Register in advance. • Tuesday, March 8 2022, 11:30 am • Friday, March 18 2022, 3:30 pm\nStep 2: Enroll in course(s) for 2022. Save your spot by March 15, 2022 (Note that we need to check your eligibility first – Step 1) • May 2 – 11, 2022 | Narratives in/of Costa Rica. Individuals, Communities and their Voices • May 13 – 22, 2022 | Environmental Arts and Food Sovereignty in Costa Rica • May 24 – June 2, 2022 | Education for a Sustainable Future • June 4 – 13, 2022 | Natural History: Environmental Education in Costa Rica • June 15 – 24, 2022 | Protected Area Management in Costa Rica • June 26 – July 5, 2022 | Fundamentals of Ecological Engineering • July 7 – 16, 2022 | Determinants of Health: Local to Global • July 18 – 27, 2022 | Environmental Psychology • July 29 – August 7, 2022 | Globalization and Indigenous Peoples • August 9 – 18, 2022 | Conservation and Development for Social-Environmental Sustainability and Wellbeing\nStep 3: Submit forms, course fee, and attend a mandatory session.\nRegister here\n
