SUMMARY:MLC Language Learning Workshop #1: “Tips and Tricks to Become a Successful Language Learner”
DESCRIPTION:The Multimedia Language Centre (MLC) is hosting a workshop on Friday, Feb. 11, at 4:30 pm by Prof. Christiane Dumont (Associate Professor, French) and Khadeja Elsibai (Master of Public Policy, Administration and Law Program, with Minor in French). On Feb 11, the professor and the student will collaborate to offer language students a workshop “Tips and Tricks to Become a Successful Language Learner”. This interactive session, featuring the language learning cycle and strategies, is the pilot workshop of the MLC Language Learning Workshop Series that aims to help all language students make language learning easier, faster, and more fun, and bring students and professors closer to York University’s language learning community. Both professors and students are welcome to join!\nRegistration\n
