SUMMARY:Inclusion Week 2022 Keynote – The Call to Solidarity: Contingencies and Incongruities in Working Toward Justice
DESCRIPTION:This keynote session, presented as a part of the Insights series through the office of the VP Equity, People and Culture ( https://www.yorku.ca/vpepc/about-vice-president-equity-people-and-culture/ ), explores the meanings of solidarity and how solidarity might figure as a framework for working toward just, caring, equitable and sustainable futures.\nThe event speaker is Rubén Gaztambide-Fernández, professor of Curriculum & Pedagogy and editor-in-chief of the journal Curriculum Inquiry at the Ontario Institute for Studies in Education at the University of Toronto.\nRegister here ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_AgmrXdCLRjWr5QxaYIwZ0g ).\n
