SUMMARY:The Department of English presents BAHAR ORANG – “On care, beauty and Where Things Touch”
DESCRIPTION:BAHAR ORANG\n“On care, beauty and Where Things Touch”\nA remote conversation with Bahar Orang, author of Where Things Touch, on staying attuned to the fragile intimacies of care beyond the stifling demands of institutional environments.\nBahar Orang, author of Where Things Touch: A Meditation on Beauty (Book*hug, 2020), is a writer and clinician scholar in the Department of Psychiatry at the University of Toronto.\nMonday, Feb. 14 from 10:30 a.m. to noon.\nClick on the link to register: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMsdOyrqDwqG9ZE9-GtSlzwZW-FssqCLXzO ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMsdOyrqDwqG9ZE9-GtSlzwZW-FssqCLXzO )\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the meeting.\n \n
