SUMMARY:Word Sound Power: An annual celebration of Black Artistic Expression
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an evening of breathtaking and thought-provoking performances showcasing Black artistic expression. Featuring musical performances by the York R&B Ensemble and Oscar Peterson Scholarship Ensemble under the direction of Mike Cado, the York University Gospel Choir under the direction of Karen Burke, and spoken word artists from Griots to Emcees.\nWatch the event at www.yorku.ca/edu/bhm2022 ( https://www.yorku.ca/edu/bhm2022 )\nThis event in presented by the Jean Augustine Chair in Education, Community & Diaspora and is sponsored funded by Unifor.\nCo-sponsors of the event include:\n– Faculty of Education, York University\n– School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design, York University\n– Department of Humanities, York University\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/word-sound-power-an-annual-celebration-of-black-artistic-expression/
