SUMMARY:Grammar On! Workshop Three: A Tense Time
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nWe often think of grammar as a series of scary rules about “what-not-to-do”, but, in reality, grammar is a tool that you can use to write more effective sentences and increase your range of syntactical choices. Come join Dunja this Thursday at 10:30am in the Writing Centre’s Grammar On! series of workshops. The workshop is open to all students who want to learn to construct effective and beautiful sentences that say what you want them to say.\nGrammar On! Workshop Three – A Tense Time Do you feel tense when you think about time? Then make time this week to come talk about the 13 ways of Looking at Time in English sentences! In this Thursday’s Grammar On!, you’ll not only learn how to time-travel in your academic essays, but you’ll also discover that the past and present are both “simple” and “perfect”.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJoin Zoom\n\n\n\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/grammar-on-workshop-three-a-tense-time/
ORGANIZER;CN=Writing Centre:MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca, dbaus@yorku.ca, lapswrit@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp;PS Writing Centre,LA&amp;PS Writing Department
LOCATION:Zoom Webinar
