SUMMARY:Moving Forward: Thriving with my English Degree
DESCRIPTION:How will a degree in English or another humanities subject help your career? Come hear from graduates of LA&PS’ Department of English, who are currently in leadership roles, as they articulate how a degree in English supported them on their career journeys. Join us as we discuss their path to success and receive valuable advice.\nOur Panelists:\n• Jennifer Gold, BA, English & Psychology ’97 & LLB, Law ‘00 Partner at Wood Gold LLP & President at Women’s Law Association of Ontario\n• Nicolas DesRoches, BA, Professional Writing & Creative Writing ‘12 Marketing Manager, ApplyProof at ApplyBoard • Shawna Hayman, BA, English ‘05 VP, Business Lead at Cossette\n• Tamer Ibrahim, BA, English ‘08 Youth Collective Impact Program at Laidlaw Foundation\nHosted by Lily M. Cho, Associate Dean, Global & Community Engagement.  Includes Q&A session.\nRegister here\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/moving-forward-thriving-with-my-english-degree/
