SUMMARY:Inclusion Week 2022: Building and Sustaining Equitable and Caring Futures
DESCRIPTION:Join York University’s Centre for Human Rights, Equity, & Inclusion from Feb. 28 to March 3 for Inclusion Week ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-2022/ ), a free virtual event series featuring keynote speakers, fireside chats and interactive, skill-building workshops where we’ll explore sustainability in unique ways.\nThrough Inclusion Week, participants will ask questions like: Who gets to rest in challenging times? How does global interdependence reflect great divides and even greater needs for cooperation? and, How can we better understand the principles, practice and politics of sustainability in the context of a global pandemic?\nFor more information about the workshops, panelists, keynote speaker and registration, please visit https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-2022/ ( https://rights.info.yorku.ca/inclusion-week-2022/ ).\nThis event is free to York Community Members.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/inclusion-week-2022-building-and-sustaining-equitable-and-caring-futures/
