SUMMARY:Live Coding and Performance Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Organized by Marcus Gordon & Ilze Briede [Kavi] in collaboration with Sensorium: Centre for Digital Arts & Technology\nHow can we use Coding as a form of spontaneous, participatory art?\nJoin artists Marcus Gordon & Ilze Briede as they demonstrate the intersection of digital wizardry with performance and image-making. These sessions will feature both demonstrations and hands-on workshops that will teach basic coding skills and DIY strategies for creating computational, interactive artworks. We invite you to join us in creating new audiovisual scenographies no matter your existing tech proficiency – beginners and experts alike are welcomed!\nMarch 22, 2022\n2:30pm-4:30pm\n(Sensorium Loft – Room M333, 4th Floor Goldfarb Centre for the Arts)\nFREE\nFor in person events please RSVP to Marcus Gordon (magfoto@yorku.ca ( mailto:magfoto@yorku.ca )) and follow York University’s COVID regulations on the Better Together ( https://www.yorku.ca/bettertogether/ ) website, most importantly the completion of the YU Screen form ( https://yorku.ubixhealth.com/login ) the day you attend and wearing a mask at the venue.\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/live-coding-and-performance-sessions-3/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/coding.jpg
END:VEVENT
