SUMMARY:FGS presents “Why Black History (Month) Matters” — A Virtual Panel Discussion!
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies invites all students, postdocs, faculty, staff and alumni to attend our webinar entitled “Why Black History (Month) Matters” on Tuesday, Feb. 22 from noon to 1:15 p.m.\nAs we honour and celebrate Black History Month, there is importance in continuing the conversation around Black history, cultural and lived experiences.\nOur moderator for this event is Thomas Loebel, Dean & Associate Vice-President Graduate. The panel is made up of current Black faculty members and graduate scholars, which include:\n\nMuna-Udbi Ali, Assistant Professor, Faculty of Environmental and Urban Change\nMichele A. Johnson, Associate Dean Students & Professor, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies\nEmmanuel Frimpong, Doctoral Scholar in Political Science\nOcéane Nyela, Doctoral Scholar in Communication & Culture\nRossini Sandjong, Master’s Scholar in Public and International Affairs\n\nThis is a free event, however registration is required.\nTo register, visit https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_xJq_k3k8RKCDZhHukl_s5Q ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_xJq_k3k8RKCDZhHukl_s5Q )\nHave any questions? Please contact our Graduate Communications Manager, Anesa Albert at anesaa@yorku.ca ( mailto:anesaa@yorku.ca ).\n\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/why-bhm-matters/
ORGANIZER;CN=Faculty of Graduate Studies:MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Black History Month,Equity, Diversity &amp; Inclusion,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Health,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp; Technology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-Legal Studies,LA&amp;PS Addressing Anti-Black Racism,LA&amp;PS Alumni,LA&amp;PS Department of Equity Studies,LA&amp;PS Department of History,LA&amp;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp;PS Department of Social Science,LA&amp;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Gender, Sexuality and Women's Studies,LA&amp;PS School of Human Resources Management,LA&amp;PS School of Public Policy &amp; Administration,LA&amp;PS School of Social Work,LA&amp;PS Students All,LA&amp;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp;PS Students-International,Lassonde School of Engineering,Osgoode Hall Law School,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design,Schulich School of Business,Students
