SUMMARY:Sensorium Lunchtime Seminar Series (Winter 2022): Dr. Sarah Bay-Cheng
DESCRIPTION:The Lunchtime Seminar Series is a weekly event which aims to foster interconnectivity between faculty, graduate students, visiting scholars and artists within the School of the Arts, Media, Performance and Design. This casual series will host a variety of scholarly presentations by both York and visiting researchers who want to interface with our community and share their work.\nThe sessions take place weekly on Wednesdays from 11:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. Lectures will be virtual until it is safe to gather in-person, at which time it will be a hybrid format, with in-person sessions at Sensorium Loft Space (4th Floor CFA, Room M333) and a virtual stream for those who cannot attend in person.\nDue to COVID-19, in-person capacity is limited. Please adhere to York’s COVID regulations, including completion of the YU Screen and wearing a mask.\nDr. Sarah Bay-Cheng (Dean of School of the Arts, Media, Performance & Design/ Prof. Theatre Studies)\nMarch 9, 2022\nZOOM LINK ( https://yorku.zoom.us/j/93240735614?pwd=MUp1eWJQbjZ0amM2ejlHK1V5RkJudz09 )\nDr. Sarah Bay-Cheng’s research focuses on the intersections among theatre, performance, and media including histories of avant-garde theatre and film, social media, and digital technologies in performance. Her publications include the books Performance and Media: Taxonomies for a Changing Field (2015), Mapping Intermediality in Performance (2010), Poets at Play: An Anthology of Modernist Drama (2010) and Mama Dada: Gertrude Stein’s Avant-Garde Drama (2004) as well as articles, essays, and invited lectures. Her current book project considers digital historiography and performance. Prior to coming to York, she was a Fulbright Visiting Senior Scholar in Media and Cultural Studies at Utrecht University in the Netherlands (2015) and the founding director of the Technē Institute for the Arts and Emerging Technologies at the University at Buffalo (2012-2015). Since 2016, she can be heard as a co-host for On TAP: A Theatre and Performance Studies podcast. Bay-Cheng has also worked as a director and dramaturg with particular interest in intermedial collaborations and a fondness for puppetry. More information: https://sarahbaycheng.net. \nMore information available at: https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/lunchtime-seminar-series/ ( https://sensorium.ampd.yorku.ca/lunchtime-seminar-series/ )\n
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/sensorium-lunchtime-seminar-series-winter-2022-dr-sarah-bay-cheng/
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp; Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/lunchtimeseminars.jpg
END:VEVENT
