SUMMARY:Community Music Symposium: “Inclusive Music Making and Creative Ensembles”
DESCRIPTION:The Helen Carswell Chair in Community Engaged Research in the Arts presents, Community Music Symposium: “Inclusive Music Making and Creative Ensembles” with members of the Helen Carswell Research Team and keynote speaker, Phil Mullen.\nThursday, February 17 – Friday, February 18, 2022\nFeb. 17: 8:30 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nFeb. 18: 10:30 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nREGISTER HERE ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_IDeBz1QfSSeOW_7_s356_A )\nPresentation and workshop topics include:\n• Inclusive music making and creative starting points\n• Creative Ensemble Workshop\n• What is Community Music?\n• Inclusive Music Pedagogy\n• Strategic approaches to inclusion and community music\n• Strategies for children and young people in challenging circumstances\n\n
